{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:19:27.510Z","ordinal":78213,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-50634799-afa0-4719-9a54-65442279f732","process_id":"4041","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,90p' /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/install.sh; rg -n '^  --|^Usage|usage|NEXUS_INSTALL|ARCHIVE|BASE_URL|RELEASE' /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/install.sh | head -80; sed -n '45,90p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-rc2-package","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,90p' /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/install.sh","name":"install.sh","path":"/tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/install.sh"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^  --|''^Usage|usage|NEXUS_INSTALL|ARCHIVE|BASE_URL|RELEASE' /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/install.sh","query":"^  --|^Usage|usage|NEXUS_INSTALL|ARCHIVE|BASE_URL|RELEASE","path":"install.sh"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '45,90p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n5:BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\n45:  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n77:ARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\n83:curl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\n85:grep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n87:ARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n90:  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n92:    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n94:    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n126:        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\n144:  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n154:    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\n179:node - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, and the mock request log. If you provide both optional screenshots, their hashes are also recorded.\nA cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Screenshot presence does not\nchange the gate. Commit the evidence directory to the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":708494519}},"started_at_ms":1793733566799,"completed_at_ms":1793733567508}}
