{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:24:35.814Z","ordinal":78480,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea34eeeebc81a38fceb1ee71682cfe","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found the cause: the package preserved a group-writable mode on its compiler-inventory helper, and the evaluator correctly refused to trust it. This comes from the shared checkout’s permissions, not a provider outage. I’m adding a regression at the packaging boundary so staged runtime files drop group/other write bits, then I’ll rebuild and repeat the exact-artifact checks."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793733870965,"completed_at_ms":1793733875813}}
