ifact-c/compatibility.json\nb243cda661eb0a57890435cfa2170fb50ea8e507aeec595d364d3f2ce71c8125  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/install.sh\nf01cee6c5611f5f404f62c9ca536b2c334f47a0192d0298855f8953342488789  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/SHA256SUMS\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3:**Status as of 2026-11-03: corrected RC2 source gates passed; artifact, installed-candidate, and publication qualification remain open.**\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:4:This record tracks the v1.1.2 candidate on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. After correcting CERI provenance to use the package build identity, `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips, including the terminal process-scope fixtures; the security lifecycle gates passed and `make build` passed (including TypeScript type checking). Full-suite log SHA-256: `39cad26938be30dbb4b073a4d93e62a80aa920789e751cccba5465795eb362bd`. The regression test was RED against the old RC1 provenance and its focused green run passed 3/3 tests (log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). The corrected candidate is based on source commit `f6d474a4` with RC2 package metadata and the CERI provenance fix; a clean exact commit build and fresh RC2 archive are still required.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:6:The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive is historical and is not eligible for release. The current source candidate is being advanced to RC2; no RC2 archive or installed-candidate evidence has been produced yet.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:22:## Work-package status\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:24:| Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence details |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:28:| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Serialized complete CLI suite passed (2,251 tests). Process-scope fixtures passed with zero orphaned processes. 6-task installed acceptance passed. | **PASSED** | Manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Evidence preserved in `docs/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-28d79f3b0f4d.json`. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:29:| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Verified package parity and standalone CLI execution outside repository checkout. | **PASSED** | Validated in `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` (5/5 passed). Verified with isolated HOME, dataset selection, and structured scoring. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:33:| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:39:| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; package qualification pending** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:40:| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Prior six-task package evidence is bound to the historical `9c1926e1` archive, not source `97945557`. Rebuild and rerun installed-candidate acceptance. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:41:| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Prior package parity evidence predates `97945557`; rebuild the archive and rerun standalone CLI parity on the new package. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42:| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite; bind the supported-endpoint metric to the rebuilt release candidate. | **SOURCE PASSED; package qualification pending** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:43:| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Corrected RC2 full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo security scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures passed. Package checksums, SBOM, installer, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility remain pending for the fresh archive. | **SOURCE GATES PASSED; artifact gates pending** |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:49:- **Package Archive:** `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz` (superseded; do not publish)\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:59:  - Total Components: 141 (119 Cargo crates + 20 npm packages + root product)\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:73:- [ ] Release scans, package checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility verified for the final archive.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:74:- [ ] CLI option compatibility and installed-candidate acceptance verified for the final archive.\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:20:# 1. Generate Rust SBOM for the exact platform shipped by package-linux.sh.\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:24:# cargo-cyclonedx can include compile-only dependencies in its package graph.\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:64:    raise SystemExit(\"Cargo SBOM has no parseable root package identity\")\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:67:    raise SystemExit(\"Cargo production dependency graph does not contain the SBOM root package\")\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:79:        raise SystemExit(f\"Cargo SBOM component has an invalid package URL: {purl!r}\")\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:150:# 2. Generate the Node production SBOM from cli/package-lock.json with npm's\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:158:  --package-lock-only \\\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:3:// The expected stable tree is rebuilt from the RC tree by taking the stable root package.json (which may differ from\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:22:const rcPackageText = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${rc}:package.json`], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:23:const rcPackage = JSON.parse(rcPackageText);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:24:const stablePackageText = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${stable}:package.json`], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:25:const stablePackage = JSON.parse(stablePackageText);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:27:const stableVersion = new RegExp(`^(${numeric}\\\\.${numeric}\\\\.${numeric})$`).exec(stablePackage.version);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:28:if (!stableVersion) fail(`stable version '${stablePackage.version}' is not a stable SemVer`);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:29:const rcVersion = new RegExp(`^(${numeric}\\\\.${numeric}\\\\.${numeric})-rc\\\\.${numeric}$`).exec(rcPackage.version);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:30:if (!rcVersion) fail(`RC version '${rcPackage.version}' is not a release-candidate SemVer`);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:31:if (stableVersion?.[1] !== rcVersion[1]) fail(`stable version ${stablePackage.version} does not match RC ${rcPackage.version}`);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:32:if (!isDeepStrictEqual({ ...rcPackage, version: null }, { ...stablePackage, version: null })) fail(\"root package.json changes more than its version\");\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:35:if (rcPackageText.replace(versionField(rcPackage.version), `$1\"${stablePackage.version}\"`) !== stablePackageText) fail(\"root package.json text changes more than its version string\");\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:40:  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(work, \"package.json\"), stablePackageText);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:43:  if (differing) fail(`stable commit differs from RC + sync-version ${stablePackage.version} in: ${differing.split(\"\\n\").join(\", \")}`);\nscripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs:45:  console.log(`version-only: ${stable} = ${rc} + v${stablePackage.version} (${changed.join(\", \")})`);\nscripts/package-smoke-server.mjs:6:    response.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \"package-smoke\" }] }));\nscripts/package-smoke-server.mjs:13:      `data: ${JSON.stringify({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { content: \"NEXUS_PACKAGE_SMOKE_OK\" } }] })}\\n\\n`,\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:25:export function stageEvaluatorRuntime(sourceRoot, packageRoot) {\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:27:  const target = path.resolve(packageRoot);\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:40:      throw new Error(`evaluator runtime path escapes package root: ${relativePath}`);\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:50:  const [, , sourceRoot, packageRoot] = process.argv;\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:51:  if (!sourceRoot || !packageRoot) {\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:52:    console.error(\"usage: stage_eval_runtime.mjs <source-root> <package-root>\");\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:55:    try { stageEvaluatorRuntime(sourceRoot, packageRoot); }\nscripts/package-smoke-pty.py:15:    print(\"usage: package-smoke-pty.py COMMAND [ARGS...]\", file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/package-smoke-pty.py:33:    # This smoke test asserts packaged TUI startup, not the workspace-trust chooser.\nscripts/registry-package-name.mjs:1:// Encode npm package names as a single registry URL path segment.\nscripts/registry-package-name.mjs:2:export function registryPackageName(name) {\nscripts/package-linux.sh:4:# An externally selected package tool may target a separate immutable RC checkout, but it must\nscripts/package-linux.sh:6:ROOT=${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:8:if [[ -n \"${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-}\" ]]; then\nscripts/package-linux.sh:12:    echo \"NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE must be the current Git worktree root\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:16:VERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:17:OUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:50:    --env HOME=/tmp/nexus-package-build-home \\\nscripts/package-linux.sh:65:cp \"$ROOT/cli/package.json\" \"$ROOT/cli/package-lock.json\" \"$PKG/lib/cli/\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:69:command -v readelf >/dev/null || { echo \"readelf is required to verify package glibc compatibility\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/package-linux.sh:91:if (!Number.isSafeInteger(version) || version < 1) throw new Error('packaged client has no valid state schema');\nscripts/package-linux.sh:135:cp \"$ROOT/scripts/release-tools/package.json\" \"$ROOT/scripts/release-tools/package-lock.json\" \"$RELEASE_TOOLS/\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:136:node \"$ROOT/scripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs\" \"$ROOT/scripts/release-tools/package-lock.json\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:161:    --mount \"type=bind,src=$PKG/lib/cli,dst=/package,readonly\" \\\nscripts/package-linux.sh:169:      exec ./node_modules/.bin/license-checker-rseidelsohn --production --plainVertical --start /package\nscripts/package-linux.sh:177:This package contains third-party software components licensed under open-source\nscripts/package-linux.sh:215:# digest even when every packaged file is identical. Use the same digest-pinned\nscripts/package-linux.sh:222:    --mount \"type=bind,src=$WORK,dst=/nexus-package,readonly\" \\\nscripts/package-linux.sh:224:    --workdir /nexus-package \\\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:2:// Fail closed when a supported npm dependency lock contains a deprecated package.\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:5:import { registryPackageName } from \"./registry-package-name.mjs\";\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:9:  console.error(\"usage: check_deprecated_lock.mjs <package-lock.json>\");\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:14:if (lock.lockfileVersion < 2 || !lock.packages || typeof lock.packages !== \"object\") {\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:18:function packageName(location) {\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:24:  if (marker < 0 || !parts[marker + 1]) throw new Error(`cannot derive package name from lock path ${location}`);\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:31:for (const [location, metadata] of Object.entries(lock.packages)) {\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:33:  const name = packageName(location);\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:41:const packages = [...entries.values()];\nscripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs:48:    if (index >= packages.length) return;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":694696587}},"started_at_ms":1793734676979,"completed_at_ms":1793734677674}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:37:59.078Z","ordinal":78826,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2eb-1a26-77b3-b2f0-bceae96513c0","call_id":"call_f1a3b73db8d54a6ab7c4108f6ff9c7e0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3434)\nTotal output lines: 88\n\n5389945 /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.2.tar.gz\n159306 /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/sbom.cdx.json\n241684 /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\ne44dfa6cd62d670a359a6b45c04ce86cc61e31ab400396adc2197fae9d4cfcb2  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/sbom.cdx.json\n36af3f42d8da5942d9ea3d669dfd68b5b72310ac9609bab237ed2acf861a4723  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\nd22b6e8311a38b72f9a606ea9c82288a5bfb3d4a10265c8c6891042ce5a1489a  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/compatibility.json\nb243cda661eb0a57890435cfa2170fb50ea8e507aeec595d364d3f2ce71c8125  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/install.sh\nf01cee6c5611f5f404f62c9ca536b2c334f47a0192d0298855f8953342488789  /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/SHA256SUMS\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:3:**Status as of 2026-11-03: corrected RC2 source gates passed; artifact, installed-candidate, and publication qualification remain open.**\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:4:This record tracks the v1.1.2 candidate on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. After correcting CERI provenance to use the package build identity, `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips, including the terminal process-scope fixtures; the security lifecycle gates passed and `make build` passed (including TypeScript type checking). Full-suite log SHA-256: `39cad26938be30dbb4b073a4d93e62a80aa920789e751cccba5465795eb362bd`. The regression test was RED against the old RC1 provenance and its focused green run passed 3/3 tests (log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). The corrected candidate is based on source commit `f6d474a4` with RC2 package metadata and the CERI provenance fix; a clean exact commit build and fresh RC2 archive are still required.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:6:The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive is historical and is not eligible for release. The current source candidate is being advanced to RC2; no RC2 archive or installed-candidate evidence has been produced yet.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:22:## Work-package status\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:24:| Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence details |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:28:| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Serialized complete CLI s…2034 tokens truncated…t, but it must\nscripts/package-linux.sh:6:ROOT=${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:8:if [[ -n \"${NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE:-}\" ]]; then\nscripts/package-linux.sh:12:    echo \"NEXUS_PACKAGE_SOURCE must be the current Git worktree root\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:16:VERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:17:OUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:50:    --env HOME=/tmp/nexus-package-build-home \\\nscripts/package-linux.sh:65:cp \"$ROOT/cli/package.json\" \"$ROOT/cli/package-lock.json\" \"$PKG/lib/cli/\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:69:command -v readelf >/dev/null || { echo \"readelf i