{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:38:24.273Z","ordinal":78837,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea3820bbe881a3be95a919e9f7db37","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dfb013c5b56d494d8579c005bd966420","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@\\n-**Status as of 2026-11-03: corrected RC2 source gates passed; artifact, installed-candidate, and publication qualification remain open.**\\n-This record tracks the v1.1.2 candidate on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). A fresh RC2 archive and installed-candidate qualification remain required.\\n+**Status as of 2026-11-03: exact RC2 source and installed-package gates passed; provider-matrix, external CI/review, and publication gates remain open.**\\n+This record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\\n@@\\n-The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive is historical and is not eligible for release. The current source candidate is being advanced to RC2; no RC2 archive or installed-candidate evidence has been produced yet.\\n+The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished.\\n@@\\n-| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Serialized complete CLI suite passed (2,251 tests). Process-scope fixtures passed with zero orphaned processes. 6-task installed acceptance passed. | **PASSED** | Manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Evidence preserved in `docs/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-28d79f3b0f4d.json`. |\\n-| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Verified package parity and standalone CLI execution outside repository checkout. | **PASSED** | Validated in `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` (5/5 passed). Verified with isolated HOME, dataset selection, and structured scoring. |\\n+| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Exact RC2 archive acceptance invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and confirmed hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. | **PASSED — dataset boundary** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Exact archive evidence: [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d.json), archive SHA-256 `3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b`. The deterministic fixture only reports task completion; hidden validators intentionally remain false, so this is not task-solving or provider-quality evidence. |\\n+| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | [`eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json) passed 5/5 tests on the exact archive with isolated HOME and a deterministic loopback provider; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. |\\n@@\\n-| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; package qualification pending** |\\n-| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Prior six-task package evidence is bound to the historical `9c1926e1` archive, not source `97945557`. Rebuild and rerun installed-candidate acceptance. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\\n-| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Prior package parity evidence predates `97945557`; rebuild the archive and rerun standalone CLI parity on the new package. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\\n-| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite; bind the supported-endpoint metric to the rebuilt release candidate. | **SOURCE PASSED; package qualification pending** |\\n-| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | On exact commit `e134dcd5`, full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo security scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures passed. Package checksums, SBOM, installer, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility remain pending for the fresh archive. | **SOURCE GATES PASSED; artifact gates pending** |\\n+| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\\n+| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\\n+| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\\n+| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\\n+| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Exact source commit passed full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo lifecycle scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures. The exact archive is reproducible, has a validated 141-component CycloneDX SBOM and checksums, installs through `install.sh`, and passes package runtime/CLI acceptance. External CodeQL/CI and release-level PTY evidence are not present in this record. | **SOURCE AND LOCAL ARTIFACT GATES PASS; EXTERNAL CI / PTY PENDING** |\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793734688.7356706}}}
