{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:42:16.862Z","ordinal":78993,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-978c2a8f-75e8-4198-b517-5154bb813e6e","process_id":"45421","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md && rg -n 'G1\\.1|constrained|99\\.5|technical debt|provider endpoint|release gate' docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2 docs/releases/v1.1.2.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md","name":"ROADMAP.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"G1\\\\.1|constrained|99\\\\.5|technical debt|provider endpoint|release gate\" docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2 docs/releases/v1.1.2.md","query":"G1\\.1|constrained|99\\.5|technical debt|provider endpoint|release gate","path":"v1.1.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code Post-v1.0.0 Roadmap: v1.1.0 – v1.3.0\n\n**Status:** Draft / Active Planning\n**Baseline:** Nexus Code `v1.0.0` (Release Candidate Baseline)\n**Parent Strategy:** Evaluation-Driven Development, Local-First Observability & Operator Sovereignty\n\n---\n\n## 1. Release Schedule Overview\n\n```\n2026-Q4                             2027-Q1                             2027-Q2\n───┬───────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬───►\n   │                                   │                                   │\n   ▼                                   ▼                                   ▼\nv1.0.0 (Baseline Freeze)            v1.1.0                              v1.2.0\n- Linux x86-64 Hardened             - OTel Local Tracing                - Session Replay Engine\n- Security Boundaries & Sandbox     - Versioned Eval Datasets           - Experiment Comparator\n- Ratatui TUI & Token Accounting    - Flight Recorder Redaction         - TUI Trace Inspector\n- Deterministic Packages & Provenance - Standalone `nexus eval` CLI      - Human Annotation Queue\n                                    - Deterministic Code Evaluators     - Failure Clustering\n                                    - GBNF Tool Grammar Engine          - Composio Dev Bridge (WP-1207)\n                                    - Dependabot Modernization (WP-1108)│\n                                                                        ▼\n                                                                        v1.3.0\n                                                                        - Standard OTLP Exporter\n                                                                        - Full Context Provenance (CTX-1)\n                                                                        - macOS / arm64 Builds\n                                                                        - Knowledge Freshness (CTX-2)\n                                                                        - Composio 250+ App Mesh (WP-1306)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Milestone v1.1.0: Observability Foundations & Eval Harness\n\n**Target:** Initial feature release post-v1.0.0\n**Theme:** Establish the local trace standard, sanitize flight recordings, and migrate evaluation from ad-hoc scripts to versioned datasets with reference oracles.\n\n### Work Packages\n\n| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n\n### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n\n- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\n- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n\n### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n\nFollowing the PR #8 integration merge to `main`, Dependabot opened 27 automated dependency update pull requests (PRs #103–#129). These are triaged into 5 distinct integration batches scheduled for the v1.1.0 development cycle (deferred from v1.0.0):\n\n#### Batch 1: Core Rust Engine Runtime (Low Risk / Initial v1.1.0 Release Cycle)\nPatches to Rust core dependencies that preserve API compatibility and improve stability and performance:\n- **PR #105:** `tokio` (1.53.1 → 1.53.3 in `/core`) — Async runtime maintenance patch.\n- **PR #107:** `similar` (2.7.0 → 3.2.0 in `/core`) — Text diffing library major SemVer upgrade.\n- **PR #110:** `libc` (0.2.189 → 0.2.191 in `/core`) — System call bindings patch.\n- **PR #113:** `serde_json` (1.0.151 → 1.0.154 in `/core`) — Serialization optimization patch.\n- *Verification Requirement:* `cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml` under isolated HOME; bit-for-bit packaging `cmp` check.\n\n#### Batch 2: Cloudflare Experimental Micro-Workers (Low Risk / Isolated)\nMaintenance updates for the isolated Cloudflare artifacts vertical slice (retired contest contract track):\n- **PRs #125, #126, #127, #128:** `vite` (8.3.3 → 8.3.4 across root and worker packages).\n- **PRs #115, #117, #118:** `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` (2.0.0-beta.sha-52b0dc0e9 → 2.0.0-beta.v.1).\n- **PRs #109, #116, #121, #122, #123:** `cf` (1.0.0-beta.10 → 1.0.0-beta.18 across worker bundles).\n- *Verification Requirement:* `npm run build --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice` and typecheck pass.\n\n#### Batch 3: GitHub Actions CI Workflows (Medium Risk / CI Pipeline Validation)\nModernization of hosted automation actions in `.github/workflows/`:\n- **PR #103:** `actions/attest-build-provenance` (commit hash update for SLSA build provenance).\n- **PR #104:** `actions/checkout` (v4.4.0 → v7.0.1) — Major runner checkout upgrade.\n- **PR #106:** `actions/download-artifact` (v4.3.0 → v8.0.2) — Artifact fetcher upgrade.\n- **PR #108:** `softprops/action-gh-release` (v2.6.2 → v3.0.3) — GitHub release asset upload upgrade.\n- **PR #112:** `actions/setup-node` (v4.4.0 → v7.1.0) — Node environment provisioning upgrade.\n- *Verification Requirement:* Staged workflow validation on test branch; assert identical artifact download and release asset publishing behavior.\n\n#### Batch 4: TypeScript Compiler & Typing Toolchain (Medium Risk / Type Safety Validation)\nModernization of the TypeScript compiler toolchain:\n- **PR #119:** `typescript` (5.9.3 → 7.0.2 in `/demo`) — Demo runner compiler bump.\n- **PR #124:** `@types/node` (22.20.4 → 26.6.5 in `/cli`) — Node.js runtime typings.\n- **PR #129:** `typescript` (5.9.3 → 7.0.2 in `/cli`) — Core CLI compiler bump.\n- *Verification Requirement:* Zero TypeScript compiler errors (`npm run build --prefix cli`, `tsc --noEmit`), clean declaration emission, and zero new `any` casts.\n\n#### Batch 5: Production CLI Runtime Libraries (High Risk / Breaking API Migration)\nMajor version bumps requiring focused API compatibility audits and code changes:\n- **PR #111:** `dotenv` (16.6.1 → 18.0.8 in `/cli`) — Environment loading library update. Verify untrusted workspace `.env` rejection invariants (REQ-SEC-001) remain strictly intact.\n- **PR #114:** `commander` (12.1.0 → 15.0.0 in `/cli`) — Major CLI option parser upgrade. Requires comprehensive audit of subcommands (`nexus run`, `check`, `models`, `upgrade`), option parsing (`--strict-token-count`, `--isolated-home`), and exit code propagation.\n- **PR #120:** `ora` (8.2.0 → 9.4.1 in `/cli`) — Terminal spinner library update. Validate stdout/stderr streaming, non-interactive CI fallback, and Ratatui TUI coexistence.\n- *Verification Requirement:* Full CLI unit and PTY suite (1,511+ tests), CLI journey tests (`cli/test/system_journey.test.ts`), and doctor verification.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Milestone v1.2.0: Experiment Comparison, Replay & Annotation\n\n**Target:** Second feature release post-v1.0.0\n**Theme:** Diagnostic reproducibility, statistical comparison across agent versions, interactive TUI trace inspection, and human annotation workflows.\n\n### Work Packages\n\n| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **WP-1201** | **Deterministic Session Replay** | Implement `nexus replay <trace-id>`: Re-executes tool calls and container steps from a recorded trace inside an isolated bubblewrap container to reproduce bugs without re-calling the model. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §1.1 |\n| **WP-1202** | **Experiment Comparator** | Implement `eval/compare.mjs` comparing two experiment runs with Wilson score 95% confidence intervals, token cost deltas, duration deltas, and regression matrices. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.4 |\n| **WP-1203** | **Interactive TUI Trace Inspector** | Add a hierarchical trace inspector panel to `nexus-tui` (Ratatui), allowing operators to view the tool call tree, intermediate stdout, and latency distributions. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n| **WP-1204** | **Human Review & Annotation Queue** | Implement `nexus review <session-id>`: Interactive CLI / TUI prompt guiding reviewers through structured rubrics (tool correctness, intent fulfillment) and recording signed audit evidence. | `REQ-AGT-010`, `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §6 |\n| **WP-1205** | **Heuristic Failure Clustering** | Implement automated classification of failing eval runs into structured failure modes (`TIMEOUT`, `LOOP_DETECTED`, `SCHEMA_CORRUPTION`, `UNAUTHORIZED_PATH`, `COMPILER_ERROR`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §7 |\n| **WP-1206** | **`/tdd` Phase Enforcement** | Enforce red-green-refactor phase invariants when running under test-driven development posture. | `VER-08`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n| **WP-1207** | **Composio Developer Ecosystem & Review Bridge** | Integrate Composio platform connectors (backed by Composio Startup Program Pro) to provide managed OAuth and bidirectional developer workflows: automated Linear and Jira issue creation from failure clusters (`WP-1205`), GitHub pull request review synchronization, and Slack/Discord notification dispatch for human annotation queues (`WP-1204`). Operates under strict zero-leak credential isolation (`CRED003`), unprivileged execution sandbox boundaries, and requires explicit operator confirmation for write actions. | Composio Startup Program, `POSITIONING.md` §3.8 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Milestone v1.3.0: Standard OTLP Exporters & Platform Expansion\n\n**Target:** Enterprise & multi-platform release\n**Theme:** Standard OpenTelemetry network export, full context provenance graphs, knowledge lifecycle management, and macOS/arm64 architecture support.\n\n### Work Packages\n\n| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **WP-1301** | **OpenTelemetry OTLP Exporter** | Add standard OTLP HTTP/gRPC exporter plug-in allowing operators to stream traces to local or network collectors (Jaeger, SigNoz, Langfuse, LangSmith) under strict egress allowlists. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §9.3 |\n| **WP-1302** | **Full Context Provenance Graph** | Implement complete graph metadata for all context admissions (tracking origin file, trust classification, transformation history, and compaction survival). | `CTX-001`, `REQ-AGT-010` |\n| **WP-1303** | **macOS & arm64 Build Pipelines** | Add native GitHub Actions packaging runners and platform sandboxing (macOS `sandbox-exec` / Linux `arm64`). | `DEC-12`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n| **WP-1304** | **Knowledge Freshness & Lifecycle** | Implement automated staleness detection, contradiction resolution, and operator prompts for expiring project knowledge. | `CTX-002`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n| **WP-1305** | **cgroup v2 Fine-Grained Limits** | Add direct per-command CPU throttling and memory caps via systemd/cgroup-v2 scopes. | `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Architectural Invariants Across All Post-v1 Releases\n\n1. **Security & Boundary Preservation:** No post-v1 observability or evaluation feature may bypass or weaken the v1.0.0 security boundaries (untrusted `.env` rejection, SSRF blocking, container path confinement, or workspace trust).\n2. **Local Sovereignty:** Nexus remains 100% operational in air-gapped, offline, and self-hosted environments. External network transmission of telemetry is disabled by default and strictly opt-in.\n3. **Open Standards:** Telemetry formats conform to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions rather than proprietary vendor SDKs.\n4. **Reproducibility:** All benchmark datasets, evaluator code, and comparison tools are committed directly to the repository and execute deterministically under isolated `$HOME`.\n5. **Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages (Inviolable Invariant):**\n   - Strictly **NO deprecated packages or unmaintained third-party library dependencies** may ever be introduced, merged, or retained in any component or release—ever.\n   - Every npm dependency and Cargo crate must be on active, supported upstream releases.\n   - Automated CI gates fail closed on:\n     - Any npm package marked `deprecated` by the npm registry (`npm audit` and package-tree deprecation scans).\n     - Any Rust crate flagged as unmaintained, yanked, or deprecated in the RustSec advisory database (`cargo deny check bans advisories`).\n   - *Platform engines vs. libraries:* Platform runtime engine requirements (such as Node.js) follow explicit project architectural decisions (DEC-12), with upstream EOL status disclosed and modern LTS versions recommended.\n   - When upstream library dependencies announce deprecation or breaking lifecycles, Nexus must refactor, migrate, or replace them before minor release qualification. Under no circumstances may technical debt be deferred into permanent legacy layers.\n6. **Opt-In External Integrations & Boundary Invariant:**\n   - All third-party services and app connectors (including Composio developer bridges and enterprise app toolsets) are strictly **opt-in** and disabled by default.\n   - Nexus Code must always retain 100% operational capability in air-gapped, zero-network environments without external API keys.\n   - External tokens (`NEXUS_COMPOSIO_API_KEY`) must never be leaked into git commits, trace logs, or flight recordings (`CRED003`).\n   - High-impact or state-mutating actions on external services require explicit operator confirmation prompts before execution.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:77:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:133:for the release gate, not for implementation.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:8:actually exists, and maps each item to specification sections, work packages, tests, and release gates. Companion\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:38:| No accepted RC and no recorded independent §8 acceptance for the stable artifact | `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 stage 5; open issues #5, #7 | v1.1.0 must not assume a fully qualified baseline. Its release gates must name which v1.0 gates are inherited as *unproven*. |\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:76:  step that entered constrained recovery; refusal starts once the model has seen the note.\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:81:  and a call's own verdict never counts for itself, so a no-op write loop is still constrained and stopped.\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:82:- A later episode on the same objective, after its notes are spent, is constrained at once.\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:88:Pinned on every request while constrained (rebuilt per request, so its budget and presence lines are current). The\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:110:  repeats are still loops, and one that runs while constrained exhausts recovery;\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:125:- `recovery_constrained`\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:142:| Incident replay (fixture `NONPROGRESS-20261101-DOCTOR`): advisory, then constrained, then refusal, then a bounded stop; all RECOVERY_REQUIRED sections; no repeat executed after the constrained note | regression fixture |\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:143:| The agent takes another path after the constrained note, and recovery completes | regression fixture |\ndocs/v1.1.2/NON_PROGRESS_RECOVERY.md:153:| Session resume while constrained keeps the constraint | continuity |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The WP-1103 and WP-1104 integration claims are held by root on `v1/v112-integrated-exact`, based on `a0d374e8`. The WP-1103 umbrella covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`; runner claims cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and the dataset tests. The current candidate-specific G1.1-2 evidence is `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-27dbbb8120e7.json`; earlier generic and `b385cd…` records are retained as historical and are not current-candidate proof. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips and record candidate archive SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, captured-request digests and validator/scorer results in a new candidate-specific evidence file. Do not overwrite prior evidence. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. This is G1.1-2 execution/isolation evidence, not a model-quality test or release gate substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:37:FRICTION: full repository regression and independent quality approval remain open. The premature remote `v1.1.0` tag is unpublished; no later tag may be created until all release gates pass.\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:118:| Final ledger and release gate | Open (issue #7) | Inherited |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:123:The earlier draft placed `trace.jsonl` beside session state under `sessions/<session-id>/`. WP-1101 follows release gate G1.1-1, which explicitly requires traces under `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`; the diagram above is the reconciled normative path. Session state remains under `sessions/`, and trace files are stored once under `traces/`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:202:To prevent JSON argument parse failures and conversational rambling from open-weights models, Nexus v1.1.0 provides a logit-level constrained decoding engine targeting near-zero repair retries on supported inference backends:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:240:- **Unconstrained Fallback:** Retains heuristic regex and `repairJson` recovery when running against servers without grammar sampling support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:165:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus currently treats evaluation as a pre-release gate (M5 qualification). Adopting the lifecycle model would make evaluation continuous: production findings feed back into the eval dataset, and RC fixes are validated offline before redeployment.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:62:| **External App Ecosystem** | Built-in CLI toolset | Manual MCP configuration per server | Git/terminal commands only | **Composio 250+ App Ecosystem Bridge (Opt-in managed OAuth, GBNF-constrained schemas, automated Linear/Jira failure filing)** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:139:- **The Problem:** Open-weights models (7B/14B parameter models like Qwen 2.5 Coder, DeepSeek R1, Llama 3) frequently derail during agentic loops due to malformed JSON outputs, hallucinated tool parameter names, trailing unescaped characters, or discursive conversational chatter before the JSON payload. In unconstrained clients, this triggers expensive iterative retry loops, context pollution, or total agent failure.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:143:  - **Hybrid CoT Grammar:** For reasoning architectures (DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), Nexus enforces a hybrid grammar: unconstrained internal reasoning within `<think>...</think>` tokens, transitioning deterministically into strict schema-constrained tool call emission.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:144:  - **Zero Repair Target:** Targets near-zero repair overhead (`repair_rate = 0.00` and `ERR_PARSER = 0`), allowing resource-constrained 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models to execute multi-turn agentic workflows with high syntactic reliability.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:148:- **The Problem:** Autonomous agents that operate exclusively on local files leave developers with the manual burden of copy-pasting compiler errors into Jira/Linear tickets, notifying teammates on Slack, or manually provisioning API keys for external cloud services. Conversely, agents with unconstrained external API tools frequently hallucinate non-existent API parameters, break JSON payloads, or leak sensitive tokens into logs.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:190:- **Nexus Solution:** High-performance Rust binary (`harness-core`), keyboard-driven Ratatui terminal UI (`nexus-tui`), and native GBNF / Outlines logit-constrained tool calling with hybrid reasoning support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:5:G1.1-5 release gate is complete.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:119:merged or as satisfying G1.1-5.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:218:or the full WP-1108 / G1.1-5 acceptance evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:55:- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:56:- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:57:- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:59:- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:155:   - When upstream library dependencies announce deprecation or breaking lifecycles, Nexus must refactor, migrate, or replace them before minor release qualification. Under no circumstances may technical debt be deferred into permanent legacy layers.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":751093901}},"started_at_ms":1793734936110,"completed_at_ms":1793734936862}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:42:17.692Z","ordinal":78994,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"SubAgentActivity","model":null,"reasoning_effort":null,"id":"subagent-completed-01a1a2ee-5d8e-75c3-89ed-6dc8149128e4","kind":"completed","agent_thread_id":"01a19373-9d11-76b2-a9f8-663d0ae07013","agent_path":"/root/review_delta"},"started_at_ms":1793734937692,"completed_at_ms":1793734937692}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:42:18.133Z","ordinal":78995,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2ef-0e14-7760-9fac-c1a3d4df91ff","call_id":"call_f00b1a84059541fbb662ecc7f9712dce","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7087)\nTotal output lines: 197\n\n# Nexus Code Post-v1.0.0 Roadmap: v1.1.0 – v1.3.0\n\n**Status:** Draft / Active Planning\n**Baseline:** Nexus Code `v1.0.0` (Release Candidate Baseline)\n**Parent Strategy:** Evaluation-Driven Development, Local-First Observability & Operator Sovereignty\n\n---\n\n## 1. Release Schedule Overview\n\n```\n2026-Q4                             2027-Q1                             2027-Q2\n───┬───────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬───►\n   │                                   │                                   │\n   ▼                                   ▼                                   ▼\nv1.0.0 (Baseline Freeze)            v1.1.0                              v1.2.0\n- Linux x86-64 Hardened             - OTel Local Tracing                - Session Replay Engine\n- Security Boundaries & Sandbox     - Versioned Eval Datasets           - Experiment Comparator\n- Ratatui TUI & Token Accounting    - Flight Recorder Redaction         - TUI Trace Inspector\n- Deterministic Packages & Provenance - Standalone `nexus eval` CLI      - Human Annotation Queue\n                                    - Deterministic Code Evaluators     - Failure Clustering\n                                    - GBNF Tool Grammar Engine          - Composio Dev Bridge (WP-1207)\n                                    - Dependabot Modernization (WP-1108)│\n                                                                        ▼\n                                                                        v1.3.0\n                                                                        - Standard OTLP Exporter\n                                                                        - Full Context Provenance (CTX-1)\n                                                                        - macOS / arm64 Builds\n                                                                        - Knowledge Freshness (CTX-2)\n                                                                        - Composio 250+ App Mesh (WP-1306)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Milestone v1.1.0: Observability Foundations & Eval Harness\n\n**Target:** Initial feature release post-v1.0.0\n**Theme:** Establish the local trace standard, sanitize flight recordings, and migrate evaluation from ad-hoc scripts to versioned datasets with reference oracles.\n\n### Work Packages\n\n| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n\n### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n\n- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\n- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n\n### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n\nFollowing the PR #8 integration merge to `main`, Dependabot opened 27 automated dependency update pull requests (PRs #103–#129). These are triaged into 5 distinct integration batches scheduled for the v1.1.0 development cycle (deferred from v1.0.0):\n\n#### Batch 1: Core Rust Engine Runtime (Low Risk / Initial v1.1.0 Release Cycle)\nPatches to Rust core dependencies that preserve API compatibility and improve stability and performance:\n- **PR #105:** `tokio` (1.53.1 → 1.53.3 in `/core`) — Async runtime maintenance patch.\n- **PR #107:** `similar` (2.7.0 → 3.2.0 in `/core`) — Text diffing library major SemVer upgrade.\n- **PR #110:** `libc` (0.2.189 → 0.2.191 in `/core`) — System call bindings patch.\n- **PR #113:** `serde_json` (1.0.151 → 1.0.154 in `/core`) — Serialization optimization patch.\n- *Verification Requirement:* `cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml` under isolated HOME; bit-for-bit packaging `cmp` check.\n\n#### Batch 2: Cloudflare Experimental Micro-Workers (Low Risk / Isolated)\nMaintenance updates for the isolated Cloudflare artifacts vertical slice (retired contest contract track):\n- **PRs #125, #126, #127, #128:** `vite` (8.3.3 → 8.3.4 across root and worker packages).\n- **PRs #115, #117, #118:** `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` (2.0.0-beta.sha-52b0dc0e9 → 2.0.0-beta.v.1).\n- **PRs #109, #11…3087 tokens truncated…claimed/current ownership:** The WP-1103 and WP-1104 integration claims are held by root on `v1/v112-integrated-exact`, based on `a0d374e8`. The WP-1103 umbrella covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`; runner claims cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and the dataset tests. The current candidate-specific G1.1-2 evidence is `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-27dbbb8120e7.json`; earlier generic and `b385cd…` records are retained as historical and are not current-candidate proof. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips and record candidate archive SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, captured-request digests and validator/scorer results in a new candidate-specific evidence file. Do not overwrite prior evidence. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. This is G1.1-2 execution/isolation evidence, not a model-quality test or release gate substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:37:FRICTION: full repository regression and independent quality approval remain open. The premature remote `v1.1.0` tag is unpublished; no later tag may be created until all release gates pass.\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:118:| Final ledger and release gate | Open (issue #7) | Inherited |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:123:The earlier draft placed `trace.jsonl` beside session state under `sessions/<session-id>/`. WP-1101 follows release gate G1.1-1, which explicitly requires traces under `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`; the diagram above is the reconciled normative path. Session state remains under `sessions/`, and trace files are stored once under `traces/`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:202:To prevent JSON argument parse failures and conversational rambling from open-weights models, Nexus v1.1.0 provides a logit-level constrained decoding engine targeting near-zero repair retries on supported inference backends:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:240:- **Unconstrained Fallback:** Retains heuristic regex and `repairJson` recovery when running against servers without grammar sampling support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:165:**Relevance to Nexus:** Nexus currently treats evaluation as a pre-release gate (M5 qualification). Adopting the lifecycle model would make evaluation continuous: production findings feed back into the eval dataset, and RC fixes are validated offline before redeployment.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:62:| **External App Ecosystem** | Built-in CLI toolset | Manual MCP configuration per server | Git/terminal commands only | **Composio 250+ App Ecosystem Bridge (Opt-in managed OAuth, GBNF-constrained schemas, automated Linear/Jira failure filing)** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:139:- **The Problem:** Open-weights models (7B/14B parameter models like Qwen 2.5 Coder, DeepSeek R1, Llama 3) frequently derail during agentic loops due to malformed JSON outputs, hallucinated tool parameter names, trailing unescaped characters, or discursive conversational chatter before the JSON payload. In unconstrained clients, this triggers expensive iterative retry loops, context pollution, or total agent failure.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:143:  - **Hybrid CoT Grammar:** For reasoning architectures (DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), Nexus enforces a hybrid grammar: unconstrained internal reasoning within `<think>...</think>` tokens, transitioning deterministically into strict schema-constrained tool call emission.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:144:  - **Zero Repair Target:** Targets near-zero repair overhead (`repair_rate = 0.00` and `ERR_PARSER = 0`), allowing resource-constrained 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models to execute multi-turn agentic workflows with high syntactic reliability.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:148:- **The Problem:** Autonomous agents that operate exclusively on local files leave developers with the manual burden of copy-pasting compiler errors into Jira/Linear tickets, notifying teammates on Slack, or manually provisioning API keys for external cloud services. Conversely, agents with unconstrained external API tools frequently hallucinate non-existent API parameters, break JSON payloads, or leak sensitive tokens into logs.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:190:- **Nexus Solution:** High-performance Rust binary (`harness-core`), keyboard-driven Ratatui terminal UI (`nexus-tui`), and native GBNF / Outlines logit-constrained tool calling with hybrid reasoning support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:5:G1.1-5 release gate is complete.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:119:merged or as satisfying G1.1-5.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md:218:or the full WP-1108 / G1.1-5 acceptance evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:55:- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:56:- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:57:- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:59:- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:155:   - When upstream library dependencies announce deprecation or breaking lifecycles, Nexus must refactor, migrate, or replace them before minor release qualification. Under no circumstances may technical debt be deferred into permanent legacy layers.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793734938.1329446}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
