{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:46:50.839Z","ordinal":79249,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-66f5ef6d-8fbf-4a36-91fe-8760ab54a463","process_id":"96973","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '99\\.5|valid.*JSON|grammar.*metric|repair rate|constrained decoding|GBNF|guided_json|llama\\.cpp|Ollama' eval cli/src cli/test docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2 docs/releases | head -180"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"99\\\\.5|valid.*JSON|grammar.*metric|repair rate|constrained decoding|GBNF|guided_json|llama\\\\.cpp|Ollama\" eval cli/src cli/test docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2 docs/releases","query":"99\\.5|valid.*JSON|grammar.*metric|repair rate|constrained decoding|GBNF|guided_json|llama\\.cpp|Ollama","path":"eval"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.1.0/README.md:60:- The `WP-11xx` post-v1 roadmap packages (OpenTelemetry tracing, `nexus eval`, GBNF tool grammars, Composio bridges,\ndocs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md:165:3. Spec-validation tests using a temporary JSON file and the real CLI entry point.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42:| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194:| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\neval/README.md:125:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\neval/README.md:126:| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\neval/README.md:352:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\ncli/test/operation_schema.test.ts:208:  assert.doesNotThrow(() => validateOperationSpec(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(valid))));\neval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs:3:// optionally shaped like llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama. The gateway token stays here; point Nexus's clean HOME at the URL\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:22:                                    - GBNF Tool Grammar Engine          - Composio Dev Bridge (WP-1207)\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:48:| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\neval/dataset.mjs:55:    catch { throw new Error(`${path.basename(file)} line ${i + 1} is invalid JSON`); }\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:196:4. **`repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parsing, measuring whether model emitted valid JSON or required schema repair.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:202:To prevent JSON argument parse failures and conversational rambling from open-weights models, Nexus v1.1.0 provides a logit-level constrained decoding engine targeting near-zero repair retries on supported inference backends:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:205:Registered Tools ──► Tool Schema Compiler ──► GBNF / Outlines Grammar ──► Local Engine (llama.cpp / vLLM)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:213:### 7.1 Dynamic GBNF Grammar Generation\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:214:Nexus compiles registered tool definitions (`run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`) into a strict Context-Free Grammar conforming to GGML GBNF:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:233:For reasoning architectures (e.g. DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), enforcing immediate JSON emission truncates internal chain-of-thought tokens. The GBNF engine supports **hybrid grammars**: allowing an optional `<think>...</think>` block before strictly locking sampling into the tool invocation schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:236:- **`llama.cpp`:** Emits raw `.gbnf` syntax via the `grammar` API parameter.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:237:- **`vLLM` / Outlines:** Emits JSON Schema via `guided_json` / `response_format`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:238:- **`Ollama`:** Emits JSON Schema via `format: <json_schema>`.\ncli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:109:  assert.ok(result.records[0].model.profileContextLookups > 0, \"llama.cpp context comes from the profile endpoint\");\ncli/test/eval_harness.test.ts:286:  const fingerprint = { alias: \"engineering/deep\", listed: true, ownedBy: \"fixture\", contextLength: 65536, weightsSha256: \"a\".repeat(64), serverBuild: \"llama.cpp b123\", sampling: { temperature: 0, seed: 17 } };\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:157:4. **`json_repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parser telemetry, scoring 1.0 for valid native JSON and 0.5 for recovered malformed JSON.\ncli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:63:    assert.match(result.stdout, /config\\.json is not valid JSON/);\ncli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:119:      assert.match(result.stderr, /Configuration error: Nexus config\\.json is not valid JSON/);\ncli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:131:    assert.match(finding.evidence[0], /config\\.json is not valid JSON/);\ncli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:153:    assert.match(result.stderr, /nexus sidecar failed to start: Configuration error: Nexus config\\.json is not valid JSON/);\ncli/test/client_robustness.test.ts:201:  assert.doesNotThrow(() => JSON.parse(args), \"arguments must be valid JSON on the wire\");\ncli/test/parser_single_quote.test.ts:11:  test(\"preserves valid JSON escapes\", () => {\ncli/test/parser_single_quote.test.ts:21:  test(\"unescapes a single-quote escape, which is invalid in JSON\", () => {\ncli/test/parser_single_quote.test.ts:29:  test(\"valid \\\\uXXXX unicode escapes are preserved as JSON escapes\", () => {\ncli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json:3:    \"id\": \"llama.cpp worker b0-live-llama-worker1 via gateway /v1/tokenize (alias engineering/b0)\",\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:3: * lists no limits (llama.cpp server, LM Studio, Ollama) are asked for the context they loaded, instead of Nexus\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:5: * Response shapes follow each server's documented API: llama.cpp `GET /props`, LM Studio `GET /api/v0/models`, Ollama\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:16:  test(\"llama.cpp /props: the runtime n_ctx, not the training size\", () => {\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:25:  test(\"Ollama /api/show: num_ctx when set, else the model's context length\", () => {\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:72:  test(\"a llama.cpp server's /props context is discovered when its catalog lists no limits\", async () => {\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:103:  test(\"an Ollama server is recognised from its catalog and asked only through its own endpoint\", async () => {\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:168:  test(\"llama.cpp exceed_context_size_error is a capacity rejection\", () => {\ncli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts:180:  test(\"Ollama prompt too long body is a capacity rejection\", () => {\ncli/test/operation_view.test.ts:752:  assert.notDeepEqual(validate(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(withDetail)), schema, \"views\"), []);\ncli/test/eval_score_diagnostics.test.ts:27:    fingerprint: { alias: \"engineering/deep\", listed: true, ownedBy: \"fixture\", contextLength: 65536, weightsSha256: \"a\".repeat(64), serverBuild: \"llama.cpp b123\", sampling },\ncli/test/doctor.test.ts:500:      assert.match(find(invalid, \"mcp.config\")!.evidence.join(\"\\n\"), /not valid JSON \\(Nexus ignores the whole file\\)/);\ncli/test/doctor.test.ts:938:  test(\"an invalid option is a doctor execution error (exit 3) with machine-readable JSON\", () => {\ncli/test/check_requirements.test.ts:415:test(\"exact-RC criterion evidence rejects digest-valid JSON primitives and arrays\", () => {\ncli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:285:    assert.deepEqual(turn.toolCallSyntax, { native: 1, trailing: 1, structural: 0, invalid: 0 }, JSON.stringify(turn.toolCallSyntax));\ncli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts:4: * llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama. Nexus's own discovery must then find the context the way it would on that server.\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:6:  GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST,\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:13:test(\"GBNF grammars are generated from exactly the four registered tool schemas\", () => {\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:15:  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(grammars), [...GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST]);\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:17:  for (const name of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) {\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:33:test(\"GBNF object states permit every property order without duplicate fields and enforce required fields\", () => {\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:47:test(\"GBNF generation fails closed for recursive or unsupported property schemas\", () => {\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:63:test(\"GBNF generation rejects missing, duplicate, out-of-scope, and overlarge schemas\", () => {\ncli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:75:  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", registered), /8-property GBNF bound/);\ncli/test/tokens.test.ts:139:  test(\"REQ-AGT-118: /tokenize works on llama.cpp (root /tokenize { tokens }) and vLLM (root /tokenize { count })\", async () => {\ncli/test/tokens.test.ts:188:      assert.ok(seenUrls.includes(\"POST /tokenize\"), \"llama.cpp root /tokenize should be called after /v1/tokenize 404s\");\ncli/test/independent_review.test.ts:157:  const malformed = `Not valid JSON at all`;\ncli/test/run_json_output.test.ts:98:  test(\"a small result is unchanged: valid JSON and the intended exit code\", async () => {\ncli/test/mcp.test.ts:100:        assert.match(result.persistError || \"\", /not valid JSON|left untouched/i);\ncli/test/engine_handshake.test.ts:165:        assert.match(err.message, /Invalid JSON in core engine hello handshake response/);\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:863:  const ok = modelFingerprint({ model: \"m\", qualification: true, fingerprint: { weightsSha256: \"b\".repeat(64), serverBuild: \"llama.cpp b6000\" }, sampling: { temperature: 0, seed: 1 } }, entry);\neval/model_proxy.mjs:19: * - context_overflow: llama.cpp's context-overflow error (HTTP 400, exceed_context_size_error);\neval/model_proxy.mjs:20: * - malformed_tool_json: the first tool call's arguments are made invalid JSON.\neval/model_proxy.mjs:28: * profile also answers as that server would about its context (llama.cpp /props, Ollama /api/show, vLLM max_model_len)\neval/model_proxy.mjs:82:    if (!FAULT_KINDS.includes(f.kind) || !Number.isInteger(f.atRequest) || f.atRequest < 1) throw new Error(`invalid fault ${JSON.stringify(f)}`);\neval/model_proxy.mjs:188:      catch { return void sendJson(res, 400, { error: { type: \"invalid_request\", message: \"evaluation proxy requires a valid JSON inference request\" } }); }\neval/validate.mjs:411:  catch { return \"qualification corpus manifest is invalid JSON\"; }\ncli/src/providers.ts:159:    // Usage is requested (OpenAI-compatible servers such as llama.cpp, vLLM and the appliance gateway report it, with\ncli/src/client.ts:784:   * Tool-call arguments must be a JSON string on the wire: servers such as llama.cpp parse the history\ncli/src/client.ts:1154:        // An OpenAI-style catalog without limits (llama.cpp, LM Studio, Ollama): ask the server itself what it loaded.\ncli/src/client.ts:1174:   * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\ncli/src/client.ts:1175:   * `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`) on the endpoint's origin with the same credential and a 2 s\ncli/src/parser.ts:32: * Tool-call argument syntax, counted per recognized call: valid JSON as sent (`native`), JSON that parsed only after a\ncli/src/parser.ts:160: * Convert the body of a single-quoted string literal into a valid JSON double-quoted string body.\ncli/src/parser.ts:162: * contents are not altered; `\\'` (valid in JS, invalid in JSON) is unescaped to `'`; any other\ncli/src/parser.ts:579:            `Tool call \"${name}\" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair (truncated or unclosed string/bracket). Re-issue the call with complete valid JSON arguments.`\ncli/src/parser.ts:625:          `Tool call \"${name}\" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair (truncated or unclosed string/bracket). Re-issue the call with complete valid JSON arguments.`\ncli/src/parser.ts:674:              `Tool call \"${name}\" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair (truncated or unclosed string/bracket). Re-issue the call with complete valid JSON arguments.`\ncli/src/parser.ts:691:      // Invalid JSON inside a tool_call tag: not executed, but counted as an attempted call that did not parse.\ncli/src/parser.ts:722:                `Tool call \"${name}\" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair (truncated or unclosed string/bracket). Re-issue the call with complete valid JSON arguments.`\ncli/src/parser.ts:753:      // Not valid JSON in code block\ncli/src/tools.ts:914:          throw new Error(`Invalid JSON in core engine hello handshake response: ${result.output}`);\ncli/src/agent.ts:4098:    // Fixed canonical few-shots ensure byte-exact prefix caching across turns (vLLM / llama.cpp / Ollama)\ncli/src/agent.ts:4878:          error: `Tool call \"${toolName}\" rejected: arguments required structural JSON repair (truncated or unclosed string/bracket). Re-issue the call with complete valid JSON arguments.`,\ncli/src/doctor.ts:374:      ? \"Inspect ~/.config/nexus/config.json: make it a regular, non-symlink file under 64 KiB with valid JSON and only supported version 1 fields; then run doctor again.\"\ncli/src/doctor.ts:926:    return f(\"credentials.store\", \"state\", \"fail\", \"Nexus's credential store is not valid JSON; stored provider connections are unavailable.\", [file], \"Move the file aside and reconnect with `nexus connect <provider>`.\");\ncli/src/doctor.ts:1006:      problems.push(`${file}: not valid JSON (Nexus ignores the whole file): ${err?.message ?? err}`);\ncli/src/model_catalog.ts:154:  // A key-less compatible server (plain vLLM, llama.cpp) the operator declared with NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH=none (PRV-14).\ncli/src/config.ts:566:    throw new Error(\"Nexus config.json is not valid JSON.\");\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:61:| **Constrained Tool Calling** | Prompt-driven schema formatting + retry | Client-side schema validation | Prompt-driven tool formatting | **Logit-Constrained GBNF Engine (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), targeting 0 repair retries on supported engines** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:62:| **External App Ecosystem** | Built-in CLI toolset | Manual MCP configuration per server | Git/terminal commands only | **Composio 250+ App Ecosystem Bridge (Opt-in managed OAuth, GBNF-constrained schemas, automated Linear/Jira failure filing)** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:77:│  Air-Gapped  │  │ Time-Travel  ││ In-Repo BYOE ││ Multi-Agent  │    │ GBNF Grammar │\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:92:  - Full functional parity when paired with local inference engines (vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama, homelab-ai gateway) while maintaining seamless support for gateway-preferred and cloud inference backends (DEC-06, DEC-16).\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:138:### 3.7 Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Grammar Engine (Zero-Repair Local Models)\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:141:  - **Dynamic GBNF Compilation:** Nexus dynamically compiles registered tool signatures (`run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`) into a Context-Free Grammar conforming to GGML GBNF and Outlines JSON schemas.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:142:  - **Logit-Level Masking:** During local model sampling on supported engines (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), logits for schema-violating tokens are masked to $-\\infty$, enforcing strict syntactic conformity to the tool schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:152:  - **GBNF-Constrained API Schemas:** Enterprise action schemas compile directly into Context-Free Grammars (`WP-1107`), enforcing JSON schema compliance and valid parameter emission on supported local engines during multi-argument external calls.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:189:- **Pain Point:** \"I run open-weights models on my local GPU rig with vLLM and Ollama, but agents constantly fail because small models produce invalid tool JSON or conversational filler instead of tool calls.\"\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:190:- **Nexus Solution:** High-performance Rust binary (`harness-core`), keyboard-driven Ratatui terminal UI (`nexus-tui`), and native GBNF / Outlines logit-constrained tool calling with hybrid reasoning support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:191:- **The Pitch:** *\"A terminal-native autonomous coding harness built in Rust and TypeScript, featuring GBNF logit constraints that target near-zero syntax repair retries on local models.\"*\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:203:| **Constrained Tool Grammar Engine (GBNF)** | `v1.1.0` | [`SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md`](./SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md) §7 | Near-zero JSON parse errors and syntax repair retries on supported local engines |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:209:| **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | `v1.3.0` | [`ROADMAP.md`](./ROADMAP.md) §4 | 250+ enterprise SaaS connectors with GBNF logit constraints & sandbox isolation |\ncli/src/protocol.ts:203:    throw new ProtocolError(\"line is not valid JSON\");\ncli/src/mcp.ts:562:          // Ignore invalid JSON configs\ncli/src/mcp.ts:626:            throw new Error(`${configFile} is not valid JSON; left untouched`);\ncli/src/core/task_message_log.ts:82:  catch { return corrupt(\"Committed message record is not valid JSON\"); }\ncli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts:83:/** Error types servers use for a request larger than the loaded context (llama.cpp server: exceed_context_size_error). */\ncli/src/core/provider_recovery.ts:85:/** Context-overflow wording of vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama error messages. */\ncli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:5: * None of this is a prerequisite. A connection that advertises nothing (LM Studio, plain llama.cpp, a cloud provider)\ncli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:41:   * context (llama.cpp `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`), or an OpenAI-style catalog with no limits.\ncli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:73: * llama.cpp (owned_by llamacpp or n_ctx_train meta), LM Studio (organization_owner), Ollama (library or ollama), or unknown.\ncli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:120: * The context a local server says it has loaded, from its own endpoint (REQ-PRV-101): llama.cpp `GET /props`\ncli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:122: * (loaded_context_length, else max_context_length), Ollama `POST /api/show` (the num_ctx parameter, else the model's\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:98:- Format validation (JSON structure, required fields)\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:4:/** The v1.1.0 GBNF pilot is intentionally limited to these registered tools. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:5:export const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:6:export type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:8:const ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:16:  if (!ALLOWED_NAMES.has(toolName)) throw new Error(`GBNF is not enabled for tool ${String(toolName)}`);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:41:  if (propertyNames.length > MAX_PROPERTIES) throw new Error(`${toolName} schema exceeds the ${MAX_PROPERTIES}-property GBNF bound`);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:102:  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\ncli/src/core/spine.ts:230:    return { valid: false, error: \"Tool arguments must be a JSON object.\" };\ncli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:69:    throw new InvalidOperationStateError(`operation record has an invalid schemaVersion (${JSON.stringify(version)})`);\ncli/src/core/turn.ts:307:  /** Argument syntax of the tool calls the model issued this turn (native, repaired or invalid JSON); absent when none. */\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":832802158}},"started_at_ms":1793735210006,"completed_at_ms":1793735210839}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:46:52.339Z","ordinal":79250,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2f3-3d33-7b90-b50d-118e7c7f7318","call_id":"call_1d2601a92d1f44899633ec1169a74478","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5310)\nTotal output lines: 131\n\ndocs/v1.1.0/README.md:60:- The `WP-11xx` post-v1 roadmap packages (OpenTelemetry tracing, `nexus eval`, GBNF tool grammars, Composio bridges,\ndocs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md:165:3. Spec-validation tests using a temporary JSON file and the real CLI entry point.\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42:| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194:| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\neval/README.md:125:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\neval/README.md:126:| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\neval/README.md:352:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\ncli/test/operation_schema.test.ts:208:  assert.doesNotThrow(() => validateOperationSpec(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(valid))));\neval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs:3:// optionally shaped like llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama. The gateway token stays here; point Nexus's clean HOME at the URL\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:22:                                    - GBNF Tool Grammar Engine          - Composio Dev Bridge (WP-1207)\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:48:| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\neval/dataset.mjs:55:    catch { throw new Error(`${path.basename(file)} line ${i + 1} is invalid JSON`); }\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:196:4. **`repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parsing, measuring whether model emitted valid JSON or required schema repair.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:202:To prevent JSON argument parse failures and conversational rambling from open-weights models, Nexus v1.1.0 provides a logit-level constrained decoding engine targeting near-zero repair retries on supported inference backends:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:205:Registered Tools ──► Tool Schema Compiler ──► GBNF / Outlines Grammar ──► Local Engine (llama.cpp / vLLM)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:213:### 7.1 Dynamic GBNF Grammar Generation\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:214:Nexus compiles registered tool definitions (`run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`) into a strict Context-Free Grammar conforming to GGML GBNF:\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:233:For reasoning architectures (e.g. DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), enforcing immediate JSON emission truncates internal chain-of-thought tokens. The GBNF engine supports **hybrid grammars**: allowing an optional `<think>.…2810 tokens truncated…le maintaining seamless support for gateway-preferred and cloud inference backends (DEC-06, DEC-16).\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:138:### 3.7 Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Grammar Engine (Zero-Repair Local Models)\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:141:  - **Dynamic GBNF Compilation:** Nexus dynamically compiles registered tool signatures (`run_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`) into a Context-Free Grammar conforming to GGML GBNF and Outlines JSON schemas.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:142:  - **Logit-Level Masking:** During local model sampling on supported engines (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), logits for schema-violating tokens are masked to $-\\infty$, enforcing strict syntactic conformity to the tool schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:152:  - **GBNF-Constrained API Schemas:** Enterprise action schemas compile directly into Context-Free Grammars (`WP-1107`), enforcing JSON schema compliance and valid parameter emission on supported local engines during multi-argument external calls.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:189:- **Pain Point:** \"I run open-weights models on my local GPU rig with vLLM and Ollama, but agents constantly fail because small models produce invalid tool JSON or conversational filler instead of tool calls.\"\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:190:- **Nexus Solution:** High-performance Rust binary (`harness-core`), keyboard-driven Ratatui terminal UI (`nexus-tui`), and native GBNF / Outlines logit-constrained tool calling with hybrid reasoning support.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:191:- **The Pitch:** *\"A terminal-native autonomous coding harness built in Rust and TypeScript, featuring GBNF logit constraints that target near-zero syntax repair retries on local models.\"*\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:203:| **Constrained Tool Grammar Engine (GBNF)** | `v1.1.0` | [`SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md`](./SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md) §7 | Near-zero JSON parse errors and syntax repair retries on supported local engines |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:209:| **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | `v1.3.0` | [`ROADMAP.md`](./ROADMAP.md) §4 | 250+ enterprise SaaS connectors with GBNF logit constraints & sandbox isolation |\ncli/src/protocol.ts:203:    throw new ProtocolError(\"line is not valid JSON\");\ncli/src/mcp.ts:562:          // Ignore invalid JSON configs\ncli/src/mcp.ts:626:            throw new Error(`${configFile} is not valid JSON; left untouched`);\ncli/src/core/task_message_log.ts:82:  catch { return corrupt(\"Committed message record is not valid JSON\"); }\ncli/src/core/provider