{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:47:49.007Z","ordinal":79306,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7fefb970-01de-4bb0-9d9b-0da89f31f8bf","process_id":"21008","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg --files docs/v1.1.0 cli/src cli/test | rg 'WP-1107|tool_grammar|client\\.ts|tool.*grammar'\nsed -n '180,215p' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md\nsed -n '1,180p' cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts\nrg -n 'WP-1107|G1\\.1-4|grammar' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107* docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg --files docs/v1.1.0 cli/src cli/test | rg 'WP-1107|tool_grammar|client\\.ts|tool.*grammar'\nsed -n '180,215p' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md\nsed -n '1,180p' cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts\nrg -n 'WP-1107|G1\\.1-4|grammar' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107* docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts\ncli/src/client.ts\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts\n## 2.5 The parallel v1.1.0 draft merged after this review\n\n`origin/main` moved from `c7d0b003` to `7b49e6ff` during this work. PR #371 merged a post-v1.0.0 roadmap\n(`docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md`, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md`, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md`, `POSITIONING.md`, `LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md`) that\nalso calls itself **v1.1.0**. It is a second, unreconciled scope: none of its work packages exist in the source.\n\n| Item | Intent | Overlap with the implemented scope | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1101 | OpenTelemetry-shaped local tracing (`trace.jsonl`) | None with `OperationEvent`; a separate trace format | **Defer**: needs its own spec and privacy review (trace content is agent output) |\n| WP-1102 | Flight-recorder credential redaction | Redaction already exists (`redactForPersistence`, `safeTerminal`) | **Investigate**: verify the existing redaction against the CRED003 fixtures before adding a second mechanism |\n| WP-1103 | Versioned eval datasets (`eval/datasets/`) | None | **Defer**: held-out custody (issue #1) is still unresolved; restructuring datasets now would disturb it |\n| WP-1104 | `nexus eval` command | None | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 and the frozen thresholds |\n| WP-1105 | Modular code evaluators | The evaluator lives in `eval/` | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 |\n| WP-1106 | `--step` single-step loop | None | **Investigate**: small and independent; needs a decision on interaction with durable turns |\n| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\n| WP-1108 | Dependency modernization (27 Dependabot PRs) | `origin/main` already merged several (#103–#129 partially) | **Partly already satisfied**; the rest is dependency work, not a v1.1 feature |\n\nConsequences recorded now:\n\n1. **The release name is contested.** Two documents on `main` claim \"v1.1.0\" with different contents. This branch calls\n   its work \"the v1.1.0 scope\" and does not claim the WP-11xx roadmap has shipped; the owner decides the naming\n   (DECISIONS Q6).\n2. **The v1.0.0 `REQUIREMENTS.md` backlog section** is the other recorded list of post-v1 work; it was not edited here.\n3. **No item from the parallel draft is marked implemented in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](REQUIREMENTS.md).** The ledger is\n   scoped to the four proposals, and a row is only `tested` when a test in this repository asserts it.\n\n## 5. Omissions and dependencies the proposals did not state\n\n1. **The schema rule was already violated.** `docs/v1.1.0/README.md:28` requires a schema version and migration for\n   any `DurableOperationState` change. Git isolation, checkpoints and the context budget all changed that state\n   without bumping `schemaVersion` (still `1`) and without a migration test. v1.1.0 must repair the omission before\n   adding more fields, or the rule can never be enforced.\n2. **Concurrency and the operation lock.** `driveOperation` holds one lock for the whole run (`operation_runner.ts:404-412`).\n   Parallel units therefore run inside a single writer process; the design cannot use multiple driver processes\n   without a lease change, which is explicitly out of scope.\n3. **Concurrency and git.** Integration mutates one shared integration worktree. Concurrent units can complete at\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { HARNESS_TOOLS } from \"../src/core/capabilities.js\";\nimport type { ToolDefinition } from \"../src/types.js\";\nimport {\n  GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST,\n  generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars,\n  generateToolArgumentsGbnf,\n} from \"../src/core/tool_grammar.js\";\n\nconst schemaFor = (name: string) => HARNESS_TOOLS.find((tool) => tool.function.name === name)!;\n\ntest(\"GBNF grammars are generated from exactly the four registered tool schemas\", () => {\n  const grammars = generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars();\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(grammars), [...GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST]);\n\n  for (const name of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) {\n    const parameters = schemaFor(name).function.parameters;\n    const grammar = grammars[name];\n    const generatedNames = [...grammar.matchAll(/^member_\\d+ ::= (\"(?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*\") ws \":\" ws /gm)]\n      .map((match) => JSON.parse(match[1]));\n    assert.deepEqual(generatedNames, Object.keys(parameters.properties), `${name} field names must match its registered schema`);\n    for (const match of grammar.matchAll(/^member_\\d+ ::= (\"(?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*\") ws \":\" ws (json-string|json-number|json-boolean)$/gm)) {\n      const field = JSON.parse(match[1]);\n      const type = parameters.properties[field as keyof typeof parameters.properties].type;\n      const expectedRule = type === \"string\" ? \"json-string\" : type === \"number\" ? \"json-number\" : \"json-boolean\";\n      assert.equal(match[2], expectedRule, `${name}.${field} value rule must match its registered schema`);\n    }\n    assert.match(grammar, /^root ::= ws \"\\{\" ws object-fields ws \"}\" ws$/m);\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF object states permit every property order without duplicate fields and enforce required fields\", () => {\n  const tool = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  const grammar = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\");\n  const names = Object.keys(tool.function.parameters.properties);\n  const requiredMask = (tool.function.parameters.required ?? []).reduce((mask, name) => mask | (1 << names.indexOf(name)), 0);\n  const requiredTail = new RegExp(`^fields_tail_${requiredMask} ::= \"\" \\\\|`, \"m\");\n  const initialTail = /^fields_tail_0 ::= \"\"/m;\n\n  assert.match(grammar, requiredTail, \"the state containing required path can terminate\");\n  assert.doesNotMatch(grammar, initialTail, \"an object cannot terminate before required path is emitted\");\n  assert.match(grammar, /\",\" ws member_0 fields_tail_/);\n  assert.match(grammar, /\",\" ws member_4 fields_tail_/);\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF generation fails closed for recursive or unsupported property schemas\", () => {\n  const original = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  const recursive = structuredClone(original) as ToolDefinition;\n  recursive.function.parameters.properties.path = {\n    type: \"object\",\n    properties: { child: { $ref: \"#/$defs/path\" } },\n  } as never;\n  const registered = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(recursive);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", registered), /unsupported JSON Schema type/);\n\n  const referenced = structuredClone(original) as ToolDefinition;\n  referenced.function.parameters.properties.path = { type: \"string\", $ref: \"#/$defs/path\" } as never;\n  const withReference = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(referenced);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", withReference), /unsupported schema keyword \\$ref/);\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF generation rejects missing, duplicate, out-of-scope, and overlarge schemas\", () => {\n  const readFile = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  assert.throws(\n    () => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\")),\n    /found 0/,\n  );\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", [...HARNESS_TOOLS, readFile]), /found 2/);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"list_dir\" as never), /not enabled/);\n\n  const oversized = structuredClone(readFile) as ToolDefinition;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) oversized.function.parameters.properties[`extra_${i}`] = { type: \"string\" };\n  const registered = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(oversized);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", registered), /8-property GBNF bound/);\n});\nzsh:4: no matches found: docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107*\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":711795256}},"started_at_ms":1793735268294,"completed_at_ms":1793735269006}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:47:50.192Z","ordinal":79307,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2f4-1f30-73e0-8fb5-7c4529421e3d","call_id":"call_410e8a49b2864e5b996591027cc8e48f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts\ncli/src/client.ts\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts\n## 2.5 The parallel v1.1.0 draft merged after this review\n\n`origin/main` moved from `c7d0b003` to `7b49e6ff` during this work. PR #371 merged a post-v1.0.0 roadmap\n(`docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md`, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md`, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md`, `POSITIONING.md`, `LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md`) that\nalso calls itself **v1.1.0**. It is a second, unreconciled scope: none of its work packages exist in the source.\n\n| Item | Intent | Overlap with the implemented scope | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1101 | OpenTelemetry-shaped local tracing (`trace.jsonl`) | None with `OperationEvent`; a separate trace format | **Defer**: needs its own spec and privacy review (trace content is agent output) |\n| WP-1102 | Flight-recorder credential redaction | Redaction already exists (`redactForPersistence`, `safeTerminal`) | **Investigate**: verify the existing redaction against the CRED003 fixtures before adding a second mechanism |\n| WP-1103 | Versioned eval datasets (`eval/datasets/`) | None | **Defer**: held-out custody (issue #1) is still unresolved; restructuring datasets now would disturb it |\n| WP-1104 | `nexus eval` command | None | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 and the frozen thresholds |\n| WP-1105 | Modular code evaluators | The evaluator lives in `eval/` | **Defer**: depends on WP-1103 |\n| WP-1106 | `--step` single-step loop | None | **Investigate**: small and independent; needs a decision on interaction with durable turns |\n| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\n| WP-1108 | Dependency modernization (27 Dependabot PRs) | `origin/main` already merged several (#103–#129 partially) | **Partly already satisfied**; the rest is dependency work, not a v1.1 feature |\n\nConsequences recorded now:\n\n1. **The release name is contested.** Two documents on `main` claim \"v1.1.0\" with different contents. This branch calls\n   its work \"the v1.1.0 scope\" and does not claim the WP-11xx roadmap has shipped; the owner decides the naming\n   (DECISIONS Q6).\n2. **The v1.0.0 `REQUIREMENTS.md` backlog section** is the other recorded list of post-v1 work; it was not edited here.\n3. **No item from the parallel draft is marked implemented in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](REQUIREMENTS.md).** The ledger is\n   scoped to the four proposals, and a row is only `tested` when a test in this repository asserts it.\n\n## 5. Omissions and dependencies the proposals did not state\n\n1. **The schema rule was already violated.** `docs/v1.1.0/README.md:28` requires a schema version and migration for\n   any `DurableOperationState` change. Git isolation, checkpoints and the context budget all changed that state\n   without bumping `schemaVersion` (still `1`) and without a migration test. v1.1.0 must repair the omission before\n   adding more fields, or the rule can never be enforced.\n2. **Concurrency and the operation lock.** `driveOperation` holds one lock for the whole run (`operation_runner.ts:404-412`).\n   Parallel units therefore run inside a single writer process; the design cannot use multiple driver processes\n   without a lease change, which is explicitly out of scope.\n3. **Concurrency and git.** Integration mutates one shared integration worktree. Concurrent units can complete at\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { HARNESS_TOOLS } from \"../src/core/capabilities.js\";\nimport type { ToolDefinition } from \"../src/types.js\";\nimport {\n  GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST,\n  generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars,\n  generateToolArgumentsGbnf,\n} from \"../src/core/tool_grammar.js\";\n\nconst schemaFor = (name: string) => HARNESS_TOOLS.find((tool) => tool.function.name === name)!;\n\ntest(\"GBNF grammars are generated from exactly the four registered tool schemas\", () => {\n  const grammars = generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars();\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(grammars), [...GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST]);\n\n  for (const name of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) {\n    const parameters = schemaFor(name).function.parameters;\n    const grammar = grammars[name];\n    const generatedNames = [...grammar.matchAll(/^member_\\d+ ::= (\"(?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*\") ws \":\" ws /gm)]\n      .map((match) => JSON.parse(match[1]));\n    assert.deepEqual(generatedNames, Object.keys(parameters.properties), `${name} field names must match its registered schema`);\n    for (const match of grammar.matchAll(/^member_\\d+ ::= (\"(?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*\") ws \":\" ws (json-string|json-number|json-boolean)$/gm)) {\n      const field = JSON.parse(match[1]);\n      const type = parameters.properties[field as keyof typeof parameters.properties].type;\n      const expectedRule = type === \"string\" ? \"json-string\" : type === \"number\" ? \"json-number\" : \"json-boolean\";\n      assert.equal(match[2], expectedRule, `${name}.${field} value rule must match its registered schema`);\n    }\n    assert.match(grammar, /^root ::= ws \"\\{\" ws object-fields ws \"}\" ws$/m);\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF object states permit every property order without duplicate fields and enforce required fields\", () => {\n  const tool = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  const grammar = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\");\n  const names = Object.keys(tool.function.parameters.properties);\n  const requiredMask = (tool.function.parameters.required ?? []).reduce((mask, name) => mask | (1 << names.indexOf(name)), 0);\n  const requiredTail = new RegExp(`^fields_tail_${requiredMask} ::= \"\" \\\\|`, \"m\");\n  const initialTail = /^fields_tail_0 ::= \"\"/m;\n\n  assert.match(grammar, requiredTail, \"the state containing required path can terminate\");\n  assert.doesNotMatch(grammar, initialTail, \"an object cannot terminate before required path is emitted\");\n  assert.match(grammar, /\",\" ws member_0 fields_tail_/);\n  assert.match(grammar, /\",\" ws member_4 fields_tail_/);\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF generation fails closed for recursive or unsupported property schemas\", () => {\n  const original = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  const recursive = structuredClone(original) as ToolDefinition;\n  recursive.function.parameters.properties.path = {\n    type: \"object\",\n    properties: { child: { $ref: \"#/$defs/path\" } },\n  } as never;\n  const registered = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(recursive);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", registered), /unsupported JSON Schema type/);\n\n  const referenced = structuredClone(original) as ToolDefinition;\n  referenced.function.parameters.properties.path = { type: \"string\", $ref: \"#/$defs/path\" } as never;\n  const withReference = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(referenced);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", withReference), /unsupported schema keyword \\$ref/);\n});\n\ntest(\"GBNF generation rejects missing, duplicate, out-of-scope, and overlarge schemas\", () => {\n  const readFile = schemaFor(\"read_file\");\n  assert.throws(\n    () => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\")),\n    /found 0/,\n  );\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", [...HARNESS_TOOLS, readFile]), /found 2/);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"list_dir\" as never), /not enabled/);\n\n  const oversized = structuredClone(readFile) as ToolDefinition;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) oversized.function.parameters.properties[`extra_${i}`] = { type: \"string\" };\n  const registered = HARNESS_TOOLS.filter((tool) => tool.function.name !== \"read_file\").concat(oversized);\n  assert.throws(() => generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\"read_file\", registered), /8-property GBNF bound/);\n});\nzsh:4: no matches found: docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107*\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735270.1920183}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
