{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:49:15.656Z","ordinal":79385,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a2f5-6d08-73a2-aefc-f5eb5cc61ad6","author":"/root/roadmap_next","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/roadmap_next\nPayload:\nThe GBNF generator is **not connected to a provider request path** on candidate `e134dcd5`. Its only references are its definitions in [tool_grammar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:12) and unit tests in [tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:13). The client’s non-streaming, streaming, and native request builders contain no `grammar`, `guided_json`, or `format` field ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1377), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1531), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1858)).\n\nThe roadmap requires integration for llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama and a ≥99.5% valid tool-call JSON result across those endpoints ([ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50), [ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58)). The qualification record marks WP-1107 passed based on four compiler tests, while its gate row still says endpoint evidence is pending ([qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32), [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42)). The older roadmap review explicitly deferred WP-1107 due to provider request changes ([ROADMAP-REVIEW.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194)); the user-approved full-roadmap scope supersedes that deferral, but the conflicting record and completion claim need reconciliation.\n\nA safe implementation sequence is a reviewed transport plan, followed by test-first request integration for each provider. Likely files are `cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, and provider request-capture tests; provider capability detection may also need adjustment. `client.ts` is actively claimed by codex-root for RC16 work, so coordinate before editing. The grammar module, its tests, `client.test.ts`, and provider-capability file have no active file claims. GATEWAY remains claimed for RC15 E5 work; endpoint inference needs owner coordination. No edits or tests were made."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735355.656252,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2764}}
