{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:52:17.771Z","ordinal":79513,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-60540992-f22c-499b-8ced-f84ac51778c2","process_id":"91929","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration status --short && sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration status --short && sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported local inference engine, I need registered tool arguments constrained by that engine so tool calls arrive as valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp chat endpoint receives the grammar generated from the active allowlisted tool schemas. Test: `client sends llama.cpp GBNF for supported tool calls`.\n- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives the provider's supported JSON-schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends vLLM structured tool schema for supported tool calls`.\n- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\n- **AC4:** Unknown and unsupported endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent without positive provider identification. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`.\n- **AC5:** The exact installed candidate produces at least 99.5% natively valid tool-call argument JSON on each supported endpoint, with no invalid calls and the measured repair counts retained. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\n\n**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\n\n**Dependencies:** Existing schema-derived grammar generator and `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; source implementation is otherwise independent. AC5 depends on an approved shared inference window and the exact candidate package.\n\n**Scope reconciliation:** The user selected the full failed v1.1.0 WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2. This explicit scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. It does not waive the required provider references, test gates, review, or G1.1-4 endpoint evidence.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n**Chunk 1 — Provider request adapter**\n\n- Add a typed adapter mapping positively identified `llamacpp`, `vllm`, and `ollama` server kinds to their documented request constraint fields.\n- Derive constraints from the current allowlisted tool schemas; preserve the existing request when provider kind is unknown or the endpoint/protocol does not support the field.\n- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new).\n- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above.\n- References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\n\n**Chunk 2 — Client integration**\n\n- Attach the adapter output to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling.\n- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\n- Tests: captured request-body tests for each applicable transport path, plus AC4 fallback.\n- Reference to retrieve: `LocalLlmClient` request construction and provider identification on the exact candidate.\n\n**Chunk 3 — Candidate endpoint matrix**\n\n- Run the exact installed candidate against one approved llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint using the same fixed tool-call stimulus; record per-endpoint native, repaired, and invalid counts and archive identity.\n- Files: `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\n- Test/evidence: AC5, at least 99.5% native JSON on every endpoint; this does not certify task correctness.\n- Dependency: explicit release of the shared `GATEWAY` claim before any inference.\n\n## Risks and reference queries\n\n- Provider request contracts may have changed since the roadmap draft. Retrieve current primary references before implementation:\n  - `llama.cpp` (`https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp`) — chat-completion grammar request field and interaction with function tools.\n  - `vLLM` (`https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm`) — current structured-output request field and function-tool compatibility.\n  - `Ollama` (`https://github.com/ollama/ollama`) — current chat `format` schema and function-tool compatibility.\n  - `nexus-cli` XERJ prefix — exact candidate request construction and provider identification.\n- A provider field that constrains the whole response may conflict with native function calling; retain only combinations shown to be supported by the primary references and captured-request tests.\n- G1.1-4 requires a real endpoint matrix. A loopback mock proves serialization only and cannot satisfy the 99.5% metric.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":274117695}},"started_at_ms":1793735536496,"completed_at_ms":1793735537770}}
