lification and reviewed candidate (phase=commit e134dcd5 complete; exact artifact qualification next, gate=Commit e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd on top of f6d474a4. Independent review_delta APPROVED after corrections. CERI version fix backed by RED/GREEN logs (RED 31c308c1..., GREEN 61e0eab4...). Full corrected make test 2314/0/5 SHA-256 39cad26938be30dbb4b073a4d93e62a80aa920789e751cccba5465795eb362bd; security gates PASS SHA-256 a9ebd74bcb62e98376fa5a1779172f815a0a80ec23af0b26b3c72e8732391180; make build/type and terminal-scope fixture PASS. Worktree clean after commit; file claims released., next=Build exact e134dcd5 RC2 archive in the digest-pinned Docker builder, run reproducibility verification, verify checksum/SBOM/installer, then qualify installation and CLI parity on the artifact., friction=No source gate friction. Exact-commit artifact, installed-RC, external CI and independent acceptance remain unqualified. Owner retains tag/publish boundary.), updated about 2 hours ago\\n  - [done] RC2 exact commit source gates (phase=clean exact e134dcd5 source gates passed, gate=Clean commit e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd built with make build, CLI version identifies e134dcd51034 on v1/v112-wp1101-integration. Exact make test PASS: 2319 tests, 2314 pass, 0 fail, 5 skipped, 2,805,889 ms; includes terminal process-scope fixtures; security lifecycle gates all passed; log SHA-256 716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963. Worktree clean., next=Update qualification record with exact clean-commit evidence, review/commit that record, build RC2 package with pinned container images, verify reproducibility and installed behavior., friction=No exact source-gate friction. Artifact, installation, exact CI/independent acceptance and owner publication are pending.), updated 42 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] RC2 exact-commit evidence record (phase=qualification record update peer review pending, gate=Clean exact source commit e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd: make build PASS, CLI reports correct 1.1.2-rc.2 identity; full make test PASS 2314/0/5 incl terminal scope fixtures and security gates, log SHA-256 716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963. Qualification record updated to this exact evidence; doc-only security gates PASS. Independent reviewer asked to approve the exact-evidence wording., next=On reviewer approval commit the doc evidence update, then build two identical RC2 archives with pinned Rust/Node images and run exact-artifact install/CLI qualification., friction=No gate friction. Artifact and installed-candidate work remains.), updated 41 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] RC2 exact-source package qualification (phase=reproducibility build 2/2, gate=Source and reproducible package generation completed; installer/hash checks PASS but installed-candidate acceptance failed before provider execution. Cause found: exact package helper inherited group-write mode 664 from shared group checkout; trusted evaluator correctly fails closed., next=Compare second output byte-for-byte; rerun installed package acceptance and release installer from canonical-mode artifact., friction=Local shared worktree permissions caused an artifact-only qualification failure; no source commit changes intended., artifact=/tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-a/nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.2.tar.gz, heartbeat=2026-11-03T19:39:00Z, installed=Archive installed through its production installer from a local HTTP feed under isolated HOME/prefix. SHA verification passed; extracted 160-ish file manifest passed. Installed launcher 1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034), TUI 1.1.2-rc.2; eval --help works. Provenance records archive fd99bd3f... and source e134dcd5. Attestation intentionally disabled because candidate is unpublished., reproducibleBuildA=Pinned Rust 1.95 and Node 24 digest image build produced archive SHA-256 3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b; scanner helper mode 0644 and direct inventory preflight PASS., reproducibleBuildB=Second independent pinned build running in isolated HOME; archive output /tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-d.), updated 20 minutes ago\\n  - [done] RC2 exact-source artifact and qualification (phase=local RC2 artifact gates complete, gate=Source make build and make test PASS 2314/0/5. Two pinned canonical-mode archive builds byte-identical: SHA-256 3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b. Installer PASS. eval/package_runtime.test.mjs 5/5 PASS (log 2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76). Security lifecycle gates PASS (ba472bb002aa50d0be9809bae62f63e9574eaf12440a275fb259e90a50108655)., evidence=docs/evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json SHA-256 37c7fcee8d1058d04a90f672b5949fbaee7710bc22677612036da140dc4cc176. Qualification record updated; /root/review_delta independent review pending., next=Coordinate with the RC15 GATEWAY holder; when cleared, run G1.1-4 on supported endpoints and then move to final stable version qualification., friction=G1.1-4 supported-provider 99.5% JSON metric remains pending because GATEWAY is held by the separate RC15 stream. External CI/CodeQL and release publication remain outside local candidate qualification., heartbeat=2026-11-03T20:10:00Z, claim=RC2 source, package, SUITE, doc and evidence claims released; only unrelated GATEWAY remains held by RC15 stream., retrieval=XERJ hit nexus-cli index.ts:1020 for eval endpoint option; helper mode issue traced to local Git mode 100644 vs worktree 0664; no implementation source changed., candidateSource=e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd, qualificationCommit=3eea888abbf20b4b63c75c2b554debd67038f5a1, review=/root/review_delta APPROVED after final scope clarification, remaining=Release not complete: G1.1-4 supported local-provider JSON metric >=99.5% is pending while GATEWAY claim is held by the RC15 E5 stream. External CI/CodeQL, stable 1.1.2 build and publication remain open. Candidate is local/unpublished; owner publish boundary retained., work_product=[{\\\"title\\\":\\\"v1.1.2 RC2 Linux archive (unpublished candidate)\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"/tmp/v112-rc2-artifact-c/nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.2.tar.gz\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"v1.1.2 qualification record\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\\"}]), updated 6 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] WP-1107 provider grammar integration (phase=SPEC and PLAN; no implementation written, finding=Read-only audit of e134dcd5 found generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars has no provider/client callsites. client.ts nonstream/stream/native bodies contain no grammar/guided_json/format fields. Existing WP row overstated completion based on 4 generator tests., scope=User explicitly selected full failed v1.1.0 WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2; this supersedes the older ROADMAP-REVIEW §2.5 deferral. GATEWAY remains held by RC15 E5; no live provider metric may run until handoff., claim=Stale RC16 client.ts claim was logged and reassigned after audit; WP-1107 implementation/plan/test/qualification files claimed., next=Write testable WP-1107 spec and chunk plan, request peer plan approval, then retrieve official provider references and implement test-first., friction=Provider request shapes need verified official references. WP-1107 code cannot be release-qualified until the remote GATEWAY owner clears or transfers the shared inference claim., heartbeat=2026-11-03T20:16:00Z), updated 2 minutes ago\"}]}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"618a83\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.274749369,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1212,\"output\":\" M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\\n\\n## Specification\\n\\n**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported local inference engine, I need registered tool arguments constrained by that engine so tool calls arrive as valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n\\n- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp chat endpoint receives the grammar generated from the active allowlisted tool schemas. Test: `client sends llama.cpp GBNF for supported tool calls`.\\n- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives the provider's supported JSON-schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends vLLM structured tool schema for supported tool calls`.\\n- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\\n- **AC4:** Unknown and unsupported endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent without positive provider identification. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`.\\n- **AC5:** The exact installed candidate produces at least 99.5% natively valid tool-call argument JSON on each supported endpoint, with no invalid calls and the measured repair counts retained. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\\n\\n**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Existing schema-derived grammar generator and `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; source implementation is otherwise independent. AC5 depends on an approved shared inference window and the exact candidate package.\\n\\n**Scope reconciliation:** The user selected the full failed v1.1.0 WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2. This explicit scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. It does not waive the required provider references, test gates, review, or G1.1-4 endpoint evidence.\\n\\n## Implementation plan\\n\\n**Chunk 1 — Provider request adapter**\\n\\n- Add a typed adapter mapping positively identified `llamacpp`, `vllm`, and `ollama` server kinds to their documented request constraint fields.\\n- Derive constraints from the current allowlisted tool schemas; preserve the existing request when provider kind is unknown or the endpoint/protocol does not support the field.\\n- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new).\\n- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above.\\n- References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\\n\\n**Chunk 2 — Client integration**\\n\\n- Attach the adapter output to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling.\\n- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\\n- Tests: captured request-body tests for each applicable transport path, plus AC4 fallback.\\n- Reference to retrieve: `LocalLlmClient` request construction and provider identification on the exact candidate.\\n\\n**Chunk 3 — Candidate endpoint matrix**\\n\\n- Run the exact installed candidate against one approved llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint using the same fixed tool-call stimulus; record per-endpoint native, repaired, and invalid counts and archive identity.\\n- Files: `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n- Test/evidence: AC5, at least 99.5% native JSON on every endpoint; this does not certify task correctness.\\n- Dependency: explicit release of the shared `GATEWAY` claim before any inference.\\n\\n## Risks and reference queries\\n\\n- Provider request contracts may have changed since the roadmap draft. Retrieve current primary references before implementation:\\n  - `llama.cpp` (`https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp`) — chat-completion grammar request field and interaction with function tools.\\n  - `vLLM` (`https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm`) — current structured-output request field and function-tool compatibility.\\n  - `Ollama` (`https://github.com/ollama/ollama`) — current chat `format` schema and function-tool compatibility.\\n  - `nexus-cli` XERJ prefix — exact candidate request construction and provider identification.\\n- A provider field that constrains the whole response may conflict with native function calling; retain only combinations shown to be supported by the primary references and captured-request tests.\\n- G1.1-4 requires a real endpoint matrix. A loopback mock proves serialization only and cannot satisfy the 99.5% metric.\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735540.8261461}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
