{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:52:44.336Z","ordinal":79534,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea3b85911081a3ad776d25b2872c65","status":"completed","call_id":"call_fcf91845708e4eda8f5d1b561570de9e","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC5:** The exact installed candidate produces at least 99.5% natively valid tool-call argument JSON on each supported endpoint, with no invalid calls and the measured repair counts retained. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\\n+- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix` and `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`.\\n@@\\n **Chunk 3 — Candidate endpoint matrix**\\n \\n-- Run the exact installed candidate against one approved llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint using the same fixed tool-call stimulus; record per-endpoint native, repaired, and invalid counts and archive identity.\\n-- Files: `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n-- Test/evidence: AC5, at least 99.5% native JSON on every endpoint; this does not certify task correctness.\\n+- Add a deterministic runner and schema validator. Fake-provider/serialization tests validate request construction and evidence validation only; they do not count as live endpoint measurements.\\n+- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n+- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\\n+- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no constraint fields.\\n+- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; native-valid/repaired/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version and SHA-256 of the finalized evidence file. Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, and other secrets.\\n+- Test/evidence: AC5 threshold and zero-invalid requirement for every provider. This measures argument JSON only; it does not certify tool selection or task correctness.\\n - Dependency: explicit release of the shared `GATEWAY` claim before any inference.\\n@@\\n - A provider field that constrains the whole response may conflict with native function calling; retain only combinations shown to be supported by the primary references and captured-request tests.\\n - G1.1-4 requires a real endpoint matrix. A loopback mock proves serialization only and cannot satisfy the 99.5% metric.\\n+- The provider lane’s immutable server and model identities are not yet confirmed because the shared `GATEWAY` claim is still held by the RC15 stream. Treat them as a pre-run gate: record and peer-review the three exact identities/configurations in the matrix plan before starting any provider call; do not substitute mutable tags or infer identity from an endpoint URL.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735557.5685346}}}
