{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:05.882Z","ordinal":79556,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cbf760f9-71b0-4622-b808-a03fc4bb417a","process_id":"18238","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"llama.cpp|vLLM|Ollama|llamacpp|vllm|ollama\" docs eval -g '*.md' -g '*.json' | head -100; git diff --check"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n \"llama.cpp|vLLM|Ollama|llamacpp|vllm|ollama\" docs eval -g '*.md' -g '*.json' | head -100; git diff --check"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:42:| `CTX-006` | Context Routing | Route fallback trust re-admission on destination boundary downgrade | **SATISFIED** | Failover from localhost vLLM to backup endpoint performs full re-admission |\ndocs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:58:  │  Private network services, e.g. localhost vLLM, RFC 1918 private IPs, .local mDNS\neval/README.md:125:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\neval/README.md:352:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:235:4. **Route Fallback:** Failover from a high-trust local model (localhost vLLM) to a lower-trust remote model re-evaluates and sanitizes the payload for the lower-trust destination (`CTX-006`).\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:66:| CTX-006 | 08: Context & Model-Route | A model route or fallback transition that alters the destination trust boundary, disclosure characteristics, or context capacity MUST trigger full re-admission of the request under the destination's applicable policies before transmission. | Fallback from a local private model to a public cloud API MUST re-admit the prompt through the outbound data-protection pipeline. Silent inheritance of local admission by external providers is strictly prohibited. | Phase 2 §12 | `cli/src/client.ts` (`LocalLlmClient.executeWithFailover()`); cli/test/egress.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None; failover from high-trust endpoint (e.g. localhost vLLM) to backup lower-trust endpoint (e.g. public cloud) triggers full egress re-admission. | Satisfied |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:76:| DEST-001 | 10: Trust-Boundary & Destination | The architecture MUST define explicit destination-aware trust boundaries across at least: `HOST_LOCAL` (local runtime and memory), `LOCAL_APPLIANCE` (private network services, e.g., local vLLM), `EXTERNAL_BOUNDED` (contracted external services, e.g., private enterprise Git), and `EXTERNAL_PUBLIC` (public cloud LLMs, public package registries, public issue trackers). | Every outbound network sink and API route MUST be assigned an explicit trust boundary classification. | Phase 2 §14 | `cli/src/core/egress.ts` (`classifyDestination()`); cli/test/egress.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None; 4 discrete destination trust ranks operational (HOST_LOCAL, LOCAL_APPLIANCE, EXTERNAL_BOUNDED, EXTERNAL_PUBLIC). | Satisfied |\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:3:Welcome to **Nexus Code**, a local-first, autonomous and interactive AI coding harness. Nexus Code connects to local inference servers (vLLM, LM Studio) and executes inside a native Linux shell environment.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:264:and never shown as success. The context window and output allowance are discovered from the active endpoint: vLLM (`/v1/models` `max_model_len`),\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:265:llama.cpp (`/props` `n_ctx`), LM Studio (`/api/v0/models` `loaded_context_length`), Ollama (`/api/show` `num_ctx` or\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:41:  against a non-gateway local server (LM Studio / plain llama.cpp) was **not** run in this session. Standalone\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:3:Nexus Code connects directly to standalone OpenAI-compatible local inference servers without requiring any external gateway. This guide covers setup, automatic context window discovery, capacity recovery, timeouts, and custom TLS certificate authorities for **LM Studio**, **llama.cpp**, **vLLM**, and **Ollama**.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:26:### llama.cpp (`llama-server`, `http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:37:3. **Context discovery:** Nexus recognizes `llama.cpp` from its `/v1/models` entry (`owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` or `meta.n_ctx_train`) and probes `GET /props` (2 s timeout) for `default_generation_settings.n_ctx`, reporting `server_probe (llamacpp)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:39:### vLLM (`http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:40:1. Start vLLM with the appropriate tool-call parser for your model family (`hermes`, `qwen`, `llama3_json`, etc.):\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:42:   vllm serve Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct \\\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:54:3. **Context discovery:** vLLM publishes `max_model_len` directly in `GET /v1/models`. Nexus reads it from the catalog entry and reports `provider_advertised` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:56:### Ollama (`http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:57:1. Pull and serve a model with Ollama:\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:59:   ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:67:3. **Context discovery:** When `/v1/models` omits limits, Nexus probes `POST /api/show` with `{\"model\": \"<id>\"}` (2 s timeout) and reads `num_ctx` from `parameters` (or `model_info[\"<arch>.context_length\"]`), reporting `server_probe (ollama)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:82:If a request exceeds the server's loaded context window (including llama.cpp `exceed_context_size_error`, LM Studio context overflow errors, vLLM `maximum context length`, or Ollama context length rejections), Nexus classifies the response as `CAPACITY_REJECTED`, compacts the conversation history once, and retries once at a reduced token budget. If the compacted retry is still rejected, the turn stops immediately with an actionable message naming `--context-limit` and the discovered window.\ndocs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:211:| `advertised` | the connection's `/models` entry (homelab-ai gateway: `context_length`, `max_completion_tokens`, `limits_version`, serving workers; vLLM: `max_model_len`) |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md:3:Evidence: `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/RESULTS.md` (commit 9b6efe9). Scope of validity: current Nexus + aihost gateway (llama.cpp prefix cache),\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:381:| **DEST-001** | The architecture MUST define explicit destination-aware trust boundaries across at least: `HOST_LOCAL` (local runtime and memory), `LOCAL_APPLIANCE` (private network services, e.g., local vLLM), `EXTERNAL_BOUNDED` (contracted external services, e.g., private enterprise Git), and `EXTERNAL_PUBLIC` (public cloud LLMs, public package registries, public issue trackers). | Every outbound network sink and API route MUST be assigned an explicit trust boundary classification. |\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:18:- **Provider capabilities and token accounting.** Context size and output allowance are discovered from the provider's `/models` when advertised (homelab-ai gateway, vLLM). When the gateway offers `/v1/tokenize`, Nexus counts the exact request body it is about to send; counts are labelled by source. `--strict-token-count` requires a provider count. Standalone servers keep working on client estimates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:120:| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:203:- In a second profile, the proxy rewrites the `/models` and overflow-error shapes into the documented formats of llama.cpp `server`, vLLM and Ollama. That exercises each server kind's discovery and capacity-error path against real model output.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:208:- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:210:- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:213:- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:216:**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:281:| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:35:- **Known failure modes (open issues):** flat 20k buffer lets one turn's tool results overshoot on 1M windows (#3620); summary treats the *latest follow-up prompt as the original request* (#3867 — objective corruption by summarization); summarization fails with thinking local llama.cpp models (#3284 — directly relevant to Nexus's local stack); user-visible \"clears the context losing all work\" (#2240); requests for low-signal pruning and for exposing remaining-context to the model (#2382, #2331).\ndocs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:52:- **Known failure modes (open issues):** agentic compaction installs a **truncated summary silently** when `incompleteReason` is set (#14732); auto-compaction never fires on native Ollama (#13989 — a local-model path); `thinking:false` hard-coded so agentic compaction 400s on reasoning-mandatory endpoints (#14551); compaction fires too early when base64 images inflate the estimate (#14512); full-context `max_output_tokens` overflows large-context models (#9651).\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:92:| Q8 | Treats local inference as first-class | the above hold with local OpenAI-compatible servers (vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio, Ollama) including their error/streaming shapes |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:105:| Q6 recovery | **PARTIAL** | 429/503 recovery with Retry-After; stream reset → one retry, one execution; timeouts kill process groups; corrupt/future state files fail closed | context-length 400 ends the turn, llama.cpp shape unrecognised (I-05); silent persistence failures (P1); timeout not bounding background children (T7); multibyte panic loses results (T8); crash findings loss (CTX-01) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:107:| Q8 local first-class | **PARTIAL** | streaming decode robust (split UTF-8, truncated streams detected); OpenAI-compatible endpoints; provider recovery | `<think>` tool extraction (I-01); prose JSON executed (I-04); `data:` without space ignored (I-06); usage from plain endpoints ignored (I-07); llama.cpp context error (I-05); fixed ~5k-token overhead per request (estimate, P-1) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:120:- **Local backends with context-window sizing** (Aider sizes Ollama `num_ctx` per request; Goose warns about silent\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:129:  (`--oss`, built-in Ollama/LM Studio providers; Responses wire format), OpenCode, Goose and Aider can be.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:204:| I-05 | P2 | REPRODUCED | Provider context-length 400 ends the turn; llama.cpp error shape unrecognised; no reactive compaction |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:272:reactive compaction-and-retry on context errors incl. llama.cpp/vLLM shapes; SSE spec conformance; empty reply →\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:298:| 3 | B5 parser safety + R5 inference recovery | 0 | parser corpus and provider-shape tests (OpenAI, vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio, Ollama captures) pass; I-01–I-08 repros fixed |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:325:| T4 Fault-injected | T2 tasks under: provider 503 bursts, stream cut mid-tool-call, context-length error (OpenAI and llama.cpp shapes), sidecar SIGKILL + resume, concurrent external file edit, slow command beyond timeout | recovery and bounded failure |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:338:OpenAI-compatible gateway, plus one llama.cpp-server and one Ollama configuration to exercise their error/streaming\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:363:- Some findings are source-supported only (labelled); the llama.cpp context-error shape was not captured live.\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md:24:│   • Local server: llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama        │\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:9:- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp chat endpoint receives the grammar generated from the active allowlisted tool schemas. Test: `client sends llama.cpp GBNF for supported tool calls`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:10:- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives the provider's supported JSON-schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends vLLM structured tool schema for supported tool calls`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:11:- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:25:- Add a typed adapter mapping positively identified `llamacpp`, `vllm`, and `ollama` server kinds to their documented request constraint fields.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:29:- References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:43:- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no constraint fields.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:51:  - `llama.cpp` (`https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp`) — chat-completion grammar request field and interaction with function tools.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:52:  - `vLLM` (`https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm`) — current structured-output request field and function-tool compatibility.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:53:  - `Ollama` (`https://github.com/ollama/ollama`) — current chat `format` schema and function-tool compatibility.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:205:Registered Tools ──► Tool Schema Compiler ──► GBNF / Outlines Grammar ──► Local Engine (llama.cpp / vLLM)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:236:- **`llama.cpp`:** Emits raw `.gbnf` syntax via the `grammar` API parameter.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:237:- **`vLLM` / Outlines:** Emits JSON Schema via `guided_json` / `response_format`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:238:- **`Ollama`:** Emits JSON Schema via `format: <json_schema>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:14:Local inference is the product's first-class mode. The quickstart first-run path is LM Studio or vLLM at `localhost:1234`. The code is gateway-optional by design (B §5): `/tokenize`, capacity headers and `limits_version` are all optional and absent-safe. The gaps are below.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:18:Every live run on record is against the homelab gateway: llama.cpp behind aihost (HIST-08). Local requests are never receipted (`client.ts:561-569`), so there is no machine-readable local evidence (B §6 G1).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:20:### 1.2 Context sizing on LM Studio and llama.cpp\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:22:Only `context_length` and `max_model_len` are parsed (`core/provider_capabilities.ts:29,72`). LM Studio's and llama.cpp's `/v1/models` do not carry these fields (INFERENCE on server behaviour; verify in G1). On those servers sizing falls back to 65536. If the loaded window is smaller, the first large turn ends with a capacity error and no compaction-and-retry (`agent.ts:4684-4689`; PRV-06). On top of that, llama.cpp's overflow body is classified as REQUEST_REJECTED, not CAPACITY_REJECTED (PRV-07, reproduced).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:55:   - covers vLLM (`max_model_len`), llama.cpp (`GET /props` → `default_generation_settings.n_ctx`), LM Studio (`GET /api/v0/models` → `loaded_context_length`), and Ollama (`POST /api/show` → `model_info.*.context_length`, or `num_ctx`);\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:58:2. **REQ-PRV-102.** A capacity rejection (classified for vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama bodies) triggers one compaction and one retry at a reduced budget. A second rejection ends the turn with an actionable message naming `--context-limit` and the discovered value.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:67:   Recorded real-server SSE fixtures from LM Studio, llama.cpp `--jinja`, vLLM (hermes and qwen parsers) and Ollama run in CI.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:69:   - **(a) Live:** Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration, through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`. The proxy strips every gateway extension and, in a second profile, emulates the llama.cpp, vLLM and Ollama `/models` and overflow shapes. In both profiles, Nexus passes the standalone T2 subset and the T4 subset at the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 threshold, and turns are recorded with receipts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:70:   - **(b) Conformance:** server-kind fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama pass in CI.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:82:- **Discovery.** Add a `ServerKind` probe in `provider_capabilities.ts`: `gateway | vllm | llamacpp | lmstudio | ollama | unknown`. It inspects the `/models` response shape, and the `/props`, `/api/v0/models` and `/api/version` endpoints. Each probe has a timeout of 2 s and is cached per endpoint per session. Report the kind and the context source in `/status` and in doctor.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:98:| ACC-INF-02 | A llama.cpp overflow body and an LM Studio overflow body are both classified CAPACITY_REJECTED. Compaction and retry happen once, then an actionable error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:106:| ACC-INF-10 | ACCEPTANCE §4.2 passes: the live stripped-proxy profiles (plain, plus emulated llama.cpp/vLLM/Ollama shapes) on the standalone T2 and T4 subsets, and server-kind conformance fixtures in CI. Receipts are archived. |\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:87:5. **Inference Providers:** Endpoints receiving context and emitting completions (local vLLM/LM Studio appliance or external cloud APIs).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:363:- **Authorized Workflows Affected by Remediation:** Seamless failover between identical trust-level endpoints (e.g. between two local vLLM nodes).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:542:- **Local Appliance vs Remote Cloud:** A local model running on localhost (e.g. vLLM or Ollama) resides inside the host/local network trust boundary. A remote provider (OpenAI, Anthropic) resides outside it.\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-homelab-ai-gateway-capability-handoff.md:63:1. The vLLM adapter's tokenize omits `tool_choice` and `response_format` (`engines.py:162-170`); llama.cpp includes\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-homelab-ai-gateway-capability-handoff.md:89:- The vLLM tokenize adapter passing `tool_choice` and `response_format`, like llama.cpp.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:61:| **Constrained Tool Calling** | Prompt-driven schema formatting + retry | Client-side schema validation | Prompt-driven tool formatting | **Logit-Constrained GBNF Engine (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), targeting 0 repair retries on supported engines** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:92:  - Full functional parity when paired with local inference engines (vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama, homelab-ai gateway) while maintaining seamless support for gateway-preferred and cloud inference backends (DEC-06, DEC-16).\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:142:  - **Logit-Level Masking:** During local model sampling on supported engines (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), logits for schema-violating tokens are masked to $-\\infty$, enforcing strict syntactic conformity to the tool schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:174:│  signed audit trails.\"│      │  travel replay.\"      │      │  vLLM native.\"        │\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:189:- **Pain Point:** \"I run open-weights models on my local GPU rig with vLLM and Ollama, but agents constantly fail because small models produce invalid tool JSON or conversational filler instead of tool calls.\"\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:58:| `CTX-006` | 08: Context & Model-Route | WP-06 (INC-07) | A model route or fallback transition that alters the destination trust boundary, disclo... | `cli/src/client.ts` (`LocalLlmClient.executeWithFailover()`) | cli/test/egress.test.ts | **DEMONSTRATED** | None; failover from high-trust endpoint (e.g. localhost vLLM) to backup lower-trust endpoint (e.g. public cloud) triggers full egress re-admission. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:25:Reasoning is stripped only when both `<think>` and `</think>` are present (`parser.ts:320-332`). With templates that drop the opening tag (Qwen3 or DeepSeek-R1 on llama.cpp or vLLM), a call the model considered and rejected inside its reasoning is executed. Combined with SEC-01 auto mode, this turns echoed content into unapproved actions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:72:   `/tokenize` is used on llama.cpp and vLLM when it is available. A calibration test runs against a pinned tokenizer fixture.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:26:| 1 | `ServerKind` probe (gateway / vllm / llamacpp / lmstudio / ollama / unknown). Context discovery through `/props`, `/api/v0/models` and `/api/show`, with 2 s timeouts, cached per endpoint. Source label shown in `/status` and doctor. | `provider_capabilities.ts:29,72,184-195`; `client.ts:939-977` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:27:| 2 | Capacity rules cover llama.cpp (`exceed_context_size_error`), LM Studio and Ollama bodies. Build the table test from recorded bodies. | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:32:| 7 | Server-kind conformance fixtures, built from each project's published API docs with version and source references recorded: llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama. Covers `/models`/`/props`/`/api/v0/models`/`/api/show` shapes, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies. Also record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp workers) with `scripts/record_sse.mjs`. Add a replay test. | `cli/test/fixtures/sse/<server>/<case>.sse`; `inference_transport.test.ts` | — (no extra hardware; DEC-16) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:39:| 14 | Docs: standalone setup per server kind (LM Studio, llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama), with how context is discovered and how to override it. | `quickstart.md`, `USER_MANUAL.md`, new `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md` | 1,12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:65:1. Record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp-served models): `node scripts/record_sse.mjs --endpoint <gateway> --case {text,tool,parallel_tools,think,overflow}`. The script is new: a thin `fetch` that tees the body to a file. Commit the redacted files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:66:2. For vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama, write the fixtures from each project's published API documentation and source. Record the project version and the doc URL in each fixture header.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:67:3. Optional: run a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` container on the dev box, built without AVX, with a ≤ 1.5B model, for a protocol smoke test.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:261:### I-05 Provider context-length errors end the turn; llama.cpp's error shape is not recognised as capacity; no reactive compaction\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:266:  I6b (llama.cpp server shape: `type:\"exceed_context_size_error\"`, message \"exceeds the available context size\", `n_ctx`) → `REQUEST_REJECTED`\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:289:- Impact: for local-first users (LM Studio/vLLM/llama.cpp via `--endpoint`) token accounting is estimated and there is no receipt trail.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:324:- Mock/own HTTP servers only; no real local inference server (llama.cpp/vLLM/LM Studio) was exercised; I6b uses llama.cpp's documented error shape from memory, not a live capture.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":931211589}},"started_at_ms":1793735584949,"completed_at_ms":1793735585881}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:08.041Z","ordinal":79557,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2f8-f8c9-7700-9f5a-e9139612943b","call_id":"call_2574a610331d4202a689bfbedb409639","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6729)\nTotal output lines: 100\n\ndocs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:42:| `CTX-006` | Context Routing | Route fallback trust re-admission on destination boundary downgrade | **SATISFIED** | Failover from localhost vLLM to backup endpoint performs full re-admission |\ndocs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:58:  │  Private network services, e.g. localhost vLLM, RFC 1918 private IPs, .local mDNS\neval/README.md:125:| `context_overflow` | llama.cpp's HTTP 400 `exceed_context_size_error` |\neval/README.md:352:`engineering/lead` (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, llama.cpp b11347) through the appliance gateway, 64k context. Six T2\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:235:4. **Route Fallback:** Failover from a high-trust local model (localhost vLLM) to a lower-trust remote model re-evaluates and sanitizes the payload for the lower-trust destination (`CTX-006`).\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:66:| CTX-006 | 08: Context & Model-Route | A model route or fallback transition that alters the destination trust boundary, disclosure characteristics, or context capacity MUST trigger full re-admission of the request under the destination's applicable policies before transmission. | Fallback from a local private model to a public cloud API MUST re-admit the prompt through the outbound data-protection pipeline. Silent inheritance of local admission by external providers is strictly prohibited. | Phase 2 §12 | `cli/src/client.ts` (`LocalLlmClient.executeWithFailover()`); cli/test/egress.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None; failover from high-trust endpoint (e.g. localhost vLLM) to backup lower-trust endpoint (e.g. public cloud) triggers full egress re-admission. | Satisfied |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:76:| DEST-001 | 10: Trust-Boundary & Destination | The architecture MUST define explicit destination-aware trust boundaries across at least: `HOST_LOCAL` (local runtime and memory), `LOCAL_APPLIANCE` (private network services, e.g., local vLLM), `EXTERNAL_BOUNDED` (contracted external services, e.g., private enterprise Git), and `EXTERNAL_PUBLIC` (public cloud LLMs, public package registries, public issue trackers). | Every outbound network sink and API route MUST be assigned an explicit trust boundary classification. | Phase 2 §14 | `cli/src/core/egress.ts` (`classifyDestination()`); cli/test/egress.test.ts | DEMONSTRATED | None; 4 discrete destination trust ranks operational (HOST_LOCAL, LOCAL_APPLIANCE, EXTERNAL_BOUNDED, EXTERNAL_PUBLIC). | Satisfied |\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:3:Welcome to **Nexus Code**, a local-first, autonomous and interactive AI coding harness. Nexus Code connects to local inference servers (vLLM, LM Studio) and executes inside a native Linux shell environment.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:264:and never shown as success. The context window and output allowance are discovered from the active endpoint: vLLM (`/v1/models` `max_model_len`),\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:265:llama.cpp (`/props` `n_ctx`), LM Studio (`/api/v0/models` `loaded_context_length`), Ollama (`/api/show` `num_ctx` or\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:41:  against a non-gateway local server (LM Studio / plain llama.cpp) was **not** run in this session. Standalone\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:3:Nexus Code connects directly to standalone OpenAI-compatible local inference servers without requiring any external gateway. This guide covers setup, automatic context window discovery, capacity recovery, timeouts, and custom TLS certificate authorities for **LM Studio**, **llama.cpp**, **vLLM**, and **Ollama**.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:26:### llama.cpp (`llama-server`, `http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:37:3. **Context discovery:** Nexus recognizes `llama.cpp` from its `/v1/models` entry (`owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` or `meta.n_ctx_train`) and probes `GET /props` (2 s timeout) for `default_generation_settings.n_ctx`, reporting `server_probe (llamacpp)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:39:### vLLM (`http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:40:1. Start vLLM with the appropriate tool-call parser for your model family (`hermes`, `qwen`, `llama3_json`, etc.):\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:42:   vllm serve Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct \\\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:54:3. **Context discovery:** vLLM publishes `max_model_len` directly in `GET /v1/models`. Nexus reads it from the catalog entry and reports `provider_advertised` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:56:### Ollama (`http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1`)\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:57:1. Pull and serve a model with Ollama:\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:59:   ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:67:3. **Context discovery:** When `/v1/models` omits limits, Nexus probes `POST /api/show` with `{\"model\": \"<id>\"}` (2 s timeout) and reads `num_ctx` from `parameters` (or `model_info[\"<arch>.context_length\"]`), reporting `server_probe (ollama)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:82:If a request exceeds the server's loaded context window (including llama.cpp `exceed_context_size_error`, LM Studio context overflow errors, vLLM `maximum context length`, or Ollama context length rejections), Nexus classifies the response as `CAPACITY_REJECTED`, compacts the conversation history once, and retries once at a reduced token budget. If the compacted retry is still rejected, the turn stops immediately with an actionable message naming `--context-limit` and the discovered window.\ndocs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:211:| `advertised` | the connection's `/models` entry (homelab-ai gateway: `context_length`, `max_completion_tokens`, `limits_version`, serving workers; vLLM: `max_model_len`) |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md:3:Evidence: `experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/RESULTS.md` (commit 9b6efe9). Scope of validity: current Nexus + aihost gateway (llama.cpp prefix cache),\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:381:| **DEST-001** | The architecture MUST define explicit destination-aware trust boundaries across at least: `HOST_LOCAL` …3729 tokens truncated…rust-level endpoints (e.g. between two local vLLM nodes).\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:542:- **Local Appliance vs Remote Cloud:** A local model running on localhost (e.g. vLLM or Ollama) resides inside the host/local network trust boundary. A remote provider (OpenAI, Anthropic) resides outside it.\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-homelab-ai-gateway-capability-handoff.md:63:1. The vLLM adapter's tokenize omits `tool_choice` and `response_format` (`engines.py:162-170`); llama.cpp includes\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-homelab-ai-gateway-capability-handoff.md:89:- The vLLM tokenize adapter passing `tool_choice` and `response_format`, like llama.cpp.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:61:| **Constrained Tool Calling** | Prompt-driven schema formatting + retry | Client-side schema validation | Prompt-driven tool formatting | **Logit-Constrained GBNF Engine (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), targeting 0 repair retries on supported engines** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:92:  - Full functional parity when paired with local inference engines (vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama, homelab-ai gateway) while maintaining seamless support for gateway-preferred and cloud inference backends (DEC-06, DEC-16).\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:142:  - **Logit-Level Masking:** During local model sampling on supported engines (`llama.cpp`, `vLLM` guided decoding, `Ollama`), logits for schema-violating tokens are masked to $-\\infty$, enforcing strict syntactic conformity to the tool schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:174:│  signed audit trails.\"│      │  travel replay.\"      │      │  vLLM native.\"        │\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:189:- **Pain Point:** \"I run open-weights models on my local GPU rig with vLLM and Ollama, but agents constantly fail because small models produce invalid tool JSON or conversational filler instead of tool calls.\"\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:58:| `CTX-006` | 08: Context & Model-Route | WP-06 (INC-07) | A model route or fallback transition that alters the destination trust boundary, disclo... | `cli/src/client.ts` (`LocalLlmClient.executeWithFailover()`) | cli/test/egress.test.ts | **DEMONSTRATED** | None; failover from high-trust endpoint (e.g. localhost vLLM) to backup lower-trust endpoint (e.g. public cloud) triggers full egress re-admission. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:25:Reasoning is stripped only when both `<think>` and `</think>` are present (`parser.ts:320-332`). With templates that drop the opening tag (Qwen3 or DeepSeek-R1 on llama.cpp or vLLM), a call the model considered and rejected inside its reasoning is executed. Combined with SEC-01 auto mode, this turns echoed content into unapproved actions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:72:   `/tokenize` is used on llama.cpp and vLLM when it is available. A calibration test runs against a pinned tokenizer fixture.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:26:| 1 | `ServerKind` probe (gateway / vllm / llamacpp / lmstudio / ollama / unknown). Context discovery through `/props`, `/api/v0/models` and `/api/show`, with 2 s timeouts, cached per endpoint. Source label shown in `/status` and doctor. | `provider_capabilities.ts:29,72,184-195`; `client.ts:939-977` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:27:| 2 | Capacity rules cover llama.cpp (`exceed_context_size_error`), LM Studio and Ollama bodies. Build the table test from recorded bodies. | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:32:| 7 | Server-kind conformance fixtures, built from each project's published API docs with version and source references recorded: llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama. Covers `/models`/`/props`/`/api/v0/models`/`/api/show` shapes, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies. Also record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp workers) with `scripts/record_sse.mjs`. Add a replay test. | `cli/test/fixtures/sse/<server>/<case>.sse`; `inference_transport.test.ts` | — (no extra hardware; DEC-16) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:39:| 14 | Docs: standalone setup per server kind (LM Studio, llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama), with how context is discovered and how to override it. | `quickstart.md`, `USER_MANUAL.md`, new `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md` | 1,12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:65:1. Record real SSE through the gateway (llama.cpp-served models): `node scripts/record_sse.mjs --endpoint <gateway> --case {text,tool,parallel_tools,think,overflow}`. The script is new: a thin `fetch` that tees the body to a file. Commit the redacted files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:66:2. For vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama, write the fixtures from each project's published API documentation and source. Record the project version and the doc URL in each fixture header.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md:67:3. Optional: run a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` container on the dev box, built without AVX, with a ≤ 1.5B model, for a protocol smoke test.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:261:### I-05 Provider context-length errors end the turn; llama.cpp's error shape is not recognised as capacity; no reactive compaction\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:266:  I6b (llama.cpp server shape: `type:\"exceed_context_size_error\"`, message \"exceeds the available context size\", `n_ctx`) → `REQUEST_REJECTED`\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:289:- Impact: for local-first users (LM Studio/vLLM/llama.cpp via `--endpoint`) token accounting is estimated and there is no receipt trail.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/trust_inference.md:324:- Mock/own HTTP servers only; no real local inference server (llama.cpp/vLLM/LM Studio) was exercised; I6b uses llama.cpp's documented error shape from memory, not a live capture.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735588.0413697}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
