{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:17.619Z","ordinal":79565,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea3ba9924081a387c32dee4e4db352","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4135fdf46ae0490fba4483a6114d3a92","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix` and `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`.\\n+- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\\n@@\\n-- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n+- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n@@\\n-- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; native-valid/repaired/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version and SHA-256 of the finalized evidence file. Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, and other secrets.\\n+- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; native-valid/repaired/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version. Store the finalized evidence file’s SHA-256 in the detached `.sha256` sidecar and qualification record (the JSON cannot hash itself). Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, and other secrets.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735593.572958}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:17.650Z","ordinal":79566,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-9233e87b-dea2-4f74-a2d6-ac26645ba1da","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -12,3 +12,3 @@\n - **AC4:** Unknown and unsupported endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent without positive provider identification. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`.\n-- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Test/evidence: `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix` and `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`.\n+- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\n \n@@ -40,6 +40,6 @@\n - Add a deterministic runner and schema validator. Fake-provider/serialization tests validate request construction and evidence validation only; they do not count as live endpoint measurements.\n-- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\n+- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\n - Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\n - Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no constraint fields.\n-- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; native-valid/repaired/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version and SHA-256 of the finalized evidence file. Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, and other secrets.\n+- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; native-valid/repaired/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version. Store the finalized evidence file’s SHA-256 in the detached `.sha256` sidecar and qualification record (the JSON cannot hash itself). Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, and other secrets.\n - Test/evidence: AC5 threshold and zero-invalid requirement for every provider. This measures argument JSON only; it does not certify tool selection or task correctness.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793735597649,"completed_at_ms":1793735597650}}
