{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:30.936Z","ordinal":79592,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a2f9-5237-7f02-a6b3-4862aad6611e","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**APPROVED_WITH_CHANGES.** AC5’s sample size, per-tool distribution, integer threshold, outcome definitions, evidence fields, and pre-run GATEWAY dependency are now auditable. Fake-provider tests are clearly separate from the live matrix.\n\nOne change remains: define what positively identifies a provider and test ambiguous catalogs. Current [`provider_capabilities.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts:75) classifies any model entry with generic `context_length` as vLLM. Matching that `serverKind` to a configured label alone could enable a constrained field for an unrelated endpoint. Specify provider-specific metadata or a trusted opt-in rule, and add a regression proving ambiguous catalogs remain `unknown` and receive no grammar field."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735610.9355862,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2775}}
