{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:53.402Z","ordinal":79615,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-4efbd9bd-091e-4e32-84c2-e0ac18963822","query":"","action":{"type":"other"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn31view0","snippet":"Total lines: 414","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/REDACTED","title":"vllm/docs/serving/online_serving/README.md at main · vllm-project/vllm · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/serving/online_serving/README.md"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn31view1","snippet":"Total lines: 1278","title":"OpenAI-Compatible Server - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/serving/online_serving/openai_compatible_server/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn31view2","snippet":"Total lines: 4104","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/REDACTED","title":"ollama/docs/openapi.yaml at main · ollama/ollama · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml"}]},"started_at_ms":1793735632022,"completed_at_ms":1793735633402}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:53:54.649Z","ordinal":79616,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a2f9-aed9-7dd1-b5e1-0f4c938cb237","call_id":"call_1e84d0e4e5d84dfc95ddd5cfa700c8a5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"vllm/docs/serving/online_serving/README.md at main · vllm-project/vllm · GitHub (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/serving/online_serving/README.md)\nciteturn31view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn30search4\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 414\nL265: ### Offline API Documentation\nL266: \nL267: The FastAPI `/docs` endpoint requires an internet connection by default. To enable offline access in air-gapped environments, use the `--enable-offline-docs` flag:\nL268: \nL269:     vllm serve NousResearch/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct --enable-offline-docs\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenAI-Compatible Server - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/serving/online_serving/openai_compatible_server/)\nciteturn31view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn30search3\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1278\nL495: # OpenAI-Compatible Server【0†¶】\nL496: \nL497: vLLM provides an HTTP server that implements OpenAI's 【363†Completions API†platform.openai.com】, 【364†Chat API†platform.openai.com】, and more! This functionality lets you serve models and interact with them using an HTTP client.\nL498: \nL499: API key authentication does not protect every endpoint\nL500: The `--api-key` option (or `VLLM_API_KEY` environment variable) only authenticates requests to endpoints under the `/v1`, `/v2`, and `/inference` path prefixes. Other endpoints on the same HTTP server are not authenticated — most notably `/invocations`, which exposes the same inference capabilities as the `/v1` endpoints. Do not rely on `--api-key` alone to secure vLLM.\nL501: See 【365†API Key Authentication Limitations】 for the full list of protected and unprotected endpoints and recommended hardening, such as deploying behind a reverse proxy.\nL505:   * 【114†Completions API】 (`/v1/completions`)\nL506:     * Only applicable to 【199†text generation models】.\nL507:     * Note: `suffix` parameter is not supported.\nL508:   * 【120†Chat Completions API】 (`/v1/chat/completions`)\nL509:     * Only applicable to 【199†text generation models】 with a 【366†chat template】.\nL510:     * Note: `user` parameter is ignored.\nL511:     * Note: Setting the `parallel_tool_calls` parameter to `false` ensures vLLM only returns zero or one tool call per request. Setting it to `true` (the default) allows returning more than one tool call per request. There is no guarantee more than one tool call will be returned if this is set to `true`, as that behavior is model dependent and not all models are designed to support parallel tool calls.\nL512:   * 【120†Chat Completions batch API】 (`/v1/chat/completions/batch`)\nL513:   * 【122†Responses API】 (`/v1/responses`, `/v1/responses/{response_id}`, `/v1/responses/{response_id}/cancel`)\nL514:     * Only applicable to 【199†text generation models】.\nL515:   * 【367†Embeddings API】 (`/v1/embeddings`)\nL516:     * Only applicable to 【202†embedding models】.\nL517:   * 【368†Transcriptions API】 (`/v1/audio/transcriptions`)\nL518:     * Only applicable to 【369†Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) models】.\nL519:   * 【370†Translation API】 (`/v1/audio/translations`)\nL520:     * Only applicable to 【369†Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) models】.\nL521: ## Completions API【114†¶】\nL522: \nL523: In your terminal, you can 【10†install】 vLLM, then start the server with the 【196†`vllm serve`】 command. (You can also use our 【138†Docker】 image.)\nL524: \nL525:     `vllm serve NousResearch/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct \\\nL526:       --dtype auto \\\nL527:       --api-key token-abc123\nL528:     `\nL529: To call the server, in your preferred text editor, create a script that uses an HTTP client. Include any messages that you want to send to the model. Then run that script. Below is an example script using the 【371†official OpenAI Python client†github.com】.\nL530: Code\nL531: \nL532:     `from openai import OpenAI\nL533:     client = OpenAI(\nL534:         base_url=\"http://localhost:8000/v1\",\nL535:         api_key=\"REDACTED\",\nL536:     )\nL537: \nL538:     completion = client.chat.completions.create(\nL539:         model=\"NousResearch/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct\",\nL540:         messages=[\nL541:             {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"},\nL542:         ],\nL543:     )\nL544: \nL545:     print(completion.choices[0].message)\nL546:     `\nL547: \nL548: Tip\nL549: vLLM supports some parameters that are not supported by OpenAI, `top_k` for example. You can pass these parameters to vLLM using the OpenAI client in the `extra_body` parameter of your requests, i.e. `extra_body={\"top_k\": 50}` for `top_k`.\nL550: \nL551: Important\nL552: \nL553: By default, the server applies `generation_config.json` from the Hugging Face model repository if it exists. This means the default values of certain sampling parameters can be overridden by those recommended by the model creator.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nollama/docs/openapi.yaml at main · ollama/ollama · GitHub (https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml)\nciteturn31view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn30search0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 4104\nL2162: title: Ollama API\nL2163: \nL2164: version: 0.1.0\nL2165: \nL2166: license:\nL2167: \nL2168: name: MIT\nL2169: \nL2170: url: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\nL2171: \nL2172: description: |\nL2173: \nL2174: OpenAPI specification for the Ollama HTTP API\nL2175: \nL2176: servers:\nL2177: \nL2178: - url: http://localhost:11434\nL2179: \nL2180: description: Ollama\nL2181: \nL2182: security: []\nL2183: \nL2184: components:\nL2185: \nL2186: securitySchemes:\nL2187: \nL2188: bearerAuth:\nL2189: \nL2190: type: http\nL2191: \nL2192: scheme: bearer\nL2193: \nL2194: bearerFormat: API Key\nL2195: \nL2196: parameters:\nL2197: \nL2198: DigestParam:\nL2199: \nL2200: name: digest\nL2201: \nL2202: in: path\nL2203: \nL2204: required: true\nL2205: \nL2206: description: SHA256 digest identifier, prefixed with `sha256:`\nL2207: \nL2208: schema:\nL2209: \nL2210: type: string\nL2211: \nL2212: schemas:\nL2213: \nL2214: ModelOptions:\nL2215: type: object\nL2216: \nL2217: description: Runtime options that control text generation\nL2218: \nL2219: properties:\nL2220: # Sampling Options\nL2221: \nL2222: seed:\nL2223: \nL2224: type: integer\nL2225: \nL2226: description: Random seed used for reproducible outputs\nL2227: \nL2228: temperature:\nL2229: \nL2230: type: number\nL2231: \nL2232: format: float\nL2233: \nL2234: description: Controls randomness in generation (higher = more random)\nL2235: \nL2236: top_k:\nL2237: \nL2238: type: integer\nL2239: \nL2240: description: Limits next token selection to the K most likely\nL2241: \nL2242: top_p:\nL2243: \nL2244: type: number\nL2245: \nL2246: format: float\nL2247: \nL2248: description: Cumulative probability threshold for nucleus sampling\nL2249: \nL2250: min_p:\nL2251: \nL2252: type: number\nL2253: \nL2254: format: float\nL2255: \nL2256: description: Minimum probability threshold for token selection\nL2257: \nL2258: stop:\nL2259: oneOf:\nL2260: \nL2261: - type: string\nL2262: \nL2263: - type: array\nL2264: \nL2265: items:\nL2266: \nL2267: type: string\nL2268: \nL2269: description: Stop sequences that will halt generation\nL2270: # Runtime Options\nL2271: \nL2272: num_ctx:\nL2273: \nL2274: type: integer\nL2275: \nL2276: description: Context length size (number of tokens)\nL2277: \nL2278: num_predict:\nL2279: \nL2280: type: integer\nL2281: \nL2282: description: Maximum number of tokens to generate\nL2283: \nL2284: additionalProperties: true\nL2285: \nL2286: GenerateRequest:\nL2287: \nL2288: type: object\nL2289: \nL2290: required: [model]\nL2291: \nL2292: properties:\nL2293: \nL2294: model:\nL2295: \nL2296: type: string\nL2297: \nL2298: description: Model name\nL2299: \nL2300: prompt:\nL2301: \nL2302: type: string\nL2303: \nL2304: description: Text for the model to generate a response from\nL2305: \nL2306: suffix:\nL2307: \nL2308: type: string\nL2309: description: Used for fill-in-the-middle models, text that appears after the user prompt and before the model response\nL2310: \nL2311: images:\nL2312: \nL2313: type: array\nL2314: \nL2315: items:\nL2316: \nL2317: type: string\nL2318: \nL2319: description: Base64-encoded images for models that support image input\nL2320: \nL2321: format:\nL2322: \nL2323: description: Structured output format for the model to generate a response from. Supports either the string `\"json\"` or a JSON schema object.\nL2324: \nL2325: oneOf:\nL2326: \nL2327: - type: string\nL2328: \nL2329: - type: object\nL2330: \nL2331: system:\nL2332: \nL2333: description: System prompt for the model to generate a response from\nL2334: type: string\nL2335: \nL2336: stream:\nL2337: \nL2338: description: When true, returns a stream of partial responses\nL2339: \nL2340: type: boolean\nL2341: \nL2342: default: true\nL2343: \nL2344: think:\nL2345: \nL2346: $ref: \"#/components/schemas/ThinkValue\"\nL2347: \nL2348: raw:\nL2349: \nL2350: type: boolean\nL2351: \nL2352: description: When true, returns the raw response from the model without any prompt templating\nL2353: \nL2354: keep_alive:\nL2355: \nL2356: oneOf:\nL2357: \nL2358: - type: string\nL2359: \nL2360: - type: number\nL2361: \nL2362: description: Model keep-alive duration (for example `5m` or `0` to unload immediately)\nL2363: \nL2364: options:\nL2365: \nL2366: $ref: \"#/components/schemas/ModelOptions\"\nL2367: \nL2368: logprobs:\nL2369: \nL2370: type: boolean\nL2371: description: Whether to return log probabilities of the output tokens\nL2372: \nL2373: top_logprobs:\nL2374: \nL2375: type: integer\nL2376: \nL2377: description: Number of most likely tokens to return at each token position when logprobs are enabled\nL2378: \nL2379: GenerateResponse:\nL2380: \nL2381: type: object\nL2382: \nL2383: properties:\nL2384: \nL2385: model:\nL2386: \nL2387: type: string\nL2388: \nL2389: description: Model name\nL2390: \nL2391: created_at:\nL2392: \nL2393: type: string\nL2394: \nL2395: description: ISO 8601 timestamp of response creation\nL2396: \nL2397: response:\nL2398: \nL2399: type: string\nL2400: \nL2401: description: The model's generated text response\nL2402: \nL2403: thinking:\nL2404: \nL2405: type: string\nL2406: description: The model's generated thinking output\nL2407: \nL2408: done:\nL2409: \nL2410: type: boolean\nL2411: \nL2412: description: Indicates whether generation has finished\nL2413: \nL2414: done_reason:\nL2415: \nL2416: type: string\nL2417: \nL2418: description: Reason the generation stopped\nL2419: \nL2420: total_duration:\nL2421: \nL2422: type: integer\nL2423: \nL2424: description: Time spent generating the response in nanoseconds\nL2425: \nL2426: load_duration:\nL2427: \nL2428: type: integer\nL2429: \nL2430: description: Time spent loading the model in nanoseconds\nL2431: \nL2432: prompt_eval_count:\nL2433: \nL2434: type: integer\nL2435: \nL2436: description: Number of input tokens in the prompt\nL2437: \nL2438: prompt_eval_cached_count:\nL2439: type: integer\nL2440: \nL2441: description: Number of prompt tokens read from the cache\nL2442: \nL2443: prompt_eval_duration:\nL2444: \nL2445: type: integer\nL2446: \nL2447: description: Time spent evaluating uncached prompt tokens in nanoseconds\nL2448: \nL2449: eval_count:\nL2450: \nL2451: type: integer\nL2452: \nL2453: description: Number of output tokens generated in the response\nL2454: \nL2455: eval_duration:\nL2456: \nL2457: type: integer\nL2458: \n