{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:54:54.966Z","ordinal":79674,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea3c037cec81a39b2f724c24e9c747","status":"completed","call_id":"call_e6313be4a093486caf5cc0363c26963a","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC4:** Unknown and unsupported endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent without positive provider identification. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`.\\n+- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`.\\n@@\\n-- Add a typed adapter mapping positively identified `llamacpp`, `vllm`, and `ollama` server kinds to their documented request constraint fields.\\n+- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented request constraint fields only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\\n@@\\n-- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new).\\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above.\\n+- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above, including the generic-catalog regression.\\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for grammar attachment, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables constrained fields.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735683.4900587}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:54:55.001Z","ordinal":79675,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-ee97cd28-c7e7-4b07-8e40-3fc97b00fb2f","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -11,3 +11,3 @@\n - **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\n-- **AC4:** Unknown and unsupported endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent without positive provider identification. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`.\n+- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`.\n - **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\n@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@\n \n-- Add a typed adapter mapping positively identified `llamacpp`, `vllm`, and `ollama` server kinds to their documented request constraint fields.\n+- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented request constraint fields only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\n - Derive constraints from the current allowlisted tool schemas; preserve the existing request when provider kind is unknown or the endpoint/protocol does not support the field.\n-- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new).\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above.\n+- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above, including the generic-catalog regression.\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for grammar attachment, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables constrained fields.\n - References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793735694999,"completed_at_ms":1793735695001}}
