{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:55:26.163Z","ordinal":79715,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a2fb-1453-7853-bf7e-96a69b39a7a6","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**APPROVED_WITH_CHANGES.** The provider-specific handshake rules resolve the generic-catalog ambiguity, and the matrix and evidence plan are auditable.\n\nBefore approval, name tests that accept each provider’s required identity handshake and reject missing, malformed, or mismatched handshakes while confirming no constraint field is sent. The generic-catalog test does not yet cover those failure cases. No broader file-scope change is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735726.163029,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2780}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:55:27.524Z","ordinal":79716,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea3c2f0ce081a3bb248eea2fc3ca3d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The provider-specific identification rule now satisfies the reviewer’s safety concern, but the plan still needs named tests for successful handshakes and for missing, malformed, or mismatched handshakes suppressing constraints. I’m adding those test names now; this is the last requested plan change before review approval."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793735727106,"completed_at_ms":1793735727524}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:55:27.528Z","ordinal":79717,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea3c2f0ce081a3bb248eea2fc3ca3d","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The provider-specific identification rule now satisfies the reviewer’s safety concern, but the plan still needs named tests for successful handshakes and for missing, malformed, or mismatched handshakes suppressing constraints. I’m adding those test names now; this is the last requested plan change before review approval.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735727.0773973,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea3c2f0ce081a3bb248eea2fc3ca3d","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1a2fb-19a8-7a71-ba6d-622b03aba7ef","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2781}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:55:29.257Z","ordinal":79718,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea3c2f7e2881a3ad807d9312d5a98f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_954f7e9d3cba4a34bd4eaecf09dad835","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`.\\n+- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\\n@@\\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above, including the generic-catalog regression.\\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793735727.4954734}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:55:29.310Z","ordinal":79719,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0dcad695-b42c-4809-beba-0bca5162d180","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -11,3 +11,3 @@\n - **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\n-- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Test: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`.\n+- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\n - **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\n@@ -27,3 +27,3 @@\n - Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape tests above, including the generic-catalog regression.\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases.\n - Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for grammar attachment, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables constrained fields.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793735729306,"completed_at_ms":1793735729310}}
