{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:02:18.178Z","ordinal":80132,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f51fe469-f629-45b4-95c8-45b98ad8e977","process_id":"52299","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,220p' cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts; rg -n \"tool grammar|WP-1107|generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars|native JSON\" docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.1.0 -g '*.md' | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts","name":"tool_grammar.ts","path":"cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'tool grammar|WP-1107|generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars|native JSON' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/v1.1.0 -g '*.md'","query":"tool grammar|WP-1107|generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars|native JSON","path":"ROADMAP.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"import { HARNESS_TOOLS } from \"./capabilities.js\";\nimport type { ToolDefinition } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/** The v1.1.0 GBNF pilot is intentionally limited to these registered tools. */\nexport const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\nexport type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\n\nconst ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\nconst MAX_PROPERTIES = 8;\n\n/** Compile the exact parameter schema registered for one allowlisted tool. Unknown JSON Schema forms fail closed. */\nexport function generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\n  toolName: GbnfToolName,\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): string {\n  if (!ALLOWED_NAMES.has(toolName)) throw new Error(`GBNF is not enabled for tool ${String(toolName)}`);\n  if (!Array.isArray(registeredTools)) throw new Error(\"registered tool definitions must be an array\");\n\n  const matches = registeredTools.filter((tool) => (tool as ToolDefinition | undefined)?.function?.name === toolName);\n  if (matches.length !== 1) {\n    throw new Error(`expected exactly one registered schema for ${toolName}; found ${matches.length}`);\n  }\n  const definition = matches[0] as ToolDefinition;\n  if (definition.type !== \"function\" || !definition.function || definition.function.name !== toolName) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} is not a function tool`);\n  }\n  const parameters = definition.function.parameters as unknown;\n  if (!parameters || typeof parameters !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(parameters)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define an object parameter schema`);\n  }\n\n  const schema = parameters as Record<string, unknown>;\n  rejectUnknownKeys(schema, new Set([\"type\", \"properties\", \"required\"]), `${toolName} parameter schema`);\n  if (schema.type !== \"object\") throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must have type object`);\n  if (!schema.properties || typeof schema.properties !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(schema.properties)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define flat properties`);\n  }\n\n  const propertyMap = schema.properties as Record<string, unknown>;\n  const propertyNames = Object.keys(propertyMap);\n  if (propertyNames.length > MAX_PROPERTIES) throw new Error(`${toolName} schema exceeds the ${MAX_PROPERTIES}-property GBNF bound`);\n  const required = schema.required === undefined ? [] : schema.required;\n  if (!Array.isArray(required) || required.some((name) => typeof name !== \"string\")) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} has an invalid required list`);\n  }\n  if (new Set(required).size !== required.length) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} repeats a required property`);\n  for (const name of required) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(propertyMap, name)) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} requires undeclared property ${name}`);\n  }\n\n  const properties = propertyNames.map((name, index) => {\n    const raw = propertyMap[name];\n    if (!raw || typeof raw !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(raw)) {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} must be a flat schema object`);\n    }\n    const property = raw as Record<string, unknown>;\n    const valueRule = property.type === \"string\" ? \"json-string\"\n      : property.type === \"number\" ? \"json-number\"\n        : property.type === \"boolean\" ? \"json-boolean\"\n          : undefined;\n    if (!valueRule) throw new Error(`unsupported JSON Schema type for ${toolName}.${name}`);\n    rejectUnknownKeys(property, new Set([\"type\", \"description\"]), `${toolName}.${name} schema`);\n    if (typeof property.description !== \"undefined\" && typeof property.description !== \"string\") {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} has an invalid description`);\n    }\n    return { name, index, valueRule };\n  });\n\n  const propertyIndex = new Map(properties.map(({ name, index }) => [name, index]));\n  const requiredMask = required.reduce((mask: number, name: string) => mask | (1 << propertyIndex.get(name)!), 0);\n  const stateCount = 1 << properties.length;\n  const rules = [\n    \"root ::= ws \\\"{\\\" ws object-fields ws \\\"}\\\" ws\",\n    \"json-string ::= \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\" json-char* \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n    String.raw`json-char ::= [^\"\\\\\\x00-\\x1f] | \"\\\\\" ([\"\\\\/bfnrt] | \"u\" [0-9a-fA-F]{4})`,\n    String.raw`json-number ::= \"-\"? (\"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*) (\".\" [0-9]+)? ([eE] [-+]? [0-9]+)?`,\n    \"json-boolean ::= \\\"true\\\" | \\\"false\\\"\",\n    \"ws ::= [ \\\\t\\\\n\\\\r]*\",\n    ...properties.map(({ name, index, valueRule }) => `member_${index} ::= ${JSON.stringify(name)} ws \":\" ws ${valueRule}`),\n  ];\n\n  const firstChoices = properties.map(({ index }) => `member_${index} fields_tail_${1 << index}`);\n  rules.push(`object-fields ::= ${requiredMask === 0 ? '\"\" | ' : \"\"}${firstChoices.length ? firstChoices.join(\" | \") : '\"\"'}`);\n  for (let mask = 0; mask < stateCount; mask++) {\n    const choices: string[] = [];\n    if ((mask & requiredMask) === requiredMask) choices.push('\"\"');\n    for (const { index } of properties) {\n      const bit = 1 << index;\n      if ((mask & bit) === 0) choices.push(`\",\" ws member_${index} fields_tail_${mask | bit}`);\n    }\n    // Only reachable states need a rule, but emitting all bounded masks keeps output deterministic and simple.\n    rules.push(`fields_tail_${mask} ::= ${choices.join(\" | \") || '\"\"'}`);\n  }\n  return rules.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\n/** Compile each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\nexport function generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars(\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): Readonly<Record<GbnfToolName, string>> {\n  const result = {} as Record<GbnfToolName, string>;\n  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction rejectUnknownKeys(value: Record<string, unknown>, allowed: ReadonlySet<string>, label: string): void {\n  const unknown = Object.keys(value).find((key) => !allowed.has(key));\n  if (unknown) throw new Error(`${label} contains unsupported schema keyword ${unknown}`);\n}\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/README.md:60:- The `WP-11xx` post-v1 roadmap packages (OpenTelemetry tracing, `nexus eval`, GBNF tool grammars, Composio bridges,\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:152:  - **GBNF-Constrained API Schemas:** Enterprise action schemas compile directly into Context-Free Grammars (`WP-1107`), enforcing JSON schema compliance and valid parameter emission on supported local engines during multi-argument external calls.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194:| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:77:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:1:# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:43:- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:157:4. **`json_repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parser telemetry, scoring 1.0 for valid native JSON and 0.5 for recovered malformed JSON.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":803620776}},"started_at_ms":1793736137374,"completed_at_ms":1793736138178}}
