e each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\nexport function generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars(\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): Readonly<Record<GbnfToolName, string>> {\n  const result = {} as Record<GbnfToolName, string>;\n  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction rejectUnknownKeys(value: Record<string, unknown>, allowed: ReadonlySet<string>, label: string): void {\n  const unknown = Object.keys(value).find((key) => !allowed.has(key));\n  if (unknown) throw new Error(`${label} contains unsupported schema keyword ${unknown}`);\n}\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/README.md:60:- The `WP-11xx` post-v1 roadmap packages (OpenTelemetry tracing, `nexus eval`, GBNF tool grammars, Composio bridges,\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:152:  - **GBNF-Constrained API Schemas:** Enterprise action schemas compile directly into Context-Free Grammars (`WP-1107`), enforcing JSON schema compliance and valid parameter emission on supported local engines during multi-argument external calls.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194:| WP-1107 | GBNF tool grammar engine | None (provider request shapes change) | **Defer**: changes provider request patterns, which the v1.1 ground rules forbid inside this release |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:77:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:1:# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` before any normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing tool-call repair path produces parseable JSON; `invalid` includes every other outcome, including provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and unparseable arguments. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995` and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax matrix`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:43:- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md:157:4. **`json_repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parser telemetry, scoring 1.0 for valid native JSON and 0.5 for recovered malformed JSON.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736139.7307386}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
