{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:04:31.415Z","ordinal":80242,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea3e4ed06881a38d2fd35ed277bf9e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The vLLM server source also shows that its structured-output parameters are not a drop-in replacement for native function calls; compatibility depends on the selected tool mode, so I’m verifying that branch before finalizing the request adapter. I’ve confirmed this is a plan correction, not a reason to push a speculative field into requests."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793736270850,"completed_at_ms":1793736271415}}
