{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:04.439Z","ordinal":80391,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a305-bbf7-7280-8c03-eadf7d434129","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...794 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 8:07pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (19,096t read) | 87,496t work | 78% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2134 v1.1.2 Release Scope Reconciliation and WP-1103 Qualification Gate — PLAN Phase with Concurrent Test Blocker (Nov 2, 12:21 PM)\nS2146 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 AC2 Mount-View Test Implementation, Source Review Approval, Release Docs Integration, and External Suite Monitoring (Nov 2, 12:39 PM)\nS2149 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate: Waiting for Shared Test Host to Clear (Nov 2, 1:16 PM)\nS2150 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate Blocked by Two External PR396 Test Streams (Nov 2, 1:35 PM)\nS2151 v1.1.2 Release — Goal Formally Blocked by Shared Test Host Contention, Awaiting External Test Stream Clearance (Nov 2, 1:45 PM)\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29266 7:35p ◆ RC2 Artifact-C/D Reproducibility Confirmed — Both Builds Produce Identical SHA-256 3e39bd36\n29267 \" ◆ RC2 Installer Acceptance Passed — v1.1.2-rc.2 Installs Correctly from Canonical Artifact-C\n29268 \" ○ Acceptance Test Fails on New Guard — \"acceptance evidence must be candidate-specific\" at Line 42\n29269 \" ✓ Evidence File Claim Rotated — Old fd99bd3f6a80 Claim Released, New 3e39bd36f31d Claim Acquired\n29270 7:36p ◆ RC2 Installed Package Acceptance Passed — 3/3 Tests Pass, Evidence Written\n29271 \" ◆ RC2 Acceptance Evidence Fully Verified — 6 Provider Requests Captured, Installed File Mode 644, Manifest PASS\n29272 7:37p ◆ RC2 Full Package Acceptance Suite — All 5 Tests Pass Including Outside-Checkout and No-Eval-Mount Tests\n29273 \" ○ release_gate_audit Agent Independently Confirmed Root Cause — core.sharedRepository=true Causes Mode 664\n29274 \" ○ RC2 Artifact-C File Sizes and SHA-256s Captured — Qualification Record Still Shows Open Gates\n29275 7:38p ○ v1.1.2 Qualification Record Current State — Release Gates G1.1-2 and G1.1-3 Still Marked REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED\n29276 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Qualification Record Updated — G1.1-2 and G1.1-3 Now PASSED, G1.1-5 Updated with Artifact Evidence\n29277 \" ✓ Qualification Record Updated — RC2 Exact Archive Section Added, Checklist Items Ticked\n29278 \" ○ Pre-Commit State — Two Evidence Files Identical, docs/evidence/v1.1.2/ Untracked, No Active GATEWAY/SUITE/V112_RC2_PACKAGE Claims\n29279 \" ○ Active Claims Audit — GATEWAY Held by RC15 E5 Provider Stream, SUITE and V112_RC2_PACKAGE Still Active\n29280 7:39p ◆ RC2 Final Pre-Commit Verification — All Installed Artifact Integrity Checks Pass\n29281 \" ✓ Duplicate Evidence File Removed — Single acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json Retained\n29282 7:41p ✓ Post-Doc Security Gates Passed — All 4 Gates Clean Before Final Commit\n29283 \" ✓ RC2 Package Worktree Removed and All Related Claims Released\n29287 7:42p ○ Independent /root Review Agent APPROVED RC2 Final Archive Evidence\n29288 \" ✓ Qualification Record Scope Clarification — Specialist Roadmap Items Separated from WP Release Scope\n29289 7:44p ✓ RC2 Qualification Evidence Commit In Progress\n29290 7:45p ✓ RC2 Qualification Evidence Committed — Commit 6aef6635\n29291 7:46p ✓ RC2 Qualification Commit Amended — Final Commit 3eea888a\n29292 \" ✓ FILE Claims Released — Qualification Record and Evidence Claims Cleared Post-Commit\n29293 \" ✓ v1.1.2 RC2 Local Qualification Phase Complete — Work State Closed as Done\n29299 7:47p ○ GBNF Grammar Module Exists but Is Not Wired into Provider Request Path\n29300 \" ○ FILE_cli_src_client.ts Claim Held by RC16 Stream-Cancel Worktree\n29310 7:50p ✓ WP-1107 Claims Acquired — Stale RC16 client.ts Claim Broken and Reassigned\n29311 \" ○ WP-1107 Completion Was Overstated — Grammar Generator Has No Provider Callsites\n29312 \" ◆ WP-1107 Implementation Plan Written — 3-Chunk Spec with AC1–AC5 Acceptance Criteria\n29313 7:51p ✓ Qualification Record Corrected — WP-1107 Downgraded from PASSED to INCOMPLETE\n29314 \" ○ RC15 E5 Provider Worktree Has Untracked Evidence Files — GATEWAY Claim May Be Stale\n29315 7:52p ⚖ WP-1107 Plan Approved With Changes — AC5 Needs Measurement Specification Before RED Phase\n29316 \" ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md Updated — AC5 Measurement Methodology and Matrix Runner Fully Specified\n29318 7:53p ○ docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md Documents Exact Provider API Endpoints Used for Server Kind Detection\n29320 \" ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md — Evidence Schema Refined with Detached SHA-256 Sidecar Pattern\n29321 \" ○ Provider Version Endpoints Confirmed — Ollama /api/version, vLLM /version, llama.cpp /props Available\n29322 \" ○ Provider API Schema Research — Ollama, vLLM, and OpenAI Compatibility Details\n29323 7:54p ○ LocalLlmClient Server Discovery Architecture — discoverAdvertisement and discoverServerContext Flow\n29324 \" ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md Updated — Provider Identity Contract Tightened for Grammar Field Injection\n29326 7:55p ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md AC4 Expanded with Provider Identity Handshake Tests\n29327 \" ○ LocalLlmClient Provider Discovery Architecture — discoverAdvertisement and serverKindOf Flow\n29328 7:56p ○ Exact Line Numbers for WP-1107 Integration Points in client.ts and provider_capabilities.ts\n29329 \" ○ provider_capabilities.ts Full Export Surface and chatCompletion Delegation Chain\n29330 \" ✓ WP-1107 File Claims Acquired — 5 of 7 Files Now Held\n29331 7:57p ✓ WP-1107 Remaining File Claims Acquired — All 7 Files Now Held\n29332 \" ✓ Provider Reference Repositories Cloned to /home/mike/xerj-references\n29333 7:59p ✓ Provider Reference Repositories Being Indexed into XERJ — wp1107-* Prefixes\n29334 8:00p ○ chatCompletionOnce and nativeCompletion Signatures Confirmed — Request Body Built Inside chatCompletionOnce\n29335 \" ○ llama.cpp Server Grammar Field Contract — GBNF vs json_schema Mutual Exclusion and tool_calls Grammar Type\n\nAccess 87k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736424.4391704,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:05.980Z","ordinal":80392,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea3ee971d481a3ae5ca94205929947","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m continuing WP-1107 at the reference-contract check. The llama.cpp source shows the request fields in the current plan would conflict with native tool handling, so I’m checking the equivalent vLLM and Ollama paths before revising the plan and asking for another review."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793736425485,"completed_at_ms":1793736425980}}
