{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:17.824Z","ordinal":80411,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4a6c5fb2-3c0e-411a-b968-710248d92405","process_id":"38858","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '3435,3505p' server/routes.go; sed -n '132,170p' api/types.go; rg -n \"func Generate|Format.*Grammar|format.*grammar|structuredOutputs\" server/routes.go server -g '*.go' | head -50"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/xerj-references/ollama","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '3435,3505p' server/routes.go","name":"routes.go","path":"server/routes.go"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '132,170p' api/types.go","name":"types.go","path":"api/types.go"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'func Generate|Format.*Grammar|format.*grammar|structuredOutputs' server/routes.go server -g '*.go'","query":"func Generate|Format.*Grammar|format.*grammar|structuredOutputs","path":"routes.go"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\t\t\t\t\t\tres.Message.Content = toolParser.Content()\n\t\t\t\t\t\tch <- res\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tch <- res\n\t\t})\n\t\tif parserErr != nil {\n\t\t\tch <- gin.H{\"error\": parserErr.Error()}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\ts.sched.expireRunnersForRuntimeOOM(m, err)\n\t\t\tvar serr api.StatusError\n\t\t\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\n\t\t\t\tch <- gin.H{\"error\": serr.ErrorMessage, \"status\": serr.StatusCode}\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tch <- gin.H{\"error\": err.Error()}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\n\twriteChatResponse(c, req, ch)\n}\n\nfunc prepareNativeChatRequest(ctx context.Context, m *Model, r llm.LlamaServer, opts *api.Options, nativeReq llm.ChatRequest, truncate bool) (llm.ChatRequest, error) {\n\tvar err error\n\tnativeReq.Messages, err = truncateNativeChatMessages(ctx, m, r, optionsForPrompt(opts, r), nativeReq, truncate)\n\treturn nativeReq, err\n}\n\nfunc (s *Server) handleNativeChat(c *gin.Context, req api.ChatRequest, m *Model, r llm.LlamaServer, opts *api.Options, msgs []api.Message, checkpointStart, checkpointLoaded time.Time) {\n\ttruncate := req.Truncate == nil || *req.Truncate\n\tnativeReq, err := prepareNativeChatRequest(c.Request.Context(), m, r, opts, llm.ChatRequest{\n\t\tMessages:    msgs,\n\t\tTools:       req.Tools,\n\t\tFormat:      req.Format,\n\t\tOptions:     opts,\n\t\tThink:       req.Think,\n\t\tShift:       req.Shift == nil || *req.Shift,\n\t\tLogprobs:    req.Logprobs,\n\t\tTopLogprobs: req.TopLogprobs,\n\t}, truncate)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tslog.Error(\"chat template prompt error\", \"error\", err)\n\t\tvar serr api.StatusError\n\t\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\n\t\t\tc.JSON(serr.StatusCode, gin.H{\"error\": serr.ErrorMessage})\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tc.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{\"error\": err.Error()})\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif req.DebugRenderOnly {\n\t\tprompt, err := r.ApplyChatTemplate(c.Request.Context(), nativeReq)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tvar serr api.StatusError\n\t\t\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\n\t\t\t\tc.JSON(serr.StatusCode, gin.H{\"error\": serr.ErrorMessage})\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tc.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{\"error\": err.Error()})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tc.JSON(http.StatusOK, api.ChatResponse{\n\t\t\tModel:     req.Model,\n\t\t\tCreatedAt: time.Now().UTC(),\n\tTopLogprobs int `json:\"top_logprobs,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// ChatRequest describes a request sent by [Client.Chat].\ntype ChatRequest struct {\n\t// Model is the model name, as in [GenerateRequest].\n\tModel string `json:\"model\"`\n\n\t// Runner selects a runner variant from a manifest list.\n\tRunner string `json:\"runner,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Messages is the messages of the chat - can be used to keep a chat memory.\n\tMessages []Message `json:\"messages\"`\n\n\t// Stream enables streaming of returned responses; true by default.\n\tStream *bool `json:\"stream,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Format is the format to return the response in (e.g. \"json\").\n\tFormat json.RawMessage `json:\"format,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// KeepAlive controls how long the model will stay loaded into memory\n\t// following the request.\n\tKeepAlive *Duration `json:\"keep_alive,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Tools is an optional list of tools the model has access to.\n\tTools `json:\"tools,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Options lists model-specific options.\n\tOptions map[string]any `json:\"options\"`\n\n\t// Think controls whether thinking/reasoning models will think before\n\t// responding. Can be a boolean (true/false) or a model-defined thinking level.\n\tThink *ThinkValue `json:\"think,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Truncate is a boolean that, when set to true, truncates the chat history messages\n\t// if the rendered prompt exceeds the context length limit.\n\tTruncate *bool `json:\"truncate,omitempty\"`\n\n\t// Shift is a boolean that, when set to true, shifts the chat history\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":719177145}},"started_at_ms":1793736437100,"completed_at_ms":1793736437819}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:17.939Z","ordinal":80412,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-992f9bee-0b15-41e3-ab0d-263fc45ef994","process_id":"10677","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short; git log -5 --oneline --decorate; rg -n \"WP-1107|grammar matrix|WP-1106|WP-1108\" docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; git log -5 --oneline --decorate; rg -n \"WP-1107|grammar matrix|WP-1106|WP-1108\" docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n3eea888a (HEAD -> v1/v112-wp1101-integration) docs(release): qualify exact RC2 archive\ne134dcd5 fix(ceri): align provenance with release build version\nf6d474a4 docs(release): reopen exact-candidate qualification gates\n97945557 (v1/v112-wp1101-tracing) feat(tracing): trace local agent lifecycle\n5828e83c (v1/v112-wp1105-hardening) feat(eval): integrate deterministic code evaluator runner\n3:**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\n4:This record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\n6:The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\n10:The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\n14:| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions connected; PR #396 review fixes present. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n15:| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating connected. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n31:| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\n33:| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n85:- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\n86:- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":781230774}},"started_at_ms":1793736437157,"completed_at_ms":1793736437939}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:20.417Z","ordinal":80413,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a305-fa61-7283-94b3-34f5acba9cd5","call_id":"call_0859950c30b74cf0b1a1984675aa8477","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 0 {\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- v1.1.2-release: state=WP-1103/1104 full qualification completed at 789b247a; WP-1105 code evaluators integrated into runner and scorer at e2bacf1a. Ready for WP-1106 single-step loop mode., phase=scope reconciliation and owner coordination, gate=WP-1101 source candidate 97945557 full CLI suite PASS 2314/0/5; RC.2 version-only test PASS 1/1; npm build PASS; current make test on f6d474a4 started with 43 Rust core tests and CLI suite active; Rust core unit group 43 PASS, TUI group 254 in progress., next=Make qualification record explicitly separate the user's approved WP-1101–WP-1108 release scope from the current specialist roadmap; then resume dependent G1.1-4 only after GATEWAY holder clears or coordinates., friction=No current assertion failures. Existing remote GATEWAY claim remains held by a separate RC15 agent on ubuntu-desktop; avoid inference-backed benchmark until cleared., updated=2026-11-03T00:33:00Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta fresh independent review requested and running., REDACTED; final narrow update confirmation pending, retrieval=XERJ nexus-cli client.ts:1317 chatCompletion signature; agent.ts:5819 recovery submit boundary; exact local call sites reviewed; XERJ follow-up field report submitted., active_agents=Read-only audit delegated to /root/v112_unblocked_work to identify safe progress that does not load the shared test host., heartbeat=2026-11-03 13:14:51 UTC, claim=WP1101_TRACING plus cli/src/agent.ts, cli/test/agent_observer.test.ts, docs/v1.1.0/WP-1101-PLAN.md and SUITE held., candidateTree=1518780db3fbc3f2bc06312aa7bea137a67ce26d clean integrated branch; 1ecdd557 detached qualification snapshot, suite=/tmp/wp1101-full-suite-rerun.log; snapshot /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-qualification; run started after copy of current WP-1101 files and local node_modules replacement., build=npm run build PASS, cargo release builds PASS, artifactAcceptance=PASS: pinned Bookworm package archive 27dbbb8120e755061e92218eaceb5e12b7d9457230b9b0aa82b96d28cc3791ee; six benchmark tasks PASS, packageRevision=1ecdd557ebe31267c67f281b49d64605e5464777, wp1102Fix=cli/src/sidecar.ts preserves typed workspace path in session.state, applies legacy credential key/value fallback after canonical sanitizer, and emits concise sanitized startup errors; 68/68 focused tests pass., suiteLog=/tmp/v112-wp1105-exact-full-suite.log, roadmapNext=/root/roadmap_next read-only audit identifies WP-1101 tracing as next unblocked item after WP-1105; prototype branch 8a83c9e7 exists but unclaimed, inspect read-only and create new slice after finishing current suite., wp1105=DONE commits e526ba90 (WP-1102 sidecar regression) and 5828e83c (WP-1105 evaluator integration); independent review approved; full exact candidate suite green, log SHA-256 a6cb0af8fc67e710934abce01d0001366e5ac68455b4a894c86b396bf243f4a4., wp1101Spec=Second reviewer pass found one omitted ExecutionState: LIMIT_REACHED. Added OTel unset mapping and limit-reached test case to AC1; requested final confirmation from /root/review_delta. No implementation code written., wp1101Red=/tmp/wp1101-red-agent-observer.log SHA-256 cc7dd19608f3b61e746473d3944f1eca34b46d1f746fcb8e2ad9adc6ebc2f7ab; four trace expectations failed as assertions; fail-safe AC already satisfied by baseline and now guarded against recorder path failure., wp1101Focused=/tmp/wp1101-focused-green.log current SHA to capture after final run; last focused run 11/11 pass., evidence=/tmp/wp1101-final-qualified-suite-evidence.txt SHA-256 e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17, rc2Version=1.1.2-rc.2 synchronized across root, CLI, Cargo manifest and lockfiles; package version unit test PASS, candidateHead=f6d474a4, activeClaim=SUITE held for exact RC.2 make test on isolated worktree; eval workspace is dedicated 128 MB tmpfs, review=/root/review_delta APPROVED final archive evidence and qualification status. Review confirms evidence hash, archive digest, six benchmark invocations, no missing/skipped tasks, hiddenPass=false as fixture expectation, G1.1-2 boundary-only, G1.1-3 package runtime, G1.1-4 and external CI/CodeQL/publication pending., updated 25 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] Resume WP-1104 full suite and roadmap release (state=Latest exact WP-1103 AC2 full-suite qualification remains pending. Historical suite on snapshot 00a8cb4d is red 2133 pass/3 fail/2 skipped (log SHA e6ea08b2), had no process-scope postcheck, and overlapped PR396 full-suite test traffic; independent review says failures are outside WP-1103 files, but cancellation/TUI need quiet rerun and upgrade test needs reachable fixture/network. Other owner's PR396 suite PID 2050438/2050464 is verified live through 12:14 UTC in /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr396-takeover; no new tests started. Added shared conflict record. Reconciled the user-approved full-roadmap scope in dedicated branch v1/v112-scope-reconciliation commit 4b63cee0, exact-doc assertions and diff check pass, independent reviewer approved; scope file claim released. The source roadmap remains under Antigravity's DOCS_POST_V1_ROADMAP claim. No release yet., work_product=/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration, details=Continue full v1.1.2 scope. WP-1104 standalone eval source slice remains reviewed/closed at 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e. WP-1103 AC2 is implemented but uncommitted pending exact-source clean suite; current host has unclaimed PR396 suite traffic, so do not run tests. Release scope documentation is corrected in 4b63cee0 on v1/v112-scope-reconciliation (not pushed/merged); reviewer APPROVED. User has authorized full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2. Continue to owner-level exact-head CI, independent acceptance, installed-RC qualification, and release publication while preserving dirty main checkout and leaving push/tag/publish to owner.), updated about 32 hours ago\\n  - [done] WP-1104 standalone evaluator integration (commit=05c49df2, 2a94f62e, test_evidence=Full npm test: 2138 tes"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 1 {\"chunk_id\":\"a1f809\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.719179542,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":892,\"output\":\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tres.Message.Content = toolParser.Content()\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tch <- res\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tch <- res\\n\\t\\t})\\n\\t\\tif parserErr != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tch <- gin.H{\\\"error\\\": parserErr.Error()}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\ts.sched.expireRunnersForRuntimeOOM(m, err)\\n\\t\\t\\tvar serr api.StatusError\\n\\t\\t\\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tch <- gin.H{\\\"error\\\": serr.ErrorMessage, \\\"status\\\": serr.StatusCode}\\n\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tch <- gin.H{\\\"error\\\": err.Error()}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}()\\n\\n\\twriteChatResponse(c, req, ch)\\n}\\n\\nfunc prepareNativeChatRequest(ctx context.Context, m *Model, r llm.LlamaServer, opts *api.Options, nativeReq llm.ChatRequest, truncate bool) (llm.ChatRequest, error) {\\n\\tvar err error\\n\\tnativeReq.Messages, err = truncateNativeChatMessages(ctx, m, r, optionsForPrompt(opts, r), nativeReq, truncate)\\n\\treturn nativeReq, err\\n}\\n\\nfunc (s *Server) handleNativeChat(c *gin.Context, req api.ChatRequest, m *Model, r llm.LlamaServer, opts *api.Options, msgs []api.Message, checkpointStart, checkpointLoaded time.Time) {\\n\\ttruncate := req.Truncate == nil || *req.Truncate\\n\\tnativeReq, err := prepareNativeChatRequest(c.Request.Context(), m, r, opts, llm.ChatRequest{\\n\\t\\tMessages:    msgs,\\n\\t\\tTools:       req.Tools,\\n\\t\\tFormat:      req.Format,\\n\\t\\tOptions:     opts,\\n\\t\\tThink:       req.Think,\\n\\t\\tShift:       req.Shift == nil || *req.Shift,\\n\\t\\tLogprobs:    req.Logprobs,\\n\\t\\tTopLogprobs: req.TopLogprobs,\\n\\t}, truncate)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tslog.Error(\\\"chat template prompt error\\\", \\\"error\\\", err)\\n\\t\\tvar serr api.StatusError\\n\\t\\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\\n\\t\\t\\tc.JSON(serr.StatusCode, gin.H{\\\"error\\\": serr.ErrorMessage})\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tc.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{\\\"error\\\": err.Error()})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif req.DebugRenderOnly {\\n\\t\\tprompt, err := r.ApplyChatTemplate(c.Request.Context(), nativeReq)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tvar serr api.StatusError\\n\\t\\t\\tif errors.As(err, &serr) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tc.JSON(serr.StatusCode, gin.H{\\\"error\\\": serr.ErrorMessage})\\n\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tc.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{\\\"error\\\": err.Error()})\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tc.JSON(http.StatusOK, api.ChatResponse{\\n\\t\\t\\tModel:     req.Model,\\n\\t\\t\\tCreatedAt: time.Now().UTC(),\\n\\tTopLogprobs int `json:\\\"top_logprobs,omitempty\\\"`\\n}\\n\\n// ChatRequest describes a request sent by [Client.Chat].\\ntype ChatRequest struct {\\n\\t// Model is the model name, as in [GenerateRequest].\\n\\tModel string `json:\\\"model\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Runner selects a runner variant from a manifest list.\\n\\tRunner string `json:\\\"runner,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Messages is the messages of the chat - can be used to keep a chat memory.\\n\\tMessages []Message `json:\\\"messages\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Stream enables streaming of returned responses; true by default.\\n\\tStream *bool `json:\\\"stream,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Format is the format to return the response in (e.g. \\\"json\\\").\\n\\tFormat json.RawMessage `json:\\\"format,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// KeepAlive controls how long the model will stay loaded into memory\\n\\t// following the request.\\n\\tKeepAlive *Duration `json:\\\"keep_alive,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Tools is an optional list of tools the model has access to.\\n\\tTools `json:\\\"tools,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Options lists model-specific options.\\n\\tOptions map[string]any `json:\\\"options\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Think controls whether thinking/reasoning models will think before\\n\\t// responding. Can be a boolean (true/false) or a model-defined thinking level.\\n\\tThink *ThinkValue `json:\\\"think,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Truncate is a boolean that, when set to true, truncates the chat history messages\\n\\t// if the rendered prompt exceeds the context length limit.\\n\\tTruncate *bool `json:\\\"truncate,omitempty\\\"`\\n\\n\\t// Shift is a boolean that, when set to true, shifts the chat history\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 2 {\"chunk_id\":\"8c126f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.781328193,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1237,\"output\":\" M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n3eea888a (HEAD -> v1/v112-wp1101-integration) docs(release): qualify exact RC2 archive\\ne134dcd5 fix(ceri): align provenance with release build version\\nf6d474a4 docs(release): reopen exact-candidate qualification gates\\n97945557 (v1/v112-wp1101-tracing) feat(tracing): trace local agent lifecycle\\n5828e83c (v1/v112-wp1105-hardening) feat(eval): integrate deterministic code evaluator runner\\n3:**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\\n4:This record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\\n6:The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\\n10:The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\\n14:| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions connected; PR #396 review fixes present. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\\n15:| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating connected. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\\n31:| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\\n32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\\n33:| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\\n85:- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\\n86:- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","cre