{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:35.358Z","ordinal":80437,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea3f06109081a3a727f1b91cc2af81","usage":{"input_tokens":59554,"cached_input_tokens":57856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":127,"reasoning_output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":59681},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":770471680,"cached_input_tokens":765552640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1152718,"reasoning_output_tokens":525693,"total_tokens":771624398},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1632883409,"cached_input_tokens":1620715264,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2968906,"reasoning_output_tokens":1450864,"total_tokens":1635852315}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:07:35.361Z","ordinal":80438,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a306-34c1-75e1-8424-8a1be1c196c0","call_id":"call_7ae206b44adc46659946fc5367a7a87c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Full-text / keyword / structured search over a XERJ index. Proxies POST /{index}/_search. Pass `prefix` (a `xerj search --prefix` value, resolved by that command) or `index` (a name or pattern) — not both; with neither, searches `ax-*`. Pass `query` as a PLAIN STRING for the definition-first code search (ranks the file that defines a symbol above files that merely mention it — the right default for code), or as an ES query-DSL object (e.g. {\"term\":{\"status\":\"open\"}}, or a bool clause) for structured queries. Omit `query` for match_all. Optional `rerank` adds a second stage that re-judges the top hits with an external relevance model — read that argument's description before using it: it needs a provider the operator configured, and it sends document text off the machine. Optional `judge` re-judges the returned hits LOCALLY (zero tokens, nothing leaves the node) and adds a `_p_relevant` probability per hit — see that argument's description for its honest ceiling. Each hit carries `match_line` when a query term sits in the passage: the absolute 1-based source line of the best-scoring match (a tie takes the earliest line), and `match_lines` for every matched line (capped). Cite `path:match_line`. Both are omitted when no term is located or the passage start line is unknown. `start_line` remains the passage start. Pass `max_tokens` to cap the response at a token budget (never exceeded; see that argument for the tokenizer and the locator-only rule).\n\nXERJ tools proxy to a running XERJ engine (ES-compatible). Use xerj_search for retrieval — pass `query` as a plain string for definition-first code search (ranks the defining file first, returns the matching passage instead of whole files, and adds `match_line` for the source line of the match inside that passage), or as an ES q"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736455.3612845}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
