{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:12:53.534Z","ordinal":80741,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea40430ed481a3aa3674e2fdcbdfbd","status":"completed","call_id":"call_693b5196c015445d85354fd7d13eee6f","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\\n+# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\\n@@\\n-**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported local inference engine, I need registered tool arguments constrained by that engine so tool calls arrive as valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\\n+**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported inference engine, I need registered tool argument schemas passed through the provider's native constrained-tool path so tool calls arrive as schema-valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\\n@@\\n-- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp chat endpoint receives the grammar generated from the active allowlisted tool schemas. Test: `client sends llama.cpp GBNF for supported tool calls`.\\n-- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives the provider's supported JSON-schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends vLLM structured tool schema for supported tool calls`.\\n-- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\\n+- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\\n+- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\\n+- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736771.0593536}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:12:53.572Z","ordinal":80742,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-db37fc9d-f5bf-4162-9182-01472b5d747a","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@\n-# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Grammar\n+# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\n \n@@ -4,3 +4,3 @@\n \n-**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported local inference engine, I need registered tool arguments constrained by that engine so tool calls arrive as valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\n+**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported inference engine, I need registered tool argument schemas passed through the provider's native constrained-tool path so tool calls arrive as schema-valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\n \n@@ -8,5 +8,5 @@\n \n-- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp chat endpoint receives the grammar generated from the active allowlisted tool schemas. Test: `client sends llama.cpp GBNF for supported tool calls`.\n-- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives the provider's supported JSON-schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends vLLM structured tool schema for supported tool calls`.\n-- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives its supported schema-constrained tool-call request shape. Test: `client sends Ollama JSON schema format for supported tool calls`.\n+- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n+- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\n+- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n - **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793736773570,"completed_at_ms":1793736773572}}
