{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:13:00.397Z","ordinal":80748,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea404781c881a38f35b54775a30569","status":"completed","call_id":"call_fa14f8cd9d064f4c96d59f66458b345c","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented request constraint fields only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\\n-- Derive constraints from the current allowlisted tool schemas; preserve the existing request when provider kind is unknown or the endpoint/protocol does not support the field.\\n+- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented native tool-schema behavior only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\\n+- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\\n@@\\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases.\\n-- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for grammar attachment, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables constrained fields.\\n-- References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases. AC1 and AC3 are baseline-preserving regression guards; AC2 is expected to fail before implementation.\\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\\n+- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151,1120-1144`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`).\\n@@\\n-- Attach the adapter output to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling.\\n+- Attach the vLLM strict-tool adaptation to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling. Preserve the current native tool-schema request for llama.cpp and Ollama.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736775.5091937}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:13:00.427Z","ordinal":80749,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-bf50af93-5a18-4487-80f4-223aefc48210","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@\n \n-- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented request constraint fields only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\n-- Derive constraints from the current allowlisted tool schemas; preserve the existing request when provider kind is unknown or the endpoint/protocol does not support the field.\n+- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented native tool-schema behavior only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\n+- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\n - Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\n-- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases.\n-- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for grammar attachment, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables constrained fields.\n-- References to retrieve: official llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama server request implementations/docs.\n+- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases. AC1 and AC3 are baseline-preserving regression guards; AC2 is expected to fail before implementation.\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\n+- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151,1120-1144`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`).\n \n@@ -33,3 +33,3 @@\n \n-- Attach the adapter output to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling.\n+- Attach the vLLM strict-tool adaptation to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling. Preserve the current native tool-schema request for llama.cpp and Ollama.\n - Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793736780426,"completed_at_ms":1793736780427}}
