{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:13:05.001Z","ordinal":80755,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea404eb8c481a3be7148aa66a71b9a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a6af3a87bfd24fe2a5811d2039ac7e0e","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- Provider request contracts may have changed since the roadmap draft. Retrieve current primary references before implementation:\\n-  - `llama.cpp` (`https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp`) — chat-completion grammar request field and interaction with function tools.\\n-  - `vLLM` (`https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm`) — current structured-output request field and function-tool compatibility.\\n-  - `Ollama` (`https://github.com/ollama/ollama`) — current chat `format` schema and function-tool compatibility.\\n-  - `nexus-cli` XERJ prefix — exact candidate request construction and provider identification.\\n-- A provider field that constrains the whole response may conflict with native function calling; retain only combinations shown to be supported by the primary references and captured-request tests.\\n+- `llama.cpp` caller `grammar` cannot accompany native tools; its chat parser builds tool grammars from the supplied function schemas. Do not pass the generated per-tool GBNF as a top-level request field.\\n+- Ollama's `format` constrains the assistant response, while native tool calls use `tools`. Do not treat response-level JSON schema as tool-argument grammar.\\n+- vLLM's `strict: true` depends on its strict-tool parser path and server configuration. The request capture test proves serialization, while the exact installed endpoint matrix is required to prove that the chosen server configuration enforces the tool schema.\\n+- The approved plan's previous request-field assumptions are superseded by these primary-source findings; obtain fresh independent plan review before writing implementation or tests.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736782.723235}}}
