{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:12.669Z","ordinal":80833,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a30c-44bd-7541-b800-fceac7a0f29a","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-11-03 8:14pm UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Oct 21, 2026\n20703 4:57p 🔵 Post-v1 Roadmap Docs Review — REQUEST_CHANGES with 7 Findings Including Timing, Overclaims, and Node 20 EOL\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27606 1:05p 🔵 WP-1105 Depends on WP-1103; Quality Plan Defers It; Evaluator Boundary Requirement (#49) Unresolved\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29337 8:02p 🔵 Existing tool_grammar.ts Module — GBNF Generator Exists but Outputs Per-Tool Argument Schemas Only"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736852.6696646,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:13.583Z","ordinal":80834,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-05b1676e-b136-49ba-a6a7-f9af0fea9910","process_id":"7623","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '43,67p'; rg -n \"think.*tool|hybrid|<think>\" docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2 | head -50"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md","name":"ROADMAP.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'think.*tool|hybrid|<think>' docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2","query":"think.*tool|hybrid|<think>","path":"v1.1.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    43\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    44\t| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n    45\t| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n    46\t| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n    47\t| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n    48\t| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n    49\t| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n    50\t| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n    51\t| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n    52\t\n    53\t### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n    54\t\n    55\t- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n    56\t- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\n    57\t- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n    58\t- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n    59\t- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n    60\t\n    61\t### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n    62\t\n    63\tFollowing the PR #8 integration merge to `main`, Dependabot opened 27 automated dependency update pull requests (PRs #103–#129). These are triaged into 5 distinct integration batches scheduled for the v1.1.0 development cycle (deferred from v1.0.0):\n    64\t\n    65\t#### Batch 1: Core Rust Engine Runtime (Low Risk / Initial v1.1.0 Release Cycle)\n    66\tPatches to Rust core dependencies that preserve API compatibility and improve stability and performance:\n    67\t- **PR #105:** `tokio` (1.53.1 → 1.53.3 in `/core`) — Async runtime maintenance patch.\ndocs/v1.1.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:236:| 12 | Self-hosted or hybrid LangSmith deployment | Platform setup | High |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:218:thought     ::= \"<think>\" [^<]* \"</think>\"\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:232:### 7.2 Hybrid Grammar for Reasoning Models\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:233:For reasoning architectures (e.g. DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), enforcing immediate JSON emission truncates internal chain-of-thought tokens. The GBNF engine supports **hybrid grammars**: allowing an optional `<think>...</think>` block before strictly locking sampling into the tool invocation schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md:286:**Evidence.** SPEC §6.2. The existing `HybridSearchEngine` is workspace-scoped (`embeddings.ts:206-320`); nothing\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:143:  - **Hybrid CoT Grammar:** For reasoning architectures (DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), Nexus enforces a hybrid grammar: unconstrained internal reasoning within `<think>...</think>` tokens, transitioning deterministically into strict schema-constrained tool call emission.\ndocs/v1.1.0/POSITIONING.md:190:- **Nexus Solution:** High-performance Rust binary (`harness-core`), keyboard-driven Ratatui terminal UI (`nexus-tui`), and native GBNF / Outlines logit-constrained tool calling with hybrid reasoning support.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":741666560}},"started_at_ms":1793736852841,"completed_at_ms":1793736853583}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:14.825Z","ordinal":80835,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a30c-4d29-7581-851f-70c54b0ed2dd","call_id":"call_6dca1514ef7d43539a98516192faed03","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    43\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    44\t| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n    45\t| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n    46\t| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n    47\t| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n    48\t| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n    49\t| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and