{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:14.837Z","ordinal":80838,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a30c-4d34-7841-86b3-d48ffe95f705","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**APPROVED_WITH_CHANGES.** The provider-specific transport changes and identity gates are sound. Two items still need plan-level reconciliation:\n\n- Explain how passing schemas to llama.cpp’s native tool path satisfies the roadmap’s dynamic GBNF requirement, and disposition the hybrid reasoning-plus-tool grammar requirement. The full WP scope should not silently omit it.\n- AC5 counts any JSON-parseable argument as valid, even if it violates the tool schema. Record syntax validity separately from schema conformance and include schema validity in acceptance, or align the stated goal with syntax-only validation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736854.8369281,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2804}}
