{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:36.717Z","ordinal":80854,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b44adc88-4e68-46e9-a1a4-35e0259a274d","process_id":"87182","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"WP-1107|grammar|valid JSON|hybrid\" docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md; sed -n '1,140p' cli/src/core/capabilities.ts | rg -n -A28 -B3 \"HARNESS_TOOLS\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'WP-1107|grammar|valid JSON|hybrid' docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md","query":"WP-1107|grammar|valid JSON|hybrid","path":"SPEC-EVALUATION.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,140p' cli/src/core/capabilities.ts","name":"capabilities.ts","path":"cli/src/core/capabilities.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -A28 -B3 HARNESS_TOOLS","query":"HARNESS_TOOLS","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:47:| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:196:4. **`repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parsing, measuring whether model emitted valid JSON or required schema repair.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:233:For reasoning architectures (e.g. DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), enforcing immediate JSON emission truncates internal chain-of-thought tokens. The GBNF engine supports **hybrid grammars**: allowing an optional `<think>...</think>` block before strictly locking sampling into the tool invocation schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:236:- **`llama.cpp`:** Emits raw `.gbnf` syntax via the `grammar` API parameter.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:240:- **Unconstrained Fallback:** Retains heuristic regex and `repairJson` recovery when running against servers without grammar sampling support.\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":651354105}},"started_at_ms":1793736876065,"completed_at_ms":1793736876717}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:14:37.916Z","ordinal":80855,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a30c-a75c-7442-afe5-04d6124cf928","call_id":"call_f025bfc550294201860e3d08d37f7c01","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:47:| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:196:4. **`repair_rate.ts`:** Evaluates tool call parsing, measuring whether model emitted valid JSON or required schema repair.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:200:## 7. Logit-Constrained Tool Calling & GBNF Engine (WP-1107)\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:233:For reasoning architectures (e.g. DeepSeek R1, Qwen QwQ), enforcing immediate JSON emission truncates internal chain-of-thought tokens. The GBNF engine supports **hybrid grammars**: allowing an optional `<think>...</think>` block before strictly locking sampling into the tool invocation schema.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:236:- **`llama.cpp`:** Emits raw `.gbnf` syntax via the `grammar` API parameter.\ndocs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:240:- **Unconstrained Fallback:** Retains heuristic regex and `repairJson` recovery when running against servers without grammar sampling support.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736877.9164634}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
