{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:16:01.976Z","ordinal":80925,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea40fef36c81a38b61a130c8a639d4","status":"completed","call_id":"call_f357f100a93e436596539764da9d4869","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151,1120-1144`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`).\\n+- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793736958.9523509}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:16:02.005Z","ordinal":80926,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-da3b3b32-b36c-4290-9816-035f25edc23a","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -32,3 +32,3 @@\n - Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\n-- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151,1120-1144`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`).\n+- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793736962004,"completed_at_ms":1793736962005}}
