{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:17:10.932Z","ordinal":81005,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d4ee8711-dfe9-437a-aad2-e377ff10e222","process_id":"71779","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"Codex GPT-6\" --used-for \"WP-1107 v1.1.2 plan reconciliation using indexed llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama, and Nexus docs/source contracts\" --verdict \"Primary-source indexing changed the design materially: llama.cpp rejects external grammar with native tools and composes reasoning/tool schemas internally; vLLM's FunctionDefinition strict flag feeds strict tool-argument grammar and its response templates support thinking plus tool calls; Ollama keeps response format distinct from tools. XERJ found precise definition-first passages and file lines; an incremental vLLM index extension hit a stale resume plan, correctly used a new prefix/state dir to index expanded paths without destructive reindex. Lexical ranking sometimes returned unrelated code, so exact symbols and local source verification were useful.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"Codex GPT-6\" --used-for \"WP-1107 v1.1.2 plan reconciliation using indexed llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama, and Nexus docs/source contracts\" --verdict \"Primary-source indexing changed the design materially: llama.cpp rejects external grammar with native tools and composes reasoning/tool schemas internally; vLLM's FunctionDefinition strict flag feeds strict tool-argument grammar and its response templates support thinking plus tool calls; Ollama keeps response format distinct from tools. XERJ found precise definition-first passages and file lines; an incremental vLLM index extension hit a stale resume plan, correctly used a new prefix/state dir to index expanded paths without destructive reindex. Lexical ranking sometimes returned unrelated code, so exact symbols and local source verification were useful.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"Codex GPT-6\" \\\n  --used-for \"WP-1107 v1.1.2 plan reconciliation using indexed llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama, and Nexus docs/source contracts\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Primary-source indexing changed the design materially: llama.cpp rejects external grammar with native tools and composes reasoning/tool schemas internally; vLLM's FunctionDefinition strict flag feeds strict tool-argument grammar and its response templates support thinking plus tool calls; Ollama keeps response format distinct from tools. XERJ found precise definition-first passages and file lines; an incremental vLLM index extension hit a stale resume plan, correctly used a new prefix/state dir to index expanded paths without destructive reindex. Lexical ranking sometimes returned unrelated code, so exact symbols and local source verification were useful.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed.md -m \"docs(field-report): wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/wp-1107-v1-1-2-plan-reconciliation-using-indexed \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: WP-1107 v1.1.2 plan reconciliation using indexed llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama, and Nexus docs/source contracts\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-1