{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:26:37.373Z","ordinal":81365,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea4372ed6081a392e3740384911030","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0370d955183f4d2cbd9ff2e2676a0a56","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning a non-empty JSON `version` string plus the selected model in `/v1/models` (`wp1107-vllmserve` `basic.py:54-55`). A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation until that endpoint responds with the vLLM version contract. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\\n@@\\n-- Reference to retrieve: `LocalLlmClient` request construction and provider identification on the exact candidate.\\n+- Retrieved: XERJ `nexus-cli` definitions locate `LocalLlmClient.chatCompletionOnce` at `client.ts:1330`, `discoverAdvertisement` at `client.ts:1133`, and `serverKindOf` at `core/provider_capabilities.ts:75`. The source index is refreshed from committed `origin/main`; exact candidate request construction was cross-checked locally at `cli/src/client.ts:1330-1393` and discovery at `cli/src/client.ts:1133-1202` because the candidate has uncommitted work.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793737586.9286215}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:26:37.411Z","ordinal":81366,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-fc9f5770-248f-42e1-ac0d-f03fbb972fcb","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -31,3 +31,3 @@\n - Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases. AC1 and AC3 are baseline-preserving regression guards; AC2 is expected to fail before implementation.\n-- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning the provider's documented JSON version response and the selected model in `/v1/models`. A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation, even if the matrix lane is configured as vLLM. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\n+- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning a non-empty JSON `version` string plus the selected model in `/v1/models` (`wp1107-vllmserve` `basic.py:54-55`). A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation until that endpoint responds with the vLLM version contract. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\n - Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\n@@ -39,3 +39,3 @@\n - Tests: captured request-body tests for each applicable transport path, plus AC4 fallback.\n-- Reference to retrieve: `LocalLlmClient` request construction and provider identification on the exact candidate.\n+- Retrieved: XERJ `nexus-cli` definitions locate `LocalLlmClient.chatCompletionOnce` at `client.ts:1330`, `discoverAdvertisement` at `client.ts:1133`, and `serverKindOf` at `core/provider_capabilities.ts:75`. The source index is refreshed from committed `origin/main`; exact candidate request construction was cross-checked locally at `cli/src/client.ts:1330-1393` and discovery at `cli/src/client.ts:1133-1202` because the candidate has uncommitted work.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793737597410,"completed_at_ms":1793737597411}}
