:    conversion to the SDK's ``cohere.types.Citation`` happens in\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/cohere/serving.py:376:    # Request conversion: Cohere V2 -> ChatCompletionRequest\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/cohere/serving.py:517:        # symmetry with the user-message conversion.\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/cohere/serving.py:1042:    # Response conversion: ChatCompletion -> Cohere V2\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/cohere/serving.py:1155:        :class:`CohereChatMessage` so downstream response conversion can\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/cohere/serving.py:1433:    # Stream conversion: chat completion stream -> Cohere V2 SSE events\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/cli_args.py:226:    - ``full`` (default): ``vllm-<version>[-<parallelism>]-<hash8>``. Encodes\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/cli_args.py:227:      server version, non-trivial parallelism degrees (tp/pp/dp/ep), and an\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/cli_args.py:229:    - ``hash``: ``vllm-<version>-<hash8>``. Parallelism stripped.\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/startup.py:16:def log_version_and_model(lgr: Logger, version: str, model_name: str) -> None:\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/startup.py:18:        message = \"vLLM server version %s, serving model %s\"\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/startup.py:22:            \" ${o}▄▄${r} ${b}▄█${r} ${w}█     █     █ ▀▄▀ █${r}  version ${w}%s${r}\\n\"\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/startup.py:38:    lgr.info(message, version, model_name)\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/common/startup.py:134:    # changing in future versions of Python, so we should use it explicitly when\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/grpc_server.py:9:    \"unsupported in a future version. Use the corresponding function from \"\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/grpc_server.py:21:        \"will likely be unsupported in a future version. \"\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/launchers/api_server/app_state.py:42:            \"init_app_state and will be required in a future version. \"\nHEAD:vllm/entrypoints/launchers/app.py:27:            \"build_app and will be required in a future ver