{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:29:16.824Z","ordinal":81421,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a31a-1098-7903-bd75-a995a92684be","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...794 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 8:29pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (19,369t read) | 143,764t work | 87% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2150 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate Blocked by Two External PR396 Test Streams (Nov 2, 1:35 PM)\nS2151 v1.1.2 Release — Goal Formally Blocked by Shared Test Host Contention, Awaiting External Test Stream Clearance (Nov 2, 1:45 PM)\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29318 7:53p ○ docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md Documents Exact Provider API Endpoints Used for Server Kind Detection\n29320 \" ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md — Evidence Schema Refined with Detached SHA-256 Sidecar Pattern\n29321 \" ○ Provider Version Endpoints Confirmed — Ollama /api/version, vLLM /version, llama.cpp /props Available\n29322 \" ○ Provider API Schema Research — Ollama, vLLM, and OpenAI Compatibility Details\n29323 7:54p ○ LocalLlmClient Server Discovery Architecture — discoverAdvertisement and discoverServerContext Flow\n29324 \" ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md Updated — Provider Identity Contract Tightened for Grammar Field Injection\n29326 7:55p ✓ WP-1107-PLAN.md AC4 Expanded with Provider Identity Handshake Tests\n29327 \" ○ LocalLlmClient Provider Discovery Architecture — discoverAdvertisement and serverKindOf Flow\n29328 7:56p ○ Exact Line Numbers for WP-1107 Integration Points in client.ts and provider_capabilities.ts\n29329 \" ○ provider_capabilities.ts Full Export Surface and chatCompletion Delegation Chain\n29330 \" ✓ WP-1107 File Claims Acquired — 5 of 7 Files Now Held\n29331 7:57p ✓ WP-1107 Remaining File Claims Acquired — All 7 Files Now Held\n29332 \" ✓ Provider Reference Repositories Cloned to /home/mike/xerj-references\n29333 7:59p ✓ Provider Reference Repositories Being Indexed into XERJ — wp1107-* Prefixes\n29334 8:00p ○ chatCompletionOnce and nativeCompletion Signatures Confirmed — Request Body Built Inside chatCompletionOnce\n29335 \" ○ llama.cpp Server Grammar Field Contract — GBNF vs json_schema Mutual Exclusion and tool_calls Grammar Type\n29336 \" ○ llama.cpp Critical Constraint — Custom Grammar Field Rejected When tools Array Is Present\n29337 8:02p ○ Existing tool_grammar.ts Module — GBNF Generator Exists but Outputs Per-Tool Argument Schemas Only\n29338 \" ○ llama.cpp Sparse Checkout Includes common/ Directory — json_schema and tools Are Internally Compatible via Chat Session\n29339 8:03p ○ llama.cpp Internal Grammar Build — Tool Grammar Derived from Tool Schemas by Server, Not Client-Supplied GBNF\n29340 \" ⚖ WP-1107 Plan Invalidated by llama.cpp Source — RED Phase Halted Pending Spec Revision\n29341 8:04p ✓ vLLM Reference Repository Indexed — 1857 Documents in wp1107-vllm-docs\n29342 \" ○ vLLM Structured Output Architecture — response_format and StructuredOutputsParams, No guided_json Field\n29343 \" ○ vLLM Structured Outputs and Tools Are Mutually Exclusive at Protocol Level\n29344 \" ○ vLLM Responses API Explicitly Rejects Grammar-Format Custom Tools\n29345 \" ○ vLLM VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING Env Var Controls Structural-Tag Parameter Schema Enforcement\n29346 \" ○ vLLM ChatCompletionToolsParam Has defer_loading Field on Both Tool and Function\n29347 8:05p ○ vLLM tool_strict_level Parameter Passed to Parser Engine in Both Chat and Responses Serving\n29348 \" ○ vLLM FunctionDefinition Imported from External Package, Not Defined in vLLM\n29349 \" ○ vLLM FunctionDefinition Defined in vllm.entrypoints.generate.base.protocol, Not openai Package\n29350 8:06p ○ llama.cpp Grammar Build Logic — include_grammar Determined by json_schema or tool_choice\n29351 \" ○ llama.cpp Server Rejects tools + grammar Simultaneously — Critical WP-1107 Constraint Confirmed in Server Code\n29352 \" ○ Ollama API ChatRequest Format Field Is json.RawMessage — Accepts Both \"json\" String and JSON Schema Object\n29353 \" ○ Ollama ChatRequest Full Field Set and Native Chat Path — Format and Tools Both Passed Through\n29354 8:07p ○ WP-1107 Work State — RETRIEVE Phase with Plan Invalidation, Awaiting Revised Plan Approval\n29355 \" ○ WP-1107-PLAN.md Full Spec Read — Provider Identity Contracts and Request Field Mapping\n29356 \" ○ Qualification Record Confirms WP-1107 INCOMPLETE — RC2 Artifact Is Historical Evidence Only\n29357 \" ○ WP-1107 Plan Approved by review_delta — Ready for RED Phase After Spec Revision\n29358 \" ○ vLLM ResponsesRequest Has structured_outputs Field Directly — Not via response_format\n29359 8:08p ○ Ollama Format Field Passed Through at Four routes.go Call Sites — No Grammar/Format Mutual Exclusion in Go Layer\n29360 \" ○ vLLM tool_parsers Directory Does Not Exist — Parser Modules Are in entrypoints/openai/parser/\n29361 \" ○ vLLM entrypoints/openai Directory Structure — Six Subdirectories Including parser/ and decisions/\n29362 \" ○ vLLM tool_strict_level Passed to ParserManager.get_parser — Server-Level Configuration, Not Per-Request\n29363 8:09p ○ Ollama ChatRequest OpenAPI Schema — format Field Is oneOf String or Object\n29364 \" ○ Ollama Structured Outputs and Tool Calls Are Documented as Independent Features — No Mutual Exclusion Found\n29365 \" ○ Ollama server/routes.go — handleNativeChat and prepareNativeChatRequest Are Distinct Functions\n29366 \" ○ vLLM sampling_params.py — STRUCTURAL_TAG_WRAPPER_NESTING Constant Caps Tool-Call Tag Nesting at 15 Levels\n29367 \" ○ WP-1107 Work State — RETRIEVE Phase with Completed RC2 Qualification and Plan Awaiting Final Verdict\n29368 \" ○ vLLM ChatCompletionToolsParam Has defer_loading Field — Propagated to FunctionDefinition via model_validator\n29369 \" ○ vLLM Chat Completion Validator Rejects structural_tag + n>1 and Triggers validate_structural_tag_response_format\n\nAccess 144k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793737756.824737,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:29:19.550Z","ordinal":81422,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea441e5ee881a392cab3a39297290e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ll resume WP-1107 in the isolated worktree, finish the provider identity/request adaptation, then run the focused tests and update the release work state. The live provider inference gate remains reserved, so I’ll keep that evidence clearly open."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793737758450,"completed_at_ms":1793737759550}}
