{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:31:05.609Z","ordinal":81523,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3a1f0552-faae-4a95-9dd2-34dd7a178a2f","process_id":"92677","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,260p' cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts; sed -n '120,300p' eval/package_runtime.test.mjs; rg -n \"toolCallSyntax|raw.*arguments|tool_calls\" cli/src/agent.ts | head -60; rg -n \"tool_grammar|allowlist\" docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts","name":"tool_grammar.ts","path":"cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '120,300p' eval/package_runtime.test.mjs","name":"package_runtime.test.mjs","path":"eval/package_runtime.test.mjs"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'toolCallSyntax|raw.*arguments|tool_calls' cli/src/agent.ts","query":"toolCallSyntax|raw.*arguments|tool_calls","path":"agent.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'tool_grammar|allowlist' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts","query":"tool_grammar|allowlist","path":"WP-1107-PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"import { HARNESS_TOOLS } from \"./capabilities.js\";\nimport type { ToolDefinition } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/** The v1.1.0 GBNF pilot is intentionally limited to these registered tools. */\nexport const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\nexport type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\n\nconst ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\nconst MAX_PROPERTIES = 8;\n\n/** Compile the exact parameter schema registered for one allowlisted tool. Unknown JSON Schema forms fail closed. */\nexport function generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\n  toolName: GbnfToolName,\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): string {\n  if (!ALLOWED_NAMES.has(toolName)) throw new Error(`GBNF is not enabled for tool ${String(toolName)}`);\n  if (!Array.isArray(registeredTools)) throw new Error(\"registered tool definitions must be an array\");\n\n  const matches = registeredTools.filter((tool) => (tool as ToolDefinition | undefined)?.function?.name === toolName);\n  if (matches.length !== 1) {\n    throw new Error(`expected exactly one registered schema for ${toolName}; found ${matches.length}`);\n  }\n  const definition = matches[0] as ToolDefinition;\n  if (definition.type !== \"function\" || !definition.function || definition.function.name !== toolName) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} is not a function tool`);\n  }\n  const parameters = definition.function.parameters as unknown;\n  if (!parameters || typeof parameters !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(parameters)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define an object parameter schema`);\n  }\n\n  const schema = parameters as Record<string, unknown>;\n  rejectUnknownKeys(schema, new Set([\"type\", \"properties\", \"required\"]), `${toolName} parameter schema`);\n  if (schema.type !== \"object\") throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must have type object`);\n  if (!schema.properties || typeof schema.properties !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(schema.properties)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define flat properties`);\n  }\n\n  const propertyMap = schema.properties as Record<string, unknown>;\n  const propertyNames = Object.keys(propertyMap);\n  if (propertyNames.length > MAX_PROPERTIES) throw new Error(`${toolName} schema exceeds the ${MAX_PROPERTIES}-property GBNF bound`);\n  const required = schema.required === undefined ? [] : schema.required;\n  if (!Array.isArray(required) || required.some((name) => typeof name !== \"string\")) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} has an invalid required list`);\n  }\n  if (new Set(required).size !== required.length) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} repeats a required property`);\n  for (const name of required) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(propertyMap, name)) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} requires undeclared property ${name}`);\n  }\n\n  const properties = propertyNames.map((name, index) => {\n    const raw = propertyMap[name];\n    if (!raw || typeof raw !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(raw)) {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} must be a flat schema object`);\n    }\n    const property = raw as Record<string, unknown>;\n    const valueRule = property.type === \"string\" ? \"json-string\"\n      : property.type === \"number\" ? \"json-number\"\n        : property.type === \"boolean\" ? \"json-boolean\"\n          : undefined;\n    if (!valueRule) throw new Error(`unsupported JSON Schema type for ${toolName}.${name}`);\n    rejectUnknownKeys(property, new Set([\"type\", \"description\"]), `${toolName}.${name} schema`);\n    if (typeof property.description !== \"undefined\" && typeof property.description !== \"string\") {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} has an invalid description`);\n    }\n    return { name, index, valueRule };\n  });\n\n  const propertyIndex = new Map(properties.map(({ name, index }) => [name, index]));\n  const requiredMask = required.reduce((mask: number, name: string) => mask | (1 << propertyIndex.get(name)!), 0);\n  const stateCount = 1 << properties.length;\n  const rules = [\n    \"root ::= ws \\\"{\\\" ws object-fields ws \\\"}\\\" ws\",\n    \"json-string ::= \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\" json-char* \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n    String.raw`json-char ::= [^\"\\\\\\x00-\\x1f] | \"\\\\\" ([\"\\\\/bfnrt] | \"u\" [0-9a-fA-F]{4})`,\n    String.raw`json-number ::= \"-\"? (\"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*) (\".\" [0-9]+)? ([eE] [-+]? [0-9]+)?`,\n    \"json-boolean ::= \\\"true\\\" | \\\"false\\\"\",\n    \"ws ::= [ \\\\t\\\\n\\\\r]*\",\n    ...properties.map(({ name, index, valueRule }) => `member_${index} ::= ${JSON.stringify(name)} ws \":\" ws ${valueRule}`),\n  ];\n\n  const firstChoices = properties.map(({ index }) => `member_${index} fields_tail_${1 << index}`);\n  rules.push(`object-fields ::= ${requiredMask === 0 ? '\"\" | ' : \"\"}${firstChoices.length ? firstChoices.join(\" | \") : '\"\"'}`);\n  for (let mask = 0; mask < stateCount; mask++) {\n    const choices: string[] = [];\n    if ((mask & requiredMask) === requiredMask) choices.push('\"\"');\n    for (const { index } of properties) {\n      const bit = 1 << index;\n      if ((mask & bit) === 0) choices.push(`\",\" ws member_${index} fields_tail_${mask | bit}`);\n    }\n    // Only reachable states need a rule, but emitting all bounded masks keeps output deterministic and simple.\n    rules.push(`fields_tail_${mask} ::= ${choices.join(\" | \") || '\"\"'}`);\n  }\n  return rules.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\n/** Compile each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\nexport function generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars(\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): Readonly<Record<GbnfToolName, string>> {\n  const result = {} as Record<GbnfToolName, string>;\n  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction rejectUnknownKeys(value: Record<string, unknown>, allowed: ReadonlySet<string>, label: string): void {\n  const unknown = Object.keys(value).find((key) => !allowed.has(key));\n  if (unknown) throw new Error(`${label} contains unsupported schema keyword ${unknown}`);\n}\n  let timer;\n  try {\n    const status = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      timer = setTimeout(() => child.kill(\"SIGTERM\"), 165_000);\n      child.once(\"error\", reject);\n      child.once(\"close\", resolve);\n    });\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    assert.equal(status, 0, `${stdout}\\n${stderr}`);\n    const artifactDir = `${outputPath}.artifacts`;\n    const resultRecords = fs.readFileSync(path.join(artifactDir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"utf8\")\n      .split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n    const score = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(artifactDir, \"score.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    assert.equal(resultRecords.length, expectedIds.length, \"every benchmark task must produce one invocation record\");\n    assert.equal(requests.length, expectedIds.length, \"every benchmark task must reach the captured local provider once\");\n    assert.deepEqual(resultRecords.map((record) => record.task).sort(), expectedIds);\n    assert.deepEqual(score.rows.map((row) => row.task).sort(), expectedIds);\n    assert.equal(score.totals.runs, expectedIds.length);\n    const requestText = (request) => (request.messages ?? []).map((message) =>\n      typeof message.content === \"string\" ? message.content : JSON.stringify(message.content)).join(\"\\n\");\n    const captured = requests.map(requestText);\n    const requestIndexByTask = new Map();\n    for (const example of benchmark) {\n      const requestIndex = captured.findIndex((messages) => messages.includes(example.objective));\n      assert.notEqual(requestIndex, -1, `captured candidate request is missing ${example.id}`);\n      requestIndexByTask.set(example.id, requestIndex);\n      const request = captured[requestIndex];\n      const oracle = oracleById.get(example.id);\n      assert.ok(oracle?.hidden?.command, `hidden validator is missing for ${example.id}`);\n      assert.equal(request.includes(`${oracle.hidden.dir}/`), false, `relative hidden oracle path leaked to candidate request for ${example.id}`);\n      assert.equal(request.includes(oracle.hidden.command), false, `hidden validator command leaked to candidate request for ${example.id}`);\n    }\n    const resultByTask = new Map(resultRecords.map((record) => [record.task, record]));\n    const scoreByTask = new Map(score.rows.map((row) => [row.task, row]));\n    const sha256File = (file) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n    const evidence = {\n      schemaVersion: 1,\n      candidate: {\n        packageArchiveSha256,\n        launcherSha256: sha256File(launcher),\n        cliBundleSha256: sha256File(path.join(packageRoot, \"lib\", \"cli\", \"dist\", \"index.js\")),\n        coreBinarySha256: sha256File(path.join(packageRoot, \"lib\", \"core\", \"harness-core\")),\n      },\n      dataset: { name: manifest.name, version: manifest.version, split: \"benchmark\", manifestSha256, manifestSha256Source: \"recomputed from final integrated eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\" },\n      provider: { kind: \"loopback-deterministic-fake\", capturedRequests: requests.length },\n      expectedTaskIds: expectedIds,\n      missingTaskIds: [],\n      skippedTaskIds: [],\n      results: expectedIds.map((taskId) => {\n        const record = resultByTask.get(taskId);\n        const scored = scoreByTask.get(taskId);\n        return {\n          taskId,\n          invocations: 1,\n          requestSha256: createHash(\"sha256\").update(JSON.stringify(requests[requestIndexByTask.get(taskId)])).digest(\"hex\"),\n          validatorResult: { hiddenPass: record.hiddenPass, regressionPass: record.regressionPass, exitCode: record.exitCode, timedOut: record.timedOut },\n          scorerResult: { claimed: scored.claimed, correct: scored.correct, errors: scored.errors, regressions: scored.regressions },\n        };\n      }),\n    };\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(evidencePath), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(evidencePath, `${JSON.stringify(evidence, null, 2)}\\n`, { mode: 0o600, flag: \"wx\" });\n  } finally {\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    if (child.exitCode === null) child.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n    await new Promise((resolve) => server.close(resolve));\n    fs.rmSync(outside, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    fs.rmSync(installRoot, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n\n  assert.ok(fs.existsSync(evidencePath), `acceptance evidence is missing: ${evidencePath}`);\n  const evidence = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(evidencePath, \"utf8\"));\n  assert.equal(evidence.dataset.name, manifest.name);\n  assert.equal(evidence.dataset.version, manifest.version);\n  assert.equal(evidence.dataset.split, \"benchmark\");\n  assert.equal(evidence.dataset.manifestSha256, createHash(\"sha256\").update(manifestBytes).digest(\"hex\"));\n  assert.equal(evidence.dataset.manifestSha256Source, \"recomputed from final integrated eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\");\n  for (const digest of [evidence.candidate.packageArchiveSha256, evidence.candidate.launcherSha256, evidence.candidate.cliBundleSha256, evidence.candidate.coreBinarySha256]) {\n    assert.match(digest, /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/);\n  }\n  assert.deepEqual([...evidence.expectedTaskIds].sort(), expectedIds);\n  assert.equal(evidence.provider.kind, \"loopback-deterministic-fake\");\n  assert.equal(evidence.provider.capturedRequests, expectedIds.length);\n  assert.deepEqual(evidence.missingTaskIds, []);\n  assert.deepEqual(evidence.skippedTaskIds, []);\n  assert.equal(evidence.results.length, expectedIds.length);\n  assert.deepEqual(evidence.results.map((result) => result.taskId).sort(), expectedIds);\n  for (const result of evidence.results) {\n    assert.equal(result.invocations, 1, result.taskId);\n    assert.ok(result.validatorResult && typeof result.validatorResult === \"object\", result.taskId);\n    assert.ok(result.scorerResult && typeof result.scorerResult === \"object\", result.taskId);\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files\", () => {\n  assert.deepEqual(EVAL_RUNTIME_FILES, expectedRuntimeFiles);\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-runtime-package-\"));\n  const source = path.join(root, \"source\");\n  const packageRoot = path.join(root, \"package\");\n  try {\n    for (const file of expectedRuntimeFiles) {\n      const sourceFile = path.join(source, file);\n      fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(sourceFile), { recursive: true });\n      fs.writeFileSync(sourceFile, `runtime:${file}\\n`);\n    }\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"datasets\", \"core-v1\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"datasets\", \"core-v1\", \"oracles.jsonl\"), \"secret oracle\\n\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"tasks\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"tasks\", \"held-out.json\"), \"held-out\\n\");\n\n    stageEvaluatorRuntime(source, packageRoot);\n\n    for (const file of expectedRuntimeFiles) {\n      assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(packageRoot, file), \"utf8\"), `runtime:${file}\\n`, file);\n    }\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(packageRoot, \"eval\", \"datasets\")), false);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(packageRoot, \"eval\", \"tasks\")), false);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"evaluator runtime staging fails when an allowlisted module is missing\", () => {\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-runtime-missing-\"));\n  try {\n    assert.throws(() => stageEvaluatorRuntime(root, path.join(root, \"package\")), /required evaluator runtime module is missing/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout\", { skip: process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT ? false : \"set NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT to a freshly built package\" }, async () => {\n  const packageRoot = fs.realpathSync(process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT);\n  const sourceRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n  assert.equal(packageRoot === sourceRoot || packageRoot.startsWith(`${sourceRoot}${path.sep}`), false, \"package must be staged outside the source checkout\");\n  const outside = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-installed-eval-smoke-\"));\n  const dataset = path.join(outside, \"dataset\");\n  const outputDir = path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\");\n  fs.mkdirSync(dataset);\n  try {\n    const examples = \"\";\n    const oracles = \"\";\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"examples.jsonl\"), examples);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"oracles.jsonl\"), oracles);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"manifest.json\"), `${JSON.stringify({\n      schemaVersion: 1,\n      name: \"empty-package-smoke\",\n      version: \"1.0.0\",\n      domains: [],\n      splits: { regression: { count: 0 }, benchmark: { count: 0 } },\n      files: {\n        \"examples.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(examples).digest(\"hex\"),\n        \"oracles.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(oracles).digest(\"hex\"),\n      },\n      tasks: {},\n    }, null, 2)}\\n`);\n\n    const launcher = path.join(packageRoot, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    const help = spawnSync(launcher, [\"eval\", \"--help\"], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: outside, NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    });\n    assert.equal(help.status, 0, `${help.stdout}${help.stderr}`);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--dataset <path>/);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--split <name>/);\n\n    const evalRun = spawnSync(launcher, [\n      \"eval\", \"--dataset\", dataset, \"--split\", \"benchmark\", \"--runs\", \"1\", \"--output\", path.join(outside, \"score.json\"),\n    ], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: {\n        PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\",\n        HOME: outside,\n        NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot,\n        LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT: \"http://127.0.0.1:1/v1\",\n        LOCAL_LLM_MODEL: \"package-smoke\",\n      },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n448:      for (const call of message.tool_calls ?? []) {\n2295:      if (this.messages[i].role === \"assistant\" && this.messages[i].tool_calls?.length) {\n2301:    const calls = this.messages[last].tool_calls!;\n2676:      if (m.role === \"assistant\") for (const c of (m as any).tool_calls ?? []) if (typeof c?.id === \"string\") used.add(c.id);\n3097:      if (message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls) {\n3098:        for (const call of message.tool_calls) {\n3157:      if (message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls) {\n3158:        for (const call of message.tool_calls) {\n3160:          const rawArgs = call?.function?.arguments;\n3421:    if (lastAssistant < 0 || !source[lastAssistant].tool_calls?.length) return [];\n3434:      .map((message, index) => message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls?.length ? index : -1)\n3538:        for (const call of message.tool_calls ?? []) {\n3919:      if (m.role !== \"assistant\" || !m.tool_calls?.length) continue;\n3921:      return m.tool_calls.filter((call) => !results.has(call.id)).map((call) => call.id);\n4857:          args = value && typeof value === \"object\" ? value : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n4860:          args = toolName === \"task_completed\" ? {} : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n4863:        args = toolName === \"task_completed\" ? {} : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n6099:        this.addToolCallSyntax(parsed.toolCallSyntax);\n6114:          countTokens(JSON.stringify(assistantMessage.tool_calls || []));\n6134:        // message is dropped so the history never holds tool_calls without tool results.\n6146:          ...(parsed.toolCalls.length > 0 ? { tool_calls: parsed.toolCalls } : {}),\n6574:      ...(Object.values(this.turnToolCallSyntax).some((n) => n > 0) ? { toolCallSyntax: { ...this.turnToolCallSyntax } } : {}),\n6962:        countTokens(JSON.stringify(assistantMessage.tool_calls || []));\n6972:      this.addToolCallSyntax(parsed.toolCallSyntax);\n6977:        ...(parsed.toolCalls.length > 0 ? { tool_calls: parsed.toolCalls } : {}),\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:5:export const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:6:export type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:8:const ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:11:/** Compile the exact parameter schema registered for one allowlisted tool. Unknown JSON Schema forms fail closed. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:97:/** Compile each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:102:  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:9:- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:10:- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:11:- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:16:**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:22:**Roadmap contract reconciliation:** Keep the existing dynamic GBNF compiler and its allowlist/schema tests as the deterministic schema-to-grammar implementation. Provider transport must use each server's compatible native tool path: llama.cpp rejects a caller grammar beside native tools but builds a dynamic tool grammar from their schemas; vLLM consumes `strict: true` through its structural-tag tool parser; Ollama carries tool schemas in `tools`, separately from response-level `format`. The hybrid `<think>...</think>` + tool-call requirement is not dropped: AC6 and the live matrix require a reasoning-plus-tool attempt on each exact endpoint. The provider's model/template/parser must build or accept that hybrid grammar; any endpoint that cannot pass AC6 remains unsupported and blocks G1.1-4. Do not claim that successful JSON syntax alone satisfies schema validity.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:29:- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:30:- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:38:- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:45:- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:47:- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Each provider's pinned configuration must use a reasoning-capable model/template/parser; 20 attempts (five for each tool) must exercise the hybrid reasoning/tool path. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no provider-specific adaptation.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":751040269}},"started_at_ms":1793737864857,"completed_at_ms":1793737865609}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:31:07.662Z","ordinal":81524,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a31b-c18e-7401-b5f9-599ad0836799","call_id":"call_5d99229f5f65438dbc77107fb31b232c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6020)\nTotal output lines: 332\n\nimport { HARNESS_TOOLS } from \"./capabilities.js\";\nimport type { ToolDefinition } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/** The v1.1.0 GBNF pilot is intentionally limited to these registered tools. */\nexport const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\nexport type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\n\nconst ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\nconst MAX_PROPERTIES = 8;\n\n/** Compile the exact parameter schema registered for one allowlisted tool. Unknown JSON Schema forms fail closed. */\nexport function generateToolArgumentsGbnf(\n  toolName: GbnfToolName,\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): string {\n  if (!ALLOWED_NAMES.has(toolName)) throw new Error(`GBNF is not enabled for tool ${String(toolName)}`);\n  if (!Array.isArray(registeredTools)) throw new Error(\"registered tool definitions must be an array\");\n\n  const matches = registeredTools.filter((tool) => (tool as ToolDefinition | undefined)?.function?.name === toolName);\n  if (matches.length !== 1) {\n    throw new Error(`expected exactly one registered schema for ${toolName}; found ${matches.length}`);\n  }\n  const definition = matches[0] as ToolDefinition;\n  if (definition.type !== \"function\" || !definition.function || definition.function.name !== toolName) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} is not a function tool`);\n  }\n  const parameters = definition.function.parameters as unknown;\n  if (!parameters || typeof parameters !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(parameters)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define an object parameter schema`);\n  }\n\n  const schema = parameters as Record<string, unknown>;\n  rejectUnknownKeys(schema, new Set([\"type\", \"properties\", \"required\"]), `${toolName} parameter schema`);\n  if (schema.type !== \"object\") throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must have type object`);\n  if (!schema.properties || typeof schema.properties !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(schema.properties)) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} must define flat properties`);\n  }\n\n  const propertyMap = schema.properties as Record<string, unknown>;\n  const propertyNames = Object.keys(propertyMap);\n  if (propertyNames.length > MAX_PROPERTIES) throw new Error(`${toolName} schema exceeds the ${MAX_PROPERTIES}-property GBNF bound`);\n  const required = schema.required === undefined ? [] : schema.required;\n  if (!Array.isArray(required) || required.some((name) => typeof name !== \"string\")) {\n    throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} has an invalid required list`);\n  }\n  if (new Set(required).size !== required.length) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} repeats a required property`);\n  for (const name of required) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(propertyMap, name)) throw new Error(`registered schema for ${toolName} requires undeclared property ${name}`);\n  }\n\n  const properties = propertyNames.map((name, index) => {\n    const raw = propertyMap[name];\n    if (!raw || typeof raw !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(raw)) {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} must be a flat schema object`);\n    }\n    const property = raw as Record<string, unknown>;\n    const valueRule = property.type === \"string\" ? \"json-string\"\n      : property.type === \"number\" ? \"json-number\"\n        : property.type === \"boolean\" ? \"json-boolean\"\n          : undefined;\n    if (!valueRule) throw new Error(`unsupported JSON Schema type for ${toolName}.${name}`);\n    rejectUnknownKeys(property, new Set([\"type\", \"description\"]), `${toolName}.${name} schema`);\n    if (typeof property.description !== \"undefined\" && typeof property.description !== \"string\") {\n      throw new Error(`registered property ${toolName}.${name} has an invalid description`);\n    }\n    return { name, index, valueRule };\n  });\n\n  const propertyIndex = new Map(properties.map(({ name, index }) => [name, index]));\n  const requiredMask = required.reduce((mask: number, name: string) => mask | (1 << propertyIndex.get(name)!), 0);\n  const stateCount = 1 << properties.length;\n  const rules = [\n    \"root ::= ws \\\"{\\\" ws object-fields ws \\\"}\\\" ws\",\n    \"json-string ::= \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\" json-char* \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n    String.raw`json-char ::= [^\"\\\\\\x00-\\x1f] | \"\\\\\" ([\"\\\\/bfnrt] | \"u\" [0-9a-fA-F]{4})`,\n    String.raw`json-number ::= \"-\"? (\"0\" | [1-9] [0-9]*) (\".\" [0-9]+)? ([eE] [-+]? [0-9]+)?`,\n    \"json-boolean ::= \\\"true\\\" | \\\"false\\\"\",\n    \"ws ::= [ \\\\t\\\\n\\\\r]*\",\n    ...properties.map(({ name, index, valueRule }) => `member_${index} ::= ${JSON.stringify(name)} ws \":\" ws ${valueRule}`),\n  ];\n\n  const firstChoices = properties.map(({ index }) => `member_${index} fields_tail_${1 << index}`);\n  rules.push(`object-fields ::= ${requiredMask === 0 ? '\"\" | ' : \"\"}${firstChoices.length ? firstChoices.join(\" | \") : '\"\"'}`);\n  for (let mask = 0; mask < stateCount; mask++) {\n    const choices: string[] = [];\n    if ((mask & requiredMask) === requiredMask) choices.push('\"\"');\n    for (const { index } of properties) {\n      const bit = 1 << index;\n      if ((mask & bit) === 0) choices.push(`\",\" ws member_${index} fields_tail_${mask | bit}`);\n    }\n    // Only reachable states need a rule, but emitting all bounded masks keeps output deterministic and simple.\n    rules.push(`fields_tail_${mask} ::= ${choices.join(\" | \") || '\"\"'}`);\n  }\n  return rules.join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\n/** Compile each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\nexport function generateRegisteredToolArgumentGrammars(\n  registeredTools: readonly ToolDefinition[] = HARNESS_TOOLS,\n): Readonly<Record<GbnfToolName, string>> {\n  const result = {} as Record<GbnfToolName, string>;\n  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction rejectUnknownKeys(value: Record<string, unknown>, allowed: ReadonlySet<string>, label: string): void {\n  const unknown = Object.keys(value).find((key) => !allowed.has(key));\n  if (unknown) throw new Error(`${label} contains unsupported schema keyword ${unknown}`);\n}\n  let timer;\n  try {\n    const status = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      timer = setTimeout(() => child.kill(\"SIGTERM\"), 165_000);\n      child.once(\"error\", reject);\n      child.once(\"close\", resolve);\n    });\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    assert.equal(status, 0, `${stdout}\\n${stderr}`);\n    const artifactDir = `${outputPath}.artifacts`;\n    const resultRecords = fs.readFileSync(path.join(artifactDir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"utf8\")\n      .split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean).map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n    const score = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(artifactDir, \"score.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    assert.equal(resultRecords.length, expectedIds.length, \"every benchmark task must produce one invocation record\");\n    assert.equal(requests.length, expectedIds.length, \"every benchmark task must reach the captured local provider once\");\n    assert.deepEqual(resultRecords.map((record) => record.task).sort(), expectedIds);\n    assert.deepEqual(score.rows.map((row) => row.task).sort(), expectedIds);\n    assert.equal(score.totals.runs, expectedIds.length);\n    const requestText = (request) => (request.messages ?? []).map((message) =>\n      typeof message.content === \"string\" ? message.content : JSON.stringify(message.content)).join(\"\\n\");\n    const captured = requests.map(requestText);\n    const requestIndexByTask = new Map();\n    for (const example of benchmark) {\n      const requestIndex = captured.findIndex((messages) => messages.includes(example.objective));\n      assert.notEqual(requestIndex, -1, `captured candidate request is missing ${example.id}`);\n      requestIndexByTask.set(example.id, requestIndex);\n      const request = captured[requestIndex];\n      const oracle = oracleById.get(example.id);\n      assert.ok(oracle?.hidden?.command, `hidden validator is missing for ${example.id}`);\n      assert.equal(request.includes(`${oracle.hidden.dir}/`), false, `relative hidden oracle path leaked to candidate request for ${example.id}`);\n      assert.equal(request.includes(oracle.hidden.command), false, `hidden validator command leaked to candidate request for ${example.id}`);\n    }\n    const resultByTask = new Map(resultRecords.map((record) => [record.task, record]));\n    const scoreByTask = new Map(score.rows.map((row) => [row.task, row]));\n    const sha256File = (file) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest(\"hex\");\n    const evidence = {\n      schemaVersion: 1,\n      candidate: {\n        packageArchiveSha256,\n        launcherSha256: sha256File(launcher),\n        cliBundleSha256: sha256File(path.join(packageRoot, \"lib\", \"cli\", \"dist\", \"index.js\")),\n        coreBinarySha256: sha256File(path.join(packageRoot, \"lib\", \"core\", \"harness-core\")),\n      },\n      dataset: { name: manifest.name, version: manifest.version, split: \"benchmark\", manifestSha256, manifestSha256Source: \"recomputed from final integrated eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\" },\n      provider: { kind: \"loopback-deterministic-fake\", capturedRequests: requests.length },\n      expectedTaskIds: expectedIds,\n      missingTaskIds: [],\n      skippedTaskIds: [],\n      results: expectedIds.map((taskId) => {\n        const record = resultByTask.get(taskId);\n        const scored = scoreByTask.get(taskId);\n        return {\n          taskId,\n          invocations: 1,\n          requestSha256: createHash(\"sha256\").update(JSON.stringify(requests[requestIndexByTask.get(taskId)])).digest(\"hex\"),\n          validatorResult: { hiddenPass: record.hiddenPass, regressionPass: record.regressionPass, exitCode: record.exitCode, timedOut: record.timedOut },\n          scorerResult: { claimed: scored.claimed, correct: scored.correct, errors: scored.errors, regressions: scored.regressions },\n        };\n      }),\n    };\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(evidencePath), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(evidencePath, `${JSO…1020 tokens truncated…, \"package must be staged outside the source checkout\");\n  const outside = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-installed-eval-smoke-\"));\n  const dataset = path.join(outside, \"dataset\");\n  const outputDir = path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\");\n  fs.mkdirSync(dataset);\n  try {\n    const examples = \"\";\n    const oracles = \"\";\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"examples.jsonl\"), examples);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"oracles.jsonl\"), oracles);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"manifest.json\"), `${JSON.stringify({\n      schemaVersion: 1,\n      name: \"empty-package-smoke\",\n      version: \"1.0.0\",\n      domains: [],\n      splits: { regression: { count: 0 }, benchmark: { count: 0 } },\n      files: {\n        \"examples.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(examples).digest(\"hex\"),\n        \"oracles.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(oracles).digest(\"hex\"),\n      },\n      tasks: {},\n    }, null, 2)}\\n`);\n\n    const launcher = path.join(packageRoot, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    const help = spawnSync(launcher, [\"eval\", \"--help\"], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: outside, NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    });\n    assert.equal(help.status, 0, `${help.stdout}${help.stderr}`);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--dataset <path>/);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--split <name>/);\n\n    const evalRun = spawnSync(launcher, [\n      \"eval\", \"--dataset\", dataset, \"--split\", \"benchmark\", \"--runs\", \"1\", \"--output\", path.join(outside, \"score.json\"),\n    ], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: {\n        PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\",\n        HOME: outside,\n        NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot,\n        LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT: \"http://127.0.0.1:1/v1\",\n        LOCAL_LLM_MODEL: \"package-smoke\",\n      },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n448:      for (const call of message.tool_calls ?? []) {\n2295:      if (this.messages[i].role === \"assistant\" && this.messages[i].tool_calls?.length) {\n2301:    const calls = this.messages[last].tool_calls!;\n2676:      if (m.role === \"assistant\") for (const c of (m as any).tool_calls ?? []) if (typeof c?.id === \"string\") used.add(c.id);\n3097:      if (message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls) {\n3098:        for (const call of message.tool_calls) {\n3157:      if (message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls) {\n3158:        for (const call of message.tool_calls) {\n3160:          const rawArgs = call?.function?.arguments;\n3421:    if (lastAssistant < 0 || !source[lastAssistant].tool_calls?.length) return [];\n3434:      .map((message, index) => message.role === \"assistant\" && message.tool_calls?.length ? index : -1)\n3538:        for (const call of message.tool_calls ?? []) {\n3919:      if (m.role !== \"assistant\" || !m.tool_calls?.length) continue;\n3921:      return m.tool_calls.filter((call) => !results.has(call.id)).map((call) => call.id);\n4857:          args = value && typeof value === \"object\" ? value : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n4860:          args = toolName === \"task_completed\" ? {} : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n4863:        args = toolName === \"task_completed\" ? {} : { raw: call.function.arguments };\n6099:        this.addToolCallSyntax(parsed.toolCallSyntax);\n6114:          countTokens(JSON.stringify(assistantMessage.tool_calls || []));\n6134:        // message is dropped so the history never holds tool_calls without tool results.\n6146:          ...(parsed.toolCalls.length > 0 ? { tool_calls: parsed.toolCalls } : {}),\n6574:      ...(Object.values(this.turnToolCallSyntax).some((n) => n > 0) ? { toolCallSyntax: { ...this.turnToolCallSyntax } } : {}),\n6962:        countTokens(JSON.stringify(assistantMessage.tool_calls || []));\n6972:      this.addToolCallSyntax(parsed.toolCallSyntax);\n6977:        ...(parsed.toolCalls.length > 0 ? { tool_calls: parsed.toolCalls } : {}),\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:5:export const GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST = [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] as const;\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:6:export type GbnfToolName = (typeof GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST)[number];\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:8:const ALLOWED_NAMES: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:11:/** Compile the exact parameter schema registered for one allowlisted tool. Unknown JSON Schema forms fail closed. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:97:/** Compile each registered schema from the allowlist; unrelated registered tools are intentionally ignored. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:102:  for (const toolName of GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST) result[toolName] = generateToolArgumentsGbnf(toolName, registeredTools);\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:9:- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:10:- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:11:- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:16:**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:22:**Roadmap contract reconciliation:** Keep the existing dynamic GBNF compiler and its allowlist/schema tests as the deterministic schema-to-grammar implementation. Provider transport must use each server's compatible native tool path: llama.cpp rejects a caller grammar beside native tools but builds a dynamic tool grammar from their schemas; vLLM consumes `strict: true` through its structural-tag tool parser; Ollama carries tool schemas in `tools`, separately from response-level `format`. The hybrid `<think>...</think>` + tool-call requirement is not dropped: AC6 and the live matrix require a reasoning-plus-tool attempt on each exact endpoint. The provider's model/template/parser must build or accept that hybrid grammar; any endpoint that cannot pass AC6 remains unsupported and blocks G1.1-4. Do not claim that successful JSON syntax alone satisfies schema validity.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:29:- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:30:- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:38:- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:45:- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:47:- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Each provider's pinned configuration must use a reasoning-capable model/template/parser; 20 attempts (five for each tool) must exercise the hybrid reasoning/tool path. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no provider-specific adaptation.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793737867.6620908}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
