{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:41:20.715Z","ordinal":81773,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9c42ae2c-0c07-4392-9a23-4afdcc2a8070","process_id":"68389","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1190,1240p' cli/src/client.ts; rg -n 'api/version|api/show' cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1190,1240p' cli/src/client.ts","name":"client.ts","path":"cli/src/client.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'api/version|api/show' cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md","query":"api/version|api/show","path":"provider_capabilities.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\n   * `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`) on the endpoint's origin with the same credential and a 2 s\n   * limit. The server is recognised from its catalog entry first, so an unrecognised server is never probed. Not\n   * content-bearing. Undefined when the server is not recognised or does not answer with a context size.\n   */\n  private async discoverServerContext(entry: Record<string, any>, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<Advertisement | undefined> {\n    const kind = serverKindOf(entry);\n    if (kind !== \"llamacpp\" && kind !== \"lmstudio\" && kind !== \"ollama\") return undefined;\n    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n    const cached = LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.get(cacheKey);\n    if (cached) return cached;\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const probes: Array<{ kind: \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\"; url: string; init?: RequestInit }> = [\n      { kind: \"llamacpp\" as const, url: `${root}/props` },\n      { kind: \"lmstudio\" as const, url: `${root}/api/v0/models` },\n      { kind: \"ollama\" as const, url: `${root}/api/show`, init: { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }), headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } } },\n    ].filter((p) => p.kind === kind);\n    for (const probe of probes) {\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(probe.url, {\n          ...probe.init,\n          headers: { ...(probe.init?.headers as Record<string, string> | undefined), ...this.authorization(probe.url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n          signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n          ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n        });\n        if (!res.ok) continue;\n        const found = parseServerContext(probe.kind, await res.json(), this.model);\n        if (found) {\n          LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\n          return found;\n        }\n      } catch {\n        if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      }\n    }\n    return undefined;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Counts the prompt tokens of the request inference would send now, through the connection's `/v1/tokenize`\n   * (advertised by the homelab-ai gateway contract). The body is `outboundChatBody` — the actual outbound messages,\n   * tools, tool_choice and settings, after the same egress quarantine and sanitization — sent to the active endpoint\n   * only, with the same credential scoping, disclosure checks and cancellation as inference. No failover: a counting\n   * failure belongs to this connection and capability, and never moves task content elsewhere.\n   * Throws TokenCountError: `unsupported` (no such endpoint or model), `unavailable` (temporary), `malformed`,\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:67:3. **Context discovery:** When `/v1/models` omits limits, Nexus probes `POST /api/show` with `{\"model\": \"<id>\"}` (2 s timeout) and reads `num_ctx` from `parameters` (or `model_info[\"<arch>.context_length\"]`), reporting `server_probe (ollama)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:75:1. **Server / provider advertisement (`provider_advertised` or `server_probe (<kind>)`):** Read from `/v1/models` (`context_length` or `max_model_len`) or the server-specific probe (`/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`), intersected with `--context-limit` if both are present.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:79:To disable extra server-kind probes (`/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`) and rely strictly on `/v1/models` or `NEXUS_CONTEXT_LIMIT`, set `NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE=0` in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`.\ncli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts:103:    if (req.url === \"/api/show\") return json(res, { parameters: \"num_ctx 8192\" });\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":702067725}},"started_at_ms":1793738480012,"completed_at_ms":1793738480715}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:41:22.152Z","ordinal":81774,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a325-21e8-7c02-970d-888ba7848bd9","call_id":"call_1dd4df9089f0479e9bc103f0dd3599ce","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\n   * `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`) on the endpoint's origin with the same credential and a 2 s\n   * limit. The server is recognised from its catalog entry first, so an unrecognised server is never probed. Not\n   * content-bearing. Undefined when the server is not recognised or does not answer with a context size.\n   */\n  private async discoverServerContext(entry: Record<string, any>, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<Advertisement | undefined> {\n    const kind = serverKindOf(entry);\n    if (kind !== \"llamacpp\" && kind !== \"lmstudio\" && kind !== \"ollama\") return undefined;\n    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n    const cached = LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.get(cacheKey);\n    if (cached) return cached;\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const probes: Array<{ kind: \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\"; url: string; init?: RequestInit }> = [\n      { kind: \"llamacpp\" as const, url: `${root}/props` },\n      { kind: \"lmstudio\" as const, url: `${root}/api/v0/models` },\n      { kind: \"ollama\" as const, url: `${root}/api/show`, init: { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }), headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } } },\n    ].filter((p) => p.kind === kind);\n    for (const probe of probes) {\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(probe.url, {\n          ...probe.init,\n          headers: { ...(probe.init?.headers as Record<string, string> | undefined), ...this.authorization(probe.url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n          signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n          ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n        });\n        if (!res.ok) continue;\n        const found = parseServerContext(probe.kind, await res.json(), this.model);\n        if (found) {\n          LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\n          return found;\n        }\n      } catch {\n        if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      }\n    }\n    return undefined;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Counts the prompt tokens of the request inference would send now, through the connection's `/v1/tokenize`\n   * (advertised by the homelab-ai gateway contract). The body is `outboundChatBody` — the actual outbound messages,\n   * tools, tool_choice and settings, after the same egress quarantine and sanitization — sent to the active endpoint\n   * only, with the same credential scoping, disclosure checks and cancellation as inference. No failover: a counting\n   * failure belongs to this connection and capability, and never moves task content elsewhere.\n   * Throws TokenCountError: `unsupported` (no such endpoint or model), `unavailable` (temporary), `malformed`,\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:67:3. **Context discovery:** When `/v1/models` omits limits, Nexus probes `POST /api/show` with `{\"model\": \"<id>\"}` (2 s timeout) and reads `num_ctx` from `parameters` (or `model_info[\"<arch>.context_length\"]`), reporting `server_probe (ollama)` in `/status` and `nexus doctor`.\ndocs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md:75:1. **Server / provider advertisement (`provider_advertised` or `server_probe (<kind>)`):** Read from `/v1/models` (`context_length` or `max_model_len`) or the server-specific probe (`/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`), intersected with `--context-limit` if both are present.\ndocs/LOC