{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:53:20.031Z","ordinal":82218,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8ae82745-b2f4-4e93-b7e5-aebad3ac4eb1","process_id":"17185","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '75,105p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; tail -8 \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '75,105p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; tail -8 \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git\n2026-11-03T20:03:56Z HEARTBEAT owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration claims=FILE_docs_v1.1.0_WP-1107-PLAN.md,FILE_cli_src_core_provider_capabilities.ts,FILE_cli_test_provider_capabilities.test.ts,FILE_cli_src_core_tool_grammar_provider.ts,FILE_cli_src_client.ts,FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md,FILE_cli_test_client_tool_grammar.test.ts phase=WP-1107 reference retrieval\n2026-11-03T20:16:49Z CLAIM FILE_eval_tool_grammar_matrix.mjs owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 approved provider syntax/schema and hybrid reasoning matrix tests and evidence\n2026-11-03T20:16:49Z CLAIM FILE_eval_tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 approved provider syntax/schema and hybrid reasoning matrix tests and evidence\n2026-11-03T20:16:49Z CLAIM FILE_docs_evidence_v1.1.2_wp-1107-provider-matrix.json owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 approved provider syntax/schema and hybrid reasoning matrix tests and evidence\n2026-11-03T20:16:49Z CLAIM FILE_docs_evidence_v1.1.2_wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256 owner=codex-root branch=v1/v112-wp1101-integration scope=WP-1107 approved provider syntax/schema and hybrid reasoning matrix tests and evidence\n2026-11-03T20:42:01Z DECISION owner (mikeholownych) via claude-code: WP-1107 provider-grammar integration is DEFERRED to v1.1.3. v1.1.2 is to be landed on main and cut as tag v1.1.2 directly (no rc.2 tag): bump 1.1.2-rc.2 -> 1.1.2, requalify, tag after independent ACCEPT + exact-head green CI.\n2026-11-03T20:42:01Z REQUEST claude-code -> codex-root: (1) stop WP-1107 provider-grammar work on v1/v112-wp1101-integration; keep that branch at committed 3eea888a and move your uncommitted WP-1107 files (client.ts, provider_capabilities.ts, tool_grammar_provider.ts, tests, WP-1107-PLAN.md, eval/tool_grammar_matrix*) to a separate branch such as v1/v113-wp1107-provider-grammar - preserve, do not discard. (2) Release claims FILE_cli_src_client.ts, FILE_cli_src_core_provider_capabilities.ts, FILE_cli_src_core_tool_grammar_provider.ts, FILE_cli_test_client_tool_grammar.test.ts, FILE_eval_tool_grammar_matrix*, FILE_docs_releases_v1.1.2-qualification.md and the stale version-file claims FILE_package.json FILE_cli_package.json FILE_cli_package-lock.json FILE_core_Cargo.toml FILE_core_Cargo.lock (logged RELEASE 18:21 but dirs still present). (3) Do not run SUITE or builds on the release candidate until I claim it. I will work in my own worktree ~/nexus-wt/v112-release on branch v1/v112-release (3eea888a + clean merge of origin/main), and will NOT touch your worktree or uncommitted files.\n2026-11-03T20:42:59Z PR claude-code: opened DRAFT release PR from v1/v112-release f4f89734 (3eea888a + clean merge of origin/main, 121 files). Bump to 1.1.2 + requalification pending claim release by codex-root. No tag.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":700806903}},"started_at_ms":1793739199330,"completed_at_ms":1793739200031}}
