{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:56:06.928Z","ordinal":82295,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea4a536bdc81a397bf194f0b5eb172","usage":{"input_tokens":214295,"cached_input_tokens":206080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":969,"reasoning_output_tokens":952,"total_tokens":215264},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":624918,"cached_input_tokens":602112,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2409,"reasoning_output_tokens":2027,"total_tokens":627327},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1667915586,"cached_input_tokens":1655335168,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3097286,"reasoning_output_tokens":1519751,"total_tokens":1671012872}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:56:06.932Z","ordinal":82296,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a332-a213-7150-96f9-fa422300e351","call_id":"call_5c6f2dc422c7475fb210149960ade952","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The `FILE_cli_src_client.ts` claim appears stale locally, but it is not cleared. The owner record has no PID, the worktree is clean at `9cc247f8` and 168 commits behind, the claimed file has no local diff against the integrated candidate, and no RC16 process or separate claimant appears in the local agent roster. I can’t verify activity outside `mike-dev`.\\n\\nThe log records a stale break and takeover for the RC16 **test** file, but not for `client.ts`. The safe route is explicit owner confirmation; if that is unavailable, the coordinator can apply CONCURRENCY §2 by recording the stale break before releasing and reassigning the claim. I left the claim unchanged.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"APPROVED. The plan reconciles dynamic GBNF with each provider’s native tool path, retains hybrid reasoning/tool calls as an acceptance requirement, and measures syntax and schema validity separately. Provider identity, immutable configuration, and the GATEWAY pre-run gate are explicit. No remaining plan gaps before RED.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The GBNF generator is **not connected to a provider request path** on candidate `e134dcd5`. Its only references are its definitions in [tool_grammar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:12) and unit tests in [tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:13). The client’s non-streaming, streaming, and native request builders contain no `grammar`, `guided_json`, or `format` field ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1377), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1531), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1858)).\\n\\nThe roadmap requires integration for llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama and a ≥99.5% valid tool-call JSON result across those endpoints ([ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50), [ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58)). The qualification record marks WP-1107 passed based on four compiler tests, while its gate row still says endpoint evidence is pending ([qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32), [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42)). The older roadmap review explicitly deferred WP-1107 due to provider request changes ([ROADMAP-REVIEW.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194)); the user-approved full-roadmap scope supersedes that deferral, but the conflicting record and completion claim need reconciliation.\\n\\nA safe implementation sequence is a reviewed transport plan, followed by test-first request integration for each provider. Likely files are `cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, and provider request-capture tests; provider capability detection may also need adjustment. `client.ts` is actively claimed by codex-root for RC16 work, so coordinate before editing. The grammar module, its tests, `client.test.ts`, and provider-capability file have no active file claims. GATEWAY remains claimed for RC15 E5 work; endpoint inference needs owner coordination. No edits or tests were made.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793739366.9319446}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
