{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:22.125Z","ordinal":82336,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea4ab07bb881a3b8556bbbabd7c094","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Confirmed your direction: WP-1107 belongs in the current v1.1.2 release work. The owner’s release branch and open draft PR are separate from this isolated feature worktree, and the shared test-runner file still has another worktree’s live claim. I’m continuing on the WP-1107 files and will keep that integration boundary visible."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793739440560,"completed_at_ms":1793739442124}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:22.139Z","ordinal":82337,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea4ab07bb881a3b8556bbbabd7c094","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Confirmed your direction: WP-1107 belongs in the current v1.1.2 release work. The owner’s release branch and open draft PR are separate from this isolated feature worktree, and the shared test-runner file still has another worktree’s live claim. I’m continuing on the WP-1107 files and will keep that integration boundary visible.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793739440.484849,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea4ab07bb881a3b8556bbbabd7c094","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1a333-c7da-73d0-83a2-3a289c556d56","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2824}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:26.444Z","ordinal":82338,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea4ab20cac81a3826bf5b018006a2a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ce9eb5f5987743c7a37586e5c76f01a3","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.allSettled([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff -- docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '1,180p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs; sed -n '180,420p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:6000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,240p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; rg -n 'WP-1107|G1.1-4' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:3500}),\n  tools.mcp__mcp_search__get_observations({ids:[26116,27554],project:\"nexus-code\"})\n]);\nfor(const x of r) text(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value:x.reason);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793739442.0509825}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:26.509Z","ordinal":82339,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-e3559944-65ad-458b-b695-cfc5543825d1","server":"mcp-search","tool":"get_observations","arguments":{"ids":[26116,27554],"project":"nexus-code"},"pluginId":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","readOnlyHint":true,"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Selected observations (2). Retrieved data; evaluate it as evidence.\n\n#27554 — Work State Updated — ORIENT Phase Blockers and Next Action Documented for v1.1.2-release (nexus-code)\nchange · 2026-11-02 12:21 UTC\nWork state records all current blockers: PR396 processes alive, agent.ts claimed, WP-1103 suite pending, no eligible WP slice available.\n\nThe work state update captures the complete ORIENT phase assessment: the session is blocked from starting any new WP slice due to PR396's long-running test processes holding the agent.ts file claim and the active SUITE. WP-1103's AC2 qualification requires a clean serialized suite run which cannot happen until PR396 exits. WP-1105 depends on WP-1103. WP-1106 needs agent.ts. WP-1108 has prior ownership concerns. The only path forward is to wait for PR396 processes to exit, then immediately acquire SUITE and run WP-1103 integration tests.\n\n- Work state phase remains ORIENT; gate is \"WP-1103 clean suite pending; v1.1.2 no release/tag\"\n- Friction documented: PR396 test child PIDs 2050464 and 2084265 still live; agent.ts claimed by claude-code for PR396; no eligible full WP slice can start without conflict\n- WP-1105 ineligible: depends on WP-1103 which is unqualified; prior owner claim and untracked evaluator files preserved\n- WP-1106 plan approved but implementation blocked: requires cli/src/agent.ts which is claimed by PR396\n- WP-1108 branch is clean but prior owner work history means no takeover without explicit handoff\n- Scope correction commit 4b63cee0 (docs/releases/v1.1.2.md) is reviewed, local, and unpushed\n- Next action: when PR396 test child exits, recheck all test PIDs, acquire SUITE claim, and run exact WP-1103 integration source\n- Review verdict APPROVED for commits 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e from reviewer /root/review_delta\n\nConcepts: why-it-exists, gotcha, what-changed\n\n#26116 — v1.1.0 Declared Failed; Roadmap WPs to Target v1.1.2 (nexus-code)\ndecision · 2026-11-01 16:53 UTC\nOwner declared v1.1.0 a failed release; full roadmap work to resume targeting v1.1.2 after v1.1.1.\n\nThe owner formally closed the v1.1.0 release attempt by declaring it failed. The stated reason is that no release files were published under the v1.1.0 tag, and semantic versions are immutable so it cannot be retroactively fixed. v1.1.1 was the published stable release that followed. The agent proposed a choice: continue the full WP-1101..1108 roadmap targeting v1.1.2, or stop at v1.1.1. The owner accepted, indicating the project will now target v1.1.2 for all remaining roadmap work.\n\n- Owner explicitly declared v1.1.0 a failed release because no release files were published and versions are immutable.\n- v1.1.1 was released as the successor to the failed v1.1.0 tag.\n- Agent asked whether to continue implementing the full WP-1101..1108 roadmap targeting v1.1.2, or treat v1.1.1 as final.\n- Owner accepted the prompt (accepted:true), implying continuation toward v1.1.2 as the next release target.\n\nConcepts: why-it-exists, trade-off"}]},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26119192}},"started_at_ms":1793739446480,"completed_at_ms":1793739446509}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:26.590Z","ordinal":82340,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea4aa72d9881a3b509457a8c77f084","usage":{"input_tokens":221212,"cached_input_tokens":218624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":818,"reasoning_output_tokens":487,"total_tokens":222030},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1714984,"cached_input_tokens":1684352,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6046,"reasoning_output_tokens":4714,"total_tokens":1721030},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1669005652,"cached_input_tokens":1656417408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3100923,"reasoning_output_tokens":1522438,"total_tokens":1672106575}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:28.524Z","ordinal":82341,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9796bf1a-45ff-470e-9c79-2e824dfebcc4","process_id":"73690","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; rg -n 'WP-1107|G1.1-4' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-release","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md","name":"v1.1.2-qualification.md","path":"docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'WP-1107|G1.1-4' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md","query":"WP-1107|G1.1-4","path":"ROADMAP.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\n\n**Status as of 2026-11-03: exact RC2 source and installed-package gates passed; provider-matrix, external CI/review, and publication gates remain open.**\nThis record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\n\nThe v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished.\n\n## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\n\nThe approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\n\n| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions connected; PR #396 review fixes present. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating connected. | Connected on the separate roadmap; not a WP-1101–WP-1108 qualification claim. |\n| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | The roadmap records this item as cut. | Cut on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | The roadmap records this item as cut; recovery behavior is supplied by PR #398. | Cut on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | The roadmap says this is not yet connected to request latency. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | The roadmap says the comparative harness entry point is not yet connected. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n| Item 7 — CERI | The roadmap says the `nexus eval` entry point is not yet connected. | Not connected on the separate roadmap; outside this release scope. |\n\n## Work-package status\n\n| Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence details |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Lifecycle instrumentation integrated in commit `97945557`, extending the existing local recorder. Public worktree-backed turns emit exactly one turn span; all four direct model request sites, tool dispatch, and compaction paths are traced with payload-free attributes. | **PASSED** | Fresh independent review APPROVED. Exact clean RC2 commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` passed 2,314/0/5; suite log SHA-256 `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. |\n| WP-1102 — Flight recorder credential redaction | Zero-leak sanitization across traces, CLI errors, and debug journals. | Integrated in commit `9c1926e1`. Comprehensive regex + token redactor applied across all flight recorder sinks. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/*_redaction.test.ts` (22/22 passed across all sinks and adversarial fixtures). |\n| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Exact RC2 archive acceptance invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and confirmed hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. | **PASSED — dataset boundary** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Exact archive evidence: [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b`. The deterministic fixture only reports task completion; hidden validators intentionally remain false, so this is not task-solving or provider-quality evidence. |\n| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | Package acceptance passed 5/5 tests with isolated HOME and the exact archive; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. The same candidate-bound evidence file is linked in WP-1103. |\n| WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`. Deterministic evaluators wired into runner and scorer. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts` (9/9 passed). |\n| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\n| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n\n## Release-gate status\n\n| Gate | Required proof | Current evidence | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\n| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\n| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\n| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\n| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Exact source commit passed full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo lifecycle scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures. The exact archive is reproducible, has a validated 141-component CycloneDX SBOM and checksums, installs through `install.sh`, and passes package runtime/CLI acceptance. External CodeQL/CI and release-level PTY evidence are not present in this record. | **SOURCE AND LOCAL ARTIFACT GATES PASS; EXTERNAL CI / PTY PENDING** |\n\n## Historical RC1 artifact (not release-qualified)\n\nThe historical RC1 distribution archive was built using the approved digest-pinned Bookworm builder (`rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb`):\n\n- **Package Archive:** `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz` (superseded; do not publish)\n  - **SHA-256 Digest:** `28d79f3b0f4d5047848af9f94ac5f7d052daa8868f66d142581f169e5b753e08`\n  - **Commit Revision:** `9c1926e15d4d3efb20738edaf3e04610118589aa`\n  - **Built At:** `2026-11-03T02:38:20Z`\n  - **Platform:** `linux-x86_64` (libc: `glibc-2.35`)\n  - **Internal Component Digests:**\n    - Launcher: `320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4`\n    - CLI Bundle: `b35396a1814a54e896b620edfa8abef8b9890352ea66c927b3c3851a87dd51da`\n    - Core Binary: `7b442f320827a532319f6a7662abb5ff22216ea8f603bd9c10591f61830d4a07`\n- **CycloneDX Software Bill of Materials (SBOM):** `sbom.cdx.json`\n  - Total Components: 141 (119 Cargo crates + 20 npm packages + root product)\n- **Compatibility Contract:** `compatibility.json`\n  - Config Schema Version: 1\n  - State Schema Version: 2\n- **Candidate Benchmark Acceptance Evidence:**\n  - `docs/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-28d79f3b0f4d.json`\n  - Manifest SHA-256: `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`\n\n## RC2 exact archive (local qualification; unpublished)\n\nThe first local RC2 archive (`fd99bd3f…`) inherited a group-writable evaluator helper from the shared-permission worktree. Its installed acceptance correctly refused to run. It was superseded and no release files were published. The final archive below uses the helper's Git-tracked mode `0644`; no tracked source content changed.\n\n- **Package Archive:** `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.2.tar.gz`\n  - **SHA-256 Digest:** `3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b`\n  - **Size:** 5,389,945 bytes\n  - **Source Revision:** `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`\n  - **Build Images:** Rust `1.95.0-bookworm` and Node `24.22.2-bookworm-slim`, both pinned by digest\n  - **Reproducibility:** two independent package runs produced byte-identical archives and matching checksums, SBOM, notices, compatibility metadata, and installer.\n  - **Installer:** local HTTP-feed installation passed archive checksum, package manifest, binary self-test, and compatibility checks. The installed launcher and TUI report `1.1.2-rc.2`; `.provenance.json` binds the installed tree to this archive digest. GitHub attestation verification was disabled because this local candidate is unpublished.\n  - **Internal component SHA-256:** launcher `320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4`; CLI bundle `b35396a1814a54e896b620edfa8abef8b9890352ea66c927b3c3851a87dd51da`; core binary `5a3ca7e8e9878bc8aec0e391e9e082372f03b678a7c6c0f3d86753211f97cc84`.\n- **CycloneDX SBOM:** `sbom.cdx.json`, 141 components (119 Cargo, 20 npm, and root product); SHA-256 `e44dfa6cd62d670a359a6b45c04ce86cc61e31ab400396adc2197fae9d4cfcb2`.\n- **Installed package acceptance:** `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 5/5 on the exact archive, including installed evaluator execution outside the checkout and a candidate launch without mounting evaluator code. Test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`.\n- **Installed-candidate evidence:** [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), SHA-256 `37c7fcee8d1058d04a90f672b5949fbaee7710bc22677612036da140dc4cc176`. The deterministic fixture submitted all six public benchmark tasks once, captured six requests, and found no hidden validator path or command in prompts. It returns a generic completion, so hidden validators are false by design and this does not measure task-solving quality. The same full run passed all five package-runtime tests.\n\n## Exact-candidate release checklist\n\n- [x] WP-1101–WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…` where required.\n- [ ] Applicable v1.1.0 release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 are qualified on the final candidate.\n- [x] Prior RC2 full source suite, security lifecycle scans, `make build`/TypeScript type build, and terminal process-scope acceptance passed before the CERI provenance correction.\n- [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on exact clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`.\n- [x] Package checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility verified for the final archive.\n- [x] Packaged CLI evaluator options and installed-candidate acceptance verified for the final archive.\n- [ ] External CI/CodeQL and the supported-provider constrained-decoding matrix are attached to the final candidate.\n- [ ] Acceptance evidence and qualification record committed for the final candidate.\n- [ ] Tag `v1.1.2` and release publication (reserved for repository owner `mikeholownych`).\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32:| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\ndocs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42:| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58:- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":709533997}},"started_at_ms":1793739447814,"completed_at_ms":1793739448524}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:28.573Z","ordinal":82342,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5f068d6d-6eda-4635-9326-db7377558a34","process_id":"45903","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff -- docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '1,180p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs; sed -n '180,420p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff -- docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '1,180p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs; sed -n '180,420p' eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\nindex 224c5d30..0ccd1646 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\n \n-**Status as of 2026-11-03: exact RC2 source and installed-package gates passed; provider-matrix, external CI/review, and publication gates remain open.**\n+**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\n This record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\n \n-The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished.\n+The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\n \n ## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\n \n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.\n | WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | Package acceptance passed 5/5 tests with isolated HOME and the exact archive; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. The same candidate-bound evidence file is linked in WP-1103. |\n | WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`. Deterministic evaluators wired into runner and scorer. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts` (9/9 passed). |\n | WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n-| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\n+| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\n | WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n \n ## Release-gate status\n@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.\n | G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\n | G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\n | G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\n-| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\n+| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | The generator is not connected to any client/provider request path on `e134dcd5`; its unit tests do not demonstrate constrained decoding. The shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric has been collected. | **IMPLEMENTATION INCOMPLETE; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\n | G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Exact source commit passed full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo lifecycle scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures. The exact archive is reproducible, has a validated 141-component CycloneDX SBOM and checksums, installs through `install.sh`, and passes package runtime/CLI acceptance. External CodeQL/CI and release-level PTY evidence are not present in this record. | **SOURCE AND LOCAL ARTIFACT GATES PASS; EXTERNAL CI / PTY PENDING** |\n \n ## Historical RC1 artifact (not release-qualified)\n@@ -82,7 +82,8 @@ The first local RC2 archive (`fd99bd3f…`) inherited a group-writable evaluator\n \n ## Exact-candidate release checklist\n \n-- [x] WP-1101–WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…` where required.\n+- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\n+- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\n - [ ] Applicable v1.1.0 release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 are qualified on the final candidate.\n - [x] Prior RC2 full source suite, security lifecycle scans, `make build`/TypeScript type build, and terminal process-scope acceptance passed before the CERI provenance correction.\n - [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on exact clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { pathToFileURL } from \"node:url\";\n\nexport const TOOL_NAMES = Object.freeze([\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"]);\nconst PROVIDER_KIND = Object.freeze({ llamacpp: \"llamacpp\", vllm: \"vllm\", ollama: \"ollama\" });\nconst sha256Pattern = /^(?:sha256:)?[a-f0-9]{64}$/i;\nconst commitPattern = /^[a-f0-9]{40}$/i;\nconst categories = [\"native_valid\", \"repaired\", \"schema_invalid\", \"invalid\"];\n\nconst sha256 = (bytes) => createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\nconst isRecord = (value) => value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\n\nfunction assertCount(value, label) {\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(value) || value < 0) throw new TypeError(`${label} count must be a non-negative integer`);\n}\n\nfunction assertNonSecretMetadata(value, location = \"evidence\") {\n  const sensitiveKey = /(?:^|[_-])(api[_-]?key|token|secret|password|credential|authorization|endpoint[_-]?url|url|raw[_-]?arguments|reasoning[_-]?text|prompt[_-]?text)(?:$|[_-])/i;\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    value.forEach((item, index) => assertNonSecretMetadata(item, `${location}[${index}]`));\n  } else if (isRecord(value)) {\n    for (const [key, nested] of Object.entries(value)) {\n      if (sensitiveKey.test(key)) throw new TypeError(`evidence contains sensitive field ${location}.${key}`);\n      assertNonSecretMetadata(nested, `${location}.${key}`);\n    }\n  } else if (typeof value === \"string\" && /(?:bearer\\s+\\S+|https?:\\/\\/[^\\s/@]+:[^\\s/@]+@)/i.test(value)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`evidence contains a credential-like value at ${location}`);\n  }\n}\n\n/** Validate the flat JSON Schema subset used by the four registered grammar pilot tools. */\nexport function validateToolArguments(schema, value) {\n  if (!isRecord(schema) || schema.type !== \"object\" || !isRecord(schema.properties)) return false;\n  if (!isRecord(value)) return false;\n  const required = schema.required ?? [];\n  if (!Array.isArray(required) || required.some((name) => typeof name !== \"string\")) return false;\n  for (const name of required) if (!Object.hasOwn(value, name)) return false;\n  if (schema.additionalProperties === false) {\n    for (const name of Object.keys(value)) if (!Object.hasOwn(schema.properties, name)) return false;\n  }\n  for (const [name, property] of Object.entries(schema.properties)) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(value, name)) continue;\n    if (!isRecord(property)) return false;\n    const actual = value[name];\n    const valid = property.type === \"string\" ? typeof actual === \"string\"\n      : property.type === \"number\" ? typeof actual === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(actual)\n        : property.type === \"integer\" ? Number.isSafeInteger(actual)\n          : property.type === \"boolean\" ? typeof actual === \"boolean\"\n            : property.type === \"object\" ? isRecord(actual)\n              : property.type === \"array\" ? Array.isArray(actual)\n                : property.type === \"null\" ? actual === null\n                  : false;\n    if (!valid) return false;\n    if (Array.isArray(property.enum) && !property.enum.some((item) => Object.is(item, actual))) return false;\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n\n/** Classify raw JSON before repair, then use the exact candidate's existing repair routine only when needed. */\nexport function classifyToolArguments({ schema, rawArguments, repairJsonWithClass }) {\n  if (typeof rawArguments !== \"string\") {\n    return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\n  }\n  let parsed;\n  try {\n    parsed = JSON.parse(rawArguments);\n  } catch {\n    if (typeof repairJsonWithClass !== \"function\") {\n      return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\n    }\n    try {\n      const repair = repairJsonWithClass(rawArguments);\n      if (!repair || !Object.hasOwn(repair, \"value\")) throw new Error(\"repair returned no value\");\n      parsed = repair.value;\n      if (!validateToolArguments(schema, parsed)) {\n        return { category: \"schema_invalid\", parsed: true, schemaValid: false, repaired: repair.repaired !== \"none\" };\n      }\n      if (repair.repaired === \"none\") {\n        return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: true, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\n      }\n      return { category: \"repaired\", parsed: true, schemaValid: true, repaired: true };\n    } catch {\n      return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\n    }\n  }\n  const schemaValid = validateToolArguments(schema, parsed);\n  return {\n    category: schemaValid ? \"native_valid\" : \"schema_invalid\",\n    parsed: true,\n    schemaValid,\n    repaired: false,\n  };\n}\n\n/** Apply the exact integer threshold and hybrid requirements; no rounded percentages are used. */\nexport function endpointPasses(endpoint) {\n  try {\n    if (!isRecord(endpoint) || !isRecord(endpoint.tools) || !isRecord(endpoint.totals)) return false;\n    if (endpoint.attempts !== 200 || endpoint.totals.attempts !== 200) return false;\n    let attemptSum = 0;\n    let nativeValid = 0;\n    let repaired = 0;\n    let schemaInvalid = 0;\n    let invalid = 0;\n    for (const name of TOOL_NAMES) {\n      const tool = endpoint.tools[name];\n      if (!isRecord(tool) || tool.attempts !== 50 || tool.hybrid_attempts !== 5) return false;\n      let toolSum = 0;\n      for (const category of categories) {\n        assertCount(tool[category], `${name}.${category}`);\n        toolSum += tool[category];\n      }\n      if (toolSum !== 50 || tool.hybrid_reasoning_present !== 5 || tool.hybrid_schema_valid !== 5) return false;\n      attemptSum += toolSum;\n      nativeValid += tool.native_valid;\n      repaired += tool.repaired;\n      schemaInvalid += tool.schema_invalid;\n      invalid += tool.invalid;\n    }\n    if (attemptSum !== 200 || endpoint.totals.native_valid !== nativeValid || endpoint.totals.repaired !== repaired || endpoint.totals.schema_invalid !== schemaInvalid || endpoint.totals.invalid !== invalid) return false;\n    return nativeValid * 1000 >= 200 * 995 && schemaInvalid === 0 && invalid === 0;\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateEndpoint(endpoint) {\n  if (!isRecord(endpoint)) throw new TypeError(\"endpoint identity and counts must be an object\");\n  const expected = PROVIDER_KIND[endpoint.provider];\n  if (!expected || endpoint.serverKind !== expected) throw new TypeError(\"provider identity mismatch\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.serverVersion !== \"string\" || !endpoint.serverVersion.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"server identity requires a version\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.imageDigest !== \"string\" || !/^sha256:[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(endpoint.imageDigest)) throw new TypeError(\"server identity requires an immutable image digest\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.modelName !== \"string\" || !endpoint.modelName.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"model identity requires a name\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.modelDigest !== \"string\" || !/^sha256:[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(endpoint.modelDigest)) throw new TypeError(\"model identity requires an immutable model digest\");\n  assertCount(endpoint.contextSize, \"context size\");\n  if (endpoint.contextSize === 0) throw new TypeError(\"context size must be positive\");\n  if (!isRecord(endpoint.sampling) || !Number.isFinite(endpoint.sampling.temperature)) throw new TypeError(\"sampling identity requires the temperature sent by the candidate\");\n  if (endpoint.sampling.max_tokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(endpoint.sampling.max_tokens) || endpoint.sampling.max_tokens <= 0)) throw new TypeError(\"sampling max_tokens must be a positive integer\");\n  if (endpoint.toolChoice !== \"auto\") throw new TypeError(\"tool choice must match the candidate client's auto selection\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.promptFixtureSha256 !== \"string\" || !/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(endpoint.promptFixtureSha256)) throw new TypeError(\"prompt fixture identity requires SHA-256\");\n  if (!Array.isArray(endpoint.serverFlags) || endpoint.serverFlags.some((flag) => typeof flag !== \"string\")) throw new TypeError(\"server flags identity must be a string array\");\n  if (endpoint.serverFlags.some((flag) => /api[-_]?key|token|secret|password|credential|authorization|bearer/i.test(flag))) throw new TypeError(\"server flags must omit credentials and authentication options\");\n  if (typeof endpoint.compatibilityMode !== \"string\" || !endpoint.compatibilityMode.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"compatibility mode identity is required\");\n  assertNonSecretMetadata(endpoint, \"endpoint\");\n  if (!isRecord(endpoint.tools) || Object.keys(endpoint.tools).length !== TOOL_NAMES.length) throw new TypeError(\"attempt counts must include exactly the four allowlisted tools\");\n  const totals = { attempts: 0, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0 };\n  for (const name of TOOL_NAMES) {\n    const tool = endpoint.tools[name];\n    if (!isRecord(tool)) throw new TypeError(`attempt counts missing ${name}`);\n    if (tool.attempts !== 50 || tool.hybrid_attempts !== 5 || tool.hybrid_reasoning_present !== 5 || tool.hybrid_schema_valid !== 5) {\n      throw new TypeError(`${name} hybrid/attempt counts violate the 50-attempt and five-hybrid matrix`);\n    }\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (const category of categories) {\n      assertCount(tool[category], `${name}.${category}`);\n      sum += tool[category];\n      totals[category] += tool[category];\n    }\n    if (sum !== 50) throw new TypeError(`${name} attempt counts do not sum to 50`);\n    totals.attempts += tool.attempts;\n  }\n  if (!isRecord(endpoint.totals) || Object.keys(totals).some((key) => endpoint.totals[key] !== totals[key])) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"aggregate attempt counts do not match per-tool counts\");\n  }\n  if (endpoint.attempts !== 200) throw new TypeError(\"endpoint attempt count must be 200\");\n  if (endpoint.passed !== true || !endpointPasses(endpoint)) throw new TypeError(\"endpoint does not pass the exact syntax, schema, and hybrid reasoning gates\");\n  return endpoint;\n}\n\n/** Validate final matrix evidence; partial endpoint results are not release evidence. */\nexport function validateMatrixEvidence(evidence) {\n  if (!isRecord(evidence) || evidence.schemaVersion !== 1) throw new TypeError(\"unsupported evidence schema version\");\n  if (!isRecord(evidence.candidate) || !sha256Pattern.test(evidence.candidate.archiveSha256) || !commitPattern.test(evidence.candidate.sourceCommit)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"candidate identity requires archive SHA-256 and full source commit\");\n  }\n  if (!Array.isArray(evidence.endpoints) || evidence.endpoints.length !== Object.keys(PROVIDER_KIND).length) throw new TypeError(\"matrix evidence must contain llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoints\");\n  const kinds = new Set();\n  for (const endpoint of evidence.endpoints) {\n  for (const endpoint of evidence.endpoints) {\n    validateEndpoint(endpoint);\n    if (kinds.has(endpoint.provider)) throw new TypeError(\"matrix evidence repeats a provider identity\");\n    kinds.add(endpoint.provider);\n  }\n  if (kinds.size !== 3) throw new TypeError(\"matrix evidence is missing a provider identity\");\n  return { valid: true, passed: evidence.endpoints.every((endpoint) => endpoint.passed) };\n}\n\nfunction validateTools(tools) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(tools)) throw new TypeError(\"candidate tool definitions are required\");\n  const selected = TOOL_NAMES.map((name) => {\n    const matches = tools.filter((tool) => tool?.type === \"function\" && tool?.function?.name === name);\n    if (matches.length !== 1 || !isRecord(matches[0].function.parameters)) throw new TypeError(`candidate must expose exactly one schema for ${name}`);\n    return matches[0];\n  });\n  return selected;\n}\n\nasync function loadInstalledRuntime(installRoot) {\n  const cliRoot = path.resolve(installRoot, \"lib\", \"cli\", \"dist\");\n  const [clientModule, capabilitiesModule, parserModule] = await Promise.all([\n    import(pathToFileURL(path.join(cliRoot, \"client.js\")).href),\n    import(pathToFileURL(path.join(cliRoot, \"core\", \"capabilities.js\")).href),\n    import(pathToFileURL(path.join(cliRoot, \"parser.js\")).href),\n  ]);\n  if (typeof clientModule.LocalLlmClient !== \"function\" || !Array.isArray(capabilitiesModule.HARNESS_TOOLS) || typeof parserModule.repairJsonWithClass !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"installed candidate is missing client, tool registry, or argument repair exports\");\n  }\n  return {\n    tools: capabilitiesModule.HARNESS_TOOLS,\n    repairJsonWithClass: parserModule.repairJsonWithClass,\n    clientFactory: async (provider) => new clientModule.LocalLlmClient({\n      model: provider.modelName,\n      endpoint: provider.endpointUrl,\n      temperature: provider.sampling.temperature,\n      contextLimit: provider.contextSize,\n      completionReserveTokens: provider.sampling.max_tokens ?? 512,\n      workspace: process.cwd(),\n      shell: \"bash\",\n      maxSteps: 1,\n      pinEndpoint: true,\n      ...(provider.apiKeyEnv && process.env[provider.apiKeyEnv] ? { apiKey: process.env[provider.apiKeyEnv] } : {}),\n    }),\n  };\n}\n\nfunction promptFor(toolName, hybrid) {\n  return `Call the ${toolName} tool exactly once with arguments that satisfy its supplied JSON Schema.${hybrid ? \" Think before the call and emit a non-empty <think>...</think> block.\" : \" Do not add prose.\"}`;\n}\n\nfunction validProviderIdentity(provider) {\n  const expected = PROVIDER_KIND[provider.provider];\n  if (!expected || provider.serverKind !== expected) throw new TypeError(\"configured provider identity is invalid\");\n  if (typeof provider.endpointUrl !== \"string\" || !provider.endpointUrl) throw new TypeError(\"provider endpoint is required\");\n  if (typeof provider.serverVersion !== \"string\" || !provider.serverVersion.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"server version must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (typeof provider.imageDigest !== \"string\" || !/^sha256:[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(provider.imageDigest)) throw new TypeError(\"immutable server image digest must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (typeof provider.modelName !== \"string\" || !provider.modelName.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"model identity requires a name\");\n  if (typeof provider.modelDigest !== \"string\" || !/^sha256:[a-f0-9]{64}$/i.test(provider.modelDigest)) throw new TypeError(\"immutable model digest must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(provider.contextSize) || provider.contextSize <= 0) throw new TypeError(\"positive context size must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (!isRecord(provider.sampling) || !Number.isFinite(provider.sampling.temperature)) throw new TypeError(\"sampling temperature must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (provider.sampling.max_tokens !== undefined && (!Number.isSafeInteger(provider.sampling.max_tokens) || provider.sampling.max_tokens <= 0)) throw new TypeError(\"sampling max_tokens must be a positive integer\");\n  if (provider.toolChoice !== \"auto\") throw new TypeError(\"tool choice must be auto for the candidate client\");\n  if (!Array.isArray(provider.serverFlags) || provider.serverFlags.some((flag) => typeof flag !== \"string\")) throw new TypeError(\"server flags must be pinned before inference\");\n  if (typeof provider.compatibilityMode !== \"string\" || !provider.compatibilityMode.trim()) throw new TypeError(\"compatibility mode must be pinned before inference\");\n  return expected;\n}\n\nfunction verifyInstalledArchive(installRoot, archiveSha256, sourceCommit) {\n  const provenancePath = path.join(path.resolve(installRoot), \".provenance.json\");\n  let provenance;\n  try {\n    provenance = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(provenancePath, \"utf8\"));\n  } catch {\n    throw new TypeError(\"installed candidate has no readable installer provenance\");\n  }\n  if (provenance.method !== \"installer\" || provenance.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256 || provenance.revision !== sourceCommit) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"installed candidate provenance does not bind the exact archive and source commit\");\n  }\n}\n\n/** Invoke the exact installed candidate client for 50 attempts/tool and retain only non-secret aggregate evidence. */\nexport async function runToolGrammarMatrix(options) {\n  if (!options || typeof options.archivePath !== \"string\" || typeof options.installRoot !== \"string\") throw new TypeError(\"candidate archive and installed root are required\");\n  if (!commitPattern.test(options.sourceCommit)) throw new TypeError(\"full candidate source commit is required\");\n  const archivePath = fs.realpathSync(options.archivePath);\n  const archiveSha256 = sha256(fs.readFileSync(archivePath));\n  if (options.archiveSha256 && options.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) throw new TypeError(\"candidate archive SHA-256 does not match the pinned digest\");\n  verifyInstalledArchive(options.installRoot, archiveSha256, options.sourceCommit);\n  const runtime = options.runtime ?? (options.tools && options.clientFactory && options.repairJsonWithClass\n    ? {}\n    : await loadInstalledRuntime(options.installRoot));\n  const tools = validateTools(options.tools ?? runtime.tools);\n  const clientFactory = options.clientFactory ?? runtime.clientFactory;\n  const repairJsonWithClass = options.repairJsonWithClass ?? runtime.repairJsonWithClass;\n  if (typeof clientFactory !== \"function\" || typeof repairJsonWithClass !== \"function\") throw new TypeError(\"installed candidate runtime is incomplete\");\n  if (!Array.isArray(options.providers) || options.providers.length !== 3) throw new TypeError(\"exactly one configuration per supported provider is required\");\n  const digests = { archiveSha256, sourceCommit: options.sourceCommit };\n  const endpoints = [];\n  for (const provider of options.providers) {\n    const expectedKind = validProviderIdentity(provider);\n    const promptFixtures = TOOL_NAMES.flatMap((toolName) => Array.from({ length: 50 }, (_, index) => promptFor(toolName, index < 5)));\n    const client = await clientFactory(provider, runtime);\n    const discovery = await client.discoverAdvertisement();\n    const detectedKind = client.getDetectedServerKind?.();\n    if (discovery?.state !== \"supported\" || detectedKind !== expectedKind) {\n      throw new Error(`provider identity mismatch: configured ${expectedKind}, detected ${detectedKind ?? \"unknown\"}`);\n    }\n    const counts = Object.fromEntries(TOOL_NAMES.map((name) => [name, {\n      attempts: 50, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0,\n      hybrid_attempts: 5, hybrid_reasoning_present: 0, hybrid_schema_valid: 0,\n    }]));\n    for (const toolName of TOOL_NAMES) {\n      const tool = tools.find((entry) => entry.function.name === toolName);\n      const toolCounts = counts[toolName];\n      for (let index = 0; index < 50; index++) {\n        const hybrid = index < 5;\n        let response;\n        try {\n          response = await client.chatCompletion([{ role: \"user\", content: promptFor(toolName, hybrid) }], [tool]);\n        } catch {\n          toolCounts.invalid++;\n          continue;\n        }\n        const calls = Array.isArray(response?.tool_calls) ? response.tool_calls : [];\n        if (calls.length !== 1 || calls[0]?.function?.name !== toolName) {\n          toolCounts.invalid++;\n          continue;\n        }\n        const classification = classifyToolArguments({\n          schema: tool.function.parameters,\n          rawArguments: calls[0].function.arguments,\n          repairJsonWithClass,\n        });\n        toolCounts[classification.category]++;\n        const reasoningMatch = /<think>\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*<\\/think>/i.exec(typeof response.content === \"string\" ? response.content : \"\");\n        const reasoningPresent = Boolean(reasoningMatch?.[1]?.trim());\n        if (hybrid && reasoningPresent) toolCounts.hybrid_reasoning_present++;\n        if (hybrid && classification.schemaValid) toolCounts.hybrid_schema_valid++;\n      }\n    }\n    const totals = { attempts: 200, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0 };\n    for (const tool of Object.values(counts)) for (const category of categories) totals[category] += tool[category];\n    const fixtureBytes = Buffer.from(promptFixtures.join(\"\\n\"), \"utf8\");\n    const endpoint = {\n      provider: provider.provider,\n      serverKind: detectedKind,\n      serverVersion: provider.serverVersion,\n      imageDigest: provider.imageDigest,\n      modelName: provider.modelName,\n      modelDigest: provider.modelDigest,\n      contextSize: provider.contextSize,\n      sampling: provider.sampling,\n      toolChoice: provider.toolChoice,\n      promptFixtureSha256: sha256(fixtureBytes),\n      serverFlags: provider.serverFlags,\n      compatibilityMode: provider.compatibilityMode,\n      attempts: 200,\n      tools: counts,\n      totals,\n      passed: false,\n    };\n    endpoint.passed = endpointPasses(endpoint);\n    endpoints.push(endpoint);\n  }\n  const evidence = { schemaVersion: 1, candidate: digests, endpoints };\n  validateMatrixEvidence(evidence);\n  if (options.outputPath) writeEvidence(options.outputPath, evidence);\n  return evidence;\n}\n\n/** Write immutable JSON evidence and a detached SHA-256 sidecar. */\nexport function writeEvidence(outputPath, evidence) {\n  validateMatrixEvidence(evidence);\n  const destination = path.resolve(outputPath);\n  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(destination), { recursive: true });\n  const bytes = Buffer.from(`${JSON.stringify(evidence, null, 2)}\\n`, \"utf8\");\n  const sidecar = `${destination}.sha256`;\n  let wroteEvidence = false;\n  try {\n    fs.writeFileSync(destination, bytes, { flag: \"wx\", mode: 0o644 });\n    wroteEvidence = true;\n    fs.writeFileSync(sidecar, `${sha256(bytes)}  ${path.basename(destination)}\\n`, { flag: \"wx\", mode: 0o644 });\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (wroteEvidence) fs.unlinkSync(destination);\n    throw error;\n  }\n  return { path: destination, sha256: sha256(bytes), sidecar };\n}\n\nfunction readArgs(argv) {\n  if (argv.length !== 2 || argv[0] !== \"--config\") throw new Error(\"usage: node eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs --config <private-config.json>\");\n  return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(argv[1], \"utf8\"));\n}\n\nif (process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]) === path.resolve(new URL(import.meta.url).pathname)) {\n  try {\n    const config = readArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n    const evidence = await runToolGrammarMatrix(config);\n    process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({ candidate: evidence.candidate, providers: evidence.endpoints.map(({ provider, passed, totals }) => ({ provider, passed, totals })) })}\\n`);\n    process.exitCode = evidence.endpoints.every((endpoint) => endpoint.passed) ? 0 : 1;\n  } catch (error) {\n    process.stderr.write(`tool grammar matrix failed: ${String(error?.message ?? error)}\\n`);\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":712954914}},"started_at_ms":1793739447857,"completed_at_ms":1793739448570}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:57:29.837Z","ordinal":82343,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a333-e5ec-75e2-b0da-773c3a481172","call_id":"call_ce9eb5f5987743c7a37586e5c76f01a3","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10520)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"bace15\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.712055529,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7981,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7981)\\nTotal output lines: 430\\n\\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\nindex 224c5d30..0ccd1646 100644\\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\\n \\n-**Status as of 2026-11-03: exact RC2 source and installed-package gates passed; provider-matrix, external CI/review, and publication gates remain open.**\\n+**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\\n This record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\\n \\n-The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished.\\n+The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\\n \\n ## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\\n \\n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.\\n | WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | Package acceptance passed 5/5 tests with isolated HOME and the exact archive; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. The same candidate-bound evidence file is linked in WP-1103. |\\n | WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`. Deterministic evaluators wired into runner and scorer. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts` (9/9 passed). |\\n | WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\\n-| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Integrated in commit `1518780d`. Bounded schema compiler with property type validation and grammar generation. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` (4/4 passed). |\\n+| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\\n | WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\\n \\n ## Release-gate status\\n@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ The approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.\\n | G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\\n | G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\\n | G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\\n-| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite. The live supported-provider endpoint matrix has not been measured on this archive; the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream. | **SOURCE PASS; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\\n+| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | The generator is not connected to any client/p