{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:00:52.326Z","ordinal":82430,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a336-fce6-7841-9805-fb204ec10fc1","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...794 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 9:00pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (17,760t read) | 101,687t work | 83% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2134 v1.1.2 Release Scope Reconciliation and WP-1103 Qualification Gate — PLAN Phase with Concurrent Test Blocker (Nov 2, 12:21 PM)\nS2146 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 AC2 Mount-View Test Implementation, Source Review Approval, Release Docs Integration, and External Suite Monitoring (Nov 2, 12:39 PM)\nS2149 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate: Waiting for Shared Test Host to Clear (Nov 2, 1:16 PM)\nS2150 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate Blocked by Two External PR396 Test Streams (Nov 2, 1:35 PM)\nS2151 v1.1.2 Release — Goal Formally Blocked by Shared Test Host Contention, Awaiting External Test Stream Clearance (Nov 2, 1:45 PM)\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29445 8:30p ✓ WP-1107 Focused GREEN Evidence Saved — TypeScript Build Clean, No Whitespace Issues\n29446 \" ○ WP-1107 Chunk 3 Scope: Deterministic Matrix Evaluator with AC5/AC6 Evidence Schema\n29447 \" ○ eval/ Directory Structure Surveyed — No tool_grammar_matrix Files Exist Yet, eval/ Has Full Evaluator Infrastructure\n29448 \" ○ WP-1107 Plan Chunk 3 Evidence Schema and json_repair_rate.mjs Evaluator Pattern Fully Documented\n29449 8:31p ○ GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST Confirmed: [\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit_file\", \"run_command\"] — Four Fixed Tools for AC5 Matrix\n29450 \" ○ validateToolArguments and HARNESS_TOOLS Locations Confirmed for WP-1107 Chunk 3 Matrix\n29451 \" ○ HARNESS_TOOLS Includes 32 Capabilities — No JSON Schema Validator Dependency (ajv/zod/jsonschema) Found in Package\n29452 8:32p ○ Four Allowlisted Tool Parameter Schemas Fully Documented for AC5 Matrix\n29456 \" ○ parser.ts repairJsonWithClass and parseModelResponse Fully Mapped\n29457 8:33p ○ WP-1107 Implementation Diff Confirmed — Full Change Set in Working Tree\n29458 \" ○ repairJsonWithClass Six-Stage Repair Pipeline Fully Documented\n29459 8:35p ◆ WP-1107 Chunk 3 RED Tests Created: tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs with Five Matrix Test Cases\n29460 \" ○ WP-1107 Chunk 3 Matrix RED Tests Confirmed: All 5 Fail with Exact Failure Modes\n29461 8:36p ✓ WP-1107 Chunk 3 RED Log SHA256 Updated After Test Tweak\n29462 8:38p ◆ WP-1107 Chunk 3 tool_grammar_matrix.mjs Full Implementation Created\n29463 8:40p ✓ WP-1107 Matrix Test Helpers Refactored: identifiedEndpoint Helper and Multi-Provider evidenceWith\n29464 \" ✓ WP-1107 Matrix Runner Test Updated for Three-Provider Coverage and Correct Tool Arguments\n29465 8:41p ● tool_grammar_matrix.mjs: Pass Validation, Provider Count, and Runtime Loading Fixed\n29466 8:42p ◆ WP-1107 Chunk 3 Matrix Evaluator GREEN — All 5 Tests Pass\n29467 8:43p ◆ WP-1107 Matrix Runner Adds Pre-Inference Identity Pinning and Provenance Verification\n29468 \" ✓ Matrix Runner Test Updated to Satisfy verifyInstalledArchive with Valid Provenance File\n29469 8:44p ✓ client_tool_grammar.test.ts Adds getDetectedServerKind Assertion for Matrix Runner Contract\n29470 \" ○ getDetectedServerKind Not Yet Implemented on LocalLlmClient — New RED Failure\n29471 \" ✓ client_tool_grammar.test.ts Adds getDetectedServerKind Assertions for llamacpp and Ollama Paths\n29472 8:45p ○ getDetectedServerKind RED Confirmed for All Three Server Kinds — Implementation Needed in client.ts\n29473 \" ◆ LocalLlmClient Gets getDetectedServerKind(), Ollama Identity Probe, and serverShowCache\n29474 8:46p ✓ discoverAdvertisement Clears Stale Cache Entries and parseOllamaVersion Unit Test Added\n29475 \" ✓ Ollama Negative Identity Test Added: Missing or Malformed /api/version Demotes Kind to unknown\n29476 \" ◆ WP-1107 All 22 Tests GREEN — client_tool_grammar and provider_capabilities Suites Pass\n29477 \" ✓ WP-1107 Chunk 3 Matrix GREEN Log Hash Captured for Qualification Gate\n29478 8:47p ○ TypeScript Build Fails: show.model Property Access on 'object' Type in discoverOllamaIdentity\n29479 \" ✓ writeEvidence Immutability Test Added and vLLM response_format Assertion Added\n29480 8:48p ✓ Matrix Evaluator Tightens Sampling and toolChoice Validation, Passes Temperature to Real Client\n29481 \" ⚷ assertNonSecretMetadata Added to Matrix Evidence Validator — Recursive Sensitive Field Scanner\n29482 8:49p ⚷ Server Flags Credential Scan Added and Secret Metadata Test Case Added\n29483 \" ◆ WP-1107 Chunk 3 Final GREEN — 6/6 Matrix Tests Pass, GREEN Log Hash Locked\n29484 \" ✓ WP-1107 Provider GREEN Log Hash Locked — 22/22 Tests Pass\n29485 8:50p ✓ discoverAdvertisement Server Identity Logic Restructured — llamacpp Also Requires Positive Context Probe\n29486 \" ✓ llamacpp Negative Identity Test Added: Invalid /props Response Demotes Kind to unknown\n29487 8:51p ✓ WP-1107 Provider Final GREEN Log — 23/23 Tests Pass, Hash Locked\n29488 \" ✓ WP-1107 Matrix Final GREEN Hash Updated After Full Implementation Changes\n29489 \" ⚖ WP-1107 Scope Reversal — Work Continues in v1.1.2 Release\n29490 \" ○ GBNF Grammar Module Not Connected to Any Provider Request Path\n29491 \" ○ WP-1107 Working Tree State Confirmed in v112-wp1101-integration Worktree\n29492 \" ○ client.ts WP-1107 Diff Fully Mapped — Provider Identity Probes and Tool Grammar Hook Confirmed\n29493 8:52p ○ run_tests.mjs Includes eval/ Tests — tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs Not Yet Registered\n29494 8:53p ○ FILE_cli_scripts_run_tests.mjs Claim Blocked — codex-root Holds It Since Nov 2\n29495 \" ○ FILE_cli_scripts_run_tests.mjs Claim Is Live — PID 6832 Still Running as codex App-Server\n29496 \" ○ nexus-claims.log Reveals Full WP-1107 Claim State and Prior Deferral Decision\n29497 8:54p ✓ Work State Updated: WP-1107 Scope Conflict Documented with Test Evidence Hashes\n\nAccess 102k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793739652.3261375,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
