result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search4","snippet":"A tool-call parser extracts tool calls from the raw text. ... When schema conformance matters, prefer `tool_choice=\"required\"` or named function calling over `\"auto\"`. ... The","title":"Tool Calling - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.18.2/features/tool_calling/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search5","snippet":"With `tool_choice=\"auto\"`, structural-tag constraints require both `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=true` (the default) and at least one tool with `strict: true`, or a server-side floor set via `--to","title":"Tool Calling - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.33.0/features/tool_calling/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search6","snippet":"A tool-call parser extracts tool calls from the raw text. ... When schema conformance matters, prefer `tool_choice=\"required\"` or named function calling over `\"auto\"`. ... The","title":"Tool Calling - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.21.0/features/tool_calling/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search7","snippet":"or params.get(\"additionalProperties\") is True ... json_schema=tool.function.parameters ... json_schema=True, style=\"glm_xml\", any_order=False ... Required keys missing from `properties` are still trea","title":"structural_tag_registry - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search8","snippet":"\"\"\"Derive native calls to `functions` in the format of the tool call ... the schema of every function's arguments where the template can. ... parameters","title":"response_template_grammar - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/parser/response_template_grammar/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search9","snippet":"json_schema_from_tool = get_json_schema_from_tools( ... # Set structured output params for tool calling ... # tool_choice: \"Forced Function\" or \"required\" will override ... strict=True,","title":"tool_parsers - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.12.0/api/vllm/entrypoints/openai/tool_parsers/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search10","snippet":"json_schema_from_tool = get_json_schema_from_tools( ... # Set structured output params for tool calling ... # tool_choice: \"Forced Function\" or \"required\" will override ... strict=True,","title":"tool_parsers - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.11.2/api/vllm/entrypoints/openai/tool_parsers/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search11","snippet":"### `` `tool_strict_level = 'auto'` `class-attribute` `instance-attribute` ¶ Server-side floor for structural-tag based tool calling, applied on top of the per-tool `strict` field. `auto` follows","title":"cli_args - vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.32.0/api/vllm/entrypoints/launchers/cli_args/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search12","snippet":"In case an argument is supplied using command line and the config file, the value from the commandline will take precedence. ... vLLM supports only","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.2/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search13","snippet":"The `tool_choice` options `auto` and `required` are **not yet supported** but on the roadmap. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.1.post2/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search14","snippet":"In case an argument is supplied using command line and the config file, the value from the commandline will take precedence. ... vLLM supports only","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.0/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search15","snippet":"```text ... For those model, you can manually specify their chat template in the `--chat-template` parameter with the file path to the chat template, or","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.3.post1/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search16","snippet":"vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The tool_choice options auto and required are not yet supported but on the roadmap.","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.4/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.vllm.ai","ref_id":"turn35search17","snippet":"vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The tool_choice options auto and required are not yet supported but on the roadmap.","title":"vLLM","url":"https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.0.post1/pdf/"}]},"started_at_ms":1793740232782,"completed_at_ms":1793740240553}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:10:41.775Z","ordinal":82770,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a33f-fb6f-77a1-9dea-a432d062cb00","call_id":"call_8f3c2ad5e77c44bfaf993ea3a17d51ae","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 9.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\"Tool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Tools with omitted or false `strict` receive broad argument-syntax constraints at levels `auto` and `function`, including for required and named calls. ... The tool-call envelope (markup and function name) is constrained whenever a structural tag applies: always for `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` and named function calling, and for `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` once at least one tool sets `strict: true` or the server raises the floor. ...   * Set `additionalProperties` to `false` for each object in `parameters`. ... When these conditions are met and the selected parser supports structural tags, vLLM constrains the tool-call envelope and pins the argument schema of each tool that sets `strict: true` (or of every tool under `--tool-strict-level parameter`). Otherwise, vLLM extracts tool calls from raw text, so arguments may occasionally be malformed or violate the function's parameter schema.\\n## Constrained Decoding Behavior¶\\n\\nStructural-tag parsers resolve call obligation, grammar activation, and argument-schema enforcement separately. With structural-tag enforcement enabled:\\n\\n`tool_choice` value  | Call obligation  | Structural-tag activation\\n--- | --- | ---\\nNamed function  | Call the selected function  | Always\\n`\\\"required\\\"`  | Produce at least one tool call  | Always\\n`\\\"auto\\\"`  | Tool calls are optional  | When at least one tool sets `strict: true`, or `--tool-strict-level` is `function` or `parameter`\\n`\\\"none\\\"`  | Tool calling is disabled  | Disabled\\n\\nWhen a structural tag applies, each tool's declared parameter schema is enforced only when that tool sets `strict: true` or the server uses `--tool-strict-level parameter`. Tools with omitted or false `strict` receive broad argument-syntax constraints at levels `auto` and `function`, including for required and named calls.\\n\\nFor parsers using schema-derived JSON constraints, required and named calls continue to enforce the declared parameter schemas.\\n\\n### Strict Mode¶\\n\\nStructural-tag constraints have two layers. The tool-call envelope (markup and function name) is constrained whenever a structural tag applies: always for `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` and named function calling, and for `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` once at least one tool sets `strict: true` or the server raises the floor. The argument schema of an individual tool is pinned only when that tool sets `strict: true` (or under `--tool-strict-level parameter`); a tool that omits `strict` keeps its arguments unconstrained, even when another tool in the same request is strict. The `strict` field is supported across all three API surfaces: Chat Completion, Responses, and Anthropic Messages.\\n\\nFor best compatibility with strict schema enforcement, define tool parameter schemas in the OpenAI strict-schema style:\\n\\n  * Set `additionalProperties` to `false` for each object in `parameters`.\\n  * Mark all fields in `properties` as required.\\n  * Represent optional fields by allowing `null`, for example `{\\\"type\\\": [\\\"string\\\", \\\"null\\\"]}`.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; When this option is set, the model will not generate any tool calls and will respond with regular text content only, even if tools are defined in the request. ... `\\\"auto\\\"`  | Only when `strict: true` is set on at least one tool  | Structural-tag parsers constrain tool-call arguments when a tool opts in with `strict: true`. ...   * Set `additionalProperties` to `false` for each object in `parameters`. ... This environment variable only affects structural-tag based tool calling; it does not change schema-derived structured outputs used by named function calling or `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"`. ... With `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"`, schema-level constraint requires both `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=true` (the default) and at least one tool with `strict: true`.\\n\\n`tool_choice` value  | Schema-constrained decoding  | Behavior\\n--- | --- | ---\\nNamed function  | Yes (via structured outputs backend)  | Arguments are guaranteed to be valid JSON conforming to the function's parameter schema.\\n`\\\"required\\\"`  | Yes (via structured outputs backend)  | Same as named function. The model must produce at least one tool call.\\n`\\\"auto\\\"`  | Only when `strict: true` is set on at least one tool  | Structural-tag parsers constrain tool-call arguments when a tool opts in with `strict: true`. Without it, the model generates freely and tool calls are extracted from raw text.\\n`\\\"none\\\"`  | N/A  | No tool calls are produced.\\n\\n### Strict Mode¶\\n\\nFor `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` or named function calling, structural-tag constraints are always applied regardless of the `strict` field. For `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"`, setting `strict: true` on at least one tool opts in to structural-tag constraints; without it, the model generates freely and tool calls are extracted from raw text. The `strict` field is supported across all three API surfaces: Chat Completion, Responses, and Anthropic Messages.\\n\\nFor best compatibility with strict schema enforcement, define tool parameter schemas in the OpenAI strict-schema style:\\n\\n  * Set `additionalProperties` to `false` for each object in `parameters`.\\n  * Mark all fields in `properties` as required.\\n  * Represent optional fields by allowing `null`, for example `{\\\"type\\\": [\\\"string\\\", \\\"null\\\"]}`.\\n\\nvLLM also provides a global toggle via the `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING` environment variable (defaults to `true`). When set to `false`, vLLM does not attach structural tags for tool calling regardless of the per-tool `strict` field. This environment variable only affects structural-tag based tool calling; it does not change schema-derived structured outputs used by named function calling or `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"`.\\n    \\n    `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=false vllm serve ...\\n    `\\n\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.31.0/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; The tool-call envelope (markup and function name) is constrained whenever a structural tag applies: always for `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` and named function calling, and for `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` once at least one tool sets `strict: true` or the server raises the floor. ...   * Set `additionalProperties` to `false` for each object in `parameters`. ... When these conditions are met and the selected parser supports structural tags, vLLM constrains the tool-call envelope and pins the argument schema of each tool that sets `strict: true` (or of every tool under `--tool-strict-level parameter`). Otherwise, vLLM extracts tool calls from raw text, so arguments may occasionally be malformed or violate the function's parameter schema.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.20.2/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; When schema conformance matters, prefer `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` or named function calling over `\\\"auto\\\"`. ... The OpenAI API supports a `strict` field on function definitions. When set to `true`, OpenAI uses constrained decoding to guarantee that tool-call arguments match the function schema, even in `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` mode.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.18.2/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; A tool-call parser extracts tool calls from the raw text. ... When schema conformance matters, prefer `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` or named function calling over `\\\"auto\\\"`. ... The OpenAI API supports a `strict` field on function definitions. When set to `true`, OpenAI uses constrained decoding to guarantee that tool-call arguments match the function schema, even in `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` mode. ... Additional tool parsers will continue to be added in the future.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.33.0/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: 2 days ago; With `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"`, structural-tag constraints require both `VLLM_ENFORCE_STRICT_TOOL_CALLING=true` (the default) and at least one tool with `strict: true`, or a server-side floor set via `--tool-strict-level`. ... When these conditions are met and the selected parser supports structural tags, vLLM constrains the tool-call envelope and pins the argument schema of each tool that sets `strict: true` (or of every tool under `--tool-strict-level parameter`). Otherwise, vLLM extracts tool calls from raw text, so arguments may occasionally be malformed or violate the function's parameter schema. ... For strict tools, required or named tool choice, and structured outputs, it derives a structural-tag grammar from the template.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nTool Calling - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.21.0/features/tool_calling/)\\nciteturn35search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; A tool-call parser extracts tool calls from the raw text. ... When schema conformance matters, prefer `tool_choice=\\\"required\\\"` or named function calling over `\\\"auto\\\"`. ... The OpenAI API supports a `strict` field on function definitions. ... When set to `true`, OpenAI uses constrained decoding to guarantee that tool-call arguments match the function schema, even in `tool_choice=\\\"auto\\\"` mode. ... Additional tool parsers will continue to be added in the future.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nstructural_tag_registry - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry/)\\nciteturn35search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;             or params.get(\\\"additionalProperties\\\") is True ...                 json_schema=tool.function.parameters ...                     json_schema=True, style=\\\"glm_xml\\\", any_order=False ... Required keys missing from `properties` are still treated as required. ... A tool without an explicit `strict` is treated as non-strict: its call envelope is still constrained, but its arguments stay free unless the server level is PARAMETER. ...         A tool without an explicit ``strict`` is treated as non-strict: its call\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nresponse_template_grammar - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/api/vllm/parser/response_template_grammar/)\\nciteturn35search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week;         \\\"\\\"\\\"Derive native calls to `functions` in the format of the tool call ...         the schema of every function's arguments where the template can. ...             parameters = function.get(\\\"parameters\\\") or {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"properties\\\": {}} ...                         field, parameters, strict=True, sorted_arguments=sorted_arguments\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ntool_parsers - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.12.0/api/vllm/entrypoints/openai/tool_parsers/)\\nciteturn35search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 11 months ago;         json_schema_from_tool = get_json_schema_from_tools( ...         # Set structured output params for tool calling ...                 # tool_choice: \\\"Forced Function\\\" or \\\"required\\\" will override ...                     strict=True,\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ntool_parsers - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.11.2/api/vllm/entrypoints/openai/tool_parsers/)\\nciteturn35search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 11 months ago;         json_schema_from_tool = get_json_schema_from_tools( ...         # Set structured output params for tool calling ...                 # tool_choice: \\\"Forced Function\\\" or \\\"required\\\" will override ...                     strict=True,\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ncli_args - vLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/en/v0.32.0/api/vllm/entrypoints/launchers/cli_args/)\\nciteturn35search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; ### `` `tool_strict_level = 'auto'` `class-attribute` `instance-attribute` ¶\\n\\nServer-side floor for structural-tag based tool calling, applied on top of the per-tool `strict` field. `auto` follows the request's tool choice and per-tool strictness; `function` constrains the tool-call envelope (markup and function name) for every request with tools; `parameter` additionally pins argument schemas, as if every tool were `strict: true`.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.2/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; In case an argument is supplied using command line and the config file, the value from the commandline will take precedence. ... vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The `tool_choice` options `auto` and `required` are not yet supported but on the roadmap. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the `tools` parameter. ... Additional tool parsers will continue to be added in the future. ... Note that the Hermes 2 Theta models are known to have degraded tool call quality & capabilities due to the merge step in their creation.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.1.post2/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; The `tool_choice` options `auto` and `required` are **not yet supported** but on the roadmap. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the `tools` parameter. ... Additional tool parsers will continue to be added in the future. ... *Note that the Hermes 2 Theta models are known to have degraded tool call quality & capabilities due to the merge step in their creation. ... - Additional mistral function-calling models are compatible as well.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.6.0/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.2 years ago; In case an argument is supplied using command line and the config file, the value from the commandline will take precedence. ... vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The tool_choice options auto and required are not yet supported but on the roadmap. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the tools parameter. ... - `--tool-call-parser` — select the tool parser to use - currently either hermes or mistral. Additional tool parsers will continue to be added in the future.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.3.post1/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; ```text ... For those model, you can manually specify their chat template in the `--chat-template` parameter with the file path to the chat template, or the template in string form. ... vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The `tool_choice` options `auto` and `required` are not yet supported but on the roadmap.\\n\\nTo use a named function you need to define the function in the `tools` parameter and call it in the `tool_choice` parameter. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the `tools` parameter.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.4/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.2 years ago; vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The tool_choice options auto and required are not yet supported but on the roadmap.\\n\\nTo use a named function you need to define the function in the tools parameter and call it in the tool_choice parameter. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the tools parameter. ... Note: You can either use the ipc=host flag or --shm-size flag to allow the container to access the host’s shared memory. vLLM uses PyTorch, which uses shared memory to share data between processes under the hood, particularly for tensor parallel inference.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nvLLM (https://docs.vllm.ai/_/downloads/en/v0.5.0.post1/pdf/)\\nciteturn35search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; vLLM supports only named function calling in the chat completion API. The tool_choice options auto and required are not yet supported but on the roadmap.\\n\\nTo use a named function you need to define the function in the tools parameter and call it in the tool_choice parameter. ... vLLM will use guided decoding to ensure the response matches the tool parameter object defined by the JSON schema in the tools parameter.\\n\""}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793740241.7751184}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
