{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:12:06.952Z","ordinal":82806,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7b6397cd-d1d4-407e-b1d8-9c31c436b724","process_id":"16685","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"WP-1107 vLLM strict schema compatibility review\" --verdict \"The configured provider-source prefix did not contain the needed strict-schema contract; targeted XERJ searches missed. Official current vLLM documentation clarified that strict tools need all properties required, optional properties nullable, and additionalProperties false. No code was based on the XERJ miss.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"WP-1107 vLLM strict schema compatibility review\" --verdict \"The configured provider-source prefix did not contain the needed strict-schema contract; targeted XERJ searches missed. Official current vLLM documentation clarified that strict tools need all properties required, optional properties nullable, and additionalProperties false. No code was based on the XERJ miss.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"WP-1107 vLLM strict schema compatibility review\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"The configured provider-source prefix did not contain the needed strict-schema contract; targeted XERJ searches missed. Official current vLLM documentation clarified that strict tools need all properties required, optional properties nullable, and additionalProperties false. No code was based on the XERJ miss.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review.md -m \"docs(field-report): wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: WP-1107 vLLM strict schema compatibility review\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-03-wp-1107-vllm-strict-schema-compatibility-review.md.\"\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":47,"nanos":42498421}},"started_at_ms":1793740279907,"completed_at_ms":1793740326950}}
