{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:13:37.697Z","ordinal":82874,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea4e80043081a38c0cabaa6c5ff063","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The vLLM contract confirmed the issue. Strict tool schemas now mark optional parameters as nullable and required, close the top-level object with `additionalProperties: false`, and leave original tool definitions unchanged. The new regression test went RED first, then the focused set passed 32/32 and the build passed. I’m refreshing the disposable snapshot and restarting the full gate against this corrected code."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793740416090,"completed_at_ms":1793740417697}}
