{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:17:27.025Z","ordinal":82993,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a346-2a71-7790-a781-b9e7f6c74692","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for the uncommitted WP-1107 diff in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration`. The qualification document correctly keeps WP-1107 and G1.1-4 incomplete; I found these implementation gaps:\n\n- **Matrix runs can lose failed results.** `runToolGrammarMatrix` calls `validateMatrixEvidence` before writing output, and that validator rejects any endpoint that fails its threshold. A provider miss therefore throws before the exact counts are saved. Preserve structurally valid failure evidence, write it, then return a failing status. See [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:168) and [the runner](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:349).\n\n- **The matrix accepts caller-supplied schemas.** `options.tools` overrides the installed candidate’s tool registry, while `validateTools` checks names and that `parameters` is an object, not that schemas match the candidate’s registered schemas. A config can therefore measure easier custom schemas and still bind the result to the candidate archive. Use the installed schemas for live runs or require a verified schema digest match. See [tool selection](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:277) and [schema validation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:189).\n\n- **The matrix validator disagrees with vLLM’s adapted schema.** The adapter requires optional fields and permits `null` for them, but matrix scoring validates responses against the original schema, which rejects `null`. This can classify schema-valid strict-mode results as invalid and distort the provider metric. Align scoring with the active adapted schema or normalize nullable fields before validating against the original schema. See [strict adaptation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:27) and [argument validation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:43).\n\n- **Streaming request coverage is missing.** The plan requires testing streaming and non-streaming request construction, but the client tests only cover non-streaming paths; the streaming path applies the adapter separately. Add a captured streaming request regression. See [the plan](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:35) and [streaming adaptation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/client.ts:1589).\n\nI reviewed the source and docs read-only. I did not run tests; the reported 32 focused passes and build do not cover these gaps."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793740647.0255404,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2847}}
