{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:27:28.809Z","ordinal":83263,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea51bf602481a39b949b79011a10cc","usage":{"input_tokens":151039,"cached_input_tokens":150784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":47,"reasoning_output_tokens":30,"total_tokens":151086},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":16031152,"cached_input_tokens":15814912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":50316,"reasoning_output_tokens":25871,"total_tokens":16081468},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1683321820,"cached_input_tokens":1670547968,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3145193,"reasoning_output_tokens":1543595,"total_tokens":1686467013}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:27:30.156Z","ordinal":83264,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a34f-5e6c-73c0-ad40-44284fd401ca","call_id":"call_2f93d911261a4431a25b674af9863f27","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The safest integration base is the clean release worktree at `f4f89734` on `v1/v112-release`. The WP-1107 provider work is still uncommitted in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration` at `3eea888a`; preserve and review that diff before integrating it.\\n\\nThe `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` claim is still formally held by codex-root under its old WP-1103/1104 scope. Its heartbeat is stale and no test runner is active, but no release or broken-claim entry exists. The proposed CLI test belongs under `cli/test/*.test.ts`, which the runner already discovers. The standalone eval matrix test is outside that discovery path, so run it as a separately claimed gate or reconcile the runner claim before adding it to the suite.\\n\\nThe WP-1107 file claims also remain on the provider worktree despite the later request to defer the work. The user’s instruction to include WP-1107 in v1.1.2 supersedes that deferral; reconcile those claims and the target branch before integration. GATEWAY remains held for RC15 E5, so the real endpoint matrix still needs an explicit handoff before inference.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for the uncommitted WP-1107 diff in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration`. The qualification document correctly keeps WP-1107 and G1.1-4 incomplete; I found these implementation gaps:\\n\\n- **Matrix runs can lose failed results.** `runToolGrammarMatrix` calls `validateMatrixEvidence` before writing output, and that validator rejects any endpoint that fails its threshold. A provider miss therefore throws before the exact counts are saved. Preserve structurally valid failure evidence, write it, then return a failing status. See [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:168) and [the runner](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:349).\\n\\n- **The matrix accepts caller-supplied schemas.** `options.tools` overrides the installed candidate’s tool registry, while `validateTools` checks names and that `parameters` is an object, not that schemas match the candidate’s registered schemas. A config can therefore measure easier custom schemas and still bind the result to the candidate archive. Use the installed schemas for live runs or require a verified schema digest match. See [tool selection](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:277) and [schema validation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:189).\\n\\n- **The matrix validator disagrees with vLLM’s adapted schema.** The adapter requires optional fields and permits `null` for them, but matrix scoring validates responses against the original schema, which rejects `null`. This can classify schema-valid strict-mode results as invalid and distort the provider metric. Align scoring with the active adapted schema or normalize nullable fields before validating against the original schema. See [strict adaptation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:27) and [argument validation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:43).\\n\\n- **Streaming request coverage is missing.** The plan requires testing streaming and non-streaming request construction, but the client tests only cover non-streaming paths; the streaming path applies the adapter separately. Add a captured streaming request regression. See [the plan](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:35) and [streaming adaptation](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/client.ts:1589).\\n\\nI reviewed the source and docs read-only. I did not run tests; the reported 32 focused passes and build do not cover these gaps.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The GBNF generator is **not connected to a provider request path** on candidate `e134dcd5`. Its only references are its definitions in [tool_grammar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:12) and unit tests in [tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:13). The client’s non-streaming, streaming, and native request builders contain no `grammar`, `guided_json`, or `format` field ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1377), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1531), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1858)).\\n\\nThe roadmap requires integration for llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama and a ≥99.5% valid tool-call JSON result across those endpoints ([ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50), [ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58)). The qualification record marks WP-1107 passed based on four compiler tests, while its gate row still says endpoint evidence is pending ([qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32), [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42)). The older roadmap review explicitly deferred WP-1107 due to provider request changes ([ROADMAP-REVIEW.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194)); the user-approved full-roadmap scope supersedes that deferral, but the conflicting record and completion claim need reconciliation.\\n\\nA safe implementation sequence is a reviewed transport plan, followed by test-first request integration for each provider. Likely files are `cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, and provider request-capture tests; provider capability detection may also need adjustment. `client.ts` is actively claimed by codex-root for RC16 work, so coordinate before editing. The grammar module, its tests, `client.test.ts`, and provider-capability file have no active file claims. GATEWAY remains claimed for RC15 E5 work; endpoint inference needs owner coordination. No edits or tests were made.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793741250.1564982}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
