{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:32:40.196Z","ordinal":83373,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a354-1983-7410-9489-11d283d85ad7","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED.** The four previous findings appear addressed: failed matrix counts can be retained, caller-supplied schemas are rejected, scoring uses the adapted schema, and streaming request capture is tested.\n\nOne AC4 gap remains: `discoverAdvertisement` stores `vllm` in the endpoint cache before checking catalog limits, then can return `unsupported` when limits are absent ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/client.ts:1161)). Both request builders apply strict adaptation from that cache anyway ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/client.ts:1452), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/src/client.ts:1607)). AC4 requires unsupported endpoints to keep their existing request shape ([WP-1107-PLAN.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:12)). Clear or avoid caching the provider kind when discovery is unsupported, or otherwise ensure unsupported discovery cannot trigger adaptation; add a regression for this case.\n\nRead-only review; I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793741560.1957355,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2856}}
