{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:36:24.872Z","ordinal":83532,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea53d78ac081a399e11aad7f6451a1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2f63de822bdb43b38b58f2be249ca3ac","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,45p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md;\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1300});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793741783.5535529}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:36:25.028Z","ordinal":83533,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea53d6ce3c81a3abdcb1ac9f06f8e8","usage":{"input_tokens":169293,"cached_input_tokens":168704,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":91,"reasoning_output_tokens":8,"total_tokens":169384},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":22001866,"cached_input_tokens":21760768,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":58351,"reasoning_output_tokens":29884,"total_tokens":22060217},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1689292534,"cached_input_tokens":1676493824,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3153228,"reasoning_output_tokens":1547608,"total_tokens":1692445762}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:36:27.042Z","ordinal":83534,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b9f4c54a-2a6b-4d30-9afe-d4f9741439d3","process_id":"33443","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,45p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,45p' 'docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md;'","name":"CONCURRENCY.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":715359103}},"started_at_ms":1793741786326,"completed_at_ms":1793741787042}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:36:28.550Z","ordinal":83535,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a357-9586-7173-98e8-6a5f80ea0371","call_id":"call_2f63de822bdb43b38b58f2be249ca3ac","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793741788.5507565}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
