{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T22:11:19.172Z","ordinal":84333,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea5c053e2c81a38d28defd42a69695","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The base comparison isolated the cause: generic `/models` entries were triggering an unsolicited `/version` request, which consumed scripted responses in gateway tests. I changed discovery to probe vLLM only when the catalog has the vLLM-specific `max_model_len` marker. The regression test and the previously hung process-lifecycle suite now pass (3/3); I’m including this final fix in peer review and the full gate rerun."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793743877282,"completed_at_ms":1793743879171}}
