{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T22:18:44.156Z","ordinal":84554,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a37e-463b-7840-980c-47aa4f04a598","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...794 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 10:18pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (18,756t read) | 77,188t work | 76% savings\n\n### Nov 3, 2026\nS2267 WP-1107 Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments — Scope Conflict Resolution and Implementation Verification (Nov 3, 8:54 PM)\n29581 9:26p ○ WP-1107 Full Gate Log Shows All Test Suites Passing — Zero Failures Across Rust and CLI\n29582 \" ○ WP-1107 Full Gate Log — Known Infrastructure Test Failures Confirmed (AgentObserver, Tracing, Inference)\n29583 9:27p ○ review_delta Sub-Agent: Four Implementation Gaps in WP-1107 Diff — CHANGES_REQUESTED\n29584 9:28p ○ Full Gate Run Hits Symlink Error on \"alias/file\" — Cannot Save Worktree State\n29585 \" ○ Full Gate Log Failure Pattern Mapped — All Failures Are Infrastructure/Network Tests, Not WP-1107 Regressions\n29594 9:33p ○ client_tool_grammar.test.ts Full Test Inventory — 9 Tests Covering All Provider Paths and Fallback\n29595 \" ◆ New Test: Unsupported vLLM Discovery Does Not Enable Strict Tool Adaptation\n29596 \" ○ New AC4 Test RED — serverKindCache Retains \"vllm\" Even When discoverAdvertisement Returns \"unsupported\"\n29597 \" ● serverKindCache No Longer Set on Unsupported Advertisement Path — Only Set on Confirmed Supported Outcomes\n29598 \" ◆ WP-1107 Full Suite GREEN — 37/37 Tests Pass Including New AC4 Negative Test, Build Clean\n29599 9:35p ○ Full Gate Run Completed — Log Ends With Terminal Acceptance Test Finishing\n29600 9:37p ✓ v1.1.2-release Work State Updated — WP-1107 Implementation Approved, Full Gate Active\n29603 9:42p ○ WP-1107 Full Gate Run Complete — 2159 Lines, Ends With \"💭 Assistant: done\"\n29604 9:43p ○ Gate Log Still Growing — New Failures: CTX-03 and Objective-Findings Persistence Tests\n29605 9:47p ○ Gate Log at 2844 Lines — Additional Failures: Memory/Findings Tests and HTTP 429 Rate Limiting\n29606 9:59p ○ Gate Run Stuck in Provider Recovery Loop — Network Error With Checkpoint Save ENOENT\n29607 10:01p ○ Gate Run Stuck — Provider Recovery Loop Interleaved with Completed Tests, Exponential Backoff Growing\n29608 10:02p ⚖ WP-1107 Scope Reversal Overridden by User — Include in v1.1.2 Release\n29609 \" ○ Gate Run Stuck on process_lifecycle.test.ts — Node Process Blocking in ep_poll for 4+ Minutes\n29610 \" ○ process_lifecycle.test.ts Uses startGateway Fixture — Gate Stall Is a Provider Fixture Hang, Not a Network Timeout\n29611 \" ○ No sleep 30.x Subprocesses Running — process_lifecycle.test.ts Stall Is Pre-Sleep, Not Post-Cancel\n29612 10:05p ✓ Gate Run Restarted — Previous Stuck Run Abandoned, New make test Launched\n29613 \" ○ Gate Run Completed — Previous PIDs Gone, Two \"Promise Still Pending\" Failures at End\n29614 10:06p ✓ Baseline Worktree Created at 3eea888a for WP-1107 Failure Comparison\n29615 \" ○ process_lifecycle.test.ts Passes GREEN on Baseline — 3/3 Tests Pass in 12 Seconds\n29616 10:07p ○ process_lifecycle.test.ts Fails on WP-1107 Branch — Provider Recovery Loop Causes Timeout Failures\n29618 10:08p ○ parseAdvertisement Classifies Mock Gateway as \"vllm\" — Root Cause of process_lifecycle Regression\n29619 10:09p ○ WP-1107 Discovery Probes /version on Every Unknown Server — Mock Fixture Receives Unexpected Probe\n29620 \" ○ process_lifecycle.test.ts Fails on WP-1107 After 157 Seconds — Assertion at Line 114 and Event Loop Resolved Error\n29621 \" ○ process_lifecycle Failure Root Cause: \"Inference provider temporarily unavailable\" — All 3 Tests Fail Due to Provider Error\n29622 \" ● client_tool_grammar.test.ts Fixed — Generic Catalog Must Not Trigger vLLM /version Probe\n29623 10:10p ○ client_tool_grammar.test.ts Has One Remaining context_length Entry at Line 135\n29624 \" ○ New Test RED — discoverAdvertisement Still Probes /version for Generic Catalogs (versionRequests=1, Expected 0)\n29625 \" ● discoverAdvertisement Fixed — /version Probe Now Gated on advertised?.via === \"vllm\"\n29626 \" ◆ WP-1107 Full Suite GREEN — 37/37 Unit Tests + 10/10 Matrix Tests Pass, Build Clean After Fix\n29627 10:11p ● process_lifecycle.test.ts Now Passes GREEN on WP-1107 Branch — 3/3 Tests Pass in 8.6 Seconds\n29629 \" ✓ WP-1107 Fix Synced to Qualification Worktree — client.ts and client_tool_grammar.test.ts Copied, dist Rsynced\n29630 10:12p ○ vLLM ModelCard Always Sets owned_by=\"vllm\" — Stronger Identity Signal Available Than max_model_len Alone\n29631 10:13p ○ WP-1107 AC4 Explicitly Requires /version Handshake for vLLM Identity — owned_by=\"vllm\" Catalog Field Is Insufficient\n29632 \" ◆ New AC4 Test: vLLM owned_by Marker With Null context_length Still Requires /version Handshake\n29633 \" ○ New Test RED — discoverAdvertisement Returns \"supported\" for vLLM Entry With null context_length After /version Succeeds\n29634 \" ○ parseAdvertisement Maps context_length:null to via:\"vllm\" With contextLength:null — Null Is Preserved as Capacity Signal\n29635 10:14p ✓ Test Fixture Corrected — owned_by=\"vllm\" With No Capacity Fields (Bare Catalog) Tests Generic Probe Guard\n29636 \" ○ Bare vLLM Catalog Entry Confirmed — No /version Probe Sent (versionRequests=0), Test Assertion Needs Fixing\n29637 \" ✓ discoverAdvertisement Extended — owned_by=\"vllm\" Catalog Marker Also Triggers /version Probe\n29638 \" ◆ WP-1107 Full Suite GREEN — 38/38 Unit Tests + 10/10 Matrix Tests Pass, Build Clean\n29640 10:16p ○ Two Concurrent Gate Runs Active — WP-1107 Qualification and Integration Branch Running Simultaneously\n29641 \" ○ Integration Branch Gate Run Spawned by make test — Parent PID 6832 Is the Primary Session\n29642 10:17p ✓ Latest WP-1107 Fixes Synced to Qualification Worktree and New Gate Run Started\n29643 \" ✓ Previous Qualification Gate Run Killed — SIGINT Sent to PID 2250289\n\nAccess 77k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793744324.1559834,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
