{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:05:12.971Z","ordinal":85600,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c6b0beb3-3249-4c79-96fe-a5703969cdb7","process_id":"44132","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^✖ ' /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final4.log | head -n 50; rg -n -A18 '^✖ failing tests:' /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final4.log | head -n 110"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^✖ ' /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final4.log","query":"^✖ ","path":"wp1107-full-gate-final4.log"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -A18 '^✖ failing tests:' /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final4.log","query":"^✖ failing tests:","path":"wp1107-full-gate-final4.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"486:✖ Inference request aborted by operator\n517:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 400): model-error-payload-marker\n642:✖ Inference error: Inference request failed: fetch failed (cause: ECONNREFUSED <- ECONNREFUSED: connect ECONNREFUSED ::1:1234 <- ECONNREFUSED: connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:1234)\n723:✖ Working: fetch_web\n724:✖ Tool Error:\n733:✖ Working: fetch_web\n734:✖ Tool Error:\n743:✖ Working: fetch_web\n744:✖ Tool Error:\n1195:✖ Inference provider overloaded\n2839:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\"error\":{\"message\":\"rate limited\",\"type\":\"rate_limit_exceeded\"}}\n2879:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\"error\":{\"message\":\"rate limited\",\"type\":\"rate_limit_exceeded\"}}\n3003:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\"error\":{\"message\":\"rate limited\",\"type\":\"rate_limit_exceeded\"}}\n3072:✖ Working: task_completed\n3074:✖ Working: task_completed\n3076:✖ Working: task_completed\n3078:✖ Working: task_completed\n3080:✖ Working: task_completed\n3414:✖ versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels (409.346728ms)\n3421:✖ pytest candidate imports cannot inspect hidden Python sources (591.029136ms)\n3426:✖ hardened checks: a correct change passes in a fresh workspace; a test-script change refuses the checks (286.95034ms)\n3427:✖ hardened checks hide oracle source from candidate code and reject empty-output commands (314.460805ms)\n3430:✖ Go and Rust hidden sources are absent during build audits and test execution (105.746024ms)\n3432:✖ a correct deliverable passes the hidden test; a wrong one fails it and is never VERIFIED (A1) (332.724949ms)\n3434:✖ a standalone server-profile run discovers context instead of forcing the harness default (296.978251ms)\n3435:✖ T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out and the task still completes; the fault is recorded (340.906433ms)\n3436:✖ T4 smoke: a reply cut at the output limit is never run as a tool call, and the run ends truthfully (326.812946ms)\n3437:✖ peer run records the executable version and effective budget (2020.301891ms)\n3438:✖ Goose adapter applies the matched turn, context, output, and temperature budgets (1749.239845ms)\n3460:✖ Python black-box oracle uses only pinned offline Go and Rust toolchains, or fails preflight (62.379699ms)\n3465:✖ qualification runtime mounts cannot overlap the task tree, held-out store, or private validator paths (755.601353ms)\n3467:✖ resource contract: candidate memory, processes, storage and CPU are kernel-bounded and every process is reaped (112.335137ms)\n3469:✖ candidate sandbox and resource supervisor compose around a staged repository (251.447324ms)\n3470:✖ repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned baseline commit (1041.644993ms)\n3473:✖ task setup and validators run with cleared env, no network, confined filesystem, bounded output and timeout (329.313414ms)\n3474:✖ candidate namespace cannot read host files or bypass pinned compilers with absolute paths (237.616325ms)\n3490:✖ a T3 run drives the real sidecar through the sandbox: steering applied, probe answered and scored (342.077249ms)\n3491:✖ the real T3 runner fails closed when a candidate-created fact path symlinks to an external canary (298.654983ms)\n3495:✖ the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem (3.5563ms)\n3568:✖ Inference provider temporarily unavailable\n3581:✖ Working: write_file\n3582:✖ Tool Error:\n3587:✖ Working: write_file\n3588:✖ Tool Error:\n3898:✖ Working: task_completed\n3899:✖ Tool Error:\n3989:✖ Working: task_completed\n3990:✖ Tool Error:\n4269:✖ Spawning isolated subagent: \"write to the original checkout...\"\n4270:✖ Tool Error:\n11615:✖ failing tests:\n11616-\n11617-test at test/eval_dataset.test.ts:27:1\n11618-✖ versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels (409.346728ms)\n11619-  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: gatewayModelRequests=0 gatewayChatRequests=0\n11620-  \n11621-  file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/eval/isolate.mjs:774\n11622-    if (mountProblem) throw new Error(mountProblem);\n11623-                            ^\n11624-  \n11625-  Error: candidate runtime path is outside its explicit allowlist: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/cli/node_modules/@esbuild\n11626-      at isolatedProcessArgv (file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/eval/isolate.mjs:774:27)\n11627-      at resolveAgentIdentity (file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/eval/run.mjs:435:18)\n11628-      at file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/eval/run.mjs:146:81\n11629-      at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:377:25)\n11630-      at async onImport.tracePromise.__proto__ (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:671:26)\n11631-      at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:101:5)\n11632-  \n11633-  Node.js v24.11.1\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41341}},"started_at_ms":1793747112970,"completed_at_ms":1793747112971}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:05:13.688Z","ordinal":85601,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c950cc8f-2303-414d-b4cf-fda5b58691de","process_id":"20476","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md; sed -n '1,180p' cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts; sed -n '1,125p' cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md","name":"WP-1107-PLAN.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts","name":"server_context_discovery.test.ts","path":"cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,125p' cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts","name":"standalone_profiles.test.ts","path":"cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported inference engine, I need registered tool argument schemas passed through the provider's native constrained-tool path so tool calls arrive as schema-valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\n- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\n- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\n- **AC6:** On each supported endpoint, 20 of the 200 attempts (five per tool) use a pinned reasoning-capable model and exercise a tool call after non-empty `<think>...</think>` reasoning. The installed client must preserve the provider's reasoning signal and the tool arguments must satisfy the selected tool's active parameter schema in the same response. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; live `WP-1107 hybrid reasoning and tool-call matrix`. This verifies reasoning/tool grammar coexistence, not reasoning quality or task correctness.\n\n**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\n\n**Dependencies:** Existing schema-derived grammar generator and `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; source implementation is otherwise independent. AC5 and AC6 depend on an approved shared inference window, pinned server/model configurations, and the exact candidate package.\n\n**Scope reconciliation:** The user selected the full failed v1.1.0 WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2. This explicit scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. It does not waive the required provider references, test gates, review, or G1.1-4 endpoint evidence.\n\n**Roadmap contract reconciliation:** Keep the existing dynamic GBNF compiler and its allowlist/schema tests as the deterministic schema-to-grammar implementation. Provider transport must use each server's compatible native tool path: llama.cpp rejects a caller grammar beside native tools but builds a dynamic tool grammar from their schemas; vLLM consumes `strict: true` through its structural-tag tool parser; Ollama carries tool schemas in `tools`, separately from response-level `format`. The hybrid `<think>...</think>` + tool-call requirement is not dropped: AC6 and the live matrix require a reasoning-plus-tool attempt on each exact endpoint. The provider's model/template/parser must build or accept that hybrid grammar; any endpoint that cannot pass AC6 remains unsupported and blocks G1.1-4. Do not claim that successful JSON syntax alone satisfies schema validity.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n**Chunk 1 — Provider request adapter**\n\n- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented native tool-schema behavior only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\n- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\n- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\n- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases. AC1 and AC3 are baseline-preserving regression guards; AC2 is expected to fail before implementation.\n- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning a non-empty JSON `version` string plus the selected model in `/v1/models` (`wp1107-vllmserve` `basic.py:54-55`). A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation until that endpoint responds with the vLLM version contract. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\n- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\n\n**Chunk 2 — Client integration**\n\n- Attach the vLLM strict-tool adaptation to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling. Preserve the current native tool-schema request for llama.cpp and Ollama.\n- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\n- Tests: captured request-body tests for each applicable transport path, plus AC4 fallback.\n- Retrieved: XERJ `nexus-cli` definitions locate `LocalLlmClient.chatCompletionOnce` at `client.ts:1330`, `discoverAdvertisement` at `client.ts:1133`, and `serverKindOf` at `core/provider_capabilities.ts:75`. The source index is refreshed from committed `origin/main`; exact candidate request construction was cross-checked locally at `cli/src/client.ts:1330-1393` and discovery at `cli/src/client.ts:1133-1202` because the candidate has uncommitted work.\n\n**Chunk 3 — Candidate endpoint matrix**\n\n- Add a deterministic runner and schema validator. Fake-provider/serialization tests validate request construction and evidence validation only; they do not count as live endpoint measurements.\n- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\n- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\n- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Each provider's pinned configuration must use a reasoning-capable model/template/parser; 20 attempts (five for each tool) must exercise the hybrid reasoning/tool path. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no provider-specific adaptation.\n- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; reasoning-present counts for hybrid attempts; native-valid/repaired/schema-invalid/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version. Store the finalized evidence file's SHA-256 in the detached `.sha256` sidecar and qualification record (the JSON cannot hash itself). Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, reasoning text, and other secrets.\n- Test/evidence: AC5's syntax threshold, schema-valid arguments, and zero schema-invalid/invalid requirement apply to all 200 attempts per provider. AC6 additionally requires non-empty reasoning signal and schema-valid tool arguments on every hybrid attempt. This measures argument validity and hybrid grammar coexistence; it does not certify tool selection, reasoning quality, or task correctness.\n- Dependency: explicit release of the shared `GATEWAY` claim before any inference.\n\n## Risks and reference queries\n\n- `llama.cpp` caller `grammar` cannot accompany native tools; its chat parser builds tool grammars from the supplied function schemas. Do not pass the generated per-tool GBNF as a top-level request field.\n- Ollama's `format` constrains the assistant response, while native tool calls use `tools`. Do not treat response-level JSON schema as tool-argument grammar.\n- vLLM's `strict: true` depends on its strict-tool parser path and server configuration. The request capture test proves serialization, while the exact installed endpoint matrix is required to prove that the chosen server configuration enforces the tool schema.\n- The approved plan's previous request-field assumptions are superseded by these primary-source findings; obtain fresh independent plan review before writing implementation or tests.\n- G1.1-4 requires a real endpoint matrix. A loopback mock proves serialization only and cannot satisfy the 99.5% metric.\n- The provider lane’s immutable server and model identities are not yet confirmed because the shared `GATEWAY` claim is still held by the RC15 stream. Treat them as a pre-run gate: record and peer-review the three exact identities/configurations in the matrix plan before starting any provider call; do not substitute mutable tags or infer identity from an endpoint URL.\n/**\n * Standalone context sizing (REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-102 classification, PRV-06/07): servers whose OpenAI-style catalog\n * lists no limits (llama.cpp server, LM Studio, Ollama) are asked for the context they loaded, instead of Nexus\n * assuming 65536; their context-overflow errors are classified as capacity rejections.\n * Response shapes follow each server's documented API: llama.cpp `GET /props`, LM Studio `GET /api/v0/models`, Ollama\n * `POST /api/show`.\n */\nimport { test, describe } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport http from \"node:http\";\nimport { LocalLlmClient } from \"../src/client.js\";\nimport { parseServerContext, serverKindOfAdvertisement } from \"../src/core/provider_capabilities.js\";\nimport { classifyHttpFailure, providerHints } from \"../src/core/provider_recovery.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"server context shapes\", () => {\n  test(\"llama.cpp /props: the runtime n_ctx, not the training size\", () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(parseServerContext(\"llamacpp\", { default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 8192 }, model_path: \"x.gguf\" }, \"m\"), { via: \"llamacpp\", contextLength: 8192, tokenize: false });\n  });\n  test(\"LM Studio /api/v0/models: the loaded context of the selected model\", () => {\n    const body = { data: [{ id: \"other\", loaded_context_length: 2048 }, { id: \"qwen\", max_context_length: 32768, loaded_context_length: 4096 }] };\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"lmstudio\", body, \"qwen\")?.contextLength, 4096);\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"lmstudio\", { data: [{ id: \"qwen\", max_context_length: 32768 }] }, \"qwen\")?.contextLength, 32768);\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"lmstudio\", body, \"missing\"), undefined);\n  });\n  test(\"Ollama /api/show: num_ctx when set, else the model's context length\", () => {\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"ollama\", { parameters: \"stop \\\"<|im_end|>\\\"\\nnum_ctx 16384\\n\", model_info: { \"qwen2.context_length\": 32768 } }, \"m\")?.contextLength, 16384);\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"ollama\", { model_info: { \"llama.context_length\": 131072 } }, \"m\")?.contextLength, 131072);\n  });\n  test(\"unknown shapes advertise nothing\", () => {\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"llamacpp\", { hello: 1 }, \"m\"), undefined);\n    assert.equal(parseServerContext(\"ollama\", null, \"m\"), undefined);\n  });\n});\n\nasync function server(routes: Record<string, (req: http.IncomingMessage) => unknown>): Promise<{ url: string; seen: string[]; close: () => Promise<void> }> {\n  const seen: string[] = [];\n  const s = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n    seen.push(`${req.method} ${req.url}`);\n    const key = `${req.method} ${req.url}`;\n    const route = Object.hasOwn(routes, key) ? routes[key] : undefined;\n    if (typeof route !== \"function\") {\n      res.writeHead(404);\n      return void res.end(\"not found\");\n    }\n    res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\");\n    res.end(JSON.stringify(route(req)));\n  });\n  await new Promise<void>((r) => s.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => r()));\n  return { url: `http://127.0.0.1:${(s.address() as any).port}/v1`, seen, close: () => new Promise((r) => s.close(() => r())) };\n}\n\ndescribe(\"discovery against a local server\", () => {\n  test(\"request paths cannot dispatch inherited route properties\", async () => {\n    let inheritedCalls = 0;\n    const routes = Object.create({\n      \"GET /v1/prototype\": () => {\n        inheritedCalls += 1;\n        return { unsafe: true };\n      },\n    }) as Record<string, (req: http.IncomingMessage) => unknown>;\n    const srv = await server(routes);\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch(`${srv.url}/prototype`);\n      assert.equal(response.status, 404);\n      assert.equal(await response.text(), \"not found\");\n      assert.equal(inheritedCalls, 0);\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n\n  test(\"a llama.cpp server's /props context is discovered when its catalog lists no limits\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({\n      \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"llamacpp\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 131072 } }] }),\n      \"GET /props\": () => ({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 4096 } }),\n    });\n    try {\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(found.state, \"supported\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \"llamacpp\");\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \"llamacpp\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 4096);\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n  test(\"an LM Studio server's /api/v0/models context is discovered\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({\n      \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"organization_owner\" }] }),\n      \"GET /api/v0/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", loaded_context_length: 4096, max_context_length: 32768 }] }),\n    });\n    try {\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(found.state, \"supported\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \"lmstudio\");\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \"lmstudio\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 4096);\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen.slice(1), [\"GET /api/v0/models\"]);\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n  test(\"an Ollama server is recognised from its catalog and asked only through its own endpoint\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({\n      \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"library\" }] }),\n      \"POST /api/show\": () => ({ model_info: { \"qwen2.context_length\": 32768 } }),\n    });\n    try {\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \"ollama\");\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \"ollama\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 32768);\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen.slice(1), [\"POST /api/show\"], \"only the recognised server's endpoint is asked\");\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n  test(\"a vLLM server advertises max_model_len directly in /v1/models\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({\n      \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", max_model_len: 16384 }] }),\n    });\n    try {\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(found.state, \"supported\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \"vllm\");\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \"vllm\");\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 16384);\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen, [\"GET /v1/models\"]);\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n  test(\"subsequent context discovery reuses cached advertisement without hitting probe endpoint again\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({\n      \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"llamacpp\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 131072 } }] }),\n      \"GET /props\": () => ({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 8192 } }),\n    });\n    try {\n      const client = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\n      const first = await client.discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(first.advertised?.contextLength, 8192);\n      const propsCallsBefore = srv.seen.filter((s) => s.startsWith(\"GET /props\")).length;\n      assert.equal(propsCallsBefore, 1);\n      const second = await client.discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(second.advertised?.contextLength, 8192);\n      const propsCallsAfter = srv.seen.filter((s) => s.startsWith(\"GET /props\")).length;\n      assert.equal(propsCallsAfter, 1, \"no second probe made to /props due to caching\");\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n  test(\"an unrecognised server is not probed and stays on labelled defaults\", async () => {\n    const srv = await server({ \"GET /v1/models\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\" }] }) });\n    try {\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n      assert.equal(found.state, \"unsupported\");\n      assert.equal(found.detail, \"catalog lists no limits\");\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen, [\"GET /v1/models\"], \"no guessed endpoints were requested\");\n    } finally {\n      await srv.close();\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"context-overflow classification (ACC-INF-02 table)\", () => {\n  const classify = (status: number, body: string) => classifyHttpFailure(status, providerHints(new Headers(), body), body).condition;\n\n  test(\"llama.cpp exceed_context_size_error is a capacity rejection\", () => {\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: { code: 400, message: \"the request exceeds the available context size, try increasing it\", type: \"exceed_context_size_error\", n_prompt_tokens: 9000, n_ctx: 8192 } });\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \"CAPACITY_REJECTED\");\n  });\n  test(\"vLLM maximum context length message is a capacity rejection\", () => {\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ object: \"error\", message: \"This model's maximum context length is 8192 tokens. However, you requested 9000 tokens\", type: \"BadRequestError\", code: 400 });\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \"CAPACITY_REJECTED\");\n  });\n  test(\"LM Studio context window exceeded body is a capacity rejection\", () => {\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: \"Context window exceeded\", message: \"The model's context window is 4096 tokens, but 5000 were submitted\" });\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \"CAPACITY_REJECTED\");\n  });\n  test(\"Ollama prompt too long body is a capacity rejection\", () => {\n/**\n * Standalone qualification without a second inference host (DEC-16, REQ-PRV-106): the harness's proxy shows Nexus the\n * gateway as a plain OpenAI-compatible server (no limits, no /tokenize, no X-AIHost-* headers), or shaped like\n * llama.cpp, vLLM or Ollama. Nexus's own discovery must then find the context the way it would on that server.\n */\nimport { test, describe, before, after } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport http from \"node:http\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { LocalLlmClient } from \"../src/client.js\";\nimport { classifyHttpFailure, providerHints } from \"../src/core/provider_recovery.js\";\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../..\");\n\ndescribe(\"standalone profiles of the model proxy\", () => {\n  let gateway: http.Server;\n  let url = \"\";\n  const seenAuth: Array<string | undefined> = [];\n  before(async () => {\n    gateway = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      seenAuth.push(req.headers.authorization);\n      req.resume();\n      res.setHeader(\"x-aihost-route\", \"worker=w1;pool=p\");\n      if (req.url === \"/v1/models\") {\n        res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\");\n        return void res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", context_length: 8192, max_completion_tokens: 2048, limits_version: \"lv1\", serving: [{ worker_id: \"w1\" }] }] }));\n      }\n      if (req.url === \"/v1/tokenize\") {\n        res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\");\n        return void res.end(JSON.stringify({ prompt_tokens: 10, source: \"exact\" }));\n      }\n      res.writeHead(400, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n      res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: { message: \"prompt is too long for the context window\", type: \"context_length_exceeded\" } }));\n    });\n    await new Promise<void>((r) => gateway.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => r()));\n    url = `http://127.0.0.1:${(gateway.address() as any).port}/v1`;\n  });\n  after(() => gateway.close());\n\n  const withProxy = async (profile: string, fn: (proxyUrl: string) => Promise<void>) => {\n    const { startModelProxy } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/model_proxy.mjs\"));\n    const proxy = await startModelProxy({ upstream: url, profile, authToken: \"gateway-token\" });\n    try {\n      await fn(proxy.url);\n    } finally {\n      await proxy.close();\n    }\n  };\n  const discover = (proxyUrl: string) => new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: proxyUrl, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1, apiKey: \"local\" } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\n\n  test(\"plain: no limits, no request counting, no gateway headers; the gateway token is added by the proxy\", async () => {\n    await withProxy(\"plain\", async (p) => {\n      const found = await discover(p);\n      assert.equal(found.state, \"unsupported\");\n      assert.equal(found.detail, \"catalog lists no limits\");\n      assert.equal((await fetch(`${p}/tokenize`, { method: \"POST\", body: \"{}\" })).status, 404);\n      const models = await fetch(`${p}/models`);\n      assert.equal(models.headers.get(\"x-aihost-route\"), null);\n      assert.deepEqual((await models.json()).data, [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"organization\" }]);\n      assert.ok(seenAuth.length && seenAuth.every((a) => a === \"Bearer gateway-token\"), \"the gateway saw only the proxy's token\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  for (const [profile, via] of [[\"llamacpp\", \"llamacpp\"], [\"vllm\", \"vllm\"], [\"ollama\", \"ollama\"]] as const) {\n    test(`${profile}: Nexus finds the gateway's real context the way that server reports it`, async () => {\n      await withProxy(profile, async (p) => {\n        const found = await discover(p);\n        assert.equal(found.state, \"supported\", JSON.stringify(found));\n        assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, via);\n        assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 8192);\n        assert.equal(found.advertised?.tokenize, false);\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  test(\"context-overflow errors take the profile's shape and stay capacity rejections\", async () => {\n    for (const profile of [\"llamacpp\", \"vllm\", \"ollama\"]) {\n      await withProxy(profile, async (p) => {\n        const res = await fetch(`${p}/chat/completions`, { method: \"POST\", body: \"{}\" });\n        const body = await res.text();\n        assert.equal(res.status, 400);\n        assert.equal(classifyHttpFailure(400, providerHints(res.headers, body), body).condition, \"CAPACITY_REJECTED\", `${profile}: ${body}`);\n        if (profile === \"llamacpp\") assert.match(body, /exceed_context_size_error/);\n        if (profile === \"vllm\") assert.match(body, /maximum context length is 8192/);\n      });\n    }\n  });\n});\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":777951489}},"started_at_ms":1793747112909,"completed_at_ms":1793747113688}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:05:13.931Z","ordinal":85602,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6f62c747-4dcf-41c6-ba1f-bf7c96b18452","process_id":"2158","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1120,1340p' cli/src/client.ts; sed -n '1,220p' cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts; sed -n '130,225p' cli/test/tokens.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1120,1340p' cli/src/client.ts","name":"client.ts","path":"cli/src/client.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts","name":"provider_capabilities.ts","path":"cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '130,225p' cli/test/tokens.test.ts","name":"tokens.test.ts","path":"cli/test/tokens.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"  public getOutputAllowance(): number {\n    return this.maxOutputTokens;\n  }\n\n  /** The gateway's report on the most recent admitted inference request (headers), when it sent one. */\n  public getLastAdmission(): AdmissionReport | undefined {\n    return this.lastAdmission;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * This connection's `/models` entry for the selected model, read from the active endpoint only (never a fallback or\n   * another provider: capability discovery is scoped to the connection in use). Not content-bearing.\n   * `unsupported`: the provider has no catalog or does not list the model; `unavailable`: it could not be read now.\n   */\n  async discoverAdvertisement(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<{ state: \"supported\" | \"unsupported\" | \"unavailable\"; advertised?: Advertisement; detail?: string }> {\n    const ep = this.endpoint;\n    LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.delete(ep);\n    LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.delete(`${ep}::${this.model}`);\n    LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.delete(`${ep}::${this.model}`);\n    if (this.conn.protocol !== \"openai-chat\") return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: `${this.conn.protocol} connection` };\n    const url = `${ep}/models`;\n    try {\n      await this.prepareCredential(ep);\n      const res = await fetch(url, {\n        // Marked so providers (and their logs) can tell a capability read from an availability probe.\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(10_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n      });\n      if (res.status === 404) return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: \"no /models catalog\" };\n      if (!res.ok) return { state: \"unavailable\", detail: `HTTP ${res.status}` };\n      const data = (await res.json()) as { data?: Array<Record<string, any>> };\n      const entry = Array.isArray(data?.data) ? data.data.find((e) => e?.id === this.model) : undefined;\n      if (!entry) return { state: \"unsupported\", detail: `model ${this.model} not listed` };\n      const advertised = parseAdvertisement(entry);\n      let entryKind = advertised?.serverKind ?? serverKindOf(entry);\n      const vllmCatalogMarker = advertised?.via === \"vllm\" || (typeof entry.owned_by === \"string\" && entry.owned_by.toLowerCase() === \"vllm\");\n      if (!this.conn.providerId) {\n        if (entryKind === \"llamacpp\" && (process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE === \"0\" || !(await this.discoverServerContext(entry, signal)))) {\n          entryKind = \"unknown\";\n        } else if (entryKind === \"ollama\" && (process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE === \"0\" || !(await this.discoverOllamaIdentity(signal)))) {\n          entryKind = \"unknown\";\n        } else if (vllmCatalogMarker && entryKind === \"unknown\" && process.env.NEXUS_SERVER_PROBE !== \"0\" && await this.discoverVllmVersion(signal)) {\n          entryKind = \"vllm\";\n        }\n      }\n      if (!advertised || (advertised.contextLength === undefined && advertised.maxCompletionTokens === undefined)) {\n        // An OpenAI-style catalog without limits (llama.cpp, LM Studio, Ollama): ask the server itself what it loaded.\n        // Only for a plain endpoint: cloud provider connections have no such endpoints.\n        const local = this.conn.providerId || entryKind === \"unknown\" ? undefined : await this.discoverServerContext(entry, signal);\n        if (local) {\n          LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, local.serverKind ?? entryKind);\n          return { state: \"supported\", advertised: local };\n        }\n        return { state: \"unsupported\", advertised, detail: \"catalog lists no limits\" };\n      }\n      LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.set(ep, entryKind);\n      return { state: \"supported\", advertised };\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return { state: \"unavailable\", detail: redactSecrets(String(err?.message ?? err)).slice(0, 160) };\n    }\n  }\n\n  private static serverContextCache = new Map<string, Advertisement>();\n  private static serverKindCache = new Map<string, ServerKind>();\n  private static serverShowCache = new Map<string, unknown>();\n\n  /** Provider identity detected for the active endpoint after capability discovery; unknown until a positive handshake. */\n  getDetectedServerKind(): ServerKind {\n    return LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(this.endpoint) ?? \"unknown\";\n  }\n\n  private async discoverVllmVersion(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<string | undefined> {\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const url = `${root}/version`;\n    try {\n      await this.prepareCredential(this.endpoint);\n      const res = await fetch(url, {\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n      });\n      if (!res.ok) return undefined;\n      return parseVllmVersion(await res.json());\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  private async discoverOllamaIdentity(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<boolean> {\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const versionUrl = `${root}/api/version`;\n    const showUrl = `${root}/api/show`;\n    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n    LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.delete(cacheKey);\n    try {\n      await this.prepareCredential(this.endpoint);\n      const versionResponse = await fetch(versionUrl, {\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(versionUrl), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n      });\n      if (!versionResponse.ok || !parseOllamaVersion(await versionResponse.json())) return false;\n      const showResponse = await fetch(showUrl, {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(showUrl), \"content-type\": \"application/json\", \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n        body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }),\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n      });\n      if (!showResponse.ok) return false;\n      const show = await showResponse.json();\n      if (!show || typeof show !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(show)) return false;\n      const showRecord = show as Record<string, unknown>;\n      if (typeof showRecord.model === \"string\" && showRecord.model !== this.model) return false;\n      LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.set(cacheKey, show);\n      return true;\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\n   * `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`) on the endpoint's origin with the same credential and a 2 s\n   * limit. The server is recognised from its catalog entry first, so an unrecognised server is never probed. Not\n   * content-bearing. Undefined when the server is not recognised or does not answer with a context size.\n   */\n  private async discoverServerContext(entry: Record<string, any>, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<Advertisement | undefined> {\n    const kind = serverKindOf(entry);\n    if (kind !== \"llamacpp\" && kind !== \"lmstudio\" && kind !== \"ollama\") return undefined;\n    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n    const cached = LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.get(cacheKey);\n    if (cached) return cached;\n    if (kind === \"ollama\" && LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.has(cacheKey)) {\n      const found = parseServerContext(kind, LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.get(cacheKey), this.model);\n      if (found) LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\n      return found;\n    }\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const probes: Array<{ kind: \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\"; url: string; init?: RequestInit }> = [\n      { kind: \"llamacpp\" as const, url: `${root}/props` },\n      { kind: \"lmstudio\" as const, url: `${root}/api/v0/models` },\n      { kind: \"ollama\" as const, url: `${root}/api/show`, init: { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }), headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } } },\n    ].filter((p) => p.kind === kind);\n    for (const probe of probes) {\n      try {\n        const res = await fetch(probe.url, {\n          ...probe.init,\n          headers: { ...(probe.init?.headers as Record<string, string> | undefined), ...this.authorization(probe.url), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n          signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n          ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n        });\n        if (!res.ok) continue;\n        const found = parseServerContext(probe.kind, await res.json(), this.model);\n        if (found) {\n          LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\n          return found;\n        }\n      } catch {\n        if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n      }\n    }\n    return undefined;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Counts the prompt tokens of the request inference would send now, through the connection's `/v1/tokenize`\n   * (advertised by the homelab-ai gateway contract). The body is `outboundChatBody` — the actual outbound messages,\n   * tools, tool_choice and settings, after the same egress quarantine and sanitization — sent to the active endpoint\n   * only, with the same credential scoping, disclosure checks and cancellation as inference. No failover: a counting\n   * failure belongs to this connection and capability, and never moves task content elsewhere.\n   * Throws TokenCountError: `unsupported` (no such endpoint or model), `unavailable` (temporary), `malformed`,\n   * `denied` (credential or disclosure), `aborted`.\n   */\n  async countRequestTokens(messages: ChatMessage[], tools: ToolDefinition[], requestId: string, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<RequestCount> {\n    if (this.conn.providerId || this.conn.protocol !== \"openai-chat\") throw new TokenCountError(\"unsupported\", \"provider connections have no request-counting endpoint\");\n    const ep = this.endpoint;\n    const denial = this.disclosureDenial(ep, requestId);\n    if (denial) throw new TokenCountError(\"denied\", denial.message);\n    if (signal?.aborted) throw new TokenCountError(\"aborted\", \"cancelled\");\n    const kind = LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(ep);\n    const root = ep.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n    const urls = (kind === \"llamacpp\" || kind === \"vllm\") && root !== ep ? [`${ep}/tokenize`, `${root}/tokenize`] : [`${ep}/tokenize`];\n    let body: any;\n    try {\n      await this.prepareCredential(ep, requestId);\n      this.preflight(ep, requestId, JSON.stringify(messages).length + JSON.stringify(tools).length);\n      body = this.outboundChatBody(ep, messages, tools);\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      throw new TokenCountError(\"denied\", boundedProviderText(String(err?.message ?? err)).slice(0, 200));\n    }\n    let res: Response | undefined;\n    let text = \"\";\n    for (let i = 0; i < urls.length; i++) {\n      const url = urls[i];\n      const reqBody = kind === \"llamacpp\" && url === `${root}/tokenize`\n        ? { content: JSON.stringify({ messages: body.messages, ...(body.tools ? { tools: body.tools } : {}) }), ...body }\n        : body;\n      try {\n        res = await fetch(url, {\n          method: \"POST\",\n          headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", ...this.authorization(url), \"X-Request-ID\": requestId, ...this.routingHeaders() },\n          body: JSON.stringify(reqBody),\n          signal: metadataSignal(signal),\n          ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n        });\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        if (signal?.aborted) throw new TokenCountError(\"aborted\", \"cancelled\");\n        throw new TokenCountError(\"unavailable\", boundedProviderText(String(err?.message ?? err)).slice(0, 160));\n      }\n      text = await res.text().catch(() => \"\");\n      if ((res.status === 404 || res.status === 405) && i + 1 < urls.length && !/blocked|capacity/i.test(text)) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      break;\n    }\n    if (!res) throw new TokenCountError(\"unsupported\", \"no tokenize endpoint\");\n/**\n * Optional provider capabilities: context capacity, output allowance and request token counting, discovered from the\n * selected connection where it advertises them, and clearly labelled estimates where it does not.\n *\n * None of this is a prerequisite. A connection that advertises nothing (LM Studio, plain llama.cpp, a cloud provider)\n * runs on the operator's configuration or the client defaults, and every number says which it is. A connection that\n * advertises capacity (the homelab-ai gateway's `/v1/models`: context_length, max_completion_tokens, limits_version,\n * serving workers; vLLM's max_model_len) has it used, refreshed when the model, the advertised limits version, the\n * serving workers or the observed capacity change. A stale client default never overrides valid advertised capacity;\n * an operator's explicit setting below it is kept (it is a choice), above it is capped (it is not physical capacity).\n *\n * Count sources, from strongest to weakest:\n * - `exact_admitted`: the gateway's own count of the request it admitted (inference response headers), after the fact;\n * - `exact_sampled_worker`: `/v1/tokenize` applied the chat template and tokenized the actual outbound request on one\n *   worker of the alias. The current gateway contract samples that worker without the routing and reasoning policy\n *   inference applies, so it is exact for that worker and template, not proven for the worker inference admits;\n * - `gateway_conservative`: the gateway could not tokenize and returned its conservative estimate;\n * - `client_estimate`: Nexus's own estimate (no counting capability, or it is unavailable).\n *\n * The tool-output headroom kept free for the next tool results is a scheduling policy, not a measurement; it is\n * reported separately from the measured prompt and the advertised output allowance.\n */\n\nexport type SizingSource = \"advertised\" | \"operator\" | \"operator_capped_by_advertised\" | \"client_default\";\nexport type CountSource = \"exact_admitted\" | \"exact_sampled_worker\" | \"gateway_conservative\" | \"client_estimate\";\nexport type CapabilityState = \"supported\" | \"unsupported\" | \"unavailable\" | \"unknown\";\n\n/** Built-in client defaults: used only when neither the provider nor the operator gives a value. */\nexport const CLIENT_DEFAULT_CONTEXT = 65_536;\nexport const CLIENT_DEFAULT_OUTPUT = 8_192;\n/** Tool-output headroom policy: min(4096, context/8). A scheduling margin for the next tool results, not capacity. */\nexport function toolHeadroomPolicy(context: number, configured?: number): number {\n  return configured ?? Math.min(4096, Math.floor(context / 8));\n}\n\nexport type ServerKind = \"gateway\" | \"vllm\" | \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\" | \"unknown\";\n\nexport interface Advertisement {\n  /**\n   * Who advertised: the homelab-ai gateway contract, a vLLM-style catalog, a server's own endpoint for its loaded\n   * context (llama.cpp `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`), or an OpenAI-style catalog with no limits.\n   */\n  via: \"aihost_gateway\" | \"vllm\" | \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\" | \"catalog\";\n  serverKind?: ServerKind;\n  /** null: the provider says the capacity is currently unknown (e.g. no serving worker observed). */\n  contextLength?: number | null;\n  maxCompletionTokens?: number;\n  limitsVersion?: string;\n  reasoning?: { mode?: string; budget?: number };\n  workers?: string[];\n  /** The connection's contract includes a request-counting endpoint (/v1/tokenize). */\n  tokenize: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface ProviderCapabilities {\n  model: string;\n  observedAt: string;\n  discovery: CapabilityState;\n  discoveryDetail?: string;\n  advertised?: Advertisement;\n  tokenCounting: CapabilityState;\n  tokenCountingDetail?: string;\n  contextLimit: number;\n  contextSource: SizingSource;\n  outputAllowance: number;\n  outputSource: SizingSource;\n}\n\nconst positiveInt = (v: unknown): number | undefined => (typeof v === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(v) && v > 0 ? Math.floor(v) : undefined);\n\n/**\n * Which server kind an entry positively identifies: gateway (limits_version), llama.cpp (owned_by llamacpp or\n * n_ctx_train meta), LM Studio (organization_owner), Ollama (library or ollama), or unknown. Generic context fields\n * describe capacity, not the server implementation; vLLM is identified separately with its /version response.\n */\nexport function serverKindOf(entry: Record<string, any> | undefined): ServerKind {\n  if (!entry || typeof entry !== \"object\") return \"unknown\";\n  if (typeof entry.limits_version === \"string\" && entry.limits_version.length > 0) return \"gateway\";\n  const owner = typeof entry.owned_by === \"string\" ? entry.owned_by.toLowerCase() : \"\";\n  if (owner === \"llamacpp\" || (entry.meta && typeof entry.meta === \"object\" && \"n_ctx_train\" in entry.meta)) return \"llamacpp\";\n  if (owner === \"organization_owner\") return \"lmstudio\";\n  if (owner === \"library\" || owner === \"ollama\") return \"ollama\";\n  return \"unknown\";\n}\n\n/** The vLLM GET /version contract; capacity fields in a generic model catalog are not identity evidence. */\nexport function parseVllmVersion(body: unknown): string | undefined {\n  if (!body || typeof body !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(body)) return undefined;\n  const version = (body as Record<string, unknown>).version;\n  return typeof version === \"string\" && version.trim().length > 0 ? version.trim() : undefined;\n}\n\n/** The Ollama GET /api/version contract; malformed or empty versions do not identify the endpoint. */\nexport function parseOllamaVersion(body: unknown): string | undefined {\n  if (!body || typeof body !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(body)) return undefined;\n  const version = (body as Record<string, unknown>).version;\n  return typeof version === \"string\" && version.trim().length > 0 ? version.trim() : undefined;\n}\n\nexport function serverKindOfAdvertisement(ad: Advertisement | undefined): ServerKind {\n  if (!ad) return \"unknown\";\n  if (ad.via === \"aihost_gateway\") return \"gateway\";\n  if (ad.via === \"vllm\") return \"vllm\";\n  if (ad.via === \"llamacpp\") return \"llamacpp\";\n  if (ad.via === \"lmstudio\") return \"lmstudio\";\n  if (ad.via === \"ollama\") return \"ollama\";\n  return \"unknown\";\n}\n\n/** Reads one `/models` entry. Unknown shapes yield a catalog advertisement with no limits (never an error). */\nexport function parseAdvertisement(entry: Record<string, any> | undefined): Advertisement | undefined {\n  if (!entry || typeof entry !== \"object\") return undefined;\n  const gateway = typeof entry.limits_version === \"string\" && entry.limits_version.length > 0;\n  const workers = Array.isArray(entry.serving)\n    ? entry.serving.map((s: any) => (typeof s?.worker_id === \"string\" ? s.worker_id : undefined)).filter((w: string | undefined): w is string => Boolean(w)).sort()\n    : undefined;\n  const contextLength = entry.context_length === null ? null : positiveInt(entry.context_length) ?? positiveInt(entry.max_model_len);\n  const reasoning = entry.reasoning && typeof entry.reasoning === \"object\"\n    ? { ...(typeof entry.reasoning.mode === \"string\" ? { mode: entry.reasoning.mode } : {}), ...(positiveInt(entry.reasoning.budget) ? { budget: positiveInt(entry.reasoning.budget) } : {}) }\n    : undefined;\n  return {\n    via: gateway ? \"aihost_gateway\" : contextLength !== undefined ? \"vllm\" : \"catalog\",\n    ...(contextLength !== undefined ? { contextLength } : {}),\n    ...(positiveInt(entry.max_completion_tokens) ? { maxCompletionTokens: positiveInt(entry.max_completion_tokens) } : {}),\n    ...(gateway ? { limitsVersion: entry.limits_version } : {}),\n    ...(reasoning && Object.keys(reasoning).length ? { reasoning } : {}),\n    ...(workers?.length ? { workers } : {}),\n    tokenize: gateway,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * The context a local server says it has loaded, from its own endpoint (REQ-PRV-101): llama.cpp `GET /props`\n * (default_generation_settings.n_ctx: the runtime window, not the model's training size), LM Studio `GET /api/v0/models`\n * (loaded_context_length, else max_context_length), Ollama `POST /api/show` (the num_ctx parameter, else the model's\n * <arch>.context_length). Returns undefined for any other shape.\n */\nexport function parseServerContext(kind: \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\", body: unknown, model: string): Advertisement | undefined {\n  if (!body || typeof body !== \"object\") return undefined;\n  const b = body as Record<string, any>;\n  let contextLength: number | undefined;\n  if (kind === \"llamacpp\") {\n    contextLength = positiveInt(b.default_generation_settings?.n_ctx) ?? positiveInt(b.n_ctx);\n  } else if (kind === \"lmstudio\") {\n    const entry = Array.isArray(b.data) ? b.data.find((e: any) => e?.id === model) : undefined;\n    contextLength = positiveInt(entry?.loaded_context_length) ?? positiveInt(entry?.max_context_length);\n  } else {\n    const fromParameters = typeof b.parameters === \"string\" ? /(?:^|\\n)\\s*num_ctx\\s+(\\d+)/.exec(b.parameters)?.[1] : undefined;\n    const info = b.model_info && typeof b.model_info === \"object\" ? Object.entries(b.model_info).find(([k]) => k.endsWith(\".context_length\"))?.[1] : undefined;\n    contextLength = positiveInt(fromParameters ? Number(fromParameters) : undefined) ?? positiveInt(info);\n  }\n  return contextLength ? { via: kind, contextLength, tokenize: false } : undefined;\n}\n\n/**\n * The context and output limits in effect, and where each came from. `operatorContext` / `operatorOutput` are values\n * the operator set explicitly (undefined otherwise).\n */\nexport function resolveLimits(advertised: Advertisement | undefined, operatorContext?: number, operatorOutput?: number): Pick<ProviderCapabilities, \"contextLimit\" | \"contextSource\" | \"outputAllowance\" | \"outputSource\"> {\n  const adCtx = typeof advertised?.contextLength === \"number\" ? advertised.contextLength : undefined;\n  let contextLimit: number;\n  let contextSource: SizingSource;\n  if (adCtx !== undefined && operatorContext !== undefined) {\n    contextLimit = Math.min(adCtx, operatorContext);\n    contextSource = operatorContext <= adCtx ? \"operator\" : \"operator_capped_by_advertised\";\n  } else if (adCtx !== undefined) {\n    contextLimit = adCtx;\n    contextSource = \"advertised\";\n  } else if (operatorContext !== undefined) {\n    contextLimit = operatorContext;\n    contextSource = \"operator\";\n  } else {\n    contextLimit = CLIENT_DEFAULT_CONTEXT;\n    contextSource = \"client_default\";\n  }\n  const adOut = advertised?.maxCompletionTokens;\n  let outputAllowance: number;\n  let outputSource: SizingSource;\n  if (adOut !== undefined && operatorOutput !== undefined) {\n    outputAllowance = Math.min(adOut, operatorOutput);\n    outputSource = operatorOutput <= adOut ? \"operator\" : \"operator_capped_by_advertised\";\n  } else if (adOut !== undefined) {\n    outputAllowance = adOut;\n    outputSource = \"advertised\";\n  } else if (operatorOutput !== undefined) {\n    outputAllowance = operatorOutput;\n    outputSource = \"operator\";\n  } else {\n    outputAllowance = Math.min(CLIENT_DEFAULT_OUTPUT, Math.floor(contextLimit / 4));\n    outputSource = \"client_default\";\n  }\n  // An output allowance can never take the whole window.\n  outputAllowance = Math.max(1, Math.min(outputAllowance, Math.floor(contextLimit / 2)));\n  return { contextLimit, contextSource, outputAllowance, outputSource };\n}\n\n/** Whether a new advertisement changes what was in effect (model, limits version, workers or capacity). */\nexport function advertisementChanged(before: Advertisement | undefined, after: Advertisement | undefined): boolean {\n  if (!before || !after) return before !== after;\n  return (\n    before.limitsVersion !== after.limitsVersion ||\n    before.contextLength !== after.contextLength ||\n    before.maxCompletionTokens !== after.maxCompletionTokens ||\n    (before.workers ?? []).join(\",\") !== (after.workers ?? []).join(\",\")\n  );\n}\n\nexport interface RequestCount {\n  promptTokens: number;\n  source: CountSource;\n  /** Worker the count was taken on, when the provider said. */\n  workerId?: string;\n  limitsVersion?: string;\n  /** Context the provider reported with the count (the counted worker's). */\n  contextLength?: number;\n  /** Why a stronger source was not available. */\n  detail?: string;\n}\n\n/**\n    assert.ok(countTokens(kana) >= 200, `expected >= 200 tokens for 200 Kana chars, got ${countTokens(kana)}`);\n\n    const digits = \"1234567890\".repeat(100); // 1000 digits\n    assert.equal(countTokens(digits), 1000, \"expected 1 token per digit\");\n\n    const b64 = Buffer.from(\"REDACTED!@#\".repeat(30)).toString(\"base64\");\n    assert.ok(countTokens(b64) >= Math.ceil(b64.length / 3), \"expected at least ceil(len/3) tokens for a base64 run\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"REQ-AGT-118: /tokenize works on llama.cpp (root /tokenize { tokens }) and vLLM (root /tokenize { count })\", async () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(parseTokenizeResponse({ tokens: [10, 20, 30, 40] }), {\n      promptTokens: 4,\n      source: \"exact_sampled_worker\",\n    });\n    assert.deepEqual(parseTokenizeResponse({ count: 128, max_model_len: 16384, tokens: [] }), {\n      promptTokens: 128,\n      source: \"exact_sampled_worker\",\n      contextLength: 16384,\n    });\n\n    const seenUrls: string[] = [];\n    let mode: \"llamacpp\" | \"vllm\" = \"llamacpp\";\n    const srv = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n      seenUrls.push(`${req.method} ${req.url}`);\n      res.setHeader(\"content-type\", \"application/json\");\n      if (req.url === \"/v1/models\") {\n        if (mode === \"llamacpp\") {\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", owned_by: \"llamacpp\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 32768 } }] }));\n        } else {\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \"m\", object: \"model\", max_model_len: 16384 }] }));\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      if (req.url === \"/props\") {\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 8192 } }));\n        return;\n      }\n      if (req.url === \"/tokenize\") {\n        if (mode === \"llamacpp\") {\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ tokens: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] }));\n        } else {\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ count: 42, max_model_len: 16384 }));\n        }\n        return;\n      }\n      res.writeHead(404);\n      res.end(\"not found\");\n    });\n    await new Promise<void>((r) => srv.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", () => r()));\n    const port = (srv.address() as any).port;\n    const endpoint = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`;\n\n    try {\n      const llamaClient = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\n      await llamaClient.discoverAdvertisement();\n      const llamaCount = await llamaClient.countRequestTokens([{ role: \"user\", content: \"hello\" }], [], \"req-1\");\n      assert.equal(llamaCount.promptTokens, 7);\n      assert.equal(llamaCount.source, \"exact_sampled_worker\");\n      assert.ok(seenUrls.includes(\"POST /tokenize\"), \"llama.cpp root /tokenize should be called after /v1/tokenize 404s\");\n\n      mode = \"vllm\";\n      const vllmClient = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint, model: \"m\", workspace: \"/tmp\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\n      await vllmClient.discoverAdvertisement();\n      const vllmCount = await vllmClient.countRequestTokens([{ role: \"user\", content: \"hello\" }], [], \"req-2\");\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.promptTokens, 42);\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.contextLength, 16384);\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.source, \"exact_sampled_worker\");\n    } finally {\n      await new Promise<void>((r) => srv.close(() => r()));\n    }\n  });\n});\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":846113731}},"started_at_ms":1793747113084,"completed_at_ms":1793747113931}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:05:15.189Z","ordinal":85603,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a3a8-dcb5-7b13-8d2e-85df3dd7370d","call_id":"call_d95aa3af9e6746ab842e7644af40e132","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12710)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"25832e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.777921906,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7087,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7087)\\nTotal output lines: 328\\n\\n# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\\n\\n## Specification\\n\\n**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported inference engine, I need registered tool argument schemas passed through the provider's native constrained-tool path so tool calls arrive as schema-valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n\\n- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\\n- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\\n- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\\n- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\\n- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\\n- **AC6:** On each supported endpoint, 20 of the 200 attempts (five per tool) use a pinned reasoning-capable model and exercise a tool call after non-empty `<think>...</think>` reasoning. The installed client must preserve the provider's reasoning signal and the tool arguments must satisfy the selected tool's active parameter schema in the same response. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; live `WP-1107 hybrid reasoning and tool-call matrix`. This verifies reasoning/tool grammar coexistence, not reasoning quality or task correctness.\\n\\n**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Existing schema-derived grammar generator and `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; source implementation is otherwise independent. AC5 and AC6 depend on an approved shared inference window, pinned server/model configurations, and the exact candidate package.\\n\\n**Scope reconciliation:** The user selected the full failed v1.1.0 WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap for v1.1.2. This explicit scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. It does not waive the required provider references, test gates, review, or G1.1-4 endpoint evidence.\\n\\n**Roadmap contract reconciliation:** Keep the existing dynamic GBNF compiler and its allowlist/schema tests as the deterministic schema-to-grammar implementation. Provider transport must use each server's compatible native tool path: llama.cpp rejects a caller grammar beside native tools but builds a dynamic tool grammar from their schemas; vLLM consumes `strict: true` through its structural-tag tool parser; Ollama carries tool schemas in `tools`, separately from response-level `format`. The hybrid `<think>...</think>` + tool-call requirement is not dropped: AC6 and the live matrix require a reasoning-plus-tool attempt on each exact endpoint. The provider's model/template/parser must build or accept that hybrid grammar; any endpoint that cannot pass AC6 remains unsupported and blocks G1.1-4. Do not claim that successful JSON syntax alone satisfies schema validity.\\n\\n## Implementation plan\\n\\n**Chunk 1 — Provider request adapter**\\n\\n- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented native tool-schema behavior only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\\n- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\\n- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\\n- Tests: AC1–AC4 request-shape and identity tests above, including positive provider-handshake fixtures and generic/missing/malformed/mismatched negative cases. AC1 and AC3 are baseline-preserving regression guards; AC2 is expected to fail before implementation.\\n- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning a non-empty JSON `version` string plus the selected model in `/v1/models` (`wp1107-vllmserve` `basic.py:54-55`). A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation until that endpoint responds with the vLLM version contract. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\\n- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\\n\\n**Chunk 2 — Client integration**\\n\\n- Attach the vLLM strict-tool adaptation to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling. Preserve the current native tool-schema request for llama.cpp and Ollama.\\n- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\\n- Tests: captured request-body tests for each applicable transport path, plus AC4 fallback.\\n- Retrieved: XERJ `nexus-cli` definitions locate `LocalLlmClient.chatCompletionOnce` at `client.ts:1330`, `discoverAdvertisement` at `client.ts:1133`, and `serverKindOf` at `core/provider_capabilities.ts:75`. The source index is refreshed from committed `origin/main`; exact candidate request construction was cross-checked locally at `cli/src/client.ts:1330-1393` and discovery at `cli/src/client.ts:1133-1202` because the candidate has uncommitted work.\\n\\n**Chunk 3 — Candidate endpoint matrix**\\n\\n- Add a deterministic runner and schema validator. Fake-provider/serialization tests validate request construction and evidence validation only; they do not count as live endpoint measurements.\\n- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\\n- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\\n- Matrix: run the exact installed archive against one allowlisted llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoint. Before the run, the matrix must pin each server to an immutable image/version and record model name plus immutable model digest, context size, sampling settings, tool choice, prompt fixture digest, server flags, and relevant compatibility mode. Each provider's pinned configuration must use a reasoning-capable model/template/parser; 20 attempts (five for each tool) must exercise the hybrid reasoning/tool path. Record provider identification from the detected `serverKind` returned by the client; the lane is valid only when that value exactly matches the configured provider (`llamacpp`, `vllm`, or `ollama`). Unknown/mismatched identities fail before attempts and receive no provider-specific adaptation.\\n- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; reasoning-present counts for hybrid attempts; native-valid/repaired/schema-invalid/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version. Store the finalized evidence file's SHA-256 in the detached `.sha256` sidecar and qualification record (the JSON cannot hash itself). Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, reasoning text, and other secret…1087 tokens truncated….push(`${req.method} ${req.url}`);\\n    const key = `${req.method} ${req.url}`;\\n    const route = Object.hasOwn(routes, key) ? routes[key] : undefined;\\n    if (typeof route !== \\\"function\\\") {\\n      res.writeHead(404);\\n      return void res.end(\\\"not found\\\");\\n    }\\n    res.setHeader(\\\"content-type\\\", \\\"application/json\\\");\\n    res.end(JSON.stringify(route(req)));\\n  });\\n  await new Promise<void>((r) => s.listen(0, \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", () => r()));\\n  return { url: `http://127.0.0.1:${(s.address() as any).port}/v1`, seen, close: () => new Promise((r) => s.close(() => r())) };\\n}\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"discovery against a local server\\\", () => {\\n  test(\\\"request paths cannot dispatch inherited route properties\\\", async () => {\\n    let inheritedCalls = 0;\\n    const routes = Object.create({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/prototype\\\": () => {\\n        inheritedCalls += 1;\\n        return { unsafe: true };\\n      },\\n    }) as Record<string, (req: http.IncomingMessage) => unknown>;\\n    const srv = await server(routes);\\n    try {\\n      const response = await fetch(`${srv.url}/prototype`);\\n      assert.equal(response.status, 404);\\n      assert.equal(await response.text(), \\\"not found\\\");\\n      assert.equal(inheritedCalls, 0);\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  test(\\\"a llama.cpp server's /props context is discovered when its catalog lists no limits\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 131072 } }] }),\\n      \\\"GET /props\\\": () => ({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 4096 } }),\\n    });\\n    try {\\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(found.state, \\\"supported\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \\\"llamacpp\\\");\\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \\\"llamacpp\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 4096);\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"an LM Studio server's /api/v0/models context is discovered\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", owned_by: \\\"organization_owner\\\" }] }),\\n      \\\"GET /api/v0/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", loaded_context_length: 4096, max_context_length: 32768 }] }),\\n    });\\n    try {\\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(found.state, \\\"supported\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \\\"lmstudio\\\");\\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \\\"lmstudio\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 4096);\\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen.slice(1), [\\\"GET /api/v0/models\\\"]);\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"an Ollama server is recognised from its catalog and asked only through its own endpoint\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", owned_by: \\\"library\\\" }] }),\\n      \\\"POST /api/show\\\": () => ({ model_info: { \\\"qwen2.context_length\\\": 32768 } }),\\n    });\\n    try {\\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \\\"ollama\\\");\\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \\\"ollama\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 32768);\\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen.slice(1), [\\\"POST /api/show\\\"], \\\"only the recognised server's endpoint is asked\\\");\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"a vLLM server advertises max_model_len directly in /v1/models\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", max_model_len: 16384 }] }),\\n    });\\n    try {\\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(found.state, \\\"supported\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.via, \\\"vllm\\\");\\n      assert.equal(serverKindOfAdvertisement(found.advertised), \\\"vllm\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.advertised?.contextLength, 16384);\\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen, [\\\"GET /v1/models\\\"]);\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"subsequent context discovery reuses cached advertisement without hitting probe endpoint again\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({\\n      \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 131072 } }] }),\\n      \\\"GET /props\\\": () => ({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 8192 } }),\\n    });\\n    try {\\n      const client = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\\n      const first = await client.discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(first.advertised?.contextLength, 8192);\\n      const propsCallsBefore = srv.seen.filter((s) => s.startsWith(\\\"GET /props\\\")).length;\\n      assert.equal(propsCallsBefore, 1);\\n      const second = await client.discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(second.advertised?.contextLength, 8192);\\n      const propsCallsAfter = srv.seen.filter((s) => s.startsWith(\\\"GET /props\\\")).length;\\n      assert.equal(propsCallsAfter, 1, \\\"no second probe made to /props due to caching\\\");\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"an unrecognised server is not probed and stays on labelled defaults\\\", async () => {\\n    const srv = await server({ \\\"GET /v1/models\\\": () => ({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\" }] }) });\\n    try {\\n      const found = await new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint: srv.url, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any).discoverAdvertisement();\\n      assert.equal(found.state, \\\"unsupported\\\");\\n      assert.equal(found.detail, \\\"catalog lists no limits\\\");\\n      assert.deepEqual(srv.seen, [\\\"GET /v1/models\\\"], \\\"no guessed endpoints were requested\\\");\\n    } finally {\\n      await srv.close();\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\\ndescribe(\\\"context-overflow classification (ACC-INF-02 table)\\\", () => {\\n  const classify = (status: number, body: string) => classifyHttpFailure(status, providerHints(new Headers(), body), body).condition;\\n\\n  test(\\\"llama.cpp exceed_context_size_error is a capacity rejection\\\", () => {\\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: { code: 400, message: \\\"the request exceeds the available context size, try increasing it\\\", type: \\\"exceed_context_size_error\\\", n_prompt_tokens: 9000, n_ctx: 8192 } });\\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \\\"CAPACITY_REJECTED\\\");\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"vLLM maximum context length message is a capacity rejection\\\", () => {\\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ object: \\\"error\\\", message: \\\"This model's maximum context length is 8192 tokens. However, you requested 9000 tokens\\\", type: \\\"BadRequestError\\\", code: 400 });\\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \\\"CAPACITY_REJECTED\\\");\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"LM Studio context window exceeded body is a capacity rejection\\\", () => {\\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: \\\"Context window exceeded\\\", message: \\\"The model's context window is 4096 tokens, but 5000 were submitted\\\" });\\n    assert.equal(classify(400, body), \\\"CAPACITY_REJECTED\\\");\\n  });\\n  test(\\\"Ollama prompt too long body is a capacity rejection\\\", () => {\\n/**\\n * Standalone qual…2710 tokens truncated…bortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\\n      });\\n      if (!versionResponse.ok || !parseOllamaVersion(await versionResponse.json())) return false;\\n      const showResponse = await fetch(showUrl, {\\n        method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n        headers: { ...this.authorization(showUrl), \\\"content-type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"X-Nexus-Purpose\\\": \\\"capabilities\\\" },\\n        body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }),\\n        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\\n        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\\n      });\\n      if (!showResponse.ok) return false;\\n      const show = await showResponse.json();\\n      if (!show || typeof show !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(show)) return false;\\n      const showRecord = show as Record<string, unknown>;\\n      if (typeof showRecord.model === \\\"string\\\" && showRecord.model !== this.model) return false;\\n      LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.set(cacheKey, show);\\n      return true;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\\n   * `/props`, LM Studio `/api/v0/models`, Ollama `/api/show`) on the endpoint's origin with the same credential and a 2 s\\n   * limit. The server is recognised from its catalog entry first, so an unrecognised server is never probed. Not\\n   * content-bearing. Undefined when the server is not recognised or does not answer with a context size.\\n   */\\n  private async discoverServerContext(entry: Record<string, any>, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<Advertisement | undefined> {\\n    const kind = serverKindOf(entry);\\n    if (kind !== \\\"llamacpp\\\" && kind !== \\\"lmstudio\\\" && kind !== \\\"ollama\\\") return undefined;\\n    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\\n    const cached = LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.get(cacheKey);\\n    if (cached) return cached;\\n    if (kind === \\\"ollama\\\" && LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.has(cacheKey)) {\\n      const found = parseServerContext(kind, LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.get(cacheKey), this.model);\\n      if (found) LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\\n      return found;\\n    }\\n    const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\\\/v1\\\\/?$/, \\\"\\\");\\n    const probes: Array<{ kind: \\\"llamacpp\\\" | \\\"lmstudio\\\" | \\\"ollama\\\"; url: string; init?: RequestInit }> = [\\n      { kind: \\\"llamacpp\\\" as const, url: `${root}/props` },\\n      { kind: \\\"lmstudio\\\" as const, url: `${root}/api/v0/models` },\\n      { kind: \\\"ollama\\\" as const, url: `${root}/api/show`, init: { method: \\\"POST\\\", body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }), headers: { \\\"content-type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" } } },\\n    ].filter((p) => p.kind === kind);\\n    for (const probe of probes) {\\n      try {\\n        const res = await fetch(probe.url, {\\n          ...probe.init,\\n          headers: { ...(probe.init?.headers as Record<string, string> | undefined), ...this.authorization(probe.url), \\\"X-Nexus-Purpose\\\": \\\"capabilities\\\" },\\n          signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\\n          ...this.fetchPolicy(),\\n        });\\n        if (!res.ok) continue;\\n        const found = parseServerContext(probe.kind, await res.json(), this.model);\\n        if (found) {\\n          LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\\n          return found;\\n        }\\n      } catch {\\n        if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return undefined;\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Counts the prompt tokens of the request inference would send now, through the connection's `/v1/tokenize`\\n   * (advertised by the homelab-ai gateway contract). The body is `outboundChatBody` — the actual outbound messages,\\n   * tools, tool_choice and settings, after the same egress quarantine and sanitization — sent to the active endpoint\\n   * only, with the same credential scoping, disclosure checks and cancellation as inference. No failover: a counting\\n   * failure belongs to this connection and capability, and never moves task content elsewhere.\\n   * Throws TokenCountError: `unsupported` (no such endpoint or model), `unavailable` (temporary), `malformed`,\\n   * `denied` (credential or disclosure), `aborted`.\\n   */\\n  async countR…1921 tokens truncated…* The Ollama GET /api/version contract; malformed or empty versions do not identify the endpoint. */\\nexport function parseOllamaVersion(body: unknown): string | undefined {\\n  if (!body || typeof body !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(body)) return undefined;\\n  const version = (body as Record<string, unknown>).version;\\n  return typeof version === \\\"string\\\" && version.trim().length > 0 ? version.trim() : undefined;\\n}\\n\\nexport function serverKindOfAdvertisement(ad: Advertisement | undefined): ServerKind {\\n  if (!ad) return \\\"unknown\\\";\\n  if (ad.via === \\\"aihost_gateway\\\") return \\\"gateway\\\";\\n  if (ad.via === \\\"vllm\\\") return \\\"vllm\\\";\\n  if (ad.via === \\\"llamacpp\\\") return \\\"llamacpp\\\";\\n  if (ad.via === \\\"lmstudio\\\") return \\\"lmstudio\\\";\\n  if (ad.via === \\\"ollama\\\") return \\\"ollama\\\";\\n  return \\\"unknown\\\";\\n}\\n\\n/** Reads one `/models` entry. Unknown shapes yield a catalog advertisement with no limits (never an error). */\\nexport function parseAdvertisement(entry: Record<string, any> | undefined): Advertisement | undefined {\\n  if (!entry || typeof entry !== \\\"object\\\") return undefined;\\n  const gateway = typeof entry.limits_version === \\\"string\\\" && entry.limits_version.length > 0;\\n  const workers = Array.isArray(entry.serving)\\n    ? entry.serving.map((s: any) => (typeof s?.worker_id === \\\"string\\\" ? s.worker_id : undefined)).filter((w: string | undefined): w is string => Boolean(w)).sort()\\n    : undefined;\\n  const contextLength = entry.context_length === null ? null : positiveInt(entry.context_length) ?? positiveInt(entry.max_model_len);\\n  const reasoning = entry.reasoning && typeof entry.reasoning === \\\"object\\\"\\n    ? { ...(typeof entry.reasoning.mode === \\\"string\\\" ? { mode: entry.reasoning.mode } : {}), ...(positiveInt(entry.reasoning.budget) ? { budget: positiveInt(entry.reasoning.budget) } : {}) }\\n    : undefined;\\n  return {\\n    via: gateway ? \\\"aihost_gateway\\\" : contextLength !== undefined ? \\\"vllm\\\" : \\\"catalog\\\",\\n    ...(contextLength !== undefined ? { contextLength } : {}),\\n    ...(positiveInt(entry.max_completion_tokens) ? { maxCompletionTokens: positiveInt(entry.max_completion_tokens) } : {}),\\n    ...(gateway ? { limitsVersion: entry.limits_version } : {}),\\n    ...(reasoning && Object.keys(reasoning).length ? { reasoning } : {}),\\n    ...(workers?.length ? { workers } : {}),\\n    tokenize: gateway,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The context a local server says it has loaded, from its own endpoint (REQ-PRV-101): llama.cpp `GET /props`\\n * (default_generation_settings.n_ctx: the runtime window, not the model's training size), LM Studio `GET /api/v0/models`\\n * (loaded_context_length, else max_context_length), Ollama `POST /api/show` (the num_ctx parameter, else the model's\\n * <arch>.context_length). Returns undefined for any other shape.\\n */\\nexport function parseServerContext(kind: \\\"llamacpp\\\" | \\\"lmstudio\\\" | \\\"ollama\\\", body: unknown, model: string): Advertisement | undefined {\\n  if (!body || typeof body !== \\\"object\\\") return undefined;\\n  const b = body as Record<string, any>;\\n  let contextLength: number | undefined;\\n  if (kind === \\\"llamacpp\\\") {\\n    contextLength = positiveInt(b.default_generation_settings?.n_ctx) ?? positiveInt(b.n_ctx);\\n  } else if (kind === \\\"lmstudio\\\") {\\n    const entry = Array.isArray(b.data) ? b.data.find((e: any) => e?.id === model) : undefined;\\n    contextLength = positiveInt(entry?.loaded_context_length) ?? positiveInt(entry?.max_context_length);\\n  } else {\\n    const fromParameters = typeof b.parameters === \\\"string\\\" ? /(?:^|\\\\n)\\\\s*num_ctx\\\\s+(\\\\d+)/.exec(b.parameters)?.[1] : undefined;\\n    const info = b.model_info && typeof b.model_info === \\\"object\\\" ? Object.entries(b.model_info).find(([k]) => k.endsWith(\\\".context_length\\\"))?.[1] : undefined;\\n    contextLength = positiveInt(fromParameters ? Number(fromParameters) : undefined) ?? positiveInt(info);\\n  }\\n  return contextLength ? { via: kind, contextLength, tokenize: false } : undefined;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The context and output limits in effect, and where each came from. `operatorContext` / `operatorOutput` are values\\n * the operator set explicitly (undefined otherwise).\\n */\\nexport function resolveLimits(advertised: Advertisement | undefined, operatorContext?: number, operatorOutput?: number): Pick<ProviderCapabilities, \\\"contextLimit\\\" | \\\"contextSource\\\" | \\\"outputAllowance\\\" | \\\"outputSource\\\"> {\\n  const adCtx = typeof advertised?.contextLength === \\\"number\\\" ? advertised.contextLength : undefined;\\n  let contextLimit: number;\\n  let contextSource: SizingSource;\\n  if (adCtx !== undefined && operatorContext !== undefined) {\\n    contextLimit = Math.min(adCtx, operatorContext);\\n    contextSource = operatorContext <= adCtx ? \\\"operator\\\" : \\\"operator_capped_by_advertised\\\";\\n  } else if (adCtx !== undefined) {\\n    contextLimit = adCtx;\\n    contextSource = \\\"advertised\\\";\\n  } else if (operatorContext !== undefined) {\\n    contextLimit = operatorContext;\\n    contextSource = \\\"operator\\\";\\n  } else {\\n    contextLimit = CLIENT_DEFAULT_CONTEXT;\\n    contextSource = \\\"client_default\\\";\\n  }\\n  const adOut = advertised?.maxCompletionTokens;\\n  let outputAllowance: number;\\n  let outputSource: SizingSource;\\n  if (adOut !== undefined && operatorOutput !== undefined) {\\n    outputAllowance = Math.min(adOut, operatorOutput);\\n    outputSource = operatorOutput <= adOut ? \\\"operator\\\" : \\\"operator_capped_by_advertised\\\";\\n  } else if (adOut !== undefined) {\\n    outputAllowance = adOut;\\n    outputSource = \\\"advertised\\\";\\n  } else if (operatorOutput !== undefined) {\\n    outputAllowance = operatorOutput;\\n    outputSource = \\\"operator\\\";\\n  } else {\\n    outputAllowance = Math.min(CLIENT_DEFAULT_OUTPUT, Math.floor(contextLimit / 4));\\n    outputSource = \\\"client_default\\\";\\n  }\\n  // An output allowance can never take the whole window.\\n  outputAllowance = Math.max(1, Math.min(outputAllowance, Math.floor(contextLimit / 2)));\\n  return { contextLimit, contextSource, outputAllowance, outputSource };\\n}\\n\\n/** Whether a new advertisement changes what was in effect (model, limits version, workers or capacity). */\\nexport function advertisementChanged(before: Advertisement | undefined, after: Advertisement | undefined): boolean {\\n  if (!before || !after) return before !== after;\\n  return (\\n    before.limitsVersion !== after.limitsVersion ||\\n    before.contextLength !== after.contextLength ||\\n    before.maxCompletionTokens !== after.maxCompletionTokens ||\\n    (before.workers ?? []).join(\\\",\\\") !== (after.workers ?? []).join(\\\",\\\")\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport interface RequestCount {\\n  promptTokens: number;\\n  source: CountSource;\\n  /** Worker the count was taken on, when the provider said. */\\n  workerId?: string;\\n  limitsVersion?: string;\\n  /** Context the provider reported with the count (the counted worker's). */\\n  contextLength?: number;\\n  /** Why a stronger source was not available. */\\n  detail?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n    assert.ok(countTokens(kana) >= 200, `expected >= 200 tokens for 200 Kana chars, got ${countTokens(kana)}`);\\n\\n    const digits = \\\"1234567890\\\".repeat(100); // 1000 digits\\n    assert.equal(countTokens(digits), 1000, \\\"expected 1 token per digit\\\");\\n\\n    const b64 = Buffer.from(\\\"REDACTED!@#\\\".repeat(30)).toString(\\\"base64\\\");\\n    assert.ok(countTokens(b64) >= Math.ceil(b64.length / 3), \\\"expected at least ceil(len/3) tokens for a base64 run\\\");\\n  });\\n\\n  test(\\\"REQ-AGT-118: /tokenize works on llama.cpp (root /tokenize { tokens }) and vLLM (root /tokenize { count })\\\", async () => {\\n    assert.deepEqual(parseTokenizeResponse({ tokens: [10, 20, 30, 40] }), {\\n      promptTokens: 4,\\n      source: \\\"exact_sampled_worker\\\",\\n    });\\n    assert.deepEqual(parseTokenizeResponse({ count: 128, max_model_len: 16384, tokens: [] }), {\\n      promptTokens: 128,\\n      source: \\\"exact_sampled_worker\\\",\\n      contextLength: 16384,\\n    });\\n\\n    const seenUrls: string[] = [];\\n    let mode: \\\"llamacpp\\\" | \\\"vllm\\\" = \\\"llamacpp\\\";\\n    const srv = http.createServer((req, res) => {\\n      seenUrls.push(`${req.method} ${req.url}`);\\n      res.setHeader(\\\"content-type\\\", \\\"application/json\\\");\\n      if (req.url === \\\"/v1/models\\\") {\\n        if (mode === \\\"llamacpp\\\") {\\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", owned_by: \\\"llamacpp\\\", meta: { n_ctx_train: 32768 } }] }));\\n        } else {\\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \\\"m\\\", object: \\\"model\\\", max_model_len: 16384 }] }));\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (req.url === \\\"/props\\\") {\\n        res.end(JSON.stringify({ default_generation_settings: { n_ctx: 8192 } }));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (req.url === \\\"/tokenize\\\") {\\n        if (mode === \\\"llamacpp\\\") {\\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ tokens: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] }));\\n        } else {\\n          res.end(JSON.stringify({ count: 42, max_model_len: 16384 }));\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      res.writeHead(404);\\n      res.end(\\\"not found\\\");\\n    });\\n    await new Promise<void>((r) => srv.listen(0, \\\"127.0.0.1\\\", () => r()));\\n    const port = (srv.address() as any).port;\\n    const endpoint = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/v1`;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const llamaClient = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\\n      await llamaClient.discoverAdvertisement();\\n      const llamaCount = await llamaClient.countRequestTokens([{ role: \\\"user\\\", content: \\\"hello\\\" }], [], \\\"req-1\\\");\\n      assert.equal(llamaCount.promptTokens, 7);\\n      assert.equal(llamaCount.source, \\\"exact_sampled_worker\\\");\\n      assert.ok(seenUrls.includes(\\\"POST /tokenize\\\"), \\\"llama.cpp root /tokenize should be called after /v1/tokenize 404s\\\");\\n\\n      mode = \\\"vllm\\\";\\n      const vllmClient = new LocalLlmClient({ endpoint, model: \\\"m\\\", workspace: \\\"/tmp\\\", maxSteps: 1 } as any);\\n      await vllmClient.discoverAdvertisement();\\n      const vllmCount = await vllmClient.countRequestTokens([{ role: \\\"user\\\", content: \\\"hello\\\" }], [], \\\"req-2\\\");\\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.promptTokens, 42);\\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.contextLength, 16384);\\n      assert.equal(vllmCount.source, \\\"exact_sampled_worker\\\");\\n    } finally {\\n      await new Promise<void>((r) => srv.close(() => r()));\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\"}\n{\"chunk_id\":\"1a94d6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000041341,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1232,\"output\":\"486:✖ Inference request aborted by operator\\n517:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 400): model-error-payload-marker\\n642:✖ Inference error: Inference request failed: fetch failed (cause: ECONNREFUSED <- ECONNREFUSED: connect ECONNREFUSED ::1:1234 <- ECONNREFUSED: connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:1234)\\n723:✖ Working: fetch_web\\n724:✖ Tool Error:\\n733:✖ Working: fetch_web\\n734:✖ Tool Error:\\n743:✖ Working: fetch_web\\n744:✖ Tool Error:\\n1195:✖ Inference provider overloaded\\n2839:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"message\\\":\\\"rate limited\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"rate_limit_exceeded\\\"}}\\n2879:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"message\\\":\\\"rate limited\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"rate_limit_exceeded\\\"}}\\n3003:✖ Inference error: Inference error (HTTP 429): {\\\"error\\\":{\\\"message\\\":\\\"rate limited\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"rate_limit_exceeded\\\"}}\\n3072:✖ Working: task_completed\\n3074:✖ Working: task_completed\\n3076:✖ Working: task_completed\\n3078:✖ Working: task_completed\\n3080:✖ Working: task_completed\\n3414:✖ versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels (409.346728ms)\\n3421:✖ pytest candidate imports cannot inspect hidden Python sources (591.029136ms)\\n3426:✖ hardened checks: a correc