{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:10:44.199Z","ordinal":85748,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fcd46793-7ab9-41d4-b38e-a60e1b77654b","process_id":"59266","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|package runtime path|eval.*workspace' cli/test eval scripts Makefile docs -g '*.md' -g '*.mjs' -g '*.sh' -g 'Makefile' | head -n 80; rg -n '^build:|^test:|npm run build|cargo build' Makefile"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|package runtime path|eval.*workspace' cli/test eval scripts Makefile docs -g '*.md' -g '*.mjs' -g '*.sh' -g Makefile","query":"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT|package runtime path|eval.*workspace","path":"test"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^build:|''^test:|npm run build|cargo build' Makefile","query":"^build:|^test:|npm run build|cargo build","path":"Makefile"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:51:- Evaluator/SWE-bench: BenchmarkEvaluator forces worktree=true, runs an agent, then directly inspects the original workspace using Git and runs runTestSuite through host execSync. It treats test command none as passing. Worktree merge is gated by agent verifier settings, while evaluator diff/test observation is rooted at evaluator workspace; evidence sources can diverge.\ndocs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:88:| Validation | TestRunResult, verifiedWorktreeCompletion boolean, SynthesizerState, tool output, evaluator result. | Discovery success advisory; configured verifier alone authorizes auto merge. TDD/evaluator/manual test have separate result semantics. | No durable validation artifact bound to exact mutation set/workspace/commit. | #11 tests prove configured success/failure behavior, not semantic quality of trusted command. |\ndocs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:196:| One workspace identity | Root vs worktree; browser/knowledge/search; MCP; evaluator; operator workspace | config.workspace alone doesn't identify every mutation or evidence source. |\neval/README.md:160:  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\neval/README.md:173:- **Repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned commit.** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages a repo task as a\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:15:| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:128:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:10:  \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\",\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_AND_PLAN.md:279:| AUTH-001..012 | Bridge, plugin, MCP, browser, operator and evaluator have different controls | Filesystem, process, network, workspace, child, merge | Exact/sibling/bounded/full-access matrix plus actual effect tests; denied requests produce no effect; no fallback |\neval/run.mjs:417:  const probeWorkspace = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(config.resources?.workspaceRoot ?? os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-version-workspace-\"));\neval/run.mjs:753:    \"eval/score.mjs\", \"eval/infra.mjs\", \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\",\neval/T3.md:13:`eval/run.mjs` runs a `\"tier\": \"T3\"` task with the same sandbox, model proxy, resource contract, workspace staging and\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:235:| VER-07 | S2 | RR | `nexus eval` | `evaluator.ts:128-213` | SRC | Invalid scores; checks out the operator's workspace | REQ-AGT-119; DEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:83:**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:210:An isolated immutable snapshot at `9344df578f8a39a55d82ead0f15c4811864d21f8` built successfully, but `make test` exited 2: 1,769 passed, 2 failed, and 1 was skipped. `eval_integrity.test.ts` observed three OOM kills during this host run, which did not have the dedicated capped workspace mount; the log does not establish that the missing mount caused those kills. `eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts` failed its precondition because `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT` were not configured. `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`, and `/home` were all on the same ext4 device. These are incomplete host-fixture checks, not a passing suite or a demonstrated source regression. The complete output is retained at `/var/tmp/nexus-pr268-make-test-9344df5.log`. Current exact-main hosted CI is still running the full CLI suite with its configured cgroups and capped tmpfs.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:646:  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:647:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\neval/runner_api.mjs:25:    TERM: config.env?.TERM ?? \"dumb\", HOME: \"/home/eval\", PWD: \"/workspace\", CI: \"1\",\neval/host/validate.mjs:166:  sourceDigests: [\"eval/host/validate.mjs\", \"eval/host/operator_home.mjs\", \"eval/host/bubblewrap.mjs\", \"eval/host/provision.sh\", \"eval/host/rollback.sh\", \"eval/host/resource-profile.json\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/isolate.mjs\", \"eval/validate.mjs\", \"eval/run.mjs\", \"eval/hardened_check.mjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.cjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.py\", \"eval/unlink_then_exec.sh\", \"eval/workspace.mjs\"].map((file) => ({ file, sha256: createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, file))).digest(\"hex\") })),\neval/isolate.mjs:906:/** Make evaluator-owned workspace files readable to the operator through the scoped ACL mask. */\neval/evaluators/code/README.md:46:The modules are a library. The dataset runner (`eval/run.mjs`, WP-1103/1104) supplies the pre-agent workspace snapshot,\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:45:| 6 | `/test` and `nexus eval` use the bridge runner instead of `execSync`. | `tester.ts:143-163`; `repl.ts:1357`; `slash/workspace_commands.ts:160`; `evaluator.ts` | 5 |\neval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs:145:/** Run the deterministic evaluator set against the actual candidate workspace and pre-agent snapshot. */\neval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs:197:        if (!baseSpec?.command || !candSpec?.command) results.push(evaluatorResult(\"typecheck_clean\", false, 0, { error: explicitBaseline ? \"no typecheck command specified\" : \"no pre-agent typecheck baseline workspace\" }));\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:33:| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\neval/package_runtime.test.mjs:17:  \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\",\neval/package_runtime.test.mjs:105:  const child = spawn(launcher, [\"eval\", \"--dataset\", dataset, \"--split\", \"benchmark\", \"--runs\", \"1\", \"--max-steps\", \"1\", \"--max-minutes\", \"1\", \"--isolated-home\", \"--workspace\", workspace, \"--output\", outputPath], {\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:91:| Semantic retrieval | **Absent.** Only a workspace code index (`embeddings.ts:206-320`) | Defer (see §5) |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:144:1. **Security & Boundary Preservation:** No post-v1 observability or evaluation feature may bypass or weaken the v1.0.0 security boundaries (untrusted `.env` rejection, SSRF blocking, container path confinement, or workspace trust).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:35:`nexus eval` (the SWE-bench-style command) scores the repo's last commit instead of the agent's change, and runs `git checkout` in the operator's workspace (VER-07). It must not be used for any published number.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:94:- **Hidden-test isolation.** Private validators and expected answers must remain outside every task process's readable namespace. A task workspace may contain only its permitted baseline and task inputs; evaluation of private expectations must be performed outside that task boundary. Corpus custody and evaluator execution isolation are separate acceptance gates: the custodian's sealed-store disposition does not establish that the runner prevents task processes from reading validators. On the current integration candidate, evaluator-boundary acceptance remains open; PR #33 is not qualified for held-out use until the actual workspace-construction and execution path demonstrates this boundary and passes independent review. Do not use filesystem ownership of the custodian store as a substitute for validating the task-process boundary.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:115:In `execution_tracking.ts evaluateStep`, if `stateIdentity === \"unknown\"` and the step had a successful `write_workspace` call whose canonical args differ from every call in the window, the step counts as progress. Add the inverse test: identical writes repeated 13 times still stagnate.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips and record candidate archive SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, captured-request digests and validator/scorer results in a new candidate-specific evidence file. Do not overwrite prior evidence. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. This is G1.1-2 execution/isolation evidence, not a model-quality test or release gate substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:51:**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:102:- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:5:| Status | Ready. `nexus eval` and `/tdd` are experimental, eval's workspace checkout is fixed, and team role tool sets are enforced ([DEC-07](../DECISIONS.md#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles)). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:99:| ACC-VER-08 | `nexus eval --help` and `/tdd` help say \"experimental\". `nexus eval` leaves the operator workspace HEAD unchanged. A reviewer unit's `write_file` is refused. |\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:197:  3. `evaluator.ts` then executes `git diff` against `this.workspace` (the root repository), which contains **no code changes**!\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:200:- **Correction Required:** `BenchmarkEvaluator` must evaluate the **exact worktree candidate** produced by the agent, extracting the patch directly from the worktree candidate identity rather than inspecting the un-isolated root workspace.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:58:| VER-07 | S2 | `nexus eval` benchmark scores | evaluator.ts:128, 155-166, 173-190, 213 | SOURCE. (a) `git checkout base_commit` runs in the operator's workspace before the worktree exists, and failure is ignored. (b) The patch is `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD`, the last commit and not the agent's change, so `hasCodeChanges` is true for almost any repo with history. (c) A `test_patch` apply failure is swallowed and grading continues on the existing suite. (d) `fail_to_pass`/`pass_to_pass` are ignored and the whole suite runs via detectTestCommand (`npm test` fallback). (e) `testRes.command === \"none\"` is unreachable. Net effect: an agent that does nothing on a repo whose tests pass scores RESOLVED. evaluator.test.ts never calls `evaluateInstance`. ISSUE12 matrices mark EXEC-011 \"DEMONSTRATED\". | Any published `nexus eval` pass rate is invalid. The workspace HEAD may be detached unexpectedly. | BLOCKER for any benchmark claim; otherwise RELEASE-REQUIRED: remove the command or label it experimental, or fix it (diff vs base in the worktree, fail on test_patch error, run FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS ids, never touch the operator checkout). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:65:| VER-14 | S3 | `/test`, `nexus eval` | tester.ts:143-163; repl.ts:1357; slash/workspace_commands.ts:160 | SOURCE. `runTestSuite` uses host `execSync` with a 120 s limit. It bypasses the configured sandbox and the Rust runner, blocks the event loop (no cancel, TUI frozen), and kills only the shell on timeout, not the process tree. | Freezes for up to 2 min. Sandbox users get an unsandboxed run. | Route through the bridge executor with the verifier deadline. |\ndocs/PHASE3_CORRECTIONS_VERIFICATION.md:56:- **Review Finding (`F-02`):** SWE-bench evaluation was previously excused as \"intentionally independent\" observing root Git diffs. This preserved the Phase 1 wrong-candidate defect where the evaluator tested the root workspace while agent mutations remained isolated in a worktree.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:720:  - *Boundary Rule:* `Provenance != Applicability`. Cross-project retrieval must filter out credentials, configuration secrets, and customer data. Source workspace provenance must be attached to every retrieved snippet.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T0338Z-synthetic.md:16:Complementary source-fixture evidence is exact integration CI run `39356488487` on the same commit. Its Node 20, 22, and 24 suites and Linux package job completed successfully. The current `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts` includes deliberate memory, process-count, workspace-write, CPU-throttle, timeout, and escaped-process cleanup fixtures; no qualification task was used to exercise them.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:48:| RES-001 | 05: Resource & Effective Scope | Authority admission MUST evaluate the effective resource actually affected by an operation, accounting for relative paths, absolute paths, lexical normalization, symbolic links, hard links, directory aliases, and renamed resources. | Path resolution MUST ensure that relative paths (e.g., `../../etc/passwd`) or symlinks pointing outside the workspace cannot access unauthorized files. | Phase 2 §9 | `cli/src/core/authority.ts, core/src/file_ops.rs`; cli/test/authority.test.ts, core/tests/segregation_boundary.rs | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:318:    - **Root Evaluation Rule:** Root workspace evaluation is valid only when root workspace is explicitly the intended evaluation candidate.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:606:- **Acceptance Properties:** Supplying `cwd: \"/etc\"` or `cwd: \"../../\"` outside workspace is rejected with code 0 mutation; full-access mode executes without interactive prompts; race-resistant containment verified evaluating candidate mechanisms (DEC-01 hypothesis); operator direct shell respects `--read-only` and binds to active workspace; browser local file access escapes denied.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:733:| **SWE-Bench / Evaluator** (`evaluator.ts`) | Independent process evaluating git diff in root workspace | Evaluates root git diff while agent operates in worktree, evaluating empty patch or wrong candidate (`F-02`) | **NO** (cannot confer merge authority on an unrelated candidate) | Explicit candidate binding to agent worktree candidate identity (`INC-05`) | Evaluator extracts and evaluates worktree candidate patch; evaluation receipt explicitly binds to evaluated `candidateId`. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-setup-failure.md:9:The only failure was test setup: the command set `TMPDIR` to a path inside the isolated temporary home but did not create that directory. The fixture returned `ENOENT` while trying to create its temporary test directory. The evaluator account, resource controls, cgroup cleanup, process-tree reaping, synthetic-store denial, and workspace cleanup checks passed. No held-out data was used. This run is preserved, excluded from the successful result, and superseded by [the corrected 10/10 run](validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.md), which creates the temporary directory before execution.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.md:13:The temporary mount was operator-owned (`uid=1000`, mode `0711`, `nosuid,nodev`) so the evaluator could traverse to the explicitly ACL-granted workspace while the mount root remained non-listable and non-writable to it. No evaluator processes or fixture files remained after teardown.\ndocs/DEC02_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION_RECORD.md:66:  5. **Immediate Mutation Invalidation (`CAND-002`):** Register `CandidateMutationHook` on `ExecutionSpine`. When a mutating capability completes, evaluate candidate workspace containment. Any successful mutation inside the workspace (including new file creation, replacement, or deletion) or touching declared material dependencies immediately transitions active receipts to `INVALIDATED`.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| **RES-001** | Authority admission MUST evaluate the effective resource actually affected by an operation, accounting for relative paths, absolute paths, lexical normalization, symbolic links, hard links, directory aliases, and renamed resources. | Path resolution MUST ensure that relative paths (e.g., `../../etc/passwd`) or symlinks pointing outside the workspace cannot access unauthorized files. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:55:preflight, and an empty evaluator workspace root. The exact-source JSON and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:90:preflight, and an empty evaluator workspace root. The exact-source JSON and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:63:1. **Harness history leak — CLOSED (`96aeef2`, PR #18; canary `6a334fa`, PR #26).** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`), with no `--shared`, alternates, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CODEQL-BAD-CODE-SANITIZATION-20261026/README.md:69:  test-only, share the already-accepted threat model (whoever controls `TMPDIR`/`NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT`\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md:5:A separate production-path regression invokes the real eval/run.mjs with an empty synthetic task set and a synthetic Goose executable. The executable checks its actual working filesystem device and size against the configured capped mount, writes a file and returns its version. The test requires successful identity discovery, manifest recording and workspace cleanup. Its local HTTP server returns only synthetic model metadata; no model inference, private tasks, gateway or credentials are used. Its child process group and pipes have bounded cleanup.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md:7:Validation: runner syntax check passed. Local WSL attempted the regression with isolated HOME/XDG and failed at its explicit precondition because that host lacks the dedicated capped/cgroup CI fixture; local-precondition.tap preserves this result. This is not a functional pass. CI and release workflows already provide NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and user-cgroup fixtures. Required exact-head hosted checks and independent review are pending. No mike-dev test started: two older foreign evaluator test processes remain live in p10i, untouched by this slice.\n10:\tcargo build --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n13:build: build-core build-cli\n16:\tcargo build --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n51:test:\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":738829965}},"started_at_ms":1793747443460,"completed_at_ms":1793747444199}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:10:45.604Z","ordinal":85749,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a3ad-e764-7f83-a2a9-cbdd1761656e","call_id":"call_ca238f4d3bf048e99b4b982100d9aa92","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5801)\nTotal output lines: 63\n\ndocs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:51:- Evaluator/SWE-bench: BenchmarkEvaluator forces worktree=true, runs an agent, then directly inspects the original workspace using Git and runs runTestSuite through host execSync. It treats test command none as passing. Worktree merge is gated by agent verifier settings, while evaluator diff/test observation is rooted at evaluator workspace; evidence sources can diverge.\ndocs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:88:| Validation | TestRunResult, verifiedWorktreeCompletion boolean, SynthesizerState, tool output, evaluator result. | Discovery success advisory; configured verifier alone authorizes auto merge. TDD/evaluator/manual test have separate result semantics. | No durable validation artifact bound to exact mutation set/workspace/commit. | #11 tests prove configured success/failure behavior, not semantic quality of trusted command. |\ndocs/PHASE1_SYSTEM_RECONSTRUCTION.md:196:| One workspace identity | Root vs worktree; browser/knowledge/search; MCP; evaluator; operator workspace | config.workspace alone doesn't identify every mutation or evidence source. |\neval/README.md:160:  evaluator UID ACL access only to the disposable workspace, home and per-run proxy directory. Before qualification,\neval/README.md:173:- **Repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned commit.** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages a repo task as a\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:15:| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:128:- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\nscripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs:10:  \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\",\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_AND_PLAN.md:279:| AUTH-001..012 | Bridge, plugin, MCP, browser, operator and evaluator have different controls | Filesystem, process, network, workspace, child, merge | Exact/sibling/bounded/full-access matrix plus actual effect tests; denied requests produce no effect; no fallback |\neval/run.mjs:417:  const probeWorkspace = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(config.resources?.workspaceRoot ?? os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-version-workspace-\"));\neval/run.mjs:753:    \"eval/score.mjs\", \"eval/infra.mjs\", \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\",\neval/T3.md:13:`eval/run.mjs` runs a `\"tier\": \"T3\"` task with the same sandbox, model proxy, resource contract, workspace staging and\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:235:| VER-07 | S2 | RR | `nexus eval` | `evaluator.ts:128-213` | SRC | Invalid scores; checks out the operator's workspace | REQ-AGT-119; DEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:43:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:83:**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:210:An isolated immutable snapshot at `9344df578f8a39a55d82ead0f15c4811864d21f8` built successfully, but `make test` exited 2: 1,769 passed, 2 failed, and 1 was skipped. `eval_integrity.test.ts` observed three OOM kills during this host run, which did not have the dedicated capped workspace mount; the log does not establish that the missing mount caused those kills. `eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts` failed its precondition because `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT` were …3301 tokens truncated… code 0 mutation; full-access mode executes without interactive prompts; race-resistant containment verified evaluating candidate mechanisms (DEC-01 hypothesis); operator direct shell respects `--read-only` and binds to active workspace; browser local file access escapes denied.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:733:| **SWE-Bench / Evaluator** (`evaluator.ts`) | Independent process evaluating git diff in root workspace | Evaluates root git diff while agent operates in worktree, evaluating empty patch or wrong candidate (`F-02`) | **NO** (cannot confer merge authority on an unrelated candidate) | Explicit candidate binding to agent worktree candidate identity (`INC-05`) | Evaluator extracts and evaluates worktree candidate patch; evaluation receipt explicitly binds to evaluated `candidateId`. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-setup-failure.md:9:The only failure was test setup: the command set `TMPDIR` to a path inside the isolated temporary home but did not create that directory. The fixture returned `ENOENT` while trying to create its temporary test directory. The evaluator account, resource controls, cgroup cleanup, process-tree reaping, synthetic-store denial, and workspace cleanup checks passed. No held-out data was used. This run is preserved, excluded from the successful result, and superseded by [the corrected 10/10 run](validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.md), which creates the temporary directory before execution.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.md:13:The temporary mount was operator-owned (`uid=1000`, mode `0711`, `nosuid,nodev`) so the evaluator could traverse to the explicitly ACL-granted workspace while the mount root remained non-listable and non-writable to it. No evaluator processes or fixture files remained after teardown.\ndocs/DEC02_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION_RECORD.md:66:  5. **Immediate Mutation Invalidation (`CAND-002`):** Register `CandidateMutationHook` on `ExecutionSpine`. When a mutating capability completes, evaluate candidate workspace containment. Any successful mutation inside the workspace (including new file creation, replacement, or deletion) or touching declared material dependencies immediately transitions active receipts to `INVALIDATED`.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:235:| **RES-001** | Authority admission MUST evaluate the effective resource actually affected by an operation, accounting for relative paths, absolute paths, lexical normalization, symbolic links, hard links, directory aliases, and renamed resources. | Path resolution MUST ensure that relative paths (e.g., `../../etc/passwd`) or symlinks pointing outside the workspace cannot access unauthorized files. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:55:preflight, and an empty evaluator workspace root. The exact-source JSON and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:90:preflight, and an empty evaluator workspace root. The exact-source JSON and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:63:1. **Harness history leak — CLOSED (`96aeef2`, PR #18; canary `6a334fa`, PR #26).** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`), with no `--shared`, alternates, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CODEQL-BAD-CODE-SANITIZATION-20261026/README.md:69:  test-only, share the already-accepted threat model (whoever controls `TMPDIR`/`NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT`\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md:5:A separate production-path regression invokes the real eval/run.mjs with an empty synthetic task set and a synthetic Goose executable. The executable checks its actual working filesystem device and size against the configured capped mount, writes a file and returns its version. The test requires successful identity discovery, manifest recording and workspace cleanup. Its local HTTP server returns only synthetic model metadata; no model inference, private tasks, gateway or credentials are used. Its child process group and pipes have bounded cleanup.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md:7:Validation: runner syntax check passed. Local WSL attempted the regression with isolated HOME/XDG and failed at its explicit precondition because that host lacks the dedicated capped/cgroup CI fixture; local-precondition.tap