ses in a fresh workspace; a test-script change refuses the checks (2880.45524ms)\n13-✖ hardened checks hide oracle source from candidate code and reject empty-output commands (3173.671713ms)\n14-✔ test data, symlinked paths, new Python packages, oversized files and manifest deletions never weaken the checks (34.802061ms)\n15-✔ Rust and Go compile-time file inclusion directives refuse hardened checks (13.422734ms)\n16:✖ Go and Rust hidden sources are absent during build audits and test execution (160.489106ms)\n17-✔ manifest guards fail closed on TOML headers they do not recognise, go.mod blocks and new manifests (13.701284ms)\n18-✔ the model proxy forwards requests and counts answers and upstream failures (430.610587ms)\n19-✔ the evaluation proxy authenticates the local run token and replaces it with the upstream credential (70.928079ms)\n20-✔ the evaluation proxy bounds request count and body size (48.026634ms)\n21-✔ the evaluation proxy bounds concurrent inference and cancels upstream work on client abort (100.822903ms)\n22-✔ the evaluation proxy enforces per-request and aggregate requested completion-token ceilings (47.845774ms)\n23-✔ the evaluation proxy never forwards the local token when the upstream is unauthenticated (22.029651ms)\n24-✔ infrastructure reruns use one rule for every agent: a crash after the model answered is scored (304.176596ms)\n25-✔ contaminated runs leave the pass rate, crashes are counted, and reruns are listed (140.579015ms)\n26-✔ T4 scoring requires all nine classes and five injected runs per class (983.670814ms)\n27-✔ task validation: pinned repos, one source, and black-box hidden oracle for qualification (30.589071ms)\n28-✔ T4 fixture evidence requires an exact CLI runner receipt and measured storage boundary (2.145622ms)\n29-✔ black-box oracle keeps canary expectations outside the candidate process and returns sanitized evidence (360.988886ms)\n30:✖ Python black-box oracle uses only pinned offline Go and Rust toolchains, or fails preflight (55.560365ms)\n31-✔ a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint (weights, server build, sampling) (1.258503ms)\n32-✔ qualification requires frozen request and aggregate output budgets (1.148074ms)\n33-✔ hidden tests must be unreadable to the agent's own user (2.18333ms)\n34-✔ candidate agents receive only the approved read-only Go and Rust toolchain mounts (1.055906ms)\n35:✖ qualification runtime mounts cannot overlap the task tree, held-out store, or private validator paths (683.381166ms)\n36-✔ qualification remains fail-closed without enforced aggregate resource controls (45073.982125ms)\n37:✖ resource contract: candidate memory, processes, storage and CPU are kernel-bounded and every process is reaped (518.904267ms)\n38-✔ resource supervisor preserves SIGTERM grace for descendants after the main payload exits (2636.402029ms)\n39:✖ candidate sandbox and resource supervisor compose around a staged repository (219.491142ms)\n40:✖ repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned baseline commit (535.084127ms)\n41-✔ task paths reject traversal, symlink escapes, and unstable task trees (5.181294ms)\n42-✔ task-tree digests frame paths, entry types, executable mode, and content lengths (22.297263ms)\n43:✖ task setup and validators run with cleared env, no network, confined filesystem, bounded output and timeout (76.65264ms)\n44-✖ candidate namespace cannot read host files or bypass pinned compilers with absolute paths (98.061021ms)\n45-✔ qualification corpus binding rejects missing, mismatched, and post-seal task content (5.090854ms)\n46-✔ run.mjs refuses to start on an invalid task (249.913132ms)\n47-✔ the model proxy injects each scheduled fault into the chat request it names, and records it (52.919866ms)\n48-✔ executable probes refuse bind sources that overlap protected corpus material (9.040084ms)\n49-✔ T3 task schema requires steering with checkable constraints, a fact sheet, a long budget and Nexus only (20.30691ms)\n50-✔ the T3 driver