_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea66ed96a081a38b58a1c23e5ca9cc","order":2904,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3a2-1479-7ba1-b8b2-dd19f2eec3d0","text":"The full suite is still progressing through higher level operation tests. Even after the suite completes, the earlier sandbox and network-dependent failures mean this run may not clear the gate; I’m waiting for its summary and then will record the precise blocker and baseline comparison.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6789178081a392e9b6639dc1ef4c","order":2905,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3a4-740e-7533-af74-a4d75708c545","text":"The run has passed more release resolution, rollback, and operation cases. One TUI approval test failed amid the existing full-suite failures; I’ll inspect its detailed assertion after the final report is emitted and compare it with baseline before deciding whether any source change is warranted.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6879c30081a38658ab8e9b716614","order":2906,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3a8-22d7-7d10-980c-e6b6795f684f","text":"The run finished red: 2,307 passed and 33 failed. Several failures are setup-related (the qualification snapshot lacked the TUI build, and its dependency symlink points outside the allowed snapshot); the provider handshake tests also expose stale expectations that need reconciliation with WP-1107. I’m recording the gate as failed, releasing its suite reservation, and will fix the test setup and contract mismatches before another full run.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea69b8c95c81a3a610f6b3c98c24f3","order":2912,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3ac-ff4d-7d71-857a-8bee85d25a9a","text":"I’ve reserved the additional test and proxy files for the fixture corrections, and the independent reviewer is checking the failure attribution and proposed changes. The release gate’s reservation is released; I’ll reacquire it only when running builds or tests, and I won’t touch the real provider gateway while it remains reserved by the RC15 work.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6a8b9c7c81a3b21244a3e9af4e2d","order":2920,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3b0-3647-78b1-ae54-670cab813f24","text":"The focused RED run is cleanly targeted: 23/26 passed, with the remaining three failures exactly at the cache and positive vLLM/Ollama identity assertions. I’m now applying those minimal corrections and adding the version endpoints to the standalone proxy fixture.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6ae7157881a3bea7ab7779950da1","order":2921,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3b1-9bf5-7563-9ae2-14b5be2f3eca","text":"The targeted regressions are now green: 54/54 passed, including all provider identity, tokenization, and discovery-cache cases. The reviewer approved the correction plan. Next I’m building the updated source and repairing the qualification snapshot’s dependencies and required evaluator fixtures before the next full gate.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6bd758c881a39a97cc261d8cd14b","order":2922,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3b5-4646-7250-bce1-cc97b9a4d079","text":"The qualification snapshot now has an in-tree dependency directory and the updated provider fixtures. I’m building the full Rust/TypeScript candidate there, with the CI-equivalent capped evaluator workspace and pinned runtime roots configured; this should clear the setup-only failures before I start the next full suite.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea6c59aae481a3a30fe8192ea6e03c","order":2923,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a3b7-4469-7302-b554-1b5ba6ce2c96","text":"The snapshot build passed, and the focused provider tests (54/54) plus the tool-grammar matrix tests (10/10) passed on the copied dependencies. I’m doing a smaller check of the sandbox/evaluator fixtures now; if those clear, I’ll start a new full `make test` run with the exact environment the release workflow expects.","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":2924,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19807-5328-7ba0-97f6-497836fe895a","order":680,"revision":"retained_01a19807-5329-7f60-8f25-58ad29e7ff4f","text":"consider v1.1.0 as failed. No release files were published and versions are immutable. This is why v1.1.1 was released.","turn_id":"01a19807-4967-7730-8c19-228841c32bbd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19808-2321-7560-a3b0-5cb35450f233","order":685,"revision":"retained_01a19808-2321-7560-a3b0-5cd378227e25","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_0ed0e8bc5d334d5d830df787f3f33c52\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"Should I continue implementing and qualifying the full failed v1.1.0 roadmap for v1.1.2 (next after published v1.1.1), or treat v1.1.1 as final and stop?\",\"answer\":\"Full roadmap in v1.1.2 (Recommended)\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","turn_id":"01a19807-4967-7730-8c19-228841c32bbd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19808-2295-7750-a559-65696a80256a","order":686,"revision":"retained_01a19808-22ce-7023-b04c-e3d0c44dd6cb","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-3"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a199b6-5641-7693-9c28-b7cb22dc5926","order":938,"revision":"retained_01a199b6-5641-7693-9c28-b7edbbe53bba","text":"continue","turn_id":"01a1991a-a2c5-7ee0-aefe-1aee971e45be"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19a58-e100-77d2-83b5-04a612c5321e","order":1196,"revision":"retained_01a19a58-e114-77d0-a971-feb22d6dbe8d","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19de1-3ce1-7960-a1e9-f7f7244d2142","order":1888,"revision":"retained_01a19de1-3ce2-7c93-9830-987531df93c8","text":"continue","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19de1-8462-73d2-a498-318bfc2f7db8","order":1911,"revision":"retained_01a19de1-846a-7a42-983b-a33d01115433","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a1a332-4a1b-7522-b84d-5724831f9a8d","order":2820,"revision":"retained_01a1a332-4a1b-7522-b84d-574ea02f20c4","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_2c886fcefc70491c897854ba813082c8\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The repo claim log records a 20:42 owner decision to defer WP-1107 to v1.1.3 and stop/release its v1.1.2 work. This conflicts with your earlier direction to complete the full roadmap in v1.1.2. Which direction should govern from here?\",\"answer\":\"Keep working on WP-1107.. it will be released with any defect fixes for the current v1.1.2 undergoing release\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a1a3be-140f-7603-84a6-1a80ebdb1436","window_number":49}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:28:25.620Z","ordinal":86262,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/mike/nexus-code","text":"## XERJ (code search)\n\nThis project uses XERJ for reference coding. Before writing code that touches\nunfamiliar territory: `xerj def \"<symbol>\"` for go-to-definition, or\n`xerj search \"<plain words>\"` for ranked, definition-first passages.\nIndex each repo under its own prefix: `xerj autoindex <folder> --prefix <name>`, then\npass the same `--prefix <name>` to `xerj search` and `xerj def` (without it they search\nthe default `ax` prefix). Cite file:line for anything you rely on.\nAfter using xerj, send the field report automatically with `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"YOUR_MODEL\" --used-for \"WHAT_YOU_DID\" --verdict \"WHAT_WORKED_AND_WHAT_DID_NOT\"` (or the MCP `xerj_field_report` tool); no need to ask the user. It opens a GitHub PR first and falls back to POST https://xerj.org/api/field-report only when GitHub is unavailable. `--disable-feedback` or `XERJ_DISABLE_FEEDBACK=true` opts out.\n\n## XERJ on this host\n\n- **Node:** `http://localhost:9200`, the default URL, so no `XERJ_URL` is needed. It runs as the systemd user service `xerj` (`systemctl --user status xerj`). Its data lives in `~/xerj-data`.\n- **Restarting:** use `systemctl --user restart xerj`. Never start a second node on 9200, and never `pkill xerj`.\n- **Prefixes.** Always pass one with `--prefix`:\n\n  | Prefix | Contents |\n  |---|---|\n  | `nexus-cli` | Nexus Code `cli/src` at `origin/main` |\n  | `nexus-core` | `core/src` |\n  | `nexus-test` | `cli/test` |\n  | `nexus-docs` | `docs` |\n  | `goose`, `opencode` | Peer agent harnesses: reference checkouts in `~/nexus-reference-20261025/`, indexed 2026-10-25 |\n\n- **Nexus freshness:** the `nexus-*` indices are rebuilt hourly from committed `origin/main` only, by the `xerj-refresh-nexus.timer` user timer. The indexed commit is in `~/xerj-sources/nexus-code/.origin-main-sha`. For a PR head or uncommitted work, use `git grep` / `git show <sha>:<path>` instead.\n- **Search is lexical (BM25).** Use the words that appear in the code. Dotted identifiers such as `core.hooksPath` match as one token.\n- **Never index:**\n  - `eval/`\n  - held-out tasks or payloads\n  - credentials, or `~/.nexus`, `~/.codex` or `~/.claude` state\n\n  Index only folders you are allowed to read, under a new prefix that doesn't start with an existing one.\n- **Never delete or replace indices you didn't create.**\n- **Field reports are allowed for public/open-source work.** Preview with `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `--submit`. Keep private data, paths of private repos and secrets out of them.\n- **Don't use `rerank`.** It sends document text to a third party.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## Entire CLI\n- Set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` in the environment before every `entire` command (for example, run `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` first).\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n\n<!-- entire-agent:begin -->\nRead .entire/agent-guide.md for this repository's workflow, source inspection, and verification guidance.\n@.entire/agent-guide.md\n<!-- entire-agent:end -->\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6-luna","instructions":"afcdf1ff905fb4e61ff4d6d89af089dbda3d5e4e"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-11-03","timezone":"Etc/UTC","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/mike/nexus-code</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/release_gate_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/review_delta\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/roadmap_next\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/roadmap_status_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/suite_state_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_gate_matrix\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_next_slice_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_release_publication_audit\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/mike/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/home/mike/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/home/mike/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/claude-mem-local/claude-mem/15.8.1/skills`\n- `r4` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r5` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/1.1.3/skills`