{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:28:28.227Z","ordinal":86267,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a3be-1e43-7d40-811d-030dd5e1d8d5","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...794 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 11:28pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (20,824t read) | 126,640t work | 84% savings\n\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29656 10:28p ○ WP-1107 Gate Log Ends With \"💭 Assistant: done\" — Terminal Acceptance Tests Completed\n29657 10:36p ○ Gate Run — New Test Failures Appear: Standalone Profile Context Discovery and T4 Smoke Tests\n29658 \" ○ Gate Failure Context — Standalone Profile, T4 Smoke, and Peer Run Failures Are All Comparative Harness Tests\n29659 10:37p ○ WP-1107 Gate Full Failure Map — 20 ✖ Lines, All Infrastructure/Sandbox/Network, No WP-1107 Regressions\n29661 11:04p ✓ WP-1107 Qualification Gate Run Restarted — New make test Launched in Qualification Worktree\n29662 \" ○ WP-1107 Full Gate Run Complete — 2345 Tests, 33 Failures, All Infrastructure/Sandbox, No WP-1107 Regressions\n29663 \" ⚖ WP-1107 Gate Triage Plan — Fix Snapshot Build and Provider Test Fixtures Before Clean Gate\n29664 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Released — Gate Run final4 Logged as Incomplete (33 Failures, Terminal Stages Not Reached)\n29665 11:05p ○ Eval Sandbox Allowlist Failure Root Cause — @esbuild Path Outside Qualification Worktree Allowlist\n29666 \" ○ WP-1107 Provider Identity Contracts — Full Spec for llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM, and Generic Catalog\n29667 \" ○ parseAdvertisement Maps context_length/max_model_len to via:\"vllm\" — Standalone Ollama Profile Failure Root Cause Identified\n29669 11:06p ○ File Claims State — client.ts and provider_capabilities.ts Still Claimed, Test Files Unclaimed\n29670 \" ○ Standalone Profiles Test Uses model_proxy.mjs — Ollama Profile Relies on Proxy Shaping, Not Direct Mock\n29671 \" ○ Four Remaining Test Failures — Exact Assertion Mismatches Traced to Test Fixture Stale Expectations\n29672 \" ○ model_proxy.mjs Injects owned_by:\"library\" for Ollama Profile — Cache Clear Bug Causes Double /props Probe\n29679 11:08p ✓ Four Files Claimed for WP-1107 Fixture Corrections — Provider Handshake Test Updates Beginning\n29680 11:09p ○ roadmap_next Sub-Agent: GBNF Generator Not Connected to Provider Request Path on WP-1107 Branch\n29682 11:11p ⚠ Primary Session Waited 30 Seconds for Agent Response After Sending Encrypted /root Message\n29683 \" ✓ WP-1107 Plan Extended with Chunk 4 — Positive-Identity Qualification Fixtures and Discovery Cache\n29684 11:12p ● server_context_discovery.test.ts Updated — Ollama and vLLM Identity Handshake Tests Corrected\n29685 \" ● standalone_profiles.test.ts Updated — Use LocalLlmClient Directly and Assert getDetectedServerKind()\n29686 \" ● tokens.test.ts vLLM Fixture Updated — owned_by and /version Endpoint Added\n29687 \" ○ Focused RED Run — 3 Failures Confirm Integration Branch Still Needs Source Fixes\n29688 11:13p ● client.ts Discovery Cache Bug Fixed — Cache Invalidation Removed and Identity Handshakes Gated on Cache Miss\n29689 \" ● model_proxy.mjs Extended — vLLM /version and Ollama /api/version Identity Handshakes Added\n29690 11:14p ◆ WP-1107 Integration Branch Focused Suite GREEN — 54/54 Tests Pass After Source and Fixture Fixes\n29691 \" ⊘ Untracked Files in nexus-code Root — Agent Scripts and Session JSONs Present\n29692 11:15p ○ Local CI Environment Partially Set Up — Go 1.26.0 Installed But Rust Pinned Path Missing\n29693 \" ○ eval/isolate.mjs Requires /usr/local/nexus-qual/rust — Absent Locally, Gate Will Fail Compiler Exposure Check\n29694 11:16p ○ Pinned Rust 1.95.0 and Go Available at /opt/nexus-qual — Can Be Used to Populate /usr/local/nexus-qual/rust\n29695 \" ○ Pinned Toolchains Confirmed at /opt/nexus-qual — Go 1.22.12 and Rust 1.95.0 Match Policy Exactly\n29696 \" ○ isolate.mjs Uses sourceRoots Fallback — /opt/nexus-qual/rust and /opt/nexus-qual/go Are Accepted Alternate Sources\n29697 \" ○ Gate Run final4 Failure Map — \"compiler exposure could not be checked\" Is Root Cause for Most Sandbox Test Failures\n29698 \" ○ Two Distinct Gate Failure Root Causes Confirmed — Compiler Exposure Scan Failure and @esbuild Allowlist Violation\n29699 11:17p ✓ WP-1107 Integration Branch Working Diff — 8 Modified + 6 New Untracked Files, 151 Insertions\n29700 \" ○ provider_capabilities.ts Is Identical Between Qualification and Integration Worktrees\n29701 \" ● Qualification Worktree Fixed — Duplicate provider_capabilities.ts Removed and node_modules Relinked\n29702 11:18p ✓ All 14 WP-1107 Files Synced to Qualification Worktree — SHA-256 Verified Clean\n29703 11:20p ◆ Qualification Worktree Full Build Succeeded — harness-core v1.1.2-rc.2 and CLI TypeScript Build Clean\n29704 \" ◆ Qualification Worktree Snapshot Tests GREEN — 54/54 Focused + 10/10 Matrix Tests Pass\n29705 11:22p ○ Evaluator Preflight Run — 11 Failures, All Sandbox/Bubblewrap Tests, No \"compiler exposure\" String in Log\n29706 \" ○ Evaluator Preflight Complete — 13/62 Failures, All Root-Caused to \"compiler exposure could not be checked\"\n29707 \" ○ Compiler Exposure Scan Root Cause Found — /opt/nexus-qual/rust/bin/pytest Is a Non-Compiler Executable Being Flagged\n29708 \" ○ Compiler Exposure Scan Logic Confirmed — System Directories Are Scanned Via GNU find; Approved Toolchain Roots Are Excluded\n29709 11:23p ○ scan-compiler-exposure.mjs Fails Due to File Permissions — mike:mike 664, Not Root-Owned Without Group/Other Write\n29710 11:24p ⚖ WP-1107 Release Scope Confirmed — Include in v1.1.2 Alongside Defect Fixes\n29711 \" ○ scanOracleCompilerExposure Returns Empty paths Even After File Mode Fix\n29712 \" ○ scanOracleCompilerExposure Passes When Run From Qualification Worktree Directory\n29713 11:25p ○ Evaluator Preflight Final Run — Hardened Tests Passing, Compiler Exposure Scan Running Live\n29714 11:26p ○ Bubblewrap Sandbox Confirmed Running — cgroup_supervisor.mjs Launches bwrap With Full Toolchain Mounts\n\nAccess 127k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793748508.2277293,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
