{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:20:15.177Z","ordinal":87268,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea7a3db6cc81a3b5ed9dae9b61af57","usage":{"input_tokens":98542,"cached_input_tokens":98048,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":49,"reasoning_output_tokens":32,"total_tokens":98591},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":92426916,"cached_input_tokens":91699840,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":176313,"reasoning_output_tokens":80063,"total_tokens":92603229},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1759717584,"cached_input_tokens":1746432896,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3271190,"reasoning_output_tokens":1597787,"total_tokens":1762988774}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:20:16.666Z","ordinal":87269,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1a3ed-8c9a-7240-8949-cd5f878a8eb0","call_id":"call_689193fb1ba94ffdaedae36298510f95","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/release_gate_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The safest integration base is the clean release worktree at `f4f89734` on `v1/v112-release`. The WP-1107 provider work is still uncommitted in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration` at `3eea888a`; preserve and review that diff before integrating it.\\n\\nThe `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` claim is still formally held by codex-root under its old WP-1103/1104 scope. Its heartbeat is stale and no test runner is active, but no release or broken-claim entry exists. The proposed CLI test belongs under `cli/test/*.test.ts`, which the runner already discovers. The standalone eval matrix test is outside that discovery path, so run it as a separately claimed gate or reconcile the runner claim before adding it to the suite.\\n\\nThe WP-1107 file claims also remain on the provider worktree despite the later request to defer the work. The user’s instruction to include WP-1107 in v1.1.2 supersedes that deferral; reconcile those claims and the target branch before integration. GATEWAY remains held for RC15 E5, so the real endpoint matrix still needs an explicit handoff before inference.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_delta\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**APPROVED** for the proposed fixture, cache, and snapshot corrections.\\n\\nThe suite log separates into:\\n\\n- **Provider fixture updates:** the Ollama fixtures lack `/api/version`; the vLLM and token-count fixtures lack `/version`. Add the documented handshakes and assert detected provider kinds; keep the unsupported/no-adaptation and bare-catalog/no-probe regressions.\\n- **Source regression:** `discoverAdvertisement` deletes the endpoint/model context cache on every call at [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/cli/src/client.ts:1137), causing the existing repeat-discovery test to make `/props` twice. Preserve valid cached context or invalidate it selectively.\\n- **Qualification setup failures:** the candidate runtime resolves `@esbuild` into the integration worktree, outside the qualification snapshot’s allowlist; the run also lacks `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` and the built `nexus-tui` binary. Provision in-tree dependencies, the CI workspace fixture, and run `make build` in that snapshot. The compiler-exposure failures are fail-closed; this log does not establish their underlying cause, so verify the pinned compiler/toolchain environment during setup.\\n- **Proxy fixture detail:** [model_proxy.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1107-qualification/eval/model_proxy.mjs:86) must allow and answer `/version` and `/api/version`; otherwise the updated vLLM/Ollama fixtures cannot complete their handshakes.\\n\\nI reviewed the log and source read-only; I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/roadmap_next\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The GBNF generator is **not connected to a provider request path** on candidate `e134dcd5`. Its only references are its definitions in [tool_grammar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts:12) and unit tests in [tool_grammar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts:13). The client’s non-streaming, streaming, and native request builders contain no `grammar`, `guided_json`, or `format` field ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1377), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1531), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/src/client.ts:1858)).\\n\\nThe roadmap requires integration for llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama and a ≥99.5% valid tool-call JSON result across those endpoints ([ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:50), [ROADMAP.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:58)). The qualification record marks WP-1107 passed based on four compiler tests, while its gate row still says endpoint evidence is pending ([qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:32), [qualification record](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:42)). The older roadmap review explicitly deferred WP-1107 due to provider request changes ([ROADMAP-REVIEW.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP-REVIEW.md:194)); the user-approved full-roadmap scope supersedes that deferral, but the conflicting record and completion claim need reconciliation.\\n\\nA safe implementation sequence is a reviewed transport plan, followed by test-first request integration for each provider. Likely files are `cli/src/core/tool_grammar.ts`, `cli/src/client.ts`, and provider request-capture tests; provider capability detection may also need adjustment. `client.ts` is actively claimed by codex-root for RC16 work, so coordinate before editing. The grammar module, its tests, `client.test.ts`, and provider-capability file have no active file claims. GATEWAY remains claimed for RC15 E5 work; endpoint inference needs owner coordination. No edits or tests were made.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793751616.6665058}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
