{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:10:21.745Z","ordinal":88183,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2e2cc82b-88d0-46b0-bbef-1a3c288061a0","process_id":"54541","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff -- cli/src/client.ts | tail -60; rg -n 'tool_grammar|WP-1107|GBNF|grammar|schema' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs | head -100; git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff -- cli/src/client.ts | tail -60; rg -n 'tool_grammar|WP-1107|GBNF|grammar|schema' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs | head -100; git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"+    const showUrl = `${root}/api/show`;\n+    const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n+    try {\n+      await this.prepareCredential(this.endpoint);\n+      const versionResponse = await fetch(versionUrl, {\n+        headers: { ...this.authorization(versionUrl), \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n+        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n+        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n+      });\n+      if (!versionResponse.ok || !parseOllamaVersion(await versionResponse.json())) return false;\n+      const showResponse = await fetch(showUrl, {\n+        method: \"POST\",\n+        headers: { ...this.authorization(showUrl), \"content-type\": \"application/json\", \"X-Nexus-Purpose\": \"capabilities\" },\n+        body: JSON.stringify({ model: this.model }),\n+        signal: signal ? AbortSignal.any([signal, AbortSignal.timeout(2_000)]) : AbortSignal.timeout(2_000),\n+        ...this.fetchPolicy(),\n+      });\n+      if (!showResponse.ok) return false;\n+      const show = await showResponse.json();\n+      if (!show || typeof show !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(show)) return false;\n+      const showRecord = show as Record<string, unknown>;\n+      if (typeof showRecord.model === \"string\" && showRecord.model !== this.model) return false;\n+      LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.set(cacheKey, show);\n+      return true;\n+    } catch (err: any) {\n+      if (signal?.aborted) throw abortedError(randomUUID());\n+      return false;\n+    }\n+  }\n \n   /**\n    * The loaded context of a local server that lists no limits in its catalog, from that server's own endpoint (llama.cpp\n@@ -1182,6 +1255,11 @@ export class LocalLlmClient {\n     const cacheKey = `${this.endpoint}::${this.model}`;\n     const cached = LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.get(cacheKey);\n     if (cached) return cached;\n+    if (kind === \"ollama\" && LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.has(cacheKey)) {\n+      const found = parseServerContext(kind, LocalLlmClient.serverShowCache.get(cacheKey), this.model);\n+      if (found) LocalLlmClient.serverContextCache.set(cacheKey, found);\n+      return found;\n+    }\n     const root = this.endpoint.replace(/\\/v1\\/?$/, \"\");\n     const probes: Array<{ kind: \"llamacpp\" | \"lmstudio\" | \"ollama\"; url: string; init?: RequestInit }> = [\n       { kind: \"llamacpp\" as const, url: `${root}/props` },\n@@ -1373,6 +1451,7 @@ export class LocalLlmClient {\n         }\n         outboundTools = toolsEgress.sanitizedPayload || tools;\n       }\n+      outboundTools = adaptToolDefinitionsForServer(LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(currentEp) ?? \"unknown\", outboundTools);\n \n       const payload: any = {\n         model: this.model,\n@@ -1527,6 +1606,7 @@ export class LocalLlmClient {\n       }\n       outboundTools = toolsEgress.sanitizedPayload || tools;\n     }\n+    outboundTools = adaptToolDefinitionsForServer(LocalLlmClient.serverKindCache.get(currentEp) ?? \"unknown\", outboundTools);\n \n     const payload: any = {\n       model: this.model,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:10:const categories = [\"native_valid\", \"repaired\", \"schema_invalid\", \"invalid\"];\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:33:/** Validate the flat JSON Schema subset used by the four registered grammar pilot tools. */\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:34:export function validateToolArguments(schema, value) {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:35:  if (!isRecord(schema) || schema.type !== \"object\" || !isRecord(schema.properties)) return false;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:37:  const required = schema.required ?? [];\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:40:  if (schema.additionalProperties === false) {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:41:    for (const name of Object.keys(value)) if (!Object.hasOwn(schema.properties, name)) return false;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:43:  for (const [name, property] of Object.entries(schema.properties)) {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:63:export function classifyToolArguments({ schema, rawArguments, repairJsonWithClass }) {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:65:    return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:72:      return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:78:      if (!validateToolArguments(schema, parsed)) {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:79:        return { category: \"schema_invalid\", parsed: true, schemaValid: false, repaired: repair.repaired !== \"none\" };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:82:        return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: true, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:84:      return { category: \"repaired\", parsed: true, schemaValid: true, repaired: true };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:86:      return { category: \"invalid\", parsed: false, schemaValid: false, repaired: false };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:89:  const schemaValid = validateToolArguments(schema, parsed);\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:91:    category: schemaValid ? \"native_valid\" : \"schema_invalid\",\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:93:    schemaValid,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:106:    let schemaInvalid = 0;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:116:      if (toolSum !== 50 || tool.hybrid_reasoning_present !== 5 || tool.hybrid_schema_valid !== 5) return false;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:120:      schemaInvalid += tool.schema_invalid;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:123:    if (attemptSum !== 200 || endpoint.totals.native_valid !== nativeValid || endpoint.totals.repaired !== repaired || endpoint.totals.schema_invalid !== schemaInvalid || endpoint.totals.invalid !== invalid) return false;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:124:    return nativeValid * 1000 >= 200 * 995 && schemaInvalid === 0 && invalid === 0;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:149:  const totals = { attempts: 0, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0 };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:157:    assertCount(tool.hybrid_schema_valid, `${name}.hybrid_schema_valid`);\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:158:    if (tool.hybrid_reasoning_present > 5 || tool.hybrid_schema_valid > 5) throw new TypeError(`${name} hybrid counts exceed the five-hybrid matrix`);\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:173:    throw new TypeError(\"endpoint pass status does not match its exact syntax, schema, and hybrid reasoning counts\");\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:180:  if (!isRecord(evidence) || evidence.schemaVersion !== 1) throw new TypeError(\"unsupported evidence schema version\");\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:199:    if (matches.length !== 1 || !isRecord(matches[0].function.parameters)) throw new TypeError(`candidate must expose exactly one schema for ${name}`);\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:207:  const [clientModule, capabilitiesModule, parserModule, grammarProviderModule] = await Promise.all([\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:211:    import(pathToFileURL(path.join(cliRoot, \"core\", \"tool_grammar_provider.js\")).href),\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:213:  if (typeof clientModule.LocalLlmClient !== \"function\" || !Array.isArray(capabilitiesModule.HARNESS_TOOLS) || typeof parserModule.repairJsonWithClass !== \"function\" || typeof grammarProviderModule.adaptToolDefinitionsForServer !== \"function\") {\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:214:    throw new TypeError(\"installed candidate is missing client, tool registry, argument repair, or provider schema adaptation exports\");\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:218:    adaptToolsForServer: grammarProviderModule.adaptToolDefinitionsForServer,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:275:  if (Object.hasOwn(options, \"tools\")) throw new TypeError(\"tool schemas must be loaded from the exact installed candidate\");\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:305:      attempts: 50, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:306:      hybrid_attempts: 5, hybrid_reasoning_present: 0, hybrid_schema_valid: 0,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:326:          schema: tool.function.parameters,\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:334:        if (hybrid && classification.schemaValid) toolCounts.hybrid_schema_valid++;\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:337:    const totals = { attempts: 200, native_valid: 0, repaired: 0, schema_invalid: 0, invalid: 0 };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:361:  const evidence = { schemaVersion: 1, candidate: digests, endpoints };\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:388:  if (argv.length !== 2 || argv[0] !== \"--config\") throw new Error(\"usage: node eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs --config <private-config.json>\");\neval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:399:    process.stderr.write(`tool grammar matrix failed: ${String(error?.message ?? error)}\\n`);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:2:import { GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST } from \"./tool_grammar.js\";\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:5:const constrainedToolNames: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(GBNF_TOOL_ALLOWLIST);\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:7:/** Enable only vLLM's documented strict function-schema path for the bounded tool grammar pilot. */\ncli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts:27:/** vLLM strict schemas require a closed object and represent optional fields as required nullable values. */\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:1:# WP-1107 — Provider-Constrained Tool Arguments\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:5:**User story:** As a Nexus user running a supported inference engine, I need registered tool argument schemas passed through the provider's native constrained-tool path so tool calls arrive as schema-valid JSON and require fewer syntax repairs.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:9:- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:10:- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:11:- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:12:- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:14:- **AC6:** On each supported endpoint, 20 of the 200 attempts (five per tool) use a pinned reasoning-capable model and exercise a tool call after non-empty `<think>...</think>` reasoning. The installed client must preserve the provider's reasoning signal and the tool arguments must satisfy the selected tool's active parameter schema in the same response. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; live `WP-1107 hybrid reasoning and tool-call matrix`. This verifies reasoning/tool grammar coexistence, not reasoning quality or task correctness.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:16:**Out of scope:** Changing tool schemas or the allowlist; applying constraints to non-tool completions; measuring task-solving quality; enabling constraints on an endpoint that does not positively identify itself.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:18:**Dependencies:** Existing schema-derived grammar generator and `toolCallSyntax` telemetry; source implementation is otherwise independent. AC5 and AC6 depend on an approved shared inference window, pinned server/model configurations, and the exact candidate package.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:22:**Roadmap contract reconciliation:** Keep the existing dynamic GBNF compiler and its allowlist/schema tests as the deterministic schema-to-grammar implementation. Provider transport must use each server's compatible native tool path: llama.cpp rejects a caller grammar beside native tools but builds a dynamic tool grammar from their schemas; vLLM consumes `strict: true` through its structural-tag tool parser; Ollama carries tool schemas in `tools`, separately from response-level `format`. The hybrid `<think>...</think>` + tool-call requirement is not dropped: AC6 and the live matrix require a reasoning-plus-tool attempt on each exact endpoint. The provider's model/template/parser must build or accept that hybrid grammar; any endpoint that cannot pass AC6 remains unsupported and blocks G1.1-4. Do not claim that successful JSON syntax alone satisfies schema validity.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:28:- Add a typed adapter mapping provider kinds to documented native tool-schema behavior only after a provider-specific positive identity check. A configured lane label or `context_length`/`max_model_len` alone is insufficient.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:29:- For vLLM, clone each active allowlisted function schema and set its documented `strict` property to `true`. For llama.cpp and Ollama, preserve the existing native `tools` schema request and never add a top-level grammar or response-format field alongside tools. Unknown providers retain their current request unchanged.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:30:- Files: `cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:32:- Identity contract: llama.cpp requires the exact `/v1/models` `owned_by: \"llamacpp\"` marker or its `meta.n_ctx_train` marker plus a successful `/props` response matching the existing llama.cpp schema; Ollama requires its `/api/version` response with a non-empty `version` string and a successful `/api/show` response for the selected model; vLLM requires a successful `GET /version` returning a non-empty JSON `version` string plus the selected model in `/v1/models` (`wp1107-vllmserve` `basic.py:54-55`). A generic catalog containing only `context_length` or `max_model_len` remains `unknown` for provider-specific adaptation until that endpoint responds with the vLLM version contract. These are provider self-identification handshakes on the operator-configured endpoint, not cryptographic server authentication; any mismatch, missing probe, or malformed response disables provider-specific adaptation.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:33:- Retrieved request contracts: llama.cpp rejects caller `grammar` when native tools are supplied and builds the tool grammar from submitted schemas (`tools/server/server-common.cpp:1380-1450`; `common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:47-83`). Its reasoning PEG is prepended to the tool parser, and tool grammar generation uses the schema-bearing tool fields (`common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp:137-153,226-238`). Ollama carries `Tools` and `Format` as distinct fields and forwards them distinctly (`api/types.go:136-150`; `server/routes.go:3468-3480`); its docs distinguish tool calling from response-level structured output (`docs/api.md:519-527`). vLLM uses `FunctionDefinition.strict` (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:208-211`; `vllm/entrypoints/generate/base/protocol.py:298-313`) and resolves tool strictness from that flag in its structural-tag registry (`vllm/tool_parsers/structural_tag_registry.py:151-175`). Its response-level `response_format` is a separate structured-output path (`vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py:852-880`). The vLLM response-template grammar accepts separate `thinking` and tool-call schema fields and can require reasoning before a strict tool call (`vllm/parser/response_template_grammar.py:865-1003`).\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:37:- Attach the vLLM strict-tool adaptation to non-streaming, streaming, and supported native client request bodies without changing message, tool, credential, or egress handling. Preserve the current native tool-schema request for llama.cpp and Ollama.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:38:- Files: `cli/src/client.ts`, `cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:44:- Add a deterministic runner and schema validator. Fake-provider/serialization tests validate request construction and evidence validation only; they do not count as live endpoint measurements.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:45:- Files: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` (new), `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json` (new), `docs/evidence/v1.1.2/wp-1107-provider-matrix.json.sha256` (new detached digest), `docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:46:- Tests: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:48:- Evidence fields: archive SHA-256 and source commit; provider/server kind; server version and immutable image digest; model name and immutable model digest; non-secret configuration and stimulus digest; total attempts and per-tool attempts; reasoning-present counts for hybrid attempts; native-valid/repaired/schema-invalid/invalid counts per endpoint; exact pass equation result; evidence schema version. Store the finalized evidence file's SHA-256 in the detached `.sha256` sidecar and qualification record (the JSON cannot hash itself). Omit endpoint URLs, credentials, reasoning text, and other secrets.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:49:- Test/evidence: AC5's syntax threshold, schema-valid arguments, and zero schema-invalid/invalid requirement apply to all 200 attempts per provider. AC6 additionally requires non-empty reasoning signal and schema-valid tool arguments on every hybrid attempt. This measures argument validity and hybrid grammar coexistence; it does not certify tool selection, reasoning quality, or task correctness.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:62:- `llama.cpp` caller `grammar` cannot accompany native tools; its chat parser builds tool grammars from the supplied function schemas. Do not pass the generated per-tool GBNF as a top-level request field.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:63:- Ollama's `format` constrains the assistant response, while native tool calls use `tools`. Do not treat response-level JSON schema as tool-argument grammar.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md:64:- vLLM's `strict: true` depends on its strict-tool parser path and server configuration. The request capture test proves serialization, while the exact installed endpoint matrix is required to prove that the chosen server configuration enforces the tool schema.\n M cli/src/client.ts\n M cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts\n M cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts\n M cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts\n M cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts\n M cli/test/tokens.test.ts\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n M eval/model_proxy.mjs\n?? cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts\n?? cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts\n?? cli/test/tool_grammar_matrix.test.ts\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md\n?? eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs\n?? eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":707224828}},"started_at_ms":1793754621037,"completed_at_ms":1793754621745}}
