{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:12:25.065Z","ordinal":88222,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea8662b92081a38bf57b6c9aeecebc","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2543641203104b13b6aa65f4a36ec0dd","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@\\n-**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\\n+**Status as of 2026-11-04: the RC2 artifact remains historical; WP-1107 provider request integration now passes the local source gates, while live provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, installed-candidate, and publication gates remain open.**\\n@@\\n The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\\n+\\n+The current WP-1107 working-tree change adds provider-specific tool-schema request integration for positively identified llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama servers, with request-shape regressions and a provider-matrix runner. The exact source diff based on `e134dcd5` passed `make test` (2,342 of 2,347 tests, 0 failures, 5 skipped), terminal process-scope fixtures, all security lifecycle gates, and `make build`; its full-gate log SHA-256 is `0d3962c5cde8459813833214082bfd095cbcb702ca197bf0e7805630b3ba1331`. This is local source qualification for the uncommitted change, not installed-artifact or live-provider evidence. No provider inference was run because the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by the RC15 E5 stream.\\n@@\\n-| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\\n+| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds the bounded schema compiler. The current WP-1107 working-tree change connects provider-specific strict tool schemas to the llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama request paths after positive identity checks. The user-approved full v1.1.2 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **SOURCE INTEGRATION QUALIFIED; LIVE PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** | Provider request and identity regressions pass; the full exact-source gate and build pass. G1.1-4's supported-endpoint 99.5% metric has not been measured. The exact RC2 archive predates this change and is not eligible for release. |\\n@@\\n-| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | The generator is not connected to any client/provider request path on `e134dcd5`; its unit tests do not demonstrate constrained decoding. The shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric has been collected. | **IMPLEMENTATION INCOMPLETE; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\\n+| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Provider-specific strict tool-schema requests are now connected and locally tested. The shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric has been collected. | **SOURCE INTEGRATION PASSED; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\\n@@\\n-- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\\n-- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\\n+- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\\n+- [x] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the local source diff based on `e134dcd5`; final committed-candidate and installed-artifact qualification remain pending.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793754722.725428}}}
