{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:12:39.664Z","ordinal":88241,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1a41d-81ef-7d22-a49d-8622b2cb405d","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED.**\n\nThe provider request adaptation, positive identity checks, explicit rediscovery behavior, regression tests, and qualification wording otherwise look aligned with the plan. The explicit refresh clears only the cached server kind while retaining the context cache, consistent with the existing repeated-discovery regression.\n\nOne release-evidence gap remains: [tool_grammar_matrix.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs:286) lets callers supply `options.runtime`, replacing the installed candidate’s client, tools, adapter, and repair function after archive provenance is checked. The matrix test uses this override, so the exported runner can produce candidate-bound evidence while measuring a substitute runtime. Keep injection behind a test-only helper or seam, and ensure the production runner always loads its runtime from `installRoot`.\n\nI did not run tests. The qualification results you supplied are positive for the reviewed diff, but they do not close this runner-integrity issue or the still-pending live provider matrix."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793754759.663827,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2966}}
