{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:28.145Z","ordinal":89174,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016aea92dd173881a3a61e52ad60184ceb","usage":{"input_tokens":195785,"cached_input_tokens":194944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":510,"reasoning_output_tokens":301,"total_tokens":196295},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":134422923,"cached_input_tokens":133548544,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":216597,"reasoning_output_tokens":93635,"total_tokens":134639520},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1801713591,"cached_input_tokens":1788281600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3311474,"reasoning_output_tokens":1611359,"total_tokens":1805025065}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:30.461Z","ordinal":89175,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-47a8cb8d-fac4-44d1-8660-941bdc7ee0f6","process_id":"13007","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sha256sum /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final7.log; sed -n '1,12p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '28,45p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '80,95p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sha256sum /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final7.log; sed -n '1,12p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '28,45p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md; sed -n '80,95p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"94046204bcb02186758c7998a1c1a05ccd172ef71d52d0519d29a5210c81cc0b  /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final7.log\n# Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\n\n**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\nThis record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\n\nThe v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\n\n## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\n\nThe approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\n\n| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification status |\n| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Exact RC2 archive acceptance invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and confirmed hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. | **PASSED — dataset boundary** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Exact archive evidence: [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b`. The deterministic fixture only reports task completion; hidden validators intentionally remain false, so this is not task-solving or provider-quality evidence. |\n| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | Package acceptance passed 5/5 tests with isolated HOME and the exact archive; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. The same candidate-bound evidence file is linked in WP-1103. |\n| WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`. Deterministic evaluators wired into runner and scorer. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts` (9/9 passed). |\n| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | Integrated in commits `1cc28f94` and `faca6e6c`. CLI flag `--step`, REPL `/step`, and TUI `/step` catalogue entry with session command handler. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/step_loop.test.ts` (8/8 passed) and `cli/test/slash_router.test.ts` (34/34 passed). |\n| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Commit `1518780d` adds a bounded schema compiler and four generator tests, but the generator has no callsite in client/provider request construction on `e134dcd5`. No GBNF, `guided_json`, or Ollama schema field is sent. The user-approved full v1.1.0 scope supersedes the older deferral in `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §2.5. | **INCOMPLETE — provider integration required** | Existing `cli/test/tool_grammar.test.ts` checks generation only (4/4). Provider request tests and G1.1-4 endpoint measurements are still required. |\n| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate 27 Dependabot updates while meeting zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Integrated in commit `5f1f0677`. All 27 Dependabot PRs triaged and merged. `cargo deny check` clean. Zero deprecated npm packages. | **PASSED** | Merged CycloneDX SBOM generated (141 total components: 119 Cargo + 20 npm). glibc <= 2.35 verified on Rust binaries. |\n\n## Release-gate status\n\n| Gate | Required proof | Current evidence | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\n| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\n| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\n| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | The generator is not connected to any client/provider request path on `e134dcd5`; its unit tests do not demonstrate constrained decoding. The shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric has been collected. | **IMPLEMENTATION INCOMPLETE; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\n| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Exact source commit passed full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo lifecycle scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures. The exact archive is reproducible, has a validated 141-component CycloneDX SBOM and checksums, installs through `install.sh`, and passes package runtime/CLI acceptance. External CodeQL/CI and release-level PTY evidence are not present in this record. | **SOURCE AND LOCAL ARTIFACT GATES PASS; EXTERNAL CI / PTY PENDING** |\n\n## Historical RC1 artifact (not release-qualified)\n- **Installed package acceptance:** `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 5/5 on the exact archive, including installed evaluator execution outside the checkout and a candidate launch without mounting evaluator code. Test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`.\n- **Installed-candidate evidence:** [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), SHA-256 `37c7fcee8d1058d04a90f672b5949fbaee7710bc22677612036da140dc4cc176`. The deterministic fixture submitted all six public benchmark tasks once, captured six requests, and found no hidden validator path or command in prompts. It returns a generic completion, so hidden validators are false by design and this does not measure task-solving quality. The same full run passed all five package-runtime tests.\n\n## Exact-candidate release checklist\n\n- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\n- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\n- [ ] Applicable v1.1.0 release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 are qualified on the final candidate.\n- [x] Prior RC2 full source suite, security lifecycle scans, `make build`/TypeScript type build, and terminal process-scope acceptance passed before the CERI provenance correction.\n- [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on exact clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`.\n- [x] Package checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility verified for the final archive.\n- [x] Packaged CLI evaluator options and installed-candidate acceptance verified for the final archive.\n- [ ] External CI/CodeQL and the supported-provider constrained-decoding matrix are attached to the final candidate.\n- [ ] Acceptance evidence and qualification record committed for the final candidate.\n- [ ] Tag `v1.1.2` and release publication (reserved for repository owner `mikeholownych`).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":754716847}},"started_at_ms":1793757929706,"completed_at_ms":1793757930461}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:32.008Z","ordinal":89176,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1a44d-e9e8-7b33-8fe8-fbb87bf97e9d","call_id":"call_c2151b7d597e43948fe1c43ca3860d2e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a9e4f5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.754753884,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2553,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2553)\\nTotal output lines: 46\\n\\n94046204bcb02186758c7998a1c1a05ccd172ef71d52d0519d29a5210c81cc0b  /tmp/wp1107-full-gate-final7.log\\n# Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\\n\\n**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\\nThis record tracks candidate commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On this clean commit, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). Two digest-pinned builds of the exact commit produced identical RC2 archives; the canonical-mode archive installed and passed all five packaged-runtime acceptance tests.\\n\\nThe v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\\n\\n## Separate specialist roadmap status (informational)\\n\\nThe approved v1.1.2 release scope is the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap from v1.1.0, as recorded in [the release scope](v1.1.2.md). The [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md) is tracked separately; its status below is informational and does not add work or gates to this release scope.\\n\\n| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification status |\\n| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Exact RC2 archive acceptance invoked all six public benchmark tasks once through a loopback provider and confirmed hidden oracle paths and commands were absent from captured prompts. | **PASSED — dataset boundary** | Dataset manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Exact archive evidence: [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), archive SHA-256 `3e39bd36f31ddd706283febe88b4ecf55cc73c08607c568ca37acd9e9a57fa8b`. The deterministic fixture only reports task completion; hidden validators intentionally remain false, so this is not task-solving or provider-quality evidence. |\\n| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Exact RC2 installed package ran the versioned evaluator outside the checkout and launched a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PASSED — package runtime** | Package acceptance passed 5/5 tests with isolated HOME and the exact archive; test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`. The same candidate-bound evidence file is linked in WP-1103. |\\n| WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Integrated in commit `e2bacf1a`. Deterministic evaluators wired into runner and scorer. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts` (9/9 passed). |\\n| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for opera…353 tokens truncated…--|---|---|\\n| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | Lifecycle, request, tool, compaction, redaction, and path-safety tests passed on source `97945557`; the exact-source full suite and process-scope acceptance passed. | **SOURCE PASSED; installed trace capture still needs release-level confirmation** |\\n| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Exact archive `3e39bd36…` invoked all six public benchmark tasks and captured six prompts with no hidden validator path or command. | **PACKAGE DATASET-BOUNDARY PASS; task quality not measured** |\\n| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Exact archive passed all five package-runtime acceptance tests, including evaluation outside checkout and launching a candidate without mounting evaluator code. | **PACKAGE PASS** |\\n| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | The generator is not connected to any client/provider request path on `e134dcd5`; its unit tests do not demonstrate constrained decoding. The shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by another release stream, so no endpoint metric has been collected. | **IMPLEMENTATION INCOMPLETE; PROVIDER MATRIX PENDING** |\\n| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Exact source commit passed full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo lifecycle scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures. The exact archive is reproducible, has a validated 141-component CycloneDX SBOM and checksums, installs through `install.sh`, and passes package runtime/CLI acceptance. External CodeQL/CI and release-level PTY evidence are not present in this record. | **SOURCE AND LOCAL ARTIFACT GATES PASS; EXTERNAL CI / PTY PENDING** |\\n\\n## Historical RC1 artifact (not release-qualified)\\n- **Installed package acceptance:** `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 5/5 on the exact archive, including installed evaluator execution outside the checkout and a candidate launch without mounting evaluator code. Test log SHA-256 `2d1f6edbb7ddb12883564e7dc71d4e42c1dfac7548495d00063e7f0100303f76`.\\n- **Installed-candidate evidence:** [`acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json`](../evidence/v1.1.2/acceptance-3e39bd36f31d-installed.json), SHA-256 `37c7fcee8d1058d04a90f672b5949fbaee7710bc22677612036da140dc4cc176`. The deterministic fixture submitted all six public benchmark tasks once, captured six requests, and found no hidden validator path or command in prompts. It returns a generic completion, so hidden validators are false by design and this does not measure task-solving quality. The same full run passed all five package-runtime tests.\\n\\n## Exact-candidate release checklist\\n\\n- [x] WP-1101–WP-1106 and WP-1108 source acceptance and test suites are bound to exact commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`; WP-1103/WP-1104 package acceptance is bound to archive `3e39bd36…`.\\n- [ ] WP-1107 provider-specific request integration and request-shape tests pass on the final source candidate.\\n- [ ] Applicable v1.1.0 release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 are qualified on the final candidate.\\n- [x] Prior RC2 full source suite, security lifecycle scans, `make build`/TypeScript type build, and terminal process-scope acceptance passed before the CERI provenance correction.\\n- [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on exact clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`.\\n- [x] Package checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility verified for the final archive.\\n- [x] Packaged CLI evaluator options and installed-candidate acceptance verified for the final archive.\\n- [ ] External CI/CodeQL and the supported-provider constrained-decoding matrix are attached to the final candidate.\\n- [ ] Acceptance evidence and qualification record committed for the final candidate.\\n- [ ] Tag `v1.1.2` and release publication (reserved for repository owner `mikeholownych`).\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793757932.008008}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
