{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:05:43.546Z","ordinal":89180,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016aea92ee8fac81a3857cce62a628a24f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_90f2634d9bd3488b8ccab62fc12204a4","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@\\n-**Status as of 2026-11-03: RC2 source and installed-package gates passed for the recorded candidate, but WP-1107 provider integration is incomplete; provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, and publication gates remain open.**\\n+**Status as of 2026-11-04: WP-1107 provider request integration passes local source gates; live provider-matrix, external CI/CodeQL, installed-candidate, and publication gates remain open.**\\n@@\\n The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive and the first local RC2 packaging attempt are superseded and are not eligible for release. The qualified local RC2 archive is not published; its checksum, installer, and installed-package evidence are recorded below. The installer test used a local HTTP feed and skipped GitHub provenance-attestation verification because this candidate is unpublished. Since WP-1107 is not connected to a provider request path on this source commit, this RC2 artifact is historical qualification evidence and is not the final release candidate.\\n+\\n+The current WP-1107 working-tree change connects provider-specific strict tool schemas to llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama request paths after positive identity checks, and adds a runner that measures the exact installed candidate. The exact source diff based on `e134dcd5` passed `make test` (2,342 of 2,347 tests, 0 failures, 5 skips), terminal process-scope fixtures, all security lifecycle gates, and `make build`; its full-gate log SHA-256 is `94046204bcb02186758c7998a1c1a05ccd172ef71d52d0519d29a5210c81cc0b`. Runner unit tests use a synthetic installed-runtime fixture and are not live provider measurements. The change remains uncommitted and has not been packaged or installed; no provider inference was run because the shared `GATEWAY` claim remains held by the RC15 E5 stream.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","create_time":1793757934.5631125}}}
