{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:08:02.370Z","ordinal":89284,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a1a331-c45a-70a3-a6bd-1ee2b1ee1a25","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5afea54f-9f78-43fb-9889-042604b485c9","process_id":"17705","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^AC[0-9]|AC[0-9]:' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md; git log -1 --format='%h %s'; git diff --cached --stat"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1101-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n '^AC[0-9]|AC[0-9]:' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md; git log -1 --format='%h %s'; git diff --cached --stat"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"9:- **AC1:** An identified llama.cpp endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and no caller-supplied top-level `grammar` while tools are active. Test: `client preserves llama.cpp native tool schemas without incompatible grammar field` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n10:- **AC2:** An identified vLLM endpoint receives `strict: true` on each active allowlisted function schema; Nexus does not substitute a response-level `response_format` constraint for tool-argument constraints. Test: `client enables vLLM strict mode for allowlisted tool schemas`.\n11:- **AC3:** An identified Ollama endpoint receives active allowlisted schemas through its native `tools` request field and Nexus does not send response-level JSON-schema `format` as a tool-argument constraint. Test: `client preserves Ollama native tool schemas without response format constraint` (baseline behavior; add a regression guard).\n12:- **AC4:** Unknown, unsupported, or ambiguously identified endpoints retain their current request shape; no grammar field is sent based only on a configured lane label or generic OpenAI-compatible catalog fields. Tests: `client omits constrained fields for unknown and unsupported providers`; `generic context catalog remains unknown and receives no grammar field`; `provider identity accepts llama.cpp only with its marker and valid props handshake`; `provider identity accepts vLLM only with its documented version response`; `provider identity accepts Ollama only with version and selected-model show response`; `client omits constrained fields for missing malformed or mismatched provider identity`.\n13:- **AC5:** On each supported endpoint, the exact installed candidate completes 200 attempts: 50 for each of four fixed allowlisted tool schemas. Each attempt requests exactly one tool call. `native_valid` means the raw provider argument string parses with `JSON.parse` and satisfies that tool's active parameter schema before normalization or repair; `repaired` means raw parsing fails and the existing repair path yields parseable, schema-conforming JSON; `schema_invalid` means raw or repaired JSON parses but fails the active parameter schema; `invalid` includes provider errors, timeouts, missing calls, and arguments that remain unparseable after repair. These four categories are mutually exclusive and sum to attempts. An endpoint passes only when `native_valid * 1000 >= attempts * 995`, `schema_invalid == 0`, and `invalid == 0`; report exact integer counts and do not round percentages for the decision. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix evidence schema rejects invalid counts and identity omissions`; `tool grammar matrix computes endpoint pass without percentage rounding`; `tool grammar matrix rejects schema-invalid tool arguments`; `tool grammar matrix runner records archive and per-endpoint identity`; live `WP-1107 supported-endpoint syntax and schema matrix`.\n14:- **AC6:** On each supported endpoint, 20 of the 200 attempts (five per tool) use a pinned reasoning-capable model and exercise a tool call after non-empty `<think>...</think>` reasoning. The installed client must preserve the provider's reasoning signal and the tool arguments must satisfy the selected tool's active parameter schema in the same response. Tests/evidence: `tool grammar matrix includes hybrid attempts and rejects missing reasoning evidence`; live `WP-1107 hybrid reasoning and tool-call matrix`. This verifies reasoning/tool grammar coexistence, not reasoning quality or task correctness.\n3eea888a docs(release): qualify exact RC2 archive\n cli/src/client.ts                         |  90 ++++++-\n cli/src/core/provider_capabilities.ts     |  21 +-\n cli/src/core/tool_grammar_provider.ts     |  43 ++++\n cli/test/client_tool_grammar.test.ts      | 324 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\n cli/test/provider_capabilities.test.ts    |  14 ++\n cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts |  11 +-\n cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts      |   4 +-\n cli/test/tokens.test.ts                   |   6 +-\n cli/test/tool_grammar_matrix.test.ts      |   2 +\n docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md     |  13 +-\n docs/v1.1.0/WP-1107-PLAN.md               |  67 +++++\n eval/model_proxy.mjs                      |  19 +-\n eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs              | 403 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n eval/tool_grammar_matrix.test.mjs         | 266 ++++++++++++++++++++\n 14 files changed, 1261 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":701833863}},"started_at_ms":1793758081667,"completed_at_ms":1793758082369}}
